vel plus one-half the ship's armor bonus (rounded down), the Pilot's Heroic Level, or the ship's Armor bonus, whichever is highest. In addition, all Gunners on your ship add one-half your Heroic Level, or one-half their Heroic Level, whichever is more, to damage rolls with Vehicle Weapons. Finally, you treat any generic crew as being one quality level higher (maximum of Ace, see Crew Quality).","description":"Prerequisites: Charisma 13, Intelligence 13, When you are the Commander of a Capital Ship, calculate its Reflex Defense using your Heroic Level plus one-half the ship's armor bonus (rounded down), the Pilot's Heroic Level, or the ship's Armor bonus, whichever is highest. In addition, all Gunners on your ship add one-half your Heroic Level, or one-half their Heroic Level, whichever is more, to damage rolls with Vehicle Weapons. Finally, you treat any generic crew as being one quality level higher (maximum of Ace, see Crew Quality).","class":"Noble","costNumeric":null,"category":"Noble","tree":"Naval Officer","treeId":"057a978a7dc1d5a7","tags":["armor","defender","noble","striker","support","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[{"_id":"f9275c38-3cb5-4ab3-aaa5-25e5722dcdd3","name":"Born Leader","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.defenses.will","mode":2,"value":"1"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Born Leader"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.born_leader"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.6a66ba6e0834dd6f"}}},{"_id":"9140bd53be223997","name":"Coordinate","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Leadership","prerequisites":null,"benefit":"All allies in line of sight gain +1 when using aid another (maximum +5).","description":"All allies gain +1 when using Aid Another, up to +5.","class":"Noble","costNumeric":null,"category":"Noble","tree":"Leadership","canonicalName":"Coordinate","canonicalTree":"Bab +12","treeId":"5964237d22681dc0","tags":["noble","striker"]},"effects":[{"_id":"25b28077-6a3c-43d8-97ba-a128e768f614","name":"Coordinate","icon":"icons/svg/handshake.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.actions.aidAnother","mode":2,"value":"1"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Coordinate"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.coordinate"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.a52044feeab3fe05"}}},{"_id":"655b3978b8550c91","name":"Dastardly Strike","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Misfortune","tree":"Misfortune","prerequisites":"Combat Reflexes","description":"Whenever you deal damage to an opponent denied its Dexterity bonus to its Reflex Defense, you can choose not to move the target down the Condition Track and instead impose a -5 penalty on all your opponent's attack and melee damage rolls until the end of your next turn. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook At the start of your turn, you may spend a Force Point. Until the start of your next turn, you can make an Attack of Opportunity against a single opponent that has just taken damage from another character. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook When attacking with a Light Melee weapon, a Lightsaber, or any other weapon that benefits from the Weapon Finesse Feat, you may add an additional point of damage on a successful attack.","benefit":"Whenever you deal damage to an opponent denied its Dexterity bonus to its Reflex Defense, you can choose not to move the target down the Condition Track and instead impose a -5 penalty on all your opponent's attack and melee damage rolls until the end of your next turn. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook At the start of your turn, you may spend a Force Point. Until the start of your next turn, you can make an Attack of Opportunity against a single opponent that has just taken damage from another character. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook When attacking with a Light Melee weapon, a Lightsaber, or any other weapon that benefits from the Weapon Finesse Feat, you may add an additional point of damage on a successful attack.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"67b59e020c1660eb","tags":["condition-removal","controller","defender","feat-chain","force","force-control","force-defense","force-offense","lightsaber","melee","mobility","striker","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.9e4345faaaa94dd8"}}},{"_id":"67b0d4d99f458932","name":"Disruptive","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Misfortune","prerequisites":"","benefit":"As a Standard Action, you can do or say something that catches your enemies off guard. All opponents within 6 squares of you, and within your line of sight take a -2 penalty to their Defenses until the start of your next turn. The penalty is negated if line of sight is broken. This Talent has a range of 6 squares at Starship Scale. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy at War Prerequisites: , Walk the Line You can create opportunities to chip away at our opponents' defenses. You can use each of the following actions once per encounter as a Standard Action: Create Opening: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any target within your Range. If you damage the target, the target takes a -5 penalty to their Reflex Defense until the start of your next turn. Crippling Attack: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any target within your Range. Until the start of your next turn, the target takes a -2 penalty to their base speed. Vicious Attack: Make a melee or ranged attack within your Range against two opponents that are within 2 squares of each other. Make separate attack rolls at a -5 penalty against each target, but roll damage once only. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy You can fill your opponent with doubt by making a Persuasion check as a Standard Action against a single target that can hear and understand you within 12 squares of you. If your check result equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, the target takes a -2 penalty to its base speed, and if the target takes a Standard Action, it must also spend its Swift Action. This penalty lasts until the end of the target's next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy","description":"As a Standard Action, you can do or say something that catches your enemies off guard. All opponents within 6 squares of you, and within your line of sight take a -2 penalty to their Defenses until the start of your next turn. The penalty is negated if line of sight is broken. This Talent has a range of 6 squares at Starship Scale. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy at War Prerequisites: , Walk the Line You can create opportunities to chip away at our opponents' defenses. You can use each of the following actions once per encounter as a Standard Action: Create Opening: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any target within your Range. If you damage the target, the target takes a -5 penalty to their Reflex Defense until the start of your next turn. Crippling Attack: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any target within your Range. Until the start of your next turn, the target takes a -2 penalty to their base speed. Vicious Attack: Make a melee or ranged attack within your Range against two opponents that are within 2 squares of each other. Make separate attack rolls at a -5 penalty against each target, but roll damage once only. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy You can fill your opponent with doubt by making a Persuasion check as a Standard Action against a single target that can hear and understand you within 12 squares of you. If your check result equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, the target takes a -2 penalty to its base speed, and if the target takes a Standard Action, it must also spend its Swift Action. This penalty lasts until the end of the target's next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy","class":"Scoundrel","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scoundrel","tree":"Misfortune","treeId":"67b59e020c1660eb","tags":["action-economy","defender","melee","mobility","positioning","ranged","scaling","scoundrel","skills","social","striker"]},"effects":[{"_id":"4eefbe8a-47cc-4cee-a02a-7c11b76bd6b5","name":"Disruptive","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.morale.bonuses_suppressed","mode":5,"value":"true"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Disruptive"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.disruptive"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.91b335f8565b90ef"}}},{"_id":"98cc765481cd44e4","name":"Indomitable","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Commando","prerequisites":null,"benefit":"Once per day, move +5 steps up the condition track (not persistent conditions); may be taken multiple times.","description":"","class":"Soldier","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","treeId":"798ed0945cbdac1c","tree":"Commando","tags":["condition-removal","controller","mobility","scaling","soldier","striker","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.indomitable"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.b8aaf500d3069938"}}},{"_id":"26e08948c80843d7","name":"Sneak Attack","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Misfortune","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Any time your opponent is Flat-Footed or otherwise denied its Dexterity bonus to Reflex Defense, you deal an additional 1d6 points of damage with a successful melee or ranged attack. You must be within 6 squares of the target to make a with a ranged weapon. You may select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select it, your damage increases by +1d6 (Maximum +10d6). Prerequisite: You can take advantage of your adversary's distractions, no matter how momentary or fleeting. Once per turn, when you Flank a target, you can treat that target as if they were Flat-Footed for one of your attacks. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy If you succeed on a Deception check against a target's Will Defense as a Swift Action, until the start of your next turn you can move though the Threatened Area of that target as part of your Move Action without provoking an Attack of Opportunity. Each Threatened square that you move through counts as 2 squares of movement. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Point-Blank Shot You can use the Talent against a target within 12 squares, instead of within 6 squares. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide You excel at seduction through deception. If you fail a Persuasion check to change a target's Attitude, you can immediately reroll the check using your Deception skill in lieu of your Persuasion skill. You must accept the result of the reroll, even if it is worse. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide Once per encounter as a Move Action, you can attempt to seize a held, carried, or worn object from an adjacent target by making a Disarm attack, with a +10 bonus on your attack roll. If the attack succeeds, you are now holding the object, and you cannot use this Talent in place of the Disarm Action. You cannot conceal the use of this Talent from the target. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy","description":"Any time your opponent is Flat-Footed or otherwise denied its Dexterity bonus to Reflex Defense, you deal an additional 1d6 points of damage with a successful melee or ranged attack. You must be within 6 squares of the target to make a with a ranged weapon. You may select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select it, your damage increases by +1d6 (Maximum +10d6). Prerequisite: You can take advantage of your adversary's distractions, no matter how momentary or fleeting. Once per turn, when you Flank a target, you can treat that target as if they were Flat-Footed for one of your attacks. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy If you succeed on a Deception check against a target's Will Defense as a Swift Action, until the start of your next turn you can move though the Threatened Area of that target as part of your Move Action without provoking an Attack of Opportunity. Each Threatened square that you move through counts as 2 squares of movement. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Point-Blank Shot You can use the Talent against a target within 12 squares, instead of within 6 squares. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide You excel at seduction through deception. If you fail a Persuasion check to change a target's Attitude, you can immediately reroll the check using your Deception skill in lieu of your Persuasion skill. You must accept the result of the reroll, even if it is worse. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide Once per encounter as a Move Action, you can attempt to seize a held, carried, or worn object from an adjacent target by making a Disarm attack, with a +10 bonus on your attack roll. If the attack succeeds, you are now holding the object, and you cannot use this Talent in place of the Disarm Action. You cannot conceal the use of this Talent from the target. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy","class":"Scoundrel","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scoundrel","tree":"Misfortune","treeId":"67b59e020c1660eb","tags":["action-economy","battlefield-control","controller","defender","melee","mobility","positioning","precision","ranged","scaling","scoundrel","skills","social","striker"]},"effects":[{"_id":"3195415b-2276-403c-9fb1-5d323d38d31a","name":"Sneak Attack","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.damage.flatfooted","mode":2,"value":"1d6"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Sneak Attack"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.sneak_attack"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.1505abc8babeeb84"}}},{"_id":"b3fcb73107a196ba","name":"Unarmed","type":"weapon","img":"icons/svg/sword.svg","system":{"damage":"1d4+5","damageType":"kinetic","attackBonus":0,"attackAttribute":"str","range":"melee","weight":1,"cost":0,"equipped":true,"description":"","properties":[],"ammunition":{"type":"none","current":0,"max":0},"weaponCategory":"simple","proficiency":"simple","subcategory":""},"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"placeholder":true,"npc":{"flatAttackBonus":7,"flatDamageFormula":"1d4+5","useFlat":true}}}},{"_id":"84c15d9292bce9b7","name":"Vibrodagger","type":"weapon","img":"icons/svg/sword.svg","system":{"damage":"2d4+5","damageType":"kinetic","attackBonus":0,"attackAttribute":"str","range":"melee","weight":0.5,"cost":250,"equipped":true,"description":"<p>A small vibroweapon easily concealed. Popular with assassins and spies.</p>\n      <p><strong>Special:</strong> Vibroweapon. Critical threat range 19-20. Can be thrown (range 6 squares).</p>","properties":["Vibroweapon","Critical 19-20","Concealable"],"ammunition":{"type":"none","current":0,"max":0},"weaponCategory":"melee","proficiency":"advanced-melee","subcategory":"advanced","costNumeric":250,"category":"advanced"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.weapons.weapon-vibrodagger"},"swse":{"npc":{"flatAttackBonus":7,"flatDamageFormula":"2d4+5","useFlat":true}}}},{"_id":"f0ef6c8db40fdddf","name":"Blaster Carbine","type":