Vehicles may immediately move a number of squares equal to their speed.","description":"As a Swift Action, you may designate a single creature, Vehicle or object within your line of sight as the target of . Any Weapon Batteries attacking the target deal an extra die of damage for every 2 points by which their attack roll exceeds the target's Reflex Defense (instead of every 3 points). In addition, when using the Tactical Fire option for a Capital Ship, you may designated a weapon or Weapon Battery to make a single attack. As a Full-Round Action, you can designate a number of Vehicles equal to your Officer Class Level and within your line of sight. Those Vehicles may immediately move a number of squares equal to their speed.","class":"Soldier","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","tree":"Naval Officer","treeId":"057a978a7dc1d5a7","tags":["action-economy","controller","defender","feat-chain","mobility","positioning","soldier","striker","sustained-damage","talent-chain"]},"effects":[{"_id":"6f88b513-9d62-4971-a686-72668a6da31d","name":"Combined Fire","icon":"icons/svg/gun.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.damage","mode":2,"value":"2"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Combined Fire"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.combined_fire"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.17518b7669101122"}}},{"_id":"313084e96b9c57d8","name":"Deceptive Shot","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Gunslinger","prerequisites":null,"benefit":"Target in line of sight within 6 squares; Deception vs Will imposes loss of Dexterity to Defense until next turn.","description":"Make a Deception check vs Will Defense; if successful, the target loses Dexterity to Defense until the end of your next turn.","class":"Gunslinger","costNumeric":null,"category":"Gunslinger","tree":"Gunslinger","treeId":"cb6f775cd227a3e3","tags":["defender","positioning","ranged","skills","social"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.deceptive_shot"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.b1afecfea833a2a5"}}},{"_id":"f7c6491aa224471b","name":"Draw Fire","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Disgrace","prerequisites":"","benefit":"You may not gain the benefit of this Talent if another character within 6 squares of you has used this talent since the end of your last turn. You may not use this Talent in the same round as the Soldier's Talent.","description":"You may not gain the benefit of this Talent if another character within 6 squares of you has used this talent since the end of your last turn. You may not use this Talent in the same round as the Soldier's Talent.","class":"Soldier","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","tree":"Disgrace","treeId":"e91cc675fbf9ba6e","tags":["positioning","soldier","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.draw_fire"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.f29d5c0628459c94"}}},{"_id":"fdca9700dcd528d7","name":"Fool's Luck","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Fortune","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Once per encounter, you can turn a Critical Hit against you into a normal hit. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisite: Once per encounter, as a Reaction, you gain a +5 luck bonus to any one Defense until the start of your next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy","description":"Once per encounter, you can turn a Critical Hit against you into a normal hit. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisite: Once per encounter, as a Reaction, you gain a +5 luck bonus to any one Defense until the start of your next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy","class":"Scoundrel","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scoundrel","tree":"Fortune","treeId":"cee9b9398682b7d0","tags":["action-economy","defender","precision","scoundrel","striker"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.fools_luck"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.5319a796f2c4ff64"}}},{"_id":"06c5b582bea5ec67","name":"Full Throttle","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Expert Pilot","prerequisites":null,"benefit":"You may take 10 to increase speed; all-out movement is x5 instead of x4.","description":"You may take 10 to increase speed; all-out movement increases speed by ×5 instead of ×4.","class":"Ace Pilot","costNumeric":null,"category":"Ace Pilot","tree":"Expert Pilot","treeId":"b17c1515c06361d6","tags":["controller","mobility","scout"]},"effects":[{"_id":"8f8724d4-e516-4f73-9d38-51fe2cd270cf","name":"Full Throttle","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.speed","mode":2,"value":"1"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Full Throttle"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.full_throttle"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.34ff9dc64050028d"}}},{"_id":"d1ad869590dfaa74","name":"Keep it Together","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Fringer","prerequisites":"Jury-Rigger","benefit":"When you jury-rig a vehicle, it moves -2 down the condition track at end (instead of -5).","description":"Once per encounter, your vehicle avoids moving down the condition track.","class":"Scout","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scout","tree":"Fringer","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.jury_rigger"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"7c47d36dc1f77d9c","tags":["condition-removal","controller","feat-chain","mobility","scout","talent-chain"]},"effects":[{"_id":"a0a072a8-d539-4e13-8542-20bca578650a","name":"Keep it Together","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.jury_rig.stability","mode":5,"value":"2_down"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Keep it Together"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.keep_it_together"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.9211e3f6268b3413"}}},{"_id":"998fea06d2d52a10","name":"Multiattack Proficiency (pistols)","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Gunslinger","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Dual Weapon Mastery I, Weapon Focus (Pistols) Immediately after making a Full Attack where you attack with two Pistols, you may move up to your Speed as a Free Action. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy of Intrigue You are a master of the elegant, if archaic, custom of dueling with Pistols. You can use each of the following Actions once per encounter as a Standard Action: End Game: You make a single ranged attack with a Pistol against an opponent within Range. The opponent's Damage Threshold is halved (rounded down) for the purpose of this attack. Snap Aiming: You make a single ranged attack with the benefits of Aiming. Stand Ready: You gain a +4 bonus to your Reflex Defense until the end of your next turn and make a single ranged attack. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy If you are within 6 squares of a target and are armed with a Pistol or a Rifle, you can act as though you occupied the nearest square adjacent to the target for purposes of determining whether or not you or any allies are Flanking that target. You may only be considered to be Flanking a single target at a time. You must spend a Swift Action on your turn to designate the target you Flank at range. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions When moving away from a pursuing target, if you either Run or use two Move Actions during this turn, you can make a single ranged attack with a -5 penalty as part of your Move Action. You can spend a Force Point to avoid the penalty. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions","description":"Dual Weapon Mastery I, Weapon Focus (Pistols) Immediately after making a Full Attack where you attack with two Pistols, you may move up to your Speed as a Free Action. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy of Intrigue You are a master of the elegant, if archaic, custom of dueling with Pistols. You can use each of the following Actions once per encounter as a Standard Action: End Game: You make a single ranged attack with a Pistol against an opponent within Range. The opponent's Damage Threshold is halved (rounded down) for the purpose of this attack. Snap Aiming: You make a single ranged attack with the benefits of Aiming. Stand Ready: You gain a +4 bonus to your Reflex Defense until the end of your next turn and make a single ranged attack. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy If you are within 6 squares of a target and are armed with a Pistol or a Rifle, you can act as though you occupied the nearest square adjacent to the target for purposes of determining whether or not you or any allies are Flanking that target. You may only be considered to be Flanking a single target at a time. You must spend a Swift Action on your turn to designate the target you Flank at range. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions When moving away from a pursuing target, if you either Run or use two Move Actions during this turn, you can make a single ranged attack with a -5 penalty as part of your Move Action. You can spend a Force Point to avoid the penalty. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions","class":"Gunslinger","costNumeric":null,"category":"Gunslinger","tree":"Gunslinger","treeId":"cb6f775cd227a3e3","tags":["action-economy","controller","defender","dual-wield","evasion","force","force-control","force-defense","force-offense","mobility","positioning","ranged","striker","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.multiattack_proficiency_pistols"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.b812c197daea93fd"}}},{"_id":"8cc9911afcef0c82","name":"Sneak Attack","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Misfortune","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Any time your opponent is Flat-Footed or otherwise denied its Dexterity bonus to Reflex Defense, you deal an additional 1d6 points of damage with a successful melee or ranged attack. You must be within 6 squares of the target to make a with a ranged weapon. You may select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select it, your damage increases by +1d6 (Maximum +10d6). Prerequisite: You can take advantage of your adversary's distractions, no matter how momentary or fleeting. Once per turn, when you Flank a target, you can treat that target as if they were Flat-Footed for one of your attacks. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy If you succeed on a Deception check against a target's Will Defense as a Swift Action, until the start of your next turn you can move though the Threatened Area of that target as part of your Move Action without provoking an Attack of Opportunity. Each Threatened square that you move through counts as 2 squares of movement. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Point-Blank Shot You can use the Talent against a target within 12 squares, instead of within 6 squares. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide You excel at seduction through deception. If you fail a Persuasion check to change a target's Attitude, you can immediately reroll the check using your Deception skill in lieu of your Persuasion skill. You must accept the result of the reroll, even if it is worse. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide Once per encounter as a Move Action, you can attempt to seize a held, carried, or worn object from an adjacent target by making a Disarm attack, with a +10 bonus on your attack roll. If the attack succeeds, you are now holding the object, and you cannot use this Talent in place of the Disarm Action. You cannot conceal the use of this Talent from the target. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy","description":"Any time your opponent is Flat-Footed or otherwise denied its Dexterity bonus to Reflex Defense, you deal an additional 1d6 points of damage with a successful melee or ranged attack. You must be within 6 squares of the target to make a with a ranged weapon. You may select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select it, your damage increases by +1d6 (Maximum +10d6). Prerequisite: You can take advantage of your adversary's distractions, no matter how momentary or fleeting. Once per turn, when you Flank a target, you can treat that target as if they were Flat-Footed for one of your attacks. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy If you succeed on a Deception check against a target's Will Defense as a Swift Action, until the start of your next turn you can move though the Threatened Area of that target as part of your Move Action without provoking an Attack of Opportunity. Each Threatened square that you move through counts as 2 squares of movement. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Point-Blank Shot You can use the Talent against a target within 12 squares, instead of within 6 squares. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide You excel at seduction through deception. If you fail a Persuasion check to change a target's Attitude, you can immediately reroll the check using your Deception skill in lieu of your Persuasion skill. You must accept the result of the reroll, even if it is worse. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide Once per encounter as a Move Action, you can attempt to seize a held, carried, or worn object from an adjacent target by making a Disarm attack, with a +10 bonus on your attack roll. If the attack succeeds, you are now holding the object, and you cannot use this Talent in place of the Disarm Action. You cannot conceal the use of this Talent from the target. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy","class":"Scoundrel","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scoundrel","tree":"Misfortune","treeId":"67b59e020c1660eb","tags":["action-economy","battlefield-control","controller","defender","melee","mobility","positioning","precision","ranged","scaling","scoundrel","skills","social","striker"]},"effects":[{"_id":"3195415b-2276-403c-9fb1-5d323d38d31a","name":"Sneak Attack","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.damage.flatfooted","mode":2,"value":"1d6"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Sneak Attack"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.sneak_attack"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.1505abc8babeeb84"}}},{"_id":"e90aa43cbc1a9762","name":"Spacehound","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Spacer","prerequisites":"","benefit":"You gain a +1 bonus on attack rolls made while aboard a Starship. This bonus applies to attacks made with Starship Weapons, as well as personal weapons used aboard a Starship. Prerequisite: Whenever you roll a Natural 20 on an attack roll made aboard a Starship, you gain one temporary Force Point. If the Force Point is not used before the end of the encounter, it is lost. This Talent works with both Weapon Systems and personal weapons used aboard a Starship. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Starship Raider When adjacent to an obstacle or barrier, you gain a +2 Cover bonus to your Reflex Defense. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions Prerequisites: , Starship Raider Whether you are taking on military targets on behalf of a resistance movement or you are out for personal gain, you are experienced at raiding Starships and similar targets. You can use each if the following Actions once per encounter: Clear a Path: Your attack forces an enemy to alter course or move out of your way. You must be fighting aboard a Starship to use this Action. As a Standard Action, make a ranged attack. If the attack hits, on its next turn your target must move its Speed to a square that is not adjacent to you. If the target is an enemy Starfighter engaged in a Dogfight, the target instead must attempt to disengage from the Dogfight. Covering Fire: You squeeze off several shots as you escape pursuing enemies. As a Full-Round Action, if you are the Pilot of a Vehicle, you may move the Vehicle up to twice its Speed and make a single ranged attack with one of the Pilot-controlled Vehicle Weapons at any point during that movement. If you hit and deal damage to a Vehicle with this attack, the target Vehicle takes a -2 penalty to attack rolls against your Vehicle until the end of your turn. Disabling Fire: Make a ranged attack with your Vehicle Weapon. If you make this attack against a Vehicle and hit and deal damage, you can choose one of the following to take effect until the end of your next turn: One of the target's Vehicle Weapons ceases to function. The target's Shield Rating is reduced to 0. The target's Hyperdrive is disabled. The target's Speed is reduced to 2 squares (Character Scale). Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Stellar Warrior Once per encounter, while on or in a Vehicle, you can move up to one-half your speed, or move the Vehicle up to one-half its speed if you are the Pilot, as a Swift Action. This movement does not provoke Attacks of Opportunity.","description":"You gain a +1 bonus on attack rolls made while aboard a Starship. This bonus applies to attacks made with Starship Weapons, as well as personal weapons used aboard a Starship. Prerequisite: Whenever you roll a Natural 20 on an attack roll made aboard a Starship, you gain one temporary Force Point. If the Force Point is not used before the end of the encounter, it is lost. This Talent works with both Weapon Systems and personal weapons used aboard a Starship. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Starship Raider When adjacent to an obstacle or barrier, you gain a +2 Cover bonus to your Reflex Defense. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions Prerequisites: , Starship Raider Whether you are taking on military targets on behalf of a resistance movement or you are out for personal gain, you are experienced at raiding Starships and similar targets. You can use each if the following Actions once per encounter: Clear a Path: Your attack forces an enemy to alter course or move out of your way. You must be fighting aboard a Starship to use this Action. As a Standard Action, make a ranged attack. If the attack hits, on its next turn your target must move its Speed to a square that is not adjacent to you. If the target is an enemy Starfighter engaged in a Dogfight, the target instead must attempt to disengage from the Dogfight. Covering Fire: You squeeze off several shots as you escape pursuing enemies. As a Full-Round Action, if you are the Pilot of a Vehicle, you may move the Vehicle up to twice its Speed and make a single ranged attack with one of the Pilot-controlled Vehicle Weapons at any point during that movement. If you hit and deal damage to a Vehicle with this attack, the target Vehicle takes a -2 penalty to attack rolls against your Vehicle until the end of your turn. Disabling Fire: Make a ranged attack with your Vehicle Weapon. If you make this attack against a Vehicle and hit and deal damage, you can choose one of the following to take effect until the end of your next turn: One of the target's Vehicle Weapons ceases to function. The target's Shield Rating is reduced to 0. The target's Hyperdrive is disabled. The target's Speed is reduced to 2 squares (Character Scale). Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Stellar Warrior Once per encounter, while on or in a Vehicle, you can move up to one-half your speed, or move the Vehicle up to one-half its speed if you are the Pilot, as a Swift Action. This movement does not provoke Attacks of Opportunity.","class":"Scoundrel","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scoundrel","tree":"Spacer","treeId":"5ea8c79492d40713","tags":["action-economy","controller","damage-reduction","defender","force","force-control","force-defense","force-offense","mobility","positioning","ranged","scaling","scoundrel","shields","striker","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.spacehound"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.fe0c3a64ca460542"}}},{"_id":"0c190ee0441ef838","name":"Trigger Work","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Gunslinger","prerequisites":null,"benefit":"No penalty to attack when using Rapid Shot.","description":"You take no attack penalty when using Rapid Shot.","class":"Gunslinger","costNumeric":null,"category":"Gunslinger","tree":"Gunslinger","treeId":"cb6f775cd227a3e3","tags":["ranged"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.trigger_work"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.86c10d63bba2d9c8"}}},{"_id":"a6919d36e83a5c51","name":"Vehicle Focus","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Expert Pilot","prerequisites":"Wisdom 13","benefit":"Gain +2 attack with a selected vehicle type and may take 10 on Pilot checks for that vehicle.","description":"Gain +2 attack with a selected vehicle type and may take 10 on Pilot checks with it.","class":"Ace Pilot","costNumeric":null,"category":"Ace Pilot","tree":"Expert Pilot","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"attribute","ability":"wis","min":13}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"b17c1515c06361d6","tags":["feat-chain","scout","striker","talent-chain"]},"effects":[{"_id":"8595413e-0dd8-4d55-a7c8-4c82752af263","name":"Vehicle Focus","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.attacks.vehicle","mode":2,"value":"2"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Vehicle Focus"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.vehicle_focus"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.4764dc69f0d11695"}}},{"_id":"ad244bef3a44eb5b","name":"Weapon Specialization","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Lightsaber Combat","prerequisites":"Weapon Focus","benefit":"+2 melee damage.","description":"Gain +2 damage with a chosen weapon.","class":"Jedi","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","tree":"Lightsaber Combat","treeId":"2359c05ff13f3feb","tags":["feat-chain","jedi","lightsaber","melee","striker","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.weapon_specialization"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.41426ecd7fade0b0"}}},{"_id":"eabe204238444ebd","name":"Unarmed","type":"weapon","img":"icons/svg/sword.svg","system":{"damage":"1d4+9","damageType":"kinetic","attackBonus":0,"attackAttribute":"str","range":"melee","weight":1,"cost":0,"equipped":true,"description":"","properties":[],"ammunition":{"type":"none","current":0,"max":0},"weaponCategory":"simple","proficiency":"simple","subcategory":""},"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"placeholder":true,"npc":{"flatAttackBonus":15,"flatDamageFormula":"1d4+9","useFlat":true}}}},{"_id":"ef2aa0aa4d795e12","name":"Heavy Blaster Pistol","type":"weapon","img":"icons/svg/sword.svg","system":{"damage":"3d8+13","damageType":"energy","attackBonus":0,"attac