ck rolls with chosen weapon."}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.c41814601364b643"}}},{"_id":"a759d30d210f7519","name":"Weapon Proficiency","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"Ignore -5 penalty on attack rolls with weapons of a particular type.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["non-force"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{"value":"Ignore -5 penalty on attack rolls with weapons of a particular type."}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.ecc2471ac96ec2d4"}}},{"_id":"a1f91ed4ef924a51","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"You are proficient with simple weapons and do not take the -5 penalty when using them.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["noble","non-force","scoundrel","scout","soldier"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier","Scout","Scoundrel","Noble"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{}},"effects":[{"_id":"220daaa7-e1b5-440d-98cd-10f5e586ef8b","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.2d680cc46a7972da"}}},{"_id":"441640175867cf6f","name":"Devastating Power","type":"feat","img":"systems/foundryvtt-swse/assets/icons/force-secret.png","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"When using a Force Power that deals damage, you can spend a Force Point to increase the Power's damage dice by 50%.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Core","page":0,"tags":["force-secret"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":"<p><strong>Cost:</strong> Force Point or Destiny Point</p><p>When using a Force Power that deals damage, you can spend a Force Point to increase the Power's damage dice by 50%.</p><p>Alternatively, you can spend a Destiny Point to double the amount of damage dice.</p>","cost":"Force Point or Destiny Point","alternativeCost":"Alternatively, you can spend a Destiny Point to double the amount of damage dice."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcesecrets.996848a2e0c0ac4f"}}},{"_id":"58f0c93e8039d94b","name":"Multitarget Power","type":"feat","img":"systems/foundryvtt-swse/assets/icons/force-secret.png","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"When using a Force Power that affects a single target, you can spend a Force Point to affect one additional target.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Core","page":0,"tags":["force-secret"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":"<p><strong>Cost:</strong> Force Point or Destiny Point</p><p>When using a Force Power that affects a single target, you can spend a Force Point to affect one additional target.</p><p>Alternatively, you can spend a Destiny Point to affect one target per four Character Levels.</p>","cost":"Force Point or Destiny Point","alternativeCost":"Alternatively, you can spend a Destiny Point to affect one target per four Character Levels."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcesecrets.af908ace9a361603"}}},{"_id":"1d779b4e15f56d85","name":"Force Power Mastery","type":"feat","img":"systems/foundryvtt-swse/assets/icons/force-technique.png","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"Choose a single Force Power. You may Take 10 on Use the Force checks to activate this Force Power even when distracted or threatened.","prerequisite":"","special":"You may select this Force Technique multiple times; each time you select this Force Technique, it applies to a different Force Power.","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Core","page":0,"tags":["force-technique"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"description":"<p>Choose a single Force Power. You may Take 10 on Use the Force checks to activate this Force Power even when distracted or threatened.</p><p><strong>Special:</strong> You may select this Force Technique multiple times; each time you select this Force Technique, it applies to a different Force Power.</p>","relatedPower":""},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcetechniques.07cea7e3e8b21d69"}}},{"_id":"56366416a25c52b0","name":"Improved Move Light Object","type":"feat","img":"systems/foundryvtt-swse/assets/icons/force-technique.png","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"You may make a Use the Force check to Move Light Object as a Swift Action instead of a Move Action. Using the light object as a projectile weapon requires a Move Action (instead of a Standard Action).","prerequisite":"Move Light Object","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Core","page":0,"tags":["force-technique"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"description":"<p>You may make a Use the Force check to Move Light Object as a Swift Action instead of a Move Action. Using the light object as a projectile weapon requires a Move Action (instead of a Standard Action).</p><p><strong>Related Power:</strong> Move Light Object</p><p><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Move Light Object</p>","relatedPower":"Move Light Object"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcetechniques.c406600924a7780e"}}},{"_id":"bb0d18f322a79736","name":"Armored Defense","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Knight's Armor","prerequisites":"","benefit":"When calculating your Reflex Defense, you may add your Heroic Level plus one-half your Armor bonus (rounded down), or your Armor bonus alone, whichever is higher. This Talent counts as both the Talent and the Improved Talent for the purposes of prerequisites. You are adept at using a Cortosis Gauntlet to parry Lightsaber attacks. You gain a +2 bonus when making an opposed Unarmed melee attack roll against a Lightsaber attack.","description":"When calculating your Reflex Defense, you may add your Heroic Level plus one-half your Armor bonus (rounded down), or your Armor bonus alone, whichever is higher. This Talent counts as both the Talent and the Improved Talent for the purposes of prerequisites. You are adept at using a Cortosis Gauntlet to parry Lightsaber attacks. You gain a +2 bonus when making an opposed Unarmed melee attack roll against a Lightsaber attack.","class":"Soldier","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","tree":"Knight's Armor","treeId":"ea01d740c91888b3","tags":["armor","defender","lightsaber","melee","scaling","soldier","striker","sustained-damage","unarmed"]},"effects":[{"_id":"28f1f3db-0c6f-4614-bdcf-000f1542a25b","name":"Armored Defense","icon":"icons/svg/shield.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.defenses.reflex.misc","mode":2,"value":"1","priority":20}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Armored Defense"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.armored_defense"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.4c236343b01ea763"}}},{"_id":"18fe35b21c2aa239","name":"Block","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Sith Alchemy","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Create Sith Amulet: You can create a Sith Amulet. The creation of a Sith Amulet requires 25,000 credits' worth of gems and other raw materials, and the creation process takes 1 week (this work can be spread out over several sessions and need not be consecutive). At the end of the process, you must spend a Force Point to complete the Sith Amulet, after which point it functions exactly as a Sith Amulet. Create Sith Armor: You can transform a suit of normal Battle Armor into the Dark Armor worn by Sith Lords. You must have a suit of Battle Armor to transform into the Dark Armor (Light Battle Armor becomes Light Dark Armor, Battle Armor becomes Dark Armor, and Heavy Battle Armor becomes Heavy Dark Armor). The transformation process takes 1 day for Light Dark Armor, 2 days for Dark Armor, and 3 days for Heavy Dark Armor. You must spend a Force Point at the end of the creation process to complete the Armor's transformation. Create Sith Talisman: You can spend a Force Point to imbue a portable object with the Dark Side, creating a Sith Talisman that provides offensive strength to a Force Power. Creating the Sith Talisman takes a Full-Round Action. While you wear or carry the Sith Talisman on your person, you add 1d6 to your damage with Force Powers. You increase your Dark Side Score by 1 when you first wear or carry a Sith Talisman. You can have only one Sith Talisman active at any given time, and if it is destroyed, you cannot create another one for 24 hours. Create Sith Weapon: You can alchemically treat a Simple Weapon (Melee) or an Advanced Melee Weapon, turning it into a Sith Weapon. You must spend a Force Point and spend 1 hour imbuing the Weapon with the properties of a Sith Alchemical Weapon (see also: Sith Alchemical Weapon Template). A Lightsaber does not ignore the Sith Weapon's DR, and characters who are proficient in the Weapon's use can treat it as a Lightsaber for the purposes of the , Deflect, and Redirect Shot Talents (and any Talents that have these Talents as a prerequisite). Additionally, as a Swift Action, the wielder of a Sith Weapon can spend a Force Point to gain a bonus equal to their Dark Side Score to the damage of their next attack made with the Weapon before the end of the encounter. This increases the wielder's Dark Side Score by 1.","description":"Create Sith Amulet: You can create a Sith Amulet. The creation of a Sith Amulet requires 25,000 credits' worth of gems and other raw materials, and the creation process takes 1 week (this work can be spread out over several sessions and need not be consecutive). At the end of the process, you must spend a Force Point to complete the Sith Amulet, after which point it functions exactly as a Sith Amulet. Create Sith Armor: You can transform a suit of normal Battle Armor into the Dark Armor worn by Sith Lords. You must have a suit of Battle Armor to transform into the Dark Armor (Light Battle Armor becomes Light Dark Armor, Battle Armor becomes Dark Armor, and Heavy Battle Armor becomes Heavy Dark Armor). The transformation process takes 1 day for Light Dark Armor, 2 days for Dark Armor, and 3 days for Heavy Dark Armor. You must spend a Force Point at the end of the creation process to complete the Armor's transformation. Create Sith Talisman: You can spend a Force Point to imbue a portable object with the Dark Side, creating a Sith Talisman that provides offensive strength to a Force Power. Creating the Sith Talisman takes a Full-Round Action. While you wear or carry the Sith Talisman on your person, you add 1d6 to your damage with Force Powers. You increase your Dark Side Score by 1 when you first wear or carry a Sith Talisman. You can have only one Sith Talisman active at any given time, and if it is destroyed, you cannot create another one for 24 hours. Create Sith Weapon: You can alchemically treat a Simple Weapon (Melee) or an Advanced Melee Weapon, turning it into a Sith Weapon. You must spend a Force Point and spend 1 hour imbuing the Weapon with the properties of a Sith Alchemical Weapon (see also: Sith Alchemical Weapon Template). A Lightsaber does not ignore the Sith Weapon's DR, and characters who are proficient in the Weapon's use can treat it as a Lightsaber for the purposes of the , Deflect, and Redirect Shot Talents (and any Talents that have these Talents as a prerequisite). Additionally, as a Swift Action, the wielder of a Sith Weapon can spend a Force Point to gain a bonus equal to their Dark Side Score to the damage of their next attack made with the Weapon before the end of the encounter. This increases the wielder's Dark Side Score by 1.","class":"Jedi","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","tree":"Sith Alchemy","treeId":"a67faf2ae089ab5d","tags":["action-economy","armor","dark-side","defender","force","force-offense","jedi","lightsaber","melee","mobility","ranged","striker","support","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.block"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.9379daa94a228c04"}}},{"_id":"7581eac3f58d2c3c","name":"Deflect","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Lightsaber Forms","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Redirect Shot","description":"Redirect Shot","class":"Jedi","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","tree":"Lightsaber Forms","treeId":"2bc2572e852832e4","tags":["jedi","lightsaber","melee","ranged"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.deflect"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.72c644f7a09b1186"}}},{"_id":"ef423d66bb7a6f93","name":"Greater Weapon Focus (lightsabers)","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Duelist","prerequisites":"Weapon Focus (lightsabers)","benefit":"Gain an additional +1 attack with lightsabers.","description":"Gain +1 attack with lightsabers.","class":"Jedi Knight","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi Knight","tree":"Duelist","treeId":"b3c5d90b5036f39b","tags":["feat-chain","jedi","lightsaber","melee","striker","talent-chain"]},"effects":[{"_id":"e871f71e-474b-4e58-b378-9ebb4f6702c3","name":"Greater Weapon Focus (lightsabers)","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.attacks.lightsaber","mode":2,"value":"1"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Greater Weapon Focus (lightsabers)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.greater_weapon_focus_lightsabers"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.3038f4c26de19e39"}}},{"_id":"3b3457cec186df4b","name":"Improved Armored Defense","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Armor Specialist","prerequisites":"Armored Defense","benefit":"Your Reflex Defense bonus equals either your heroic level + half your armor bonus, or your armor bonus.","description":"Your Reflex Defense bonus equals either your heroic level plus half your armor bonus or your armor bonus.","class":"Soldier","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","tree":"Armor Specialist","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.armored_defense"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"17cec542331cb4e4","tags":["armor","defender","feat-chain","soldier","striker","talent-chain"]},"effects":[{"_id":"842ee02b-8f7e-4a40-802a-c6fe553379a5","name":"Improved Armored Defense","icon":"icons/svg/shield.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.defenses.reflex","mode":2,"value":"2"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Improved Armored Defense"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.improved_armored_defense"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.394809ed8baff1b9"}}},{"_id":"1a9a4cb571b4f54b","name":"Juggernaut","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Armor Specialist","prerequisites":"Armored Defense","benefit":"Armor does not reduce speed or distance moved.","description":"Armor does not reduce your speed or distance moved.","class":"Soldier","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","tree":"Armor Specialist","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.armored_defense"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"17cec542331cb4e4","tags":["armor","controller","damage-reduction","defender","feat-chain","mobility","positioning","soldier","talent-chain"]},"effects":[{"_id":"bbba797f-b820-4645-90ee-c462bc890f35","name":"Juggernaut","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.armor.speedPenalty","mode":5,"value":"0"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Juggernaut","effectType":"armor_speed_penalty"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.juggernaut"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.55f4a04087dacddc"}}},{"_id":"8a5eb0840a5b1b0a","name":"Multiattack Proficiency (lightsabers)","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Jedi Battlemaster","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Dual Weapon Mastery I, Weapon Focus (Lightsabers) Immediately after making a Full Attack where you attacked with two Lightsabers (or both ends of a Double-Bladed Lightsaber), you may Move up to your Speed as a Free Action.","description":"Dual Weapon Mastery I, Weapon Focus (Lightsabers) Immediately after making a Full Attack where you attacked with two Lightsabers (or both ends of a Double-Bladed Lightsaber), you may Move up to your Speed as a Free Action.","class":"Jedi Knight","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi Knight","tree":"Jedi Battlemaster","treeId":"dfc4142435b4356d","tags":["action-economy","controller","dual-wield","force","force-control","force-offense","jedi","light-side","lightsaber","melee","mobility"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.multiattack_proficiency_lightsabers"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.317400e9ea2b66c7"}}},{"_id":"c1a9882f7a7a5212","name":"Weapon Specialization (Lightsabers)","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Duelist","tree":"Duelist","prerequisites":"","description":"Greater Weapon Focus (Lightsabers) You gain a +2 bonus on melee damage rolls with Lightsabers. This bonus stacks with the bonus granted by the Talent. Whenever you make multiple attacks with any type of Lightsaber as part of a Full Attack, you reduce the penalty on your attack rolls by 2. You can take this Talent multiple times; each time you take this Talent, you reduce the penalty on your attack rolls by an additional 2. See also: Maiming Foes When you deal damage with a Lightsaber that is equal to or greater than both the target's current Hit Points and the target's Damage Threshold (that is, when you would deal enough damage to kill your target), you may choose to use this Talent. Instead of dealing full damage, you instead deal half damage to your target and move it -1 step on the Condition Track. In addition, you sever one of your target's arms at the wrist or elbow joint, or one of the target's legs at the knee or ankle joint (your choice). Severing part of an arm prevents the target from wielding weapons or using tools in that hand, and imposes a -5 penalty on Skill Checks and Ability Checks keyed to Strength and Dexterity. Severing part of a leg knocks the target Prone, reduces the target's Speed by half, reduces its Carrying Capacity by half, and imposes a -5 penalty on Skill Checks and Ability Checks keyed to Strength and Dexterity. Because of the severity of such an injury, losing part of a limb causes a Persistent Condition that can only be removed by having Surgery successfully performed on you. A Cybernetic Prosthesis negates these reductions and penalties. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","benefit":"Greater Weapon Focus (Lightsabers) You gain a +2 bonus on melee damage rolls with Lightsabers. This bonus stacks with the bonus granted by the Talent. Whenever you make multiple attacks with any type of Lightsaber as part of a Full Attack, you reduce the penalty on your attack rolls by 2. You can take this Talent multiple times; each time you take this Talent, you reduce the penalty on your attack rolls by an additional 2. See also: Maiming Foes When you deal damage with a Lightsaber that is equal to or greater than both the target's current Hit Points and the target's Damage Threshold (that is, when you would deal enough damage to kill your target), you may choose to use this Talent. Instead of dealing full damage, you instead deal half damage to your target and move it -1 step on the Condition Track. In addition, you sever one of your target's arms at the wrist or elbow joint, or one of the target's legs at the knee or ankle joint (your choice). Severing part of an arm prevents the target from wielding weapons or using tools in that hand, and imposes a -5 penalty on Skill Checks and Ability Checks keyed to Strength and Dexterity. Severing part of a leg knocks the target Prone, reduces the target's Speed by half, reduces its Carrying Capacity by half, and imposes a -5 penalty on Skill Checks and Ability Checks keyed to Strength and Dexterity. Because of the severity of such an injury, losing part of a limb causes a Persistent Condition that can only be removed by having Surgery successfully performed on you. A Cybernetic Prosthesis negates these reductions and penalties. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"b3c5d90b5036f39b","tags":["burst-damage","condition-removal","controller","damage-reduction","defender","force","force-control","force-offense","leader","lightsaber","melee","mobility","scaling","striker","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.00a9210772a64a19"}}},{"_id":"574524727cab38c4","name":"Wicked Strike","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Sith","prerequisites":"Weapon Focus (Lightsabers), Weapon Specialization (Lightsabers)","benefit":"On a lightsaber critical hit, move the target 2 steps down the condition track.","description":"On a lightsaber critical hit, move the target two steps down the condition track.","class":"Sith Apprentice","costNumeric":null,"category":"Sith Apprentice","tree":"Sith","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.weapon_specialization"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"d1037bc7a08ea80b","tags":["condition-removal","controller","dark-side","feat-chain","force","force-control","jedi","lightsaber","melee","mobility","precision","striker","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.wicked_strike"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.d350b28e72652d29"}}},{"_id":"ed90951c471274d2","name":"Battle Strike","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"telekinetic","useTheForce":15,"time":"Swift Action","range":"Personal","target":"You","duration":"1 round","effect":"<p>You channel the Force to enhance your next melee attack. Your next melee attack this round gains a +1d6 bonus to damage.</p>","special":"<p>This bonus damage is Force damage and bypasses Damage Reduction.</p>","descriptor":["Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":94,"tags":["enhancement","damage","melee"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":2,"max":2},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.f177dc6d65f76de9"}}},{"_id":"678b936d20b9d9a4","name":"Force Grip","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":3,"discipline":"dark-side","useTheForce":15,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One creature","duration":"Concentration","effect":"<p>You use the Force to telekinetically choke or crush your target. The target takes damage each round based on your Use the Force check result.</p>","special":"<p>This is a Dark Side power. The target is immobilized while gripped.</p>","descriptor":["Dark Side","Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[{"dc":15,"effect":"2d6 damage/round","description":"Target takes 2d6 damage per round and is immobilized"},{"dc":20,"effect":"4d6 damage/round","description":"Target takes 4d6 damage per round and is immobilized"},{"dc":25,"effect":"6d6 damage/round + lift","description":"Target takes 6d6 damage per round, is immobilized, and lifted off ground"},{"dc":30,"effect":"8d6 damage/round + crush","description":"Target takes 8d6 damage per round and is being crushed (fort save or die)"}],"maintainable":true,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":96,"tags":["attack","damage","dark-side","telekinetic","immobilize"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.f41a957f71e98a6a"}}},{"_id":"2fdea1279f046013","name":"Force Shield","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/eye.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"Unknown","useTheForce":"","time":"standard","range":"","target":"","duration":"","effect":"","special":"","descriptor":"","dcChart":"","maintainable":false,"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1,"perDay":true}},"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"placeholder":true,"unresolved":"Force Shield"}}},{"_id":"9a5e28a55a73380f","name":"Rebuke","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telepathic","useTheForce":20,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One Force-sensitive creature","duration":"1 round","effect":"<p>You overwhelm a Force user with a powerful Force presence. If the target is Force-sensitive, they must make a Will save (DC = your UTF check) or be dazed for 1 round.</p>","special":"<p>This power only affects Force-sensitive creatures.</p>","descriptor":["Mind-Affecting"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":99,"tags":["debuff","force-user","daze"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":2,"max":2},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.390074b44aedfa2a"}}},{"_id":"692bd4290a76ab09","name":"Double-Bladed Lightsaber","type":"weapon","img":"icons/svg/sword.svg","system":{"damage":"2d8+13","damageType":"energy","attackBonus":0,"attackAttribute":"str","range":"melee","weight":2,"cost":24000,"equipped":true,"description":"<p>A lightsaber with blades on both ends. Wielded by some Sith and Jedi, most famously Darth Maul.</p>\n      <p><strong>Special:</strong> Double weapon. Ignores armor bonuses. Can deflect blaster bolts. Critical threat range 19-20. Requires exotic weapon proficiency.</p>","properties":["Lightsaber","Double Weapon","Critical 19-20","Exotic","Armor-Piercing"],"ammunition":{"type":"none","current":0,"max":0},"weaponCategory":"melee","proficiency":"exotic","subcategory":"lightsaber","costNumeric":24000,"category":"lightsaber"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.weapons.weapon-double-bladed-lightsaber"},"swse":{"npc":{"flatAttackBonus":21,"flatDamageFormula":"2d8+13","useFlat":true}}}},{"_id":"40fc8b1026a5e9ed","name":"Double-Bladed Lightsaber (*)","type":"weapon","img":"icons/svg/sword.svg","system":{"damage":"2d8+23","damageType":"energy","attackBonus":0,"attackAttribute":"str","range":"melee","weig