alse},"costNumeric":null,"description":{}},"effects":[{"_id":"220daaa7-e1b5-440d-98cd-10f5e586ef8b","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.2d680cc46a7972da"}}},{"_id":"928224a047957bce","name":"Distant Power","type":"feat","img":"systems/foundryvtt-swse/assets/icons/force-secret.png","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"When using a Force Power that has a range expressed numerically, you can spend a Force Point to multiply the range by 10.","prerequisite":"","special":"This Force Secret does not remove the line of sight requirements.","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Core","page":0,"tags":["force-secret"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":"<p><strong>Cost:</strong> Force Point or Destiny Point</p><p>When using a Force Power that has a range expressed numerically, you can spend a Force Point to multiply the range by 10.</p><p>Alternatively, you can spend a Destiny Point to increase the range to anywhere in the same Star System.</p><p><strong>Special:</strong> This Force Secret does not remove the line of sight requirements.</p>","cost":"Force Point or Destiny Point","alternativeCost":"Alternatively, you can spend a Destiny Point to increase the range to anywhere in the same Star System."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcesecrets.43f9645eabce838e"}}},{"_id":"e70b5d2fc44b993a","name":"Quicken Power","type":"feat","img":"systems/foundryvtt-swse/assets/icons/force-secret.png","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"When using a Force Power that requires a Standard Action or Move Action to activate, you can spend a Force Point to activate the Force Power as a Swift Action instead.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Core","page":0,"tags":["force-secret"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":"<p><strong>Cost:</strong> Force Point or Destiny Point</p><p>When using a Force Power that requires a Standard Action or Move Action to activate, you can spend a Force Point to activate the Force Power as a Swift Action instead.</p><p>Alternatively, you can spend a Destiny Point to activate the Force Power as a Reaction instead.</p>","cost":"Force Point or Destiny Point","alternativeCost":"Alternatively, you can spend a Destiny Point to activate the Force Power as a Reaction instead."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcesecrets.52bf7b9a1a41de2b"}}},{"_id":"2058ddb24b50e444","name":"Force Point Recovery","type":"feat","img":"systems/foundryvtt-swse/assets/icons/force-technique.png","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"At the end of an encounter, you automatically recover 1 Force Point spent during the encounter.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Core","page":0,"tags":["force-technique"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"description":"<p>At the end of an encounter, you automatically recover 1 Force Point spent during the encounter.</p>","relatedPower":""},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcetechniques.056ab39b3ab9df10"}}},{"_id":"f2a85986f9b52731","name":"Improved Sense Surroundings","type":"feat","img":"systems/foundryvtt-swse/assets/icons/force-technique.png","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"You may use the Sense Surroundings application of the Use the Force Skill as a Free Action rather than a Swift Action.","prerequisite":"Sense Surroundings","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Core","page":0,"tags":["force-technique"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"description":"<p>You may use the Sense Surroundings application of the Use the Force Skill as a Free Action rather than a Swift Action.</p><p><strong>Related Power:</strong> Sense Surroundings</p><p><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Sense Surroundings</p>","relatedPower":"Sense Surroundings"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcetechniques.4955b5076ca5da89"}}},{"_id":"3f8b54fe11459aa3","name":"Adept Negotiator","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Jedi Consular","prerequisites":"","benefit":"You can use your Use the Force modifier instead of your Persuasion check modifier when making a Persuasion check. You are considered Trained in the Persuasion skill. If you are entitled to a Persuasion check reroll, you may reroll your Use the Force check instead (subject to the same circumstances and limitations). Prerequisite: If you successfully use the Talent, your target moves an additional -1 step along the Condition Track. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. You affect the Condition Track of the specific character (usually the Vehicle's Commander), not a Starship. You can spend a Full-Round Action advising an ally, thereby granting them a +5 bonus on their next Skill Check. If you spend a Force Point, the bonus increases to +10. The target must be able to (and willing) to hear and understand your voice. You cannot advise yourself. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual As a Standard Action, you can peer into The Force and search for weaknesses in the defenses of your enemies. Make a Use the Force check against the Will Defense of a target creature within 12 squares of you and in your line of sight. If the Skill Check equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, that target takes a -2 penalty to their Reflex Defense against you and all allies who can hear and understand you until the end of your next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide Prerequisite: Whenever you damage an opponent with a Lightsaber attack, you can Take 10 on any Persuasion checks you make before the end of your next turn, even if you would not normally be able to. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide Prerequisite: Once per encounter as a Swift Action, you can choose one ally within your line of sight that can hear and understand you. Until the end of the encounter, that ally adds your Wisdom bonus to its Will Defense against Mind-Affecting effects. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide Once per turn as a Swift Action, you can spend a Force Point to let one adjacent ally use the Aid Another Action (as a Reaction) to assist you with a Skill Check. You must make the Skill Check before the end of your turn, or the benefit of the Aid Another Action is lost. An ally that has already used the Aid Another Action to assist you since the end of your last turn may not be targeted by this Talent. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide You gain a +2 insight bonus to your Will Defense. Also, as a Swift Action, you can spend a Force Point to give all allies within 6 squares of you a +2 insight bonus to their Will Defense that lasts for the remainder of the encounter. This bonus does not extend to allies outside the range of the effect, even if they move within 6 squares of you later on. Allies who benefit from this Talent must remain within 6 squares of you to retain the insight bonus, and they lose it if you are knocked unconscious or killed. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Rebellion Era Campaign Guide When you deal damage to a target by making a Lightsaber attack on your turn, you can use a Swift Action before the end of your turn to activate this Talent. If you do so, allies adjacent to the target at the time you make the attack gain a +2 circumstance bonus to melee attack rolls against the target until the start of your next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide","description":"You can use your Use the Force modifier instead of your Persuasion check modifier when making a Persuasion check. You are considered Trained in the Persuasion skill. If you are entitled to a Persuasion check reroll, you may reroll your Use the Force check instead (subject to the same circumstances and limitations). Prerequisite: If you successfully use the Talent, your target moves an additional -1 step along the Condition Track. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. You affect the Condition Track of the specific character (usually the Vehicle's Commander), not a Starship. You can spend a Full-Round Action advising an ally, thereby granting them a +5 bonus on their next Skill Check. If you spend a Force Point, the bonus increases to +10. The target must be able to (and willing) to hear and understand your voice. You cannot advise yourself. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual As a Standard Action, you can peer into The Force and search for weaknesses in the defenses of your enemies. Make a Use the Force check against the Will Defense of a target creature within 12 squares of you and in your line of sight. If the Skill Check equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, that target takes a -2 penalty to their Reflex Defense against you and all allies who can hear and understand you until the end of your next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide Prerequisite: Whenever you damage an opponent with a Lightsaber attack, you can Take 10 on any Persuasion checks you make before the end of your next turn, even if you would not normally be able to. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide Prerequisite: Once per encounter as a Swift Action, you can choose one ally within your line of sight that can hear and understand you. Until the end of the encounter, that ally adds your Wisdom bonus to its Will Defense against Mind-Affecting effects. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide Once per turn as a Swift Action, you can spend a Force Point to let one adjacent ally use the Aid Another Action (as a Reaction) to assist you with a Skill Check. You must make the Skill Check before the end of your turn, or the benefit of the Aid Another Action is lost. An ally that has already used the Aid Another Action to assist you since the end of your last turn may not be targeted by this Talent. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide You gain a +2 insight bonus to your Will Defense. Also, as a Swift Action, you can spend a Force Point to give all allies within 6 squares of you a +2 insight bonus to their Will Defense that lasts for the remainder of the encounter. This bonus does not extend to allies outside the range of the effect, even if they move within 6 squares of you later on. Allies who benefit from this Talent must remain within 6 squares of you to retain the insight bonus, and they lose it if you are knocked unconscious or killed. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Rebellion Era Campaign Guide When you deal damage to a target by making a Lightsaber attack on your turn, you can use a Swift Action before the end of your turn to activate this Talent. If you do so, allies adjacent to the target at the time you make the attack gain a +2 circumstance bonus to melee attack rolls against the target until the start of your next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide","class":"Jedi","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","tree":"Jedi Consular","treeId":"e99cfa9db8493573","tags":["action-economy","condition-removal","controller","defender","force","force-control","force-defense","force-offense","jedi","leader","light-side","lightsaber","melee","mobility","positioning","scout","skills","social","striker","support","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.adept_negotiator"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.7acc479dee2d3b10"}}},{"_id":"d83bfcd623c55f2f","name":"Apprentice Boon","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Jedi Instructor","prerequisites":null,"benefit":"Add your Force Point result to an ally within 12 squares whose Use the Force modifier is lower than yours.","description":"Add your Force Point result to an ally's roll if they have a lower Use the Force modifier.","class":"Jedi Knight","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi Knight","tree":"Jedi Instructor","treeId":"303d91124d4548c0","tags":["force","jedi","light-side","positioning","support"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.apprentice_boon"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.53c5a847e3396d13"}}},{"_id":"01b869836e24ce2f","name":"Battle Meditation","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Sense","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Link Using a meditative battle trance, Force-users are able to join their minds together, collectively becoming stronger. However, a masterful degree of will is required to prevent the participants from sharing their weaknesses as well as their strengths. As a Full-Round Action, you can designate a number of willing allies equal to your Charisma modifier within 12 squares of you. These allies must be Trained in the Use the Force skill. As long as you remain within 12 squares of each other, you can Aid Another on attack rolls and Skill Checks as a Reaction.","description":"Link Using a meditative battle trance, Force-users are able to join their minds together, collectively becoming stronger. However, a masterful degree of will is required to prevent the participants from sharing their weaknesses as well as their strengths. As a Full-Round Action, you can designate a number of willing allies equal to your Charisma modifier within 12 squares of you. These allies must be Trained in the Use the Force skill. As long as you remain within 12 squares of each other, you can Aid Another on attack rolls and Skill Checks as a Reaction.","class":"Jedi","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","tree":"Sense","treeId":"d6b4331c0e31f7e3","tags":["action-economy","force","force-offense","jedi","positioning","striker","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[{"_id":"0cdcb68b-7eeb-45d0-ae5c-575d13648a00","name":"Battle Meditation","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.attacks.allies","mode":2,"value":"1"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Battle Meditation"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.battle_meditation"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.9461c7aa79dd07c6"}}},{"_id":"87f769da64c9a63e","name":"Force Harmony","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Control","prerequisites":null,"benefit":"Once per encounter, activate a Force talent that requires a Force Point without spending one.","description":"Once per encounter, activate a Force talent that normally requires a Force Point without spending one.","costNumeric":null,"tree":"Control","treeId":"d3661aa9906bdc79","tags":["force"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.force_harmony"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.5b949c8cd8e78ee8"}}},{"_id":"28f0d718566e7853","name":"Force Persuasion","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Jedi Consular","prerequisites":"Adept Negotiator","benefit":"Use the Force instead of Persuasion for checks; considered trained in Persuasion.","description":"You may use Use the Force instead of Persuasion and are considered trained in Persuasion.","class":"Jedi","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","tree":"Jedi Consular","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.adept_negotiator"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"e99cfa9db8493573","tags":["feat-chain","force","jedi","light-side","skills","social","talent-chain"]},"effects":[{"_id":"f8c30152-0d87-4368-a330-0f73d55cd21d","name":"Force Persuasion","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.skills.persuasion.substitute","mode":5,"value":"useTheForce"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Force Persuasion"}}},{"name":"Force Persuasion (Trained)","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.skills.persuasion.trained","mode":5,"value":"true"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Force Persuasion","effectType":"skill-trained"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.force_persuasion"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.d1fd547124c1901c"}}},{"_id":"73350e64adb814bd","name":"Share Force Secret","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Jedi Instructor","prerequisites":"Force Secret","benefit":"Once per turn, grant use of a Force Secret to an ally within 12 squares who is trained in Use the Force.","description":"Once per turn, grant use of a Force Secret to an ally within 12 squares trained in Use the Force.","class":"Jedi Knight","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi Knight","tree":"Jedi Instructor","treeId":"303d91124d4548c0","tags":["feat-chain","force","jedi","leader","light-side","positioning","support","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.share_force_secret"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.2dc6ad1667133f2d"}}},{"_id":"4ce35ebd8e3252d8","name":"Share Force Technique","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Jedi Instructor","prerequisites":"Force Technique","benefit":"Once per turn, grant use of a Force Technique to an ally within 12 squares who is trained in Use the Force; not for Force Point recovery.","description":"Once per turn, grant use of a Force Technique to an ally within 12 squares trained in Use the Force.","class":"Jedi Knight","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi Knight","tree":"Jedi Instructor","treeId":"303d91124d4548c0","tags":["feat-chain","force","jedi","leader","light-side","positioning","support","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.share_force_technique"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.7d02251f13fd5645"}}},{"_id":"440aea4399fd0bf2","name":"Skilled Advisor","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Jedi Archivist","prerequisites":"","benefit":"You can Aid Another on the Knowledge checks of an ally within 6 squares of you as a Reaction for Knowledge skills you are Trained in. You can make a Use the Force check in place of a Knowledge check for any Knowledge skill you are not Trained in. You are considered Trained in that Knowledge skill for the purposes of using this Talent. If you are entitled to a Knowledge check reroll, you can reroll your Use the Force check instead (subject to the same circumstances and limitations). Prerequisite: When you use the Talent, the ally you aid gains one temporary Force Point at the end of their next turn. If the Force Point is not spent before the end of the encounter, it is lost. As a Swift Action, you can reroll a Knowledge check and keep the better of the two results. This can be used with any Knowledge skill you are Trained in.","description":"You can Aid Another on the Knowledge checks of an ally within 6 squares of you as a Reaction for Knowledge skills you are Trained in. You can make a Use the Force check in place of a Knowledge check for any Knowledge skill you are not Trained in. You are considered Trained in that Knowledge skill for the purposes of using this Talent. If you are entitled to a Knowledge check reroll, you can reroll your Use the Force check instead (subject to the same circumstances and limitations). Prerequisite: When you use the Talent, the ally you aid gains one temporary Force Point at the end of their next turn. If the Force Point is not spent before the end of the encounter, it is lost. As a Swift Action, you can reroll a Knowledge check and keep the better of the two results. This can be used with any Knowledge skill you are Trained in.","class":"Jedi","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","tree":"Jedi Archivist","treeId":"152047d6ab7896ad","tags":["action-economy","force","jedi","light-side","mobility","positioning","striker","support"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.skilled_advisor"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.35cbdbe9c91ba1d0"}}},{"_id":"9f66a518953b8fd0","name":"Transfer Power","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Jedi Instructor","prerequisites":"Force Training","benefit":"Spend a power from your suite and give it to an ally trained in Use the Force within 12 squares and line of sight; lost if unused by end of encounter.","description":"Spend a Force power to grant it to an ally trained in Use the Force; it is lost if unused by the end of the encounter.","class":"Jedi Knight","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi Knight","tree":"Jedi Instructor","treeId":"303d91124d4548c0","tags":["feat-chain","force","jedi","light-side","positioning","support","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.transfer_power"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.488aaac69a9829bc"}}},{"_id":"64ce2809f3956e52","name":"Battle Strike","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"telekinetic","useTheForce":15,"time":"Swift Action","range":"Personal","target":"You","duration":"1 round","effect":"<p>You channel the Force to enhance your next melee attack. Your next melee attack this round gains a +1d6 bonus to damage.</p>","special":"<p>This bonus damage is Force damage and bypasses Damage Reduction.</p>","descriptor":["Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":94,"tags":["enhancement","damage","melee"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.f177dc6d65f76de9"}}},{"_id":"0d97f0c85f7d7747","name":"Force Light","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/eye.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"Unknown","useTheForce":"","time":"standard","range":"","target":"","duration":"","effect":"","special":"","descriptor":"","dcChart":"","maintainable":false,"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":2,"max":2,"perDay":true}},"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"placeholder":true,"unresolved":"Force Light"}}},{"_id":"120648d78b6cdddb","name":"Force Slam","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telekinetic","useTheForce":20,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One creature or object","duration":"Instantaneous","effect":"<p>You use telekinetic force to violently slam your target against a surface. The target takes 4d6 damage and is knocked prone.</p>","special":"<p>The target must be within 6 squares of a solid surface (wall, floor, ceiling).</p>","descriptor":["Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":97,"tags":["attack","damage","telekinetic","prone"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.462a6c23e00c4dfc"}}},{"_id":"87fb442cbfde8f8d","name":"Inspire","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"telepathic","useTheForce":15,"time":"Swift Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One ally","duration":"1 round","effect":"<p>You inspire an ally through the Force, granting them confidence and clarity. The target gains a +2 morale bonus to their next attack roll or skill check.</p>","special":"","descriptor":["Mind-Affecting"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":98,"tags":["buff","support","morale"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.dc331021badb59ed"}}},{"_id":"a0af81209f770077","name":"Mind Trick","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"telepathic","useTheForce":15,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One creature","duration":"1 minute or until completed","effect":"<p>You influence a weak mind to believe what you tell them or follow a simple suggestion. The target must make a Will save (DC = your UTF check) or be affected.</p>","special":"<p>The suggestion must be reasonable and the target must be able to understand you.</p>","descriptor":["Mind-Affecting"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":98,"tags":["mind-control","suggestion","social"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.e6649f366d6c5737"}}},{"_id":"f86116651fc4d6d4","name":"Move Object","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telekinetic","useTheForce":15,"time":"Standard Action","range":"12 squares","target":"One object or creature","duration":"Concentration","effect":"<p>You move objects or creatures through the air using telekinesis. The maximum size/weight you can move depends on your Use the Force check result.</p>","special":"<p>Unwilling creatures can make a Will save (DC = your UTF check) to resist being moved.</p>","descriptor":["Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[{"dc":15,"effect":"Medium (50 kg)","description":"Move objects up to Medium size or 50 kg"},{"dc":20,"effect":"Large (250 kg)","description":"Move objects up to Large size or 250 kg"},{"dc":25,"effect":"Huge (1 ton)","description":"Move objects up to Huge size or 1 metric ton"},{"dc":30,"effect":"Gargantuan (5 tons)","description":"Move objects up to Gargantuan size or 5 metric tons"},{"dc":35,"effect":"Colossal (20 tons)","description":"Move objects up to Colossal size or 20 metric tons (starfighter-sized)"}],"maintainable":true,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":98,"tags":["telekinetic","movement","utility"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":2,"max":2},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.289013a32bd179ad"}}},{"_id":"a4c4ba7b30c0faa7","name":"Rebuke","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telepathic","useTheForce":20,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One Force-sensitive creature","duration":"1 round","effect":"<p>You overwhelm a Force user with a powerful Force presence. If the target is Force-sensitive, they must make a Will save (DC = your UTF check) or be dazed for 1 round.</p>","special":"<p>This power only affects Force-sensitive creatures.</p>","descriptor":["Mind-Affecting"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":99,"tags":["debuff","force-user","daze"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":2,"max":2},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.390074b44aedfa2a"}}},{"_id":"424c79a26931b8d2","name":"Sever Force","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":6,"discipline":"dark-side","useTheForce":30,"time":"1 minute","range":"Touch","target":"One Force-sensitive creature","duration":"Permanent","effect":"<p>You permanently sever a Force user's connection to the Force. The target loses all Force abilities permanently.</p>","special":"<p>This is an extremely powerful and cruel Dark Side power. Using it gains you 3 Dark Side Points. The target can make a Will save (DC = your UTF check) to resist. Master-level power.</p>","descriptor":["Dark Side","Force Drain"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":99,"tags":["debuff","dark-side","permanent","master"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.b52769dd11b4e52c"}}},{"_id":"1dffede44c915860","name":"Surge","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"vital","useTheForce":15,"time":"Swift Action","range":"Personal","target":"You","duration":"1 round","effect":"<p>You use the Force to push your body beyond normal limits. You gain an additional move action this turn.</p>","special":"<p>This extra move action can be used to move or perform other move-action tasks.</p>","descriptor":["Vital"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":99,"tags":["enhancement","action-economy","movement"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.1ac1084ca8f07114"}}},{"_id":"cc99b229e81fff75","name":"Vital Transfer","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":3,"discipline":"vital","useTheForce":15,"time":"Standard Action","range":"Touch","target":"One living creature","duration":"Instantaneous","effect":"<p>You channel the Force to heal injuries and restore vitality. The target recovers hit points based on your Use the Force check result.</p>","special":"<p>You cannot heal yourself with this power.</p>","descriptor":["Vital","Healing"],"dcChart":[{"dc":15,"effect":"2d6 healing","description":"Target heals 2d6 hit points"},{"dc":20,"effect":"4d6 healing","description":"Target heals 4d6 hit points"},{"dc":25,"effect":"6d6 healing + condition","description":"Target heals 6d6 hit points and removes one ongoing condition"},{"dc":30,"effect":"8d6 healing + all conditions","description":"Target heals 8d6 hit points and removes all ongoing conditions"}],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":99,"tags":["healing","vital","support"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.00b65e47a4dd7d76"}}},{"_id":"c7717717b38cedb3","name":"Unarmed","type":"weapon","img":"icons/svg/sword.svg","system":{"damage":"1d8+12","damageType":"kinetic","attackBonus":0,"attackAttribute":"str","range":"melee","weight":1,"cost":0,"equipped":true,"description":"","properties":[],"ammunition":{"type":"none","current":0,"max":0},"weaponCategory":"simple","proficiency":"simple","subcategory":""},"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"placeholder":true,"npc":{"flatAttackBonus":20,"flatDamageFormula":"1d8+12","useFlat":true}}}},{"_id":"a3f7b8f2788c61de","name":"Unarmed (*)","type":"weapon","img":"icons/svg/sword.svg","system":{"damage":"1d8+16","damageT