"name":"Fringe Savant","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Fringer","prerequisites":null,"benefit":"Natural 20 on a skill check grants one extra Force Point for the encounter.","description":"A natural 20 on a skill check grants a temporary Force Point.","class":"Scout","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scout","tree":"Fringer","treeId":"7c47d36dc1f77d9c","tags":["force","leader","scout","striker"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.fringe_savant"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.d4a9f83d180934b5"}}},{"_id":"022c9d104d7c44bd","name":"Jury-Rigger","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Master Scout","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Tripwire Prerequisites: , Trained in Mechanics As a Standard Action, you can set up a simple snare or trap across an opening up to 3 squares wide. You must have the required items to set the trap. Make a successful DC 20 Mechanics check to set the trap. Make a Deception check to conceal the wire. Compare the result of the Deception check to the Perception check of the next creature that passes through that square (-10 if it observes you setting the trap). If the creature fails the Perception check, it takes the indicated use of the trap. If the creature succeeds, it can make a DC 10 Acrobatics check to avoid the wire. Select one of the following options: Clothesline: Requires thin wire, set at neck height. Success results in the target falling Prone in the trapped square, ending its Actions for the turn and taking 1d6 points of damage. Electronic Tripwire: Success results in Mine damage (Treat as Frag Grenade, 2-square blast radius centered on one end of the wire). Target is automatically hit; roll 1d20+10 against the Reflex Defense of adjacent targets. Tripwire: Requires thin wire, set at ankle height. Add 2 to the Deception check result. Success results in the target immediately falling Prone in the trapped square and ending its Actions for the turn.","description":"Tripwire Prerequisites: , Trained in Mechanics As a Standard Action, you can set up a simple snare or trap across an opening up to 3 squares wide. You must have the required items to set the trap. Make a successful DC 20 Mechanics check to set the trap. Make a Deception check to conceal the wire. Compare the result of the Deception check to the Perception check of the next creature that passes through that square (-10 if it observes you setting the trap). If the creature fails the Perception check, it takes the indicated use of the trap. If the creature succeeds, it can make a DC 10 Acrobatics check to avoid the wire. Select one of the following options: Clothesline: Requires thin wire, set at neck height. Success results in the target falling Prone in the trapped square, ending its Actions for the turn and taking 1d6 points of damage. Electronic Tripwire: Success results in Mine damage (Treat as Frag Grenade, 2-square blast radius centered on one end of the wire). Target is automatically hit; roll 1d20+10 against the Reflex Defense of adjacent targets. Tripwire: Requires thin wire, set at ankle height. Add 2 to the Deception check result. Success results in the target immediately falling Prone in the trapped square and ending its Actions for the turn.","class":"Scout","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scout","tree":"Master Scout","treeId":"dca33c0215264a02","tags":["action-economy","controller","defender","evasion","heavy-weapons","mechanics","perception","positioning","scout","skills","social","striker","support"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.jury_rigger"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.e15a3408b9474354"}}},{"_id":"d9b61be4d66cad1f","name":"Keep it Together","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Fringer","prerequisites":"Jury-Rigger","benefit":"When you jury-rig a vehicle, it moves -2 down the condition track at end (instead of -5).","description":"Once per encounter, your vehicle avoids moving down the condition track.","class":"Scout","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scout","tree":"Fringer","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.jury_rigger"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"7c47d36dc1f77d9c","tags":["condition-removal","controller","feat-chain","mobility","scout","talent-chain"]},"effects":[{"_id":"a0a072a8-d539-4e13-8542-20bca578650a","name":"Keep it Together","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.jury_rig.stability","mode":5,"value":"2_down"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Keep it Together"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.keep_it_together"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.9211e3f6268b3413"}}},{"_id":"c3cbe8e648928335","name":"Surefooted","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Survivor","prerequisites":null,"benefit":"Speed is not reduced by difficult terrain.","description":"Your speed is not reduced by difficult terrain.","class":"Scout","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scout","tree":"Survivor","treeId":"9b06340233eb3cdd","tags":["controller","damage-reduction","mobility","scout"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.surefooted"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.f87bd82a892f69ea"}}},{"_id":"d0b4a1770c7c99f0","name":"Unarmed","type":"weapon","img":"icons/svg/sword.svg","system":{"damage":"1d4+4","damageType":"kinetic","attackBonus":0,"attackAttribute":"str","range":"melee","weight":1,"cost":0,"equipped":true,"description":"","properties":[],"ammunition":{"type":"none","current":0,"max":0},"weaponCategory":"simple","proficiency":"simple","subcategory":""},"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"placeholder":true,"npc":{"fla