 Proficiency","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"Ignore -5 penalty on attack rolls with weapons of a particular type.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["non-force"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{"value":"Ignore -5 penalty on attack rolls with weapons of a particular type."}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.ecc2471ac96ec2d4"}}},{"_id":"954cd14c5b897166","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Pistols)","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"You are proficient with pistols and do not take the -5 penalty when using them.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["non-force","ranged","scoundrel","scout","soldier"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier","Scout","Scoundrel"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{}},"effects":[{"_id":"04733e85-193e-4f4b-8792-c359083557d1","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Pistols)","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Weapon Proficiency (Pistols)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Pistols)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.e5d361d01d1b44e4"}}},{"_id":"a18b1e733ab1dd1f","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"You are proficient with simple weapons and do not take the -5 penalty when using them.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["noble","non-force","scoundrel","scout","soldier"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier","Scout","Scoundrel","Noble"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{}},"effects":[{"_id":"220daaa7-e1b5-440d-98cd-10f5e586ef8b","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.2d680cc46a7972da"}}},{"_id":"81c5eee8a4e06187","name":"Mentor","type":"feat","img":"systems/foundryvtt-swse/assets/icons/force-secret.png","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"Whenever you activate a Force Power, you can spend a Force Point to add one use of that Force Power to the Force Power Suite of one ally within 12 squares of you and in your line of sight. Once used, the Force Power cannot be regained by any means, and if the Force Power is not used by the end of the ally's next turn, it is lost.","prerequisite":"Successfully trained an Apprentice to knighthood (or the equivalent rank for other Force Traditions)","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Jedi Academy Training Manual","page":0,"tags":["force-secret"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":"<p><strong>Cost:</strong> Force Point or Destiny Point</p><p>Whenever you activate a Force Power, you can spend a Force Point to add one use of that Force Power to the Force Power Suite of one ally within 12 squares of you and in your line of sight. Once used, the Force Power cannot be regained by any means, and if the Force Power is not used by the end of the ally's next turn, it is lost.</p><p>You or the ally can spend a Destiny Point to have the Force Power lost at the end of the encounter, instead of the end of the ally's next turn.</p><p><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Successfully trained an Apprentice to knighthood (or the equivalent rank for other Force Traditions)</p>","cost":"Force Point or Destiny Point","alternativeCost":"You or the ally can spend a Destiny Point to have the Force Power lost at the end of the encounter, instead of the end of the ally's next turn."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcesecrets.9b1346beabbd68bd"}}},{"_id":"13cf5cf86952d347","name":"Quicken Power","type":"feat","img":"systems/foundryvtt-swse/assets/icons/force-secret.png","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"When using a Force Power that requires a Standard Action or Move Action to activate, you can spend a Force Point to activate the Force Power as a Swift Action instead.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Core","page":0,"tags":["force-secret"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":"<p><strong>Cost:</strong> Force Point or Destiny Point</p><p>When using a Force Power that requires a Standard Action or Move Action to activate, you can spend a Force Point to activate the Force Power as a Swift Action instead.</p><p>Alternatively, you can spend a Destiny Point to activate the Force Power as a Reaction instead.</p>","cost":"Force Point or Destiny Point","alternativeCost":"Alternatively, you can spend a Destiny Point to activate the Force Power as a Reaction instead."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcesecrets.52bf7b9a1a41de2b"}}},{"_id":"93b3af04183ce2fb","name":"Shaped Power","type":"feat","img":"systems/foundryvtt-swse/assets/icons/force-secret.png","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"When using a Force Power with a Cone Area Effect (such as Force Slam), you can spend a Force Point to instead affect a 1 square wide and (5 x Cone's length) squares long line.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Core","page":0,"tags":["force-secret"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":"<p><strong>Cost:</strong> Force Point or Destiny Point</p><p>When using a Force Power with a Cone Area Effect (such as Force Slam), you can spend a Force Point to instead affect a 1 square wide and (5 x Cone's length) squares long line.</p><p>Alternatively, when using a Force Power with a Cone Area Effect, you can spend a Destiny Point to instead affect one or more targets of your choice within a number of squares of you equal to the Cone's length.</p>","cost":"Force Point or Destiny Point","alternativeCost":"Alternatively, when using a Force Power with a Cone Area Effect, you can spend a Destiny Point to instead affect one or more targets of your choice within a number of squares of you equal to the Cone's length."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcesecrets.d687b624feb2d351"}}},{"_id":"9806faa57e9f5736","name":"Improved Sense Force","type":"feat","img":"systems/foundryvtt-swse/assets/icons/force-technique.png","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"You may use the Sense Force ability of the Use the Force Skill as a Move Action rather than a Full-Round Action.","prerequisite":"Sense Force","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Core","page":0,"tags":["force-technique"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"description":"<p>You may use the Sense Force ability of the Use the Force Skill as a Move Action rather than a Full-Round Action.</p><p><strong>Related Power:</strong> Sense Force</p><p><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Sense Force</p>","relatedPower":"Sense Force"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcetechniques.ad67b8f3959860f2"}}},{"_id":"56dfff577f286405","name":"Improved Sense Surroundings","type":"feat","img":"systems/foundryvtt-swse/assets/icons/force-technique.png","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"You may use the Sense Surroundings application of the Use the Force Skill as a Free Action rather than a Swift Action.","prerequisite":"Sense Surroundings","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Core","page":0,"tags":["force-technique"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"description":"<p>You may use the Sense Surroundings application of the Use the Force Skill as a Free Action rather than a Swift Action.</p><p><strong>Related Power:</strong> Sense Surroundings</p><p><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Sense Surroundings</p>","relatedPower":"Sense Surroundings"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcetechniques.4955b5076ca5da89"}}},{"_id":"9127810fc5e834f0","name":"Born Leader","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Naval Officer","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Prerequisites: Charisma 13, Intelligence 13, When you are the Commander of a Capital Ship, calculate its Reflex Defense using your Heroic Level plus one-half the ship's armor bonus (rounded down), the Pilot's Heroic Level, or the ship's Armor bonus, whichever is highest. In addition, all Gunners on your ship add one-half your Heroic Level, or one-half their Heroic Level, whichever is more, to damage rolls with Vehicle Weapons. Finally, you treat any generic crew as being one quality level higher (maximum of Ace, see Crew Quality).","description":"Prerequisites: Charisma 13, Intelligence 13, When you are the Commander of a Capital Ship, calculate its Reflex Defense using your Heroic Level plus one-half the ship's armor bonus (rounded down), the Pilot's Heroic Level, or the ship's Armor bonus, whichever is highest. In addition, all Gunners on your ship add one-half your Heroic Level, or one-half their Heroic Level, whichever is more, to damage rolls with Vehicle Weapons. Finally, you treat any generic crew as being one quality level higher (maximum of Ace, see Crew Quality).","class":"Noble","costNumeric":null,"category":"Noble","tree":"Naval Officer","treeId":"057a978a7dc1d5a7","tags":["armor","defender","noble","striker","support","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[{"_id":"f9275c38-3cb5-4ab3-aaa5-25e5722dcdd3","name":"Born Leader","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.defenses.will","mode":2,"value":"1"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Born Leader"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.born_leader"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.6a66ba6e0834dd6f"}}},{"_id":"b50b460d00390d3e","name":"Channel Aggression","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Dark Side Devotee","prerequisites":"","benefit":"You let your anger swell into a Rage. As a Swift Action, you may spend a Force Point to gain a +2 Rage bonus on melee attack rolls and melee damage rolls for a number of rounds equal to 5 + your Constitution modifier. At the end of this duration, you move -1 step along the Condition Track. While Raging, you cannot use Skills that require patience and concentration, such as Mechanics, Stealth, or Use the Force. Prerequisite: Whenever you score a Critical Hit, you may spend a Force Point to also reduce the target's Speed by half until they are fully healed (that is, restored to maximum Hit Points). Prerequisites: , Channel Anger Whenever you use a Force Power with the [Dark Side] descriptor, you may reroll your Use the Force check, but you must accept the result of the reroll, even if it is worse. Upon choosing this Talent, you can no longer use Force Powers with the [Light Side] descriptor. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual","description":"You let your anger swell into a Rage. As a Swift Action, you may spend a Force Point to gain a +2 Rage bonus on melee attack rolls and melee damage rolls for a number of rounds equal to 5 + your Constitution modifier. At the end of this duration, you move -1 step along the Condition Track. While Raging, you cannot use Skills that require patience and concentration, such as Mechanics, Stealth, or Use the Force. Prerequisite: Whenever you score a Critical Hit, you may spend a Force Point to also reduce the target's Speed by half until they are fully healed (that is, restored to maximum Hit Points). Prerequisites: , Channel Anger Whenever you use a Force Power with the [Dark Side] descriptor, you may reroll your Use the Force check, but you must accept the result of the reroll, even if it is worse. Upon choosing this Talent, you can no longer use Force Powers with the [Light Side] descriptor. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual","class":"Force Adept","costNumeric":null,"category":"Force Adept","tree":"Dark Side Devotee","treeId":"96ef43a3054dcb58","tags":["action-economy","condition-removal","controller","damage-reduction","dark-side","force","force-control","force-offense","force-support","light-side","mechanics","medicine","melee","mobility","precision","skills","stealth","striker","support","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.channel_aggression"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.ef3ec55015c60bda"}}},{"_id":"5d1a6ca66e026dd0","name":"Channel Anger","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Dark Side Devotee","prerequisites":"Channel Aggression","benefit":"Gain +2 melee attack and damage for a number of rounds equal to 5 + Constitution modifier, then move down one step on the condition track.","description":"Gain +2 melee attack and damage for a number of rounds equal to 5 + Constitution modifier, then move –1 down the condition track.","class":"Force Adept","costNumeric":null,"category":"Force Adept","tree":"Dark Side Devotee","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.channel_aggression"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"96ef43a3054dcb58","tags":["condition-removal","controller","feat-chain","melee","mobility","striker","sustained-damage","talent-chain"]},"effects":[{"_id":"c7e68fc9-d1bc-484b-a797-a04a539232fe","name":"Channel Anger","icon":"icons/svg/fire.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.attacks.melee","mode":2,"value":"2"},{"key":"system.damage.melee","mode":2,"value":"2"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Channel Anger"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.channel_anger"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.37ee909a7de54768"}}},{"_id":"8f68ad9ce7a9df44","name":"Crippling Strike","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Dark Side Devotee","prerequisites":"Channel Aggression","benefit":"On a critical hit, you can reduce the target’s speed by half until fully healed.","description":"On a critical hit, reduce the target's speed by half until fully healed.","class":"Force Adept","costNumeric":null,"category":"Force Adept","tree":"Dark Side Devotee","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.channel_aggression"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"96ef43a3054dcb58","tags":["damage-reduction","feat-chain","medicine","mobility","precision","skills","striker","support","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.crippling_strike"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.8b3cb561c294fa11"}}},{"_id":"95acfbc7757699f7","name":"Dark Side Adept","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Sith","prerequisites":"Prerequisites: Any One Force Technique, Weapon Focus (Lightsabers)","benefit":"Force Powers that are strongly tied to the Dark Side flow through you more easily. You can reroll any Use the Force check made when activating Force Powers with the [Dark Side] descriptor, and can spend a Force Point to keep the better of the two results. You can use your Use the Force modifier instead of your Deception check modifier when making Deception checks, as you use The Force to cloak your vile treachery. You are considered Trained in the Deception skill. If you are entitled to a Deception check reroll, you may reroll your Use the Force check instead (subject to the same circumstances and limitations). Prerequisites: , Dark Side Master Your knowledge of Sith sorcery allows you to imbue talismans and other objects with the power of the Dark Side. Create Sith Talisman: You can spend one Force Point to imbue a portable object with the Dark Side, creating a Sith Talisman that provides offensive strength to a Force Power or Lightsaber attack. Creating the talisman takes a Full-Round Action. While you wear or carry a Sith Talisman on your person, add 1d6 to damage rolls with your Force Powers. You increase your Dark Side Score by one when you first put on or carry a Sith Talisman. You can only have one Sith Talisman active at any given time, and if it is destroyed, you cannot create another one for 24 hours. Create Sith Weapon: You can alchemically treat a properly prepared weapon to become a Sith Weapon. You may spend a Force Point to imbue the weapon with the properties of the Sith Alchemical Weapon Template (this process takes one hour to complete). Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Threats of the Galaxy You have learned how to use a Jedi fighting technique to defeat Jedi in combat. Choose one Talent from the Lightsaber Forms Talent Tree; you gain the benefits of this Talent and are considered to have this Talent for the purpose of satisfying prerequisites. You must meet all the prerequisites as normal for the chosen Talent, in addition to the prerequisites of this Talent. You can select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select it, choose a different Talent from the Lightsaber Forms Talent Tree. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook Prerequisites: Any One Force Technique, Whenever you successfully activate a Force Power with the [Dark Side] descriptor that causes the target to move down the Condition Track, they gain a Persistent Condition, which can only be removed if the target receives Surgery (for living beings) or Repairs (for Droids, Vehicles, and objects). Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook Prerequisites: , Dark Side Master Once per encounter, you can spend a Force Point as a Standard Action to call upon the vengeful spirits of the ancient Sith. Doing so grants you 3 Followers with the Vengeful Spirit Template. These Followers appear in any unoccupied square adjacent to you, and last until the end of the encounter (at which point they vanish).","description":"Force Powers that are strongly tied to the Dark Side flow through you more easily. You can reroll any Use the Force check made when activating Force Powers with the [Dark Side] descriptor, and can spend a Force Point to keep the better of the two results. You can use your Use the Force modifier instead of your Deception check modifier when making Deception checks, as you use The Force to cloak your vile treachery. You are considered Trained in the Deception skill. If you are entitled to a Deception check reroll, you may reroll your Use the Force check instead (subject to the same circumstances and limitations). Prerequisites: , Dark Side Master Your knowledge of Sith sorcery allows you to imbue talismans and other objects with the power of the Dark Side. Create Sith Talisman: You can spend one Force Point to imbue a portable object with the Dark Side, creating a Sith Talisman that provides offensive strength to a Force Power or Lightsaber attack. Creating the talisman takes a Full-Round Action. While you wear or carry a Sith Talisman on your person, add 1d6 to damage rolls with your Force Powers. You increase your Dark Side Score by one when you first put on or carry a Sith Talisman. You can only have one Sith Talisman active at any given time, and if it is destroyed, you cannot create another one for 24 hours. Create Sith Weapon: You can alchemically treat a properly prepared weapon to become a Sith Weapon. You may spend a Force Point to imbue the weapon with the properties of the Sith Alchemical Weapon Template (this process takes one hour to complete). Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Threats of the Galaxy You have learned how to use a Jedi fighting technique to defeat Jedi in combat. Choose one Talent from the Lightsaber Forms Talent Tree; you gain the benefits of this Talent and are considered to have this Talent for the purpose of satisfying prerequisites. You must meet all the prerequisites as normal for the chosen Talent, in addition to the prerequisites of this Talent. You can select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select it, choose a different Talent from the Lightsaber Forms Talent Tree. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook Prerequisites: Any One Force Technique, Whenever you successfully activate a Force Power with the [Dark Side] descriptor that causes the target to move down the Condition Track, they gain a Persistent Condition, which can only be removed if the target receives Surgery (for living beings) or Repairs (for Droids, Vehicles, and objects). Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook Prerequisites: , Dark Side Master Once per encounter, you can spend a Force Point as a Standard Action to call upon the vengeful spirits of the ancient Sith. Doing so grants you 3 Followers with the Vengeful Spirit Template. These Followers appear in any unoccupied square adjacent to you, and last until the end of the encounter (at which point they vanish).","class":"Sith Apprentice","costNumeric":null,"category":"Sith Apprentice","tree":"Sith","treeId":"d1037bc7a08ea80b","tags":["action-economy","condition-removal","controller","dark-side","feat-chain","force","force-control","force-offense","jedi","leader","light-side","lightsaber","mechanics","melee","mobility","positioning","scaling","skills","social","striker","support","sustained-damage","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.dark_side_adept"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.cfdd73f3d939799d"}}},{"_id":"374e6318742174d7","name":"Dark Side Master","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Sith","prerequisites":"Dark Side Adept","benefit":"Reroll any Dark Side skill check.","description":"You may reroll Dark Side skill checks.","class":"Sith Apprentice","costNumeric":null,"category":"Sith Apprentice","tree":"Sith","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.dark_side_adept"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"d1037bc7a08ea80b","tags":["dark-side","feat-chain","force","jedi","striker","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.dark_side_master"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.d4fe49ef1701891e"}}},{"_id":"facc640ede29387e","name":"Force Focus","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Control","prerequisites":null,"benefit":"DC 15 Use the Force check to regain one Force power.","description":"Make a Use the Force check to regain one expended Force power.","costNumeric":null,"tree":"Control","treeId":"d3661aa9906bdc79","tags":["force"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.force_focus"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.af51d4e76675b183"}}},{"_id":"2fa3ec095de1b9a1","name":"Power of the Dark Side","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Dark Side","prerequisites":"Dark Side Score equal to Wisdom Score","benefit":"Charisma 13 As a Standard Action, you grant yourself and all allies within 6 squares of you a +1 Force bonus to all Defenses until the end of the encounter. These bonuses are lost if you fall unconscious or die. Affected allies that move out of range lose the benefits for as long as they remain out of range. Prerequisite: Once per day, you can use a Force Power that normally takes a Standard Action or a Move Action as a Swift Action. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide Sometimes your anger consumes you. As a Swift Action, you can take a -5 penalty to your Will Defense to gain a +2 Force bonus on attack rolls. The penalty and bonus last until the beginning of your next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide Prerequisite: Whenever an effect would normally move you down the Condition Track, you may spend a Force Point and increase your Dark Side Score by 1 to negate that movement down the Condition Track. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual Once per encounter as a Swift Action, you can return one Force Power with the [Dark Side] descriptor to your Force Power Suite without spending a Force Point. You can select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select it, you can use it one additional time per encounter. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Threats of the Galaxy As a Standard Action, you can spend a Force Point to drain the knowledge of an opponent you touch; you must succeed on a Use the Force check (DC equal to the target's Will Defense) to activate this Talent, and if you fail to activate this Talent, you may not try again on the same target for one day. If successful, you immediately become Trained in one Skill that the target is Trained in; if you are already Trained in that Skill, you instead gain Skill Focus in that Skill. This effect lasts for one day. Additionally, your target moves -1 Persistent step along the Condition Track, and the Persistent Condition can be removed only by resting for 8 hours. Additionally, you can choose to instead sift through the mind of the target, looking for a specific piece of knowledge or information. Doing so requires you to make a Perception check against the target's Will Defense; success indicates that you pull the relevant information from the target's mind. When you do so, you do not gain the bonus Trained Skill or Skill Focus normally granted by this Talent, but otherwise the Talent functions as normal. Using this Talent increases your Dark Side Score by 1. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual When you die, you become a Dark Side Spirit until the end of the encounter. You continue to occupy a space in this form, but other creatures can occupy the same space or move through your space without impediment. As a Standard Action, you can attempt to possess an adjacent target. You must succeed on a Use the Force check against an adjacent target's Will Defense. If your check result equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, you deal 8d6 points of Stun damage to the target; if you reduce the target to 0 Hit Points or move it to the bottom of the Condition Track with this attack, you possess the target as though it were a willing host. Alternatively, as a Standard Action, you can transfer your essence into a single adjacent object, such as a Holocron or a Lightsaber. If you do so, you lie dormant within the object until another creature attempts to use that object, at which time you can emerge and attempt to possess the creature, as described above. If you do not possess a creature or object within 10 rounds of manifesting as a Dark Side Spirit, your spirit dissipates and ceases to exist. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide Prerequisite: When you roll a Natural 20 on a Use the Force check to activate a Force Power that directly deals damage to a target, you can choose not to regain all of your spent Force Powers as normal and instead the targets damaged by the Force Power take half that damage again at the start of their next turn. Only Force Powers that directly damage the target are subject to this Talent, including Corruption, Force Blast, Force Grip, Force Lightning, Force Slam, Force Thrust (only when spending a Force Point), and Repulse (only when spending a Force Point). Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook Prerequisite: You can create balls of unnatural energy, enabling you to make a ranged attack roll against the Reflex Defense of one target within 12 squares and line of sight, dealing 2d6 points of energy damage to the target on a successful attack. Using this Talent increases your Dark Side Score by 1. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook Prerequisites: , Swift Power When using a Force Power that directly inflicts damage, you treat the target's Damage Threshold as though it were 5 points lower when determining if the target moves along the Condition Track. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook Prerequisite: Whenever your character moves 3 or more squares in a round you gain Concealment; you may choose not to use this Talent when you move.","description":"Charisma 13 As a Standard Action, you grant yourself and all allies within 6 squares of you a +1 Force bonus to all Defenses until the end of the encounter. These bonuses are lost if you fall unconscious or die. Affected allies that move out of range lose the benefits for as long as they remain out of range. Prerequisite: Once per day, you can use a Force Power that normally takes a Standard Action or a Move Action as a Swift Action. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide Sometimes your anger consumes you. As a Swift Action, you can take a -5 penalty to your Will Defense to gain a +2 Force bonus on attack rolls. The penalty and bonus last until the beginning of your next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide Prerequisite: Whenever an effect would normally move you down the Condition Track, you may spend a Force Point and increase your Dark Side Score by 1 to negate that movement down the Condition Track. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual Once per encounter as a Swift Action, you can return one Force Power with the [Dark Side] descriptor to your Force Power Suite without spending a Force Point. You can select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select it, you can use it one additional time per encounter. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Threats of the Galaxy As a Standard Action, you can spend a Force Point to drain the knowledge of an opponent you touch; you must succeed on a Use the Force check (DC equal to the target's Will Defense) to activate this Talent, and if you fail to activate this Talent, you may not try again on the same target for one day. If successful, you immediately become Trained in one Skill that the target is Trained in; if you are already Trained in that Skill, you instead gain Skill Focus in that Skill. This effect lasts for one day. Additionally, your target moves -1 Persistent step along the Condition Track, and the Persistent Condition can be removed only by resting for 8 hours. Additionally, you can choose to instead sift through the mind of the target, looking for a specific piece of knowledge or information. Doing so requires you to make a Perception check against the target's Will Defense; success indicates that you pull the relevant information from the target's mind. When you do so, you do not gain the bonus Trained Skill or Skill Focus normally granted by this Talent, but otherwise the Talent functions as normal. Using this Talent increases your Dark Side Score by 1. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual When you die, you become a Dark Side Spirit until the end of the encounter. You continue to occupy a space in this form, but other creatures can occupy the same space or move through your space without impediment. As a Standard Action, you can attempt to possess an adjacent target. You must succeed on a Use the Force check against an adjacent target's Will Defense. If your check result equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, you deal 8d6 points of Stun damage to the target; if you reduce the target to 0 Hit Points or move it to the bottom of the Condition Track with this attack, you possess the target as though it were a willing host. Alternatively, as a Standard Action, you can transfer your essence into a single adjacent object, such as a Holocron or a Lightsaber. If you do so, you lie dormant within the object until another creature attempts to use that object, at which time you can emerge and attempt to possess the creature, as described above. If you do not possess a creature or object within 10 rounds of manifesting as a Dark Side Spirit, your spirit dissipates and ceases to exist. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide Prerequisite: When you roll a Natural 20 on a Use the Force check to activate a Force Power that directly deals damage to a target, you can choose not to regain all of your spent Force Powers as normal and instead the targets damaged by the Force Power take half that damage again at the start of their next turn. Only Force Powers that directly damage the target are subject to this Talent, including Corruption, Force Blast, Force Grip, Force Lightning, Force Slam, Force Thrust (only when spending a Force Point), and Repulse (only when spending a Force Point). Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook Prerequisite: You can create balls of unnatural energy, enabling you to make a ranged attack roll against the Reflex Defense of one target within 12 squares and line of sight, dealing 2d6 points of energy damage to the target on a successful attack. Using this Talent increases your Dark Side Score by 1. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook Prerequisites: , Swift Power When using a Force Power that directly inflicts damage, you treat the target's Damage Threshold as though it were 5 points lower when determining if the target moves along the Condition Track. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook Prerequisite: Whenever your character moves 3 or more squares in a round you gain Concealment; you may choose not to use this Talent when you move.","costNumeric":null,"tree":"Dark Side","treeId":"de95d37c72b1c4cd","tags":["action-economy","condition-removal","controller","damage-reduction","dark-side","defender","feat-chain","force","force-control","force-defense","force-offense","leader","light-side","lightsaber","melee","mobility","perception","positioning","ranged","scaling","skills","stealth","striker","support","sustained-damage","talent-chain"]},"effects":[{"_id":"b3ad7fe2-78a8-42b3-83dc-385122d061ed","name":"Power of the Dark Side","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.damage","mode":2,"value":"1"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Power of the Dark Side"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.power_of_the_dark_side"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.627bd3abd30b973f"}}},{"_id":"703843063db74397","name":"Swift Power","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Dark Side","prerequisites":"Power of the Dark Side","benefit":"Once per day, use a swift action in place of a move or standard action to activate a Force power.","description":"Once per day, activate a Force power as a swift action.","costNumeric":null,"tree":"Dark Side","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.power_of_the_dark_side"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"de95d37c72b1c4cd","tags":["action-economy","controller","dark-side","feat-chain","force","force-control","mobility","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.swift_power"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.09609e71ba6cd4aa"}}},{"_id":"66512b1c2d1ff3ac","name":"Battle Strike","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"telekinetic","useTheForce":15,"time":"Swift Action","range":"Personal","target":"You","duration":"1 round","effect":"<p>You channel the Force to enhance your next melee attack. Your next melee attack this round gains a +1d6 bonus to damage.</p>","special":"<p>This bonus damage is Force damage and bypasses Damage Reduction.</p>","descriptor":["Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":94,"tags":["enhancement","damage","melee"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.f177dc6d65f76de9"}}},{"_id":"db4211f4635963fa","name":"Dark Rage","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/eye.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"Unknown","useTheForce":"","time":"standard","range":"","target":"","duration":"","effect":"","special":"","descriptor":"","dcChart":"","maintainable":false,"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1,"perDay":true}},"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"placeholder":true,"unresolved":"Dark Rage"}}},{"_id":"1fe0b76e86ebf8e5","name":"Force Grip","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":3,"discipline":"dark-side","useTheForce":15,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One creature","duration":"Concentration","effect":"<p>You use the Force to telekinetically choke or crush your target. The target takes damage each round based on your Use the Force check result.</p>","special":"<p>This is a Dark Side power. The target is immobilized while gripped.</p>","descriptor":["Dark Side","Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[{"dc":15,"effect":"2d6 damage/round","description":"Target takes 2d6 damage per round and is immobilized"},{"dc":20,"effect":"4d6 damage/round","description":"Target takes 4d6 damage per round and is immobilized"},{"dc":25,"effect":"6d6 damage/round + lift","description":"Target takes 6d6 damage per round, is immobilized, and lifted off ground"},{"dc":30,"effect":"8d6 damage/round + crush","description":"Target takes 8d6 damage per round and is being crushed (fort save or die)"}],"maintainable":true,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":96,"tags":["attack","damage","dark-side","telekinetic","immobilize"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.f41a957f71e98a6a"}}},{"_id":"f99a47dd80a6fc8d","name":"Force Lightning","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":4,"discipline":"dark-side","useTheForce":15,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One creature","duration":"Instantaneous","effect":"<p>You unleash devastating arcs of Force Lightning from your fingertips. The target takes lightning damage based on your Use the Force check result.</p>","special":"<p>This is a Dark Side power. Using it gains you a Dark Side Point.</p>","descriptor":["Dark Side","Force Lightning"],"dcChart":[{"dc":15,"effect":"2d6 lightning damage","description":"Target takes 2d6 lightning damage"},{"dc":20,"effect":"4d6 lightning damage","description":"Target takes 4d6 lightning damage"},{"dc":25,"effect":"6d6 lightning damage + stun","description":"Target takes 6d6 lightning damage and is stunned for 1 round"},{"dc":30,"effect":"8d6 lightning damage + stun 1d4","description":"Target takes 8d6 lightning damage and is stunned for 1d4 rounds"}],"maintainable":true,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":96,"tags":["a