,{"_id":"fa19afdc5af4a741","name":"Bolster Ally","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Inspiration","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Inspire Confidence Whenever you hit an opponent with a melee or ranged attack, you can (as a Free Action) choose to give one ally within your line of sight a bonus to damage on their next attack equal to their Character Level. Once their fervor has been ignited, the affected ally doesn't need to remain within line of sight of you; if their next attack misses, they lose the bonus to damage granted by this Talent. Prerequisites: , Inspire Confidence, Ignite Fervor Whenever an ally within line of sight of you makes an attack that moves an opponent down the Condition Track (such as dealing damage that equals of exceeds the target's Damage Threshold), that ally moves the target an additional -1 step down the Condition Track. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Inspire Confidence Your allies hold you in such esteem that when you are threatened or injured, you can impel them to action. You can use each of the following actions once per encounter: Guardian: Choose one ally as a Swift Action. As long as you remain within 6 squares of the ally, you gain a +2 bonus to your Reflex Defense until the start of your next turn. Reprisal: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any target within your Range as a Standard Action. If your attack roll succeeds and if that target attacks you before the end of your next turn, one ally within 6 squares can make an attack against that target as a Reaction. To Me!: Spend a Swift Action. Whenever you take any damage before the beginning of your next turn, each ally within line of sight can move 2 squares as a Reaction. This movement does not provoke Attacks of Opportunity. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","description":"Inspire Confidence Whenever you hit an opponent with a melee or ranged attack, you can (as a Free Action) choose to give one ally within your line of sight a bonus to damage on their next attack equal to their Character Level. Once their fervor has been ignited, the affected ally doesn't need to remain within line of sight of you; if their next attack misses, they lose the bonus to damage granted by this Talent. Prerequisites: , Inspire Confidence, Ignite Fervor Whenever an ally within line of sight of you makes an attack that moves an opponent down the Condition Track (such as dealing damage that equals of exceeds the target's Damage Threshold), that ally moves the target an additional -1 step down the Condition Track. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Inspire Confidence Your allies hold you in such esteem that when you are threatened or injured, you can impel them to action. You can use each of the following actions once per encounter: Guardian: Choose one ally as a Swift Action. As long as you remain within 6 squares of the ally, you gain a +2 bonus to your Reflex Defense until the start of your next turn. Reprisal: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any target within your Range as a Standard Action. If your attack roll succeeds and if that target attacks you before the end of your next turn, one ally within 6 squares can make an attack against that target as a Reaction. To Me!: Spend a Swift Action. Whenever you take any damage before the beginning of your next turn, each ally within line of sight can move 2 squares as a Reaction. This movement does not provoke Attacks of Opportunity. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","class":"Noble","costNumeric":null,"category":"Noble","tree":"Inspiration","treeId":"72d32ebcbb607314","tags":["action-economy","condition-removal","controller","defender","force","force-control","force-defense","force-offense","leader","melee","mobility","noble","positioning","ranged","striker","support"]},"effects":[{"_id":"c5626626-5e0d-4051-b4c2-928434aef891","name":"Bolster Ally","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.hp.regen","mode":2,"value":"1"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Bolster Ally"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.bolster_ally"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.d6e7f7178e643717"}}},{"_id":"b143c3e18d81917d","name":"Coordinate","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Leadership","prerequisites":null,"benefit":"All allies in line of sight gain +1 when using aid another (maximum +5).","description":"All allies gain +1 when using Aid Another, up to +5.","class":"Noble","costNumeric":null,"category":"Noble","tree":"Leadership","canonicalName":"Coordinate","canonicalTree":"Bab +12","treeId":"5964237d22681dc0","tags":["noble","striker"]},"effects":[{"_id":"25b28077-6a3c-43d8-97ba-a128e768f614","name":"Coordinate","icon":"icons/svg/handshake.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.actions.aidAnother","mode":2,"value":"1"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Coordinate"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.coordinate"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.a52044feeab3fe05"}}},{"_id":"21cd8e0d0edd433d","name":"Expert Shaper","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Shaper","prerequisites":"Biotech Surgery","benefit":"You can temporarily mend a damaged or disabled Biotech device using the Treat Injury Skill as a Standard Action instead of a Full-Round Action. You may reroll any Treat Injury check made to repair or modify a Biotech object, but the result of the reroll must be accepted, even if it is worse. Prerequisite: Whenever you temporarily mend a Biotech device using the Treat Injury Skill, the mended device moves +4 steps on the Condition Track. In addition, the mended device only moves -3 steps down the Condition Track at the end of the scene or encounter, and is only disabled if this reduction brings it to -5 steps on the Condition Track. Whenever you use the Biotech Surgery Feat to install a Bio-Implant, the Bio-Implant's attack bonus against the recipient's Fortitude Defense is halved.","description":"You can temporarily mend a damaged or disabled Biotech device using the Treat Injury Skill as a Standard Action instead of a Full-Round Action. You may reroll any Treat Injury check made to repair or modify a Biotech object, but the result of the reroll must be accepted, even if it is worse. Prerequisite: Whenever you temporarily mend a Biotech device using the Treat Injury Skill, the mended device moves +4 steps on the Condition Track. In addition, the mended device only moves -3 steps down the Condition Track at the end of the scene or encounter, and is only disabled if this reduction brings it to -5 steps on the Condition Track. Whenever you use the Biotech Surgery Feat to install a Bio-Implant, the Bio-Implant's attack bonus against the recipient's Fortitude Defense is halved.","class":"Shaper","costNumeric":null,"category":"Shaper","tree":"Shaper","treeId":"cdbee578d65154fc","tags":["action-economy","condition-removal","controller","defender","feat-chain","mechanics","mobility","skills","striker","sustained-damage","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.expert_shaper"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.f9047f30ef6712af"}}},{"_id":"edace510c205bfb8","name":"Inspire Confidence","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Inspiration","prerequisites":"","benefit":"You can't in yourself. As a Swift Action, you can encourage one of your allies within line of sight to make haste with a Skill Check. On that ally's next turn, that ally can make a Skill Check that normally requires a Standard Action, as a Move Action instead. Prerequisite: You can share your strength of will with your allies. Once per encounter as a Swift Action, you can grant all allies within line of sight a +2 morale bonus to their Will Defense. This bonus lasts for the remainder of the encounter, and once it is granted your allies need not remain within line of sight of you to retain this bonus.","description":"You can't in yourself. As a Swift Action, you can encourage one of your allies within line of sight to make haste with a Skill Check. On that ally's next turn, that ally can make a Skill Check that normally requires a Standard Action, as a Move Action instead. Prerequisite: You can share your strength of will with your allies. Once per encounter as a Swift Action, you can grant all allies within line of sight a +2 morale bonus to their Will Defense. This bonus lasts for the remainder of the encounter, and once it is granted your allies need not remain within line of sight of you to retain this bonus.","class":"Noble","costNumeric":null,"category":"Noble","tree":"Inspiration","treeId":"72d32ebcbb607314","tags":["action-economy","controller","defender","leader","mobility","noble","striker","support"]},"effects":[{"_id":"1faa089c-9609-46d8-8543-9a68ace3553b","name":"Inspire Confidence","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.attacks","mode":2,"value":"1"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Inspire Confidence"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.inspire_confidence"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.4d8882a28da30454"}}},{"_id":"6f6baa84a1e59ed2","name":"Inspire Haste","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Inspiration","prerequisites":null,"benefit":"An ally may make a skill check as a move action instead of a standard action.","description":"An ally may make a skill check as a move action instead of a standard action.","class":"Noble","costNumeric":