ake the -5 penalty when using them.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["noble","non-force","scoundrel","scout","soldier"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier","Scout","Scoundrel","Noble"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{}},"effects":[{"_id":"220daaa7-e1b5-440d-98cd-10f5e586ef8b","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.2d680cc46a7972da"}}},{"_id":"5023000420457ed1","name":"Improved Move Light Object","type":"feat","img":"systems/foundryvtt-swse/assets/icons/force-technique.png","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"You may make a Use the Force check to Move Light Object as a Swift Action instead of a Move Action. Using the light object as a projectile weapon requires a Move Action (instead of a Standard Action).","prerequisite":"Move Light Object","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Core","page":0,"tags":["force-technique"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"description":"<p>You may make a Use the Force check to Move Light Object as a Swift Action instead of a Move Action. Using the light object as a projectile weapon requires a Move Action (instead of a Standard Action).</p><p><strong>Related Power:</strong> Move Light Object</p><p><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Move Light Object</p>","relatedPower":"Move Light Object"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcetechniques.c406600924a7780e"}}},{"_id":"9fdcfb15881933e2","name":"Acute Senses","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Master Scout","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Keen Shot You are skilled at fighting armored characters, taking advantage of their weaknesses. You can use each of the following Actions once per encounter: Binding Hit: You dislodge an enemy's Armor, causing it to hinder the wearer's defenses. Make a melee or ranged attack as a Standard Action. If you hit and damage your target, the target loses its Armor bonus to its Reflex Defense and is Flat-Footed. This effect remains until the target spends a Standard Action to adjust its Armor. Blinding Fire: Make a melee or ranged attack as a Standard Action. If the attack hits and damages the target, the target takes a -2 penalty to all attacks until the end of your next turn. Additionally, all other creatures, Droids, and Vehicles have Concealment from the target until the end of your next turn. Slowing Shot: Your hit damages your target's Armor so that the target's movement is hindered. Make a melee or ranged attack as a Standard Action. If you hit and damage the target, the target's Speed is reduced by two squares until the end of your next turn.","description":"Keen Shot You are skilled at fighting armored characters, taking advantage of their weaknesses. You can use each of the following Actions once per encounter: Binding Hit: You dislodge an enemy's Armor, causing it to hinder the wearer's defenses. Make a melee or ranged attack as a Standard Action. If you hit and damage your target, the target loses its Armor bonus to its Reflex Defense and is Flat-Footed. This effect remains until the target spends a Standard Action to adjust its Armor. Blinding Fire: Make a melee or ranged attack as a Standard Action. If the attack hits and damages the target, the target takes a -2 penalty to all attacks until the end of your next turn. Additionally, all other creatures, Droids, and Vehicles have Concealment from the target until the end of your next turn. Slowing Shot: Your hit damages your target's Armor so that the target's movement is hindered. Make a melee or ranged attack as a Standard Action. If you hit and damage the target, the target's Speed is reduced by two squares until the end of your next turn.","class":"Scout","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scout","tree":"Master Scout","treeId":"dca33c0215264a02","tags":["action-economy","armor","controller","damage-reduction","defender","force","force-control","force-defense","force-offense","melee","mobility","positioning","ranged","scout","striker","support"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.acute_senses"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.f0166d26d9f6252a"}}},{"_id":"fc0529d208fa0d24","name":"Armored Defense","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Knight's Armor","prerequisites":"","benefit":"When calculating your Reflex Defense, you may add your Heroic Level plus one-half your Armor bonus (rounded down), or your Armor bonus alone, whichever is higher. This Talent counts as both the Talent and the Improved Talent for the purposes of prerequisites. You are adept at using a Cortosis Gauntlet to parry Lightsaber attacks. You gain a +2 bonus when making an opposed Unarmed melee attack roll against a Lightsaber attack.","description":"When calculating your Reflex Defense, you may add your Heroic Level plus one-half your Armor bonus (rounded down), or your Armor bonus alone, whichever is higher. This Talent counts as both the Talent and the Improved Talent for the purposes of prerequisites. You are adept at using a Cortosis Gauntlet to parry Lightsaber attacks. You gain a +2 bonus when making an opposed Unarmed melee attack roll against a Lightsaber attack.","class":"Soldier","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","tree":"Knight's Armor","treeId":"ea01d740c91888b3","tags":["armor","defender","lightsaber","melee","scaling","soldier","striker","sustained-damage","unarmed"]},"effects":[{"_id":"28f1f3db-0c6f-4614-bdcf-000f1542a25b","name":"Armored Defense","icon":"icons/svg/shield.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.defenses.reflex.misc","mode":2,"value":"1","priority":20}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Armored Defense"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.armored_defense"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.4c236343b01ea763"}}},{"_id":"012357ab10210180","name":"Block","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Sith Alchemy","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Create Sith Amulet: You can create a Sith Amulet. The creation of a Sith Amulet requires 25,000 credits' worth of gems and other raw materials, and the creation process takes 1 week (this work can be spread out over several sessions and need not be consecutive). At the end of the process, you must spend a Force Point to complete the Sith Amulet, after which point it functions exactly as a Sith Amulet. Create Sith Armor: You can transform a suit of normal Battle Armor into the Dark Armor worn by Sith Lords. You must have a suit of Battle Armor to transform into the Dark Armor (Light Battle Armor becomes Light Dark Armor, Battle Armor becomes Dark Armor, and Heavy Battle Armor becomes Heavy Dark Armor). The transformation process takes 1 day for Light Dark Armor, 2 days for Dark Armor, and 3 days for Heavy Dark Armor. You must spend a Force Point at the end of the creation process to complete the Armor's transformation. Create Sith Talisman: You can spend a Force Point to imbue a portable object with the Dark Side, creating a Sith Talisman that provides offensive strength to a Force Power. Creating the Sith Talisman takes a Full-Round Action. While you wear or carry the Sith Talisman on your person, you add 1d6 to your damage with Force Powers. You increase your Dark Side Score by 1 when you first wear or carry a Sith Talisman. You can have only one Sith Talisman active at any given time, and if it is destroyed, you cannot create another one for 24 hours. Create Sith Weapon: You can alchemically treat a Simple Weapon (Melee) or an Advanced Melee Weapon, turning it into a Sith Weapon. You must spend a Force Point and spend 1 hour imbuing the Weapon with the properties of a Sith Alchemical Weapon (see also: Sith Alchemical Weapon Template). A Lightsaber does not ignore the Sith Weapon's DR, and characters who are proficient in the Weapon's use can treat it as a Lightsaber for the purposes of the , Deflect, and Redirect Shot Talents (and any Talents that have these Talents as a prerequisite). Additionally, as a Swift Action, the wielder of a Sith Weapon can spend a Force Point to gain a bonus equal to their Dark Side Score to the damage of their next attack made with the Weapon before the end of the encounter. This increases the wielder's Dark Side Score by 1.","description":"Create Sith Amulet: You can create a Sith Amulet. The creation of a Sith Amulet requires 25,000 credits' worth of gems and other raw materials, and the creation process takes 1 week (this work can be spread out over several sessions and need not be consecutive). At the end of the process, you must spend a Force Point to complete the Sith Amulet, after which point it functions exactly as a Sith Amulet. Create Sith Armor: You can transform a suit of normal Battle Armor into the Dark Armor worn by Sith Lords. You must have a suit of Battle Armor to transform into the Dark Armor (Light Battle Armor becomes Light Dark Armor, Battle Armor becomes Dark Armor, and Heavy Battle Armor becomes Heavy Dark Armor). The transformation process takes 1 day for Light Dark Armor, 2 days for Dark Armor, and 3 days for Heavy Dark Armor. You must spend a Force Point at the end of the creation process to complete the Armor's transformation. Create Sith Talisman: You can spend a Force Point to imbue a portable object with the Dark Side, creating a Sith Talisman that provides offensive strength to a Force Power. Creating the Sith Talisman takes a Full-Round Action. While you wear or carry the Sith Talisman on your person, you add 1d6 to your damage with Force Powers. You increase your Dark Side Score by 1 when you first wear or carry a Sith Talisman. You can have only one Sith Talisman active at any given time, and if it is destroyed, you cannot create another one for 24 hours. Create Sith Weapon: You can alchemically treat a Simple Weapon (Melee) or an Advanced Melee Weapon, turning it into a Sith Weapon. You must spend a Force Point and spend 1 hour imbuing the Weapon with the properties of a Sith Alchemical Weapon (see also: Sith Alchemical Weapon Template). A Lightsaber does not ignore the Sith Weapon's DR, and characters who are proficient in the Weapon's use can treat it as a Lightsaber for the purposes of the , Deflect, and Redirect Shot Talents (and any Talents that have these Talents as a prerequisite). Additionally, as a Swift Action, the wielder of a Sith Weapon can spend a Force Point to gain a bonus equal to their Dark Side Score to the damage of their next attack made with the Weapon before the end of the encounter. This increases the wielder's Dark Side Score by 1.","class":"Jedi","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","tree":"Sith Alchemy","treeId":"a67faf2ae089ab5d","tags":["action-economy","armor","dark-side","defender","force","force-offense","jedi","lightsaber","melee","mobility","ranged","striker","support","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.block"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.9379daa94a228c04"}}},{"_id":"60b840cd81ae6cc3","name":"Deflect","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Lightsaber Forms","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Redirect Shot","description":"Redirect Shot","class":"Jedi","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","tree":"Lightsaber Forms","treeId":"2bc2572e852832e4","tags":["jedi","lightsaber","melee","ranged"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.deflect"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.72c644f7a09b1186"}}},{"_id":"6d96b75fcd81c198","name":"Elusive Target","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Jedi Guardian","prerequisites":null,"benefit":"If you are in a melee, ranged attacks against you take an additional -5 penalty (on top of the firing-into-melee penalty).","description":"Ranged attacks against you while in melee take an additional -5 penalty.","class":"Jedi","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","tree":"Jedi Guardian","treeId":"10c843cef8ce2798","tags":["force","force-offense","jedi","light-side","melee","positioning","ranged"]},"effects":[{"_id":"d82c4204-1b7d-41b9-b88a-062970ca8db9","name":"Elusive Target","icon":"icons/svg/wind.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.defenses.reflex.misc","mode":2,"value":"2","priority":20}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Elusive Target"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.elusive_target"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.a0ace6dcc1c67d48"}}},{"_id":"68a1da4acf1c708b","name":"Hunter's Mark","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Bounty Hunter","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Once per encounter as a Free Action, you may designate an opponent. For the rest of the encounter, when you succeed on a melee or ranged attack against that opponent, you gain a bonus on damage equal to your Class Level. Your skill as a Bounty Hunter is known throughout the galaxy, even on fringe worlds. When you are not Disguised, you may reroll any Persuasion checks made to Intimidate, keeping the better of the two results. You may choose to reroll any Gather Information checks made to Locate Individual, but you must accept the result of the reroll, even if it is worse. Prerequisites: , Hunter's Target This Talent applies only to an opponent you've designated as your Hunter's Target. Any attack or effect originating from the target that would normally move you along the Condition Track does not, in fact, move you along the Condition Track. Prerequisites: , Hunter's Target Prerequisites: , Hunter's Target, Nowhere to Hide Prerequisites: , Hunter's Target","description":"Once per encounter as a Free Action, you may designate an opponent. For the rest of the encounter, when you succeed on a melee or ranged attack against that opponent, you gain a bonus on damage equal to your Class Level. Your skill as a Bounty Hunter is known throughout the galaxy, even on fringe worlds. When you are not Disguised, you may reroll any Persuasion checks made to Intimidate, keeping the better of the two results. You may choose to reroll any Gather Information checks made to Locate Individual, but you must accept the result of the reroll, even if it is worse. Prerequisites: , Hunter's Target This Talent applies only to an opponent you've designated as your Hunter's Target. Any attack or effect originating from the target that would normally move you along the Condition Track does not, in fact, move you along the Condition Track. Prerequisites: , Hunter's Target Prerequisites: , Hunter's Target, Nowhere to Hide Prerequisites: , Hunter's Target","class":"Bounty Hunter","costNumeric":null,"category":"Bounty Hunter","tree":"Bounty Hunter","treeId":"a47ed82a822e3962","tags":["action-economy","condition-removal","controller","dual-wield","melee","mobility","positioning","ranged","scoundrel","skills","social","stealth","striker","support"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.hunters_mark"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.74fb6b37af983a4c"}}},{"_id":"d2da7eb4c0c4c880","name":"Improved Initiative","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Awareness","prerequisites":"Acute Senses","benefit":"Reroll Initiative checks.","description":"Reroll Initiative checks and keep the better result.","class":"Scout","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scout","tree":"Awareness","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.acute_senses"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"1c48d1cd9ab1f5c8","tags":["feat-chain","scout","skills","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.improved_initiative"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.9840f0e8b8f53bb5"}}},{"_id":"473cf931d1d6e00c","name":"Battle Strike","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"telekinetic","useTheForce":15,"time":"Swift Action","range":"Personal","target":"You","duration":"1 round","effect":"<p>You channel the Force to enhance your next melee attack. Your next melee attack this round gains a +1d6 bonus to damage.</p>","special":"<p>This bonus damage is Force damage and bypasses Damage Reduction.</p>","descriptor":["Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":94,"tags":["enhancement","damage","melee"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.f177dc6d65f76de9"}}},{"_id":"9cbb97d0068e06f5","name":"Force Slam","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telekinetic","useTheForce":20,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One creature or object","duration":"Instantaneous","effect":"<p>You use telekinetic force to violently slam your target against a surface. The target takes 4d6 damage and is knocked prone.</p>","special":"<p>The target must be within 6 squares of a solid surface (wall, floor, ceiling).</p>","descriptor":["Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":97,"tags":["attack","damage","telekinetic","prone"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.462a6c23e00c4dfc"}}},{"_id":"0dd6afe7c14f078b","name":"Mind Trick","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"telepathic","useTheForce":15,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One creature","duration":"1 minute or until completed","effect":"<p>You influence a weak mind to believe what you tell them or follow a simple suggestion. The target must make a Will save (DC = your UTF check) or be affected.</p>","special":"<p>The suggestion must be reasonable and the target must be able to understand you.</p>","descriptor":["Mind-Affecting"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":98,"tags":["mind-control","suggestion","social"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.e6649f366d6c5737"}}},{"_id":"0591120c61a2f488","name":"Rebuke","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telepathic","useTheForce":20,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One Force-sensitive creature","duration":"1 round","effect":"<p>You overwhelm a Force user with a powerful Force presence. If the target is Force-sensitive, they must make a Will save (DC = your UTF check) or be dazed for 1 round.</p>","special":"<p>This power only affects Force-sensitive creatures.</p>","descriptor":["Mind-Affecting"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":99,"tags":["debuff","force-user","daze"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.390074b44aedfa2a"}}},{"_id":"4f51d10c56280966","name":"Lightsaber","type":"weapon","img":"icons/svg/sword.svg","system":{"damage":"2d8+5","damageType":"energy","attackBonus":0,"attackAttribute":"str","range":"melee","weight":1,"cost":12000,"equipped":true,"description":"<p>The elegant weapon of the Jedi and Sith. A blade of pure energy capable of cutting through nearly anything.</p>\n      <p><strong>Special:</strong> Ignores armor bonuses to Reflex Defense. Can deflect blaster bolts. Critical threat range 19-20. Requires exotic weapon proficiency.</p>","properties":["Lightsaber","Critical 19-20","Exotic","Armor-Piercing"],"ammunition":{"type":"none","current":0,"max":0},"weaponCategory":"melee","proficiency":"exotic","subcategory":"lightsaber","costNumeric":12000,"category":"lightsaber"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.weapons.weapon-lightsaber"},"swse":{"npc":{"flatAttackBonus":14,"flatDamageFormula":"2d8+5","useFlat":true}}}},{"_id":"d5eceed651861b78","name":"Heavy Blaster Pistol","type":"weapon","img":"icons/svg/sword.svg","system":{"damage":"3d8+5","damageType":"energy","attackBonus":0,"attackAttribute":"dex","range":"ranged","weight":1.3,"cost":750,"equipped":true,"description":"<p>A more powerful variant of the standard blaster pistol, delivering higher damage at the cost of increased weight and power consumption.</p>","properties":[],"ammunition":{"type":"none","current":0,"max":0},"weaponCategory":"ranged","proficiency":"pistols","subcategory":"pistol","costNumeric":750,"category":"pistol"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.weapons.weapon-heavy-blaster-pistol"},"swse":{"npc":{"flatAttackBonus":12,"flatDamageFormula":"3d8+5","useFlat":true}}}}],"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"import":{"source":"books","raw":{"Size":"Medium","Species":"Human","Nonheroic Level":0,"Class Levels":{"Jedi":5,"Scout":3,"Hunter":1,"Knight":3},"Destiny Points":1,"Force Points":5,"Dark Side Points":0,"Initiative":12,"Senses":"Low-Light Vision, Perception +15","Languages":["Basic","Bocce"],"Unassigned Languages":0,"Reflex Defense":32,"Flat-Footed Defense":30,"Fortitude Defense":21,"Will Defense":27,"Hit Points":80,"Damage Threshold":21,"Speed":"4 Squares","Melee Weapons":"Lightsaber +14 (2d8+5)","Ranged Weapons":"Heavy Blaster Pistol +12 (3d8+5)","Base Attack Bonus":10,"Grapple":12,"Attack Options":["Weapon Finesse"],"Special Actions":["Hunter's Mark"],"Force Powers":["Battle Strike","Force Slam","Mind Trick","Rebuke"],"Force Secrets":[],"Force Techniques":["Force Techniques : Improved Move Light Object"],"Strength":10,"Dexterity":14,"Constitution":10,"Intelligence":12,"Wisdom":16,"Charisma":14,"Talents":["Talents : Acute Senses","Armored Defense","Block","Deflect","Elusive Target","Hunter's Mark","Improved Initiative"],"Feats":["Feats : Armor Proficiency (Light)","Armor Proficiency (Medium)","Force Sensitivity","Force Training","Improved Defenses","Skill Focus (Use the Force)","Skill Training (Survival)","Weapon Finesse","Weapon Focus (Lightsabers)","Weapon Proficiency (Lightsabers)","Weapon Proficiency (Lightsabers)","Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)"],"Skills":["Skills : Initiative","must take second result)","Perception","must take second result)","Pilot","Survival","Use the Force"],"Trained Skills":["Skills : Initiative","must take second result)","Perception","must take second result)","Pilot","Survival","Use the Force"],"Species Traits":[],"Gear":"Imperial Knight Armor with Helmet Package (+8 Reflex , +2 Fortitude ; +2 Perception , Low-light Vision), Heavy Blaster Pistol , Lightsaber ( Self-Built ), Comlink (Short-Range), Various Personal Belongings"},"mode":"play","sourcePack":"heroic","sourceAuthority":"statblock","playReady":true,"normalizedForPlay":true,"playNormalizationVersion":1}}}}
{"_id":"4bb916eb183ae933","name":"Quinlan Vos","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"isDroid":false,"droidDegree":"","attributes":{"str":{"base":14,"racial":0,"enhancement":0,"temp":0},"dex":{"base":13,"racial":0,"enhancement":0,"temp":0},"con":{"base":14,"racial":0,"enhancement":0,"temp":0},"int":{"base":12,"racial":0,"enhancement":0,"temp":0},"wis":{"base":15,"racial":0,"enhancement":0,"temp":0},"cha":{"base":14,"racial":0,"enhancement":0,"temp":0}},"skills":{"acrobatics":{"trained":true,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"dex","favorite":false},"climb":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"str","favorite":false},"deception":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"cha","favorite":false},"endurance":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"con","favorite":false},"gatherInformation":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"cha","favorite":false},"initiative":{"trained":true,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"dex","favorite":false},"jump":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"str","favorite":false},"knowledgeBureaucracy":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"int","favorite":false},"knowledgeGalacticLore":{"trained":true,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"int","favorite":false},"knowledgeLifeSciences":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"int","favorite":false},"knowledgePhysicalSciences":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"int","favorite":false},"knowledgeSocialSciences":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"int","favorite":false},"knowledgeTactics":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"int","favorite":false},"knowledgeTechnology":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"int","favorite":false},"mechanics":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"int","favorite":false},"perception":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"wis","favorite":false},"persuasion":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"cha","favorite":false},"pilot":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"dex","favorite":false},"ride":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"dex","favorite":false},"stealth":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"dex","favorite":false},"survival":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"wis","favorite":false},"swim":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"str","favorite":false},"treatInjury":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"wis","favorite":false},"useComputer":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"int","favorite":false},"useTheForce":{"trained":true,"focused":true,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"cha","favorite":false}},"hp":{"value":114,"max":114,"temp":0,"bonus":0},"conditionTrack":{"current":0,"persistent":false,"penalty":0},"level":12,"size":"medium","speed":6,"defenses":{"reflex":{"total":25,"armor":0,"classBonus":0,"misc":{"auto":{},"user":{}},"ability":"dex","source":"level","level":0},"fort":{"total":26,"classBonus":0,"misc":{"auto":{},"user":{}},"ability":"con","level":0},"will":{"total":26,"classBonus":0,"misc":{"auto":{},"user":{}},"ability":"wis","level":0},"flatFooted":{"total":24}},"languages":["Basic","Ryl"],"destinyPoints":{"value":2,"max":2},"forcePoints":{"value":6,"max":6,"die":"1d6"},"darkSideScore":7,"damageThreshold":26,"bab":12,"race":"Near-Human","class":"Jedi 7 / Knight 5","className":"Jedi 7 / Knight 5","biography":"<p><strong>Gear:</strong> Lightsaber ( Self-Built ), Jedi Robes</p>\n<p><strong>Senses:</strong> Improved Sense Force , Use the Force +18</p>\n<p><strong>Attack Options:</strong> Rapid Strike, Triple Crit (Lightsabers)</p>\n<p><strong>Special Actions:</strong> Psychometry</p>","derived":{},"npcProfile":{"kind":"heroic","mode":"play","sourceAuthority":"statblock","legalProfile":"heroic","legalState":"unchecked","importMode":"play","playReady":true,"statblockAuthority":true,"sourcePack":"heroic","normalizationVersion":1,"authority":{"hp":"statblock","defenses":"statblock","bab":"statblock","attacks":"statblock","skills":"statblock","damageThreshold":"statblock"}}},"items":[{"_id":"3033bc88b244be49","name":"Near-Human","type":"species","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"size":"Medium","speed":6,"abilities":"None","skillBonuses":[],"special":["Genetic Drift"],"languages":["Basic"],"source":"Multiple","description":"","tags":[],"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":8600,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.species.species-near-human"}}},{"_id":"59c3085f7c7b7900","name":"Combat Reflexes","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"You may make a number of attacks of opportunity per round equal to your Dexterity modifier.","prerequisite":"Dex 13","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":85,"tags":["feat-chain","non-force","scout","soldier","sustained-damage"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier","Scout"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{"value":"Gain additional <a href=\"/wiki/Attacks_of_Opportunity\" title=\"Attacks of Opportunity\">Attacks of Opportunity</a>."}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.7146640744fdf052"}}},{"_id":"33df1033574c6056","name":"Force Sensitivity","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"You can make Use the Force checks and gain access to Force Talents.","prerequisite":"Non-Droid","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":86,"tags":["feat-chain","force"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{"value":"You can make <a href=\"/wiki/Use_the_Force\" title=\"Use the Force\">Use the Force</a> checks and gain access to <a href=\"/wiki/Force_Talents\" title=\"Force Talents\">Force Talents</a>."}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.ddbeb23013d9e917"}}},{"_id":"7895936e03f6ecd6","name":"Force Training","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"You learn a number of Force powers equal to 1 + your Wisdom modifier.","prerequisite":"Force Sensitivity, Trained in Use the Force","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":94,"tags":["feat-chain","force","jedi","striker"],"bonus_feat_for":["Jedi"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"forcePowerGrants":1,"description":{"value":"Learn a number of <a href=\"/wiki/Force_Powers\" title=\"Force Powers\">Force Powers</a> equal to 1 + your <a href=\"/wiki/Wisdom\" title=\"Wisdom\">Wisdom</a> modifier (minimum 1)."},"prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"skillTrained","skill":"usetheforce"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"}},"effects":[{"_id":"d1c60a9b-78e6-4601-85a4-320794fa5a91","name":"Force Training","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Force Training","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Force Training"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.9b7b869a86f39190"}}},{"_id":"0dbcdd3b36e40f3d","name":"Rapid Strike","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"When making a full attack with a melee weapon, you may make one additional attack. All attacks take a -2 penalty.","prerequisite":"Dex 13","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":88,"tags":["feat-chain","melee","non-force","soldier"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{"value":"Take a -2 penalty on a melee attack roll to deal +1 die of damage."},"prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"bab","min":1}],"_source":"canonical-csv"}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.ccb33e58342499a3"}}},{"_id":"6f085e3acd4f97c5","name":"Running Attack","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"You may make a single melee or ranged attack at any point during a move action taken on your turn.","prerequisite":"Dex 13","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":88,"tags":["action-economy","controller","feat-chain","melee","mobility","non-force","positioning","ranged","scout","soldier"],"bonus_feat_for":["Scout","Soldier"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{"value":"Move before and after making an attack."},"prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"attribute","ability":"dex","min":13}],"_source":"canonical-csv"}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.4d6a68d553fb0449"}}},{"_id":"1c2f0ab2f58d47b4","name":"Skill Focus","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"You gain a +5 bonus on all checks with the selected skill.","prerequisite":"Trained in the chosen skill","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":88,"tags":["feat-chain","noble","non-force","scoundrel","striker"],"bonus_feat_for":["Noble","Scoundrel"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{"value":"Gain +5 competence bonus on <a href=\"/wiki/Skill_Checks\" title=\"Skill Checks\">Skill Checks</a> with one <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Trained_Skill\" title=\"Trained Skill\">Trained Skill</a>."}},"effects":[{"name":"Skill Focus","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.skills.perception.miscMod","mode":2,"value":"5","priority":20}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"transfer":true,"flags":{"swse":{"type":"skill-bonus","skill":"43c5941072ec78af","source":"Skill Focus"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.1592aaedf4b6e40a"}}},{"_id":"fd8009ab0bacbe4f","name":"Triple Crit","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"When you score a critical hit with the selected weapon group, you deal triple damage instead of double.","prerequisite":"Weapon Focus with selected weapon group, base attack bonus +12","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Galaxy at War","page":27,"tags":["feat-chain","non-force","precision","soldier","striker"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{"value":"Deal triple damage on a <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Critical_Hit\" title=\"Critical Hit\">Critical Hit</a>."},"prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"bab","min":8}],"_source":"canonical-csv"}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.3d4a4e93ced26712"}}},{"_id":"488af66e210b4038","name":"Weapon Focus","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"You gain a +1 bonus on attack rolls with the selected weapon group.","prerequisite":"Proficient with selected weapon group","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":88,"tags":["feat-chain","non-force","soldier","striker"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{"value":"+1 bonus on attack rolls with chosen weapon."}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.c41814601364b643"}}},{"_id":"c678272235cb1bfb","name":"Weapon Proficiency","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"Ignore -5 penalty on attack rolls with weapons of a particular type.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["non-force"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{"value":"Ignore -5 penalty on attack rolls with weapons of a particular type."}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.ecc2471ac96ec2d4"}}},{"_id":"7783e97d27a61775","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"You are proficient with simple weapons and do not take the -5 penalty when using them.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["noble","non-force","scoundrel","scout","soldier"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier","Scout","Scoundrel","Noble"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{}},"effects":[{"_id":"220daaa7-e1b5-440d-98cd-10f5e586ef8b","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.2d680cc46a7972da"}}},{"_id":"77d717a1895aa789","name":"Force Point Recovery","type":"feat","img":"systems/foundryvtt-swse/assets/icons/force-technique.png","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"At the end of an encounter, you automatically recover 1 Force Point spent during the encounter.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Core","page":0,"tags":["force-technique"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"description":"<p>At the end of an encounter, you automatically recover 1 Force Point spent during the encounter.</p>","relatedPower":""},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcetechniques.056ab39b3ab9df10"}}},{"_id":"3988aa67aac79726","name":"Improved Sense Force","type":"feat","img":"systems/foundryvtt-swse/assets/icons/force-technique.png","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"You may use the Sense Force ability of the Use the Force Skill as a Move Action rather than a Full-Round Action.","prerequisite":"Sense Force","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Core","page":0,"tags":["force-technique"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"description":"<p>You may use the Sense Force ability of the Use the Force Skill as a Move Action rather than a Full-Round Action.</p><p><strong>Related Power:</strong> Sense Force</p><p><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Sense Force</p>","relatedPower":"Sense Force"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcetechniques.ad67b8f3959860f2"}}},{"_id":"d38690c8303ddf6e","name":"Block","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Sith Alchemy","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Create Sith Amulet: You can create a Sith Amulet. The creation of a Sith Amulet requires 25,000 credits' worth of gems and other raw materials, and the creation process takes 1 week (this work can be spread out over several sessions and need not be consecutive). At the end of the process, you must spend a Force Point to complete the Sith Amulet, after which point it functions exactly as a Sith Amulet. Create Sith Armor: You can transform a suit of normal Battle Armor into the Dark Armor worn by Sith Lords. You must have a suit of Battle Armor to transform into the Dark Armor (Light Battle Armor becomes Light Dark Armor, Battle Armor becomes Dark Armor, and Heavy Battle Armor becomes Heavy Dark Armor). The transformation process takes 1 day for Light Dark Armor, 2 days for Dark Armor, and 3 days for Heavy Dark Armor. You must spend a Force Point at the end of the creation process to complete the Armor's transformation. Create Sith Talisman: You can spend a Force Point to imbue a portable object with the Dark Side, creating a Sith Talisman that provides offensive strength to a Force Power. Creating the Sith Talisman takes a Full-Round Action. While you wear or carry the Sith Talisman on your person, you add 1d6 to your damage with Force Powers. You increase your Dark Side Score by 1 when you first wear or carry a Sith Talisman. You can have only one Sith Talisman active at any given time, and if it is destroyed, you cannot create another one for 24 hours. Create Sith Weapon: You can alchemically treat a Simple Weapon (Melee) or an Advanced Melee Weapon, turning it into a Sith Weapon. You must spend a Force Point and spend 1 hour imbuing the Weapon with the properties of a Sith Alchemical Weapon (see also: Sith Alchemical Weapon Template). A Lightsaber does not ignore the Sith Weapon's DR, and characters who are proficient in the Weapon's use can treat it as a Lightsaber for the purposes of the , Deflect, and Redirect Shot Talents (and any Talents that have these Talents as a prerequisite). Additionally, as a Swift Action, the wielder of a Sith Weapon can spend a Force Point to gain a bonus equal to their Dark Side Score to the damage of their next attack made with the Weapon before the end of the encounter. This increases the wielder's Dark Side Score by 1.","description":"Create Sith Amulet: You can create a Sith Amulet. The creation of a Sith Amulet requires 25,000 credits' worth of gems and other raw materials, and the creation process takes 1 week (this work can be spread out over several sessions and need not be consecutive). At the end of the process, you must spend a Force Point to complete the Sith Amulet, after which point it functions exactly as a Sith Amulet. Create Sith Armor: You can transform a suit of normal Battle Armor into the Dark Armor worn by Sith Lords. You must have a suit of Battle Armor to transform into the Dark Armor (Light Battle Armor becomes Light Dark Armor, Battle Armor becomes Dark Armor, and Heavy Battle Armor becomes Heavy Dark Armor). The transformation process takes 1 day for Light Dark Armor, 2 days for Dark Armor, and 3 days for Heavy Dark Armor. You must spend a Force Point at the end of the creation process to complete the Armor's transformation. Create Sith Talisman: You can spend a Force Point to imbue a portable object with the Dark Side, creating a Sith Talisman that provides offensive strength to a Force Power. Creating the Sith Talisman takes a Full-Round Action. While you wear or carry the Sith Talisman on your person, you add 1d6 to your damage with Force Powers. You increase your Dark Side Score by 1 when you first wear or carry a Sith Talisman. You can have only one Sith Talisman active at any given time, and if it is destroyed, you cannot create another one for 24 hours. Create Sith Weapon: You can alchemically treat a Simple Weapon (Melee) or an Advanced Melee Weapon, turning it into a Sith Weapon. You must spend a Force Point and spend 1 hour imbuing the Weapon with the properties of a Sith Alchemical Weapon (see also: Sith Alchemical Weapon Template). A Lightsaber does not ignore the Sith Weapon's DR, and characters who are proficient in the Weapon's use can treat it as a Lightsaber for the purposes of the , Deflect, and Redirect Shot Talents (and any Talents that have these Talents as a prerequisite). Additionally, as a Swift Action, the wielder of a Sith Weapon can spend a Force Point to gain a bonus equal to their Dark Side Score to the damage of their next attack made with the Weapon before the end of the encounter. This increases the wielder's Dark Side Score by 1.","class":"Jedi","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","tree":"Sith Alchemy","treeId":"a67faf2ae089ab5d","tags":["action-economy","armor","dark-side","defender","force","force-offense","jedi","lightsaber","melee","mobility","ranged","striker","support","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.block"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.9379daa94a228c04"}}},{"_id":"9d08ac6813bb2534","name":"Dark Side Sense","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Jedi Sentinel","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Against creatures with a Dark Side Score of 1 or higher, you deal extra damage on melee attacks equal to your Charisma bonus (minimum +1). Prerequisite: You gain a +5 Force bonus to all Defense scores against Force Powers with the [Dark Side] descriptor, and Force Powers originating from any dark Force-user (that is, any Force-use whose Dark Side Score equals their Wisdom score). Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide When you interact with another sentient creature, you can use a Swift Action to reduce the impression you leave on it. When you have finished interacting with the creature, you make a Use the Force check, and if the check result exceeds the target's Will Defense, it does not remember interacting with you once you are gone. A target that is higher in level than you gains a +5 bonus to its Will Defense to resist this ability. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide Prerequisite: When you use a damage-dealing Force Power against a creature with a Dark Side Score of 1 or higher, you deal extra damage on a successful hit equal to your Charisma bonus (minimum +1). Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Rebellion Era Campaign Guide If you take damage from the use of a Force Power, until the end of the encounter you gain a +2 Force bonus to all Defenses against that Force Power. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual You gain a +1 Force bonus on attack rolls and deal +1 die of damage on Lightsaber attacks made against a Beast with a Dark Side Score of 1+. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy","description":"Against creatures with a Dark Side Score of 1 or higher, you deal extra damage on melee attacks equal to your Charisma bonus (minimum +1). Prerequisite: You gain a +5 Force bonus to all Defense scores against Force Powers with the [Dark Side] descriptor, and Force Powers originating from any dark Force-user (that is, any Force-use whose Dark Side Score equals their Wisdom score). Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide When you interact with another sentient creature, you can use a Swift Action to reduce the impression you leave on it. When you have finished interacting with the creature, you make a Use the Force check, and if the check result exceeds the target's Will Defense, it does not remember interacting with you once you are gone. A target that is higher in level than you gains a +5 bonus to its Will Defense to resist this ability. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide Prerequisite: When you use a damage-dealing Force Power against a creature with a Dark Side Score of 1 or higher, you deal extra damage on a successful hit equal to your Charisma bonus (minimum +1). Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Rebellion Era Campaign Guide If you take damage from the use of a Force Power, until the end of the encounter you gain a +2 Force bonus to all Defenses against that Force Power. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual You gain a +1 Force bonus on attack rolls and deal +1 die of damage on Lightsaber attacks made against a Beast with a Dark Side Score of 1+. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy","class":"Jedi","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","tree":"Jedi Sentinel","treeId":"36f18f3e974feb33","tags":["action-economy","damage-reduction","dark-side","defender","force","force-defense","force-offense","jedi","light-side","lightsaber","melee","mobility","striker"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.dark_side_sense"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.e885f64758f5e2bd"}}},{"_id":"2527b428f8e9be18","name":"Deflect","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Lightsaber Forms","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Redirect Shot","description":"Redirect Shot","class":"Jedi","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","tree":"Lightsaber Forms","treeId":"2bc2572e852832e4","tags":["jedi","lightsaber","melee","ranged"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.deflect"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.72c644f7a09b1186"}}},{"_id":"9228e32db8227d70","name":"Force Perception","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Sense","prerequisites":"","benefit":"You may spend a Force Point to reroll an Initiative check, keeping the better of the two rolls. Additionally, if you roll a natural 20 on the Initiative check reroll, you immediately regain the Force Point spent to activate this talent. Prerequisite: By focusing on a specific creature in your line of sight, you can gauge how strong in The Force they are. This takes a Standard Action and requires a Use the Force check. If your check result meets or beats the target's Will Defense, you know whether or not they have the Force Sensitivity feat, you know how many Force Powers they know (but not which ones specifically), and you know how many Force Points they currently have. Prerequisites: , Farseeing See also: On the Force, Visions, and Discretion Whenever you use the Farseeing Force Power, you can spend a Force Point as a Swift Action to see into the target's past or future instead of the present. You declare how far into the target's past or future you wish to look, up to a maximum of 1 year per your Character Level. Any information gained about a target's future is subject to change, depending on whether steps are taken to alter that future. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide As a Standard Action, you can spend a Force Point to ignore all Concealment for 1 minute. Prerequisites: , Farseeing As a Swift Action, you can peer into the future in search of signs of danger, removing one use of the Farseeing Force Power from your active Force Power Suite (as though you had just activated the Force Power). Any time before the end of your next turn when you are the target of an attack or Force Power, you can force your attacker to reroll the attack roll (or Use the Force check) against you, keeping the second result. This counts as using the Farseeing Force Power against the attacker, but this Talent replaces the normal rules and effect of that Force Power. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide Prerequisites: , Farseeing When you use the Farseeing Force Power, you can choose to target an object you hold instead of a character or creature. You can look into the targeted item's past, up to a maximum of 5 years per your Character Level. Any information gained about the object's past is based on the thoughts and emotions of the person holding or carrying the object at the time you perceive, which can skew the results of the vision. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide You can spend a Force Point to gain Low-Light Vision (see Visibility) for 1 minute or until the end of the encounter, whichever is longer. Homebrew Reference Book: Clone Wars Saga Edition Fan Sourcebook - Jedi Padawans Prerequisites: Once per encounter, you may spend a Force Point to gain a +1 insight bonus to your Reflex Defense and Will Defense for the remainder of the encounter, or until you are knocked unconscious.","description":"You may spend a Force Point to reroll an Initiative check, keeping the better of the two rolls. Additionally, if you roll a natural 20 on the Initiative check reroll, you immediately regain the Force Point spent to activate this talent. Prerequisite: By focusing on a specific creature in your line of sight, you can gauge how strong in The Force they are. This takes a Standard Action and requires a Use the Force check. If your check result meets or beats the target's Will Defense, you know whether or not they have the Force Sensitivity feat, you know how many Force Powers they know (but not which ones specifically), and you know how many Force Points they currently have. Prerequisites: , Farseeing See also: On the Force, Visions, and Discretion Whenever you use the Farseeing Force Power, you can spend a Force Point as a Swift Action to see into the target's past or future instead of the present. You declare how far into the target's past or future you wish to look, up to a maximum of 1 year per your Character Level. Any information gained about a target's future is subject to change, depending on whether steps are taken to alter that future. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide As a Standard Action, you can spend a Force Point to ignore all Concealment for 1 minute. Prerequisites: , Farseeing As a Swift Action, you can peer into the future in search of signs of danger, removing one use of the Farseeing Force Power from your active Force Power Suite (as though you had just activated the Force Power). Any time before the end of your next turn when you are the target of an attack or Force Power, you can force your attacker to reroll the attack roll (or Use the Force check) against you, keeping the second result. This counts as using the Farseeing Force Power against the attacker, but this Talent replaces the normal rules and effect of that Force Power. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide Prerequisites: , Farseeing When you use the Farseeing Force Power, you can choose to target an object you hold instead of a character or creature. You can look into the targeted item's past, up to a maximum of 5 years per your Character Level. Any information gained about the object's past is based on the thoughts and emotions of the person holding or carrying the object at the time you perceive, which can skew the results of the vision. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide You can spend a Force Point to gain Low-Light Vision (see Visibility) for 1 minute or until the end of the encounter, whichever is longer. Homebrew Reference Book: Clone Wars Saga Edition Fan Sourcebook - Jedi Padawans Prerequisites: Once per encounter, you may spend a Force Point to gain a +1 insight bonus to your Reflex Defense and Will Defense for the remainder of the encounter, or until you are knocked unconscious.","costNumeric":null,"tree":"Sense","treeId":"d6b4331c0e31f7e3","tags":["action-economy","defender","force","force-defense","force-offense","light-side","mobility","scout","skills","stealth","striker","support"]},"effects":[{"name":"Force Perception (Trained)","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.skills.perception.trained","mode":5,"value":"true"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Force Perception","effectType":"skill-trained"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.force_perception"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.a358402a9fc26c02"}}},{"_id":"8793bfffef1022a6","name":"Lightsaber Defense","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Lightsaber Forms","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Niman When you use the Talent, you gain twice the normal deflection bonus to your Reflex Defense when you are wielding two Lightsabers. Prerequisite: When wielding a single Lightsaber in one hand, the deflection bonus you gain from the Talent increases by 2 (to a maximum of +5). When wielding a Lightsaber, you gain a +1 bonus to your Reflex Defense and Will Defense.","description":"Niman When you use the Talent, you gain twice the normal deflection bonus to your Reflex Defense when you are wielding two Lightsabers. Prerequisite: When wielding a single Lightsaber in one hand, the deflection bonus you gain from the Talent increases by 2 (to a maximum of +5). When wielding a Lightsaber, you gain a +1 bonus to your Reflex Defense and Will Defense.","class":"Jedi","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","tree":"Lightsaber Forms","treeId":"2bc2572e852832e4","tags":["defender","jedi","lightsaber","melee","striker"]},"effects":[{"_id":"fcdbf882-923a-4095-b0df-a1079c214099","name":"Lightsaber Defense","icon":"icons/svg/shield.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.defenses.reflex.misc","mode":2,"value":"1","priority":20}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Lightsaber Defense"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.lightsaber_defense"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.e8bf1222fd6289e4"}}},{"_id":"9f6ff62272ad2742","name":"Psychometry","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Sense","prerequisites":"Farseeing, Force Perception","benefit":"Target an object you hold; read impressions up to 5 years per level.","description":"Read impressions from an object you hold, seeing events from the past.","costNumeric":null,"tree":"Sense","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.force_perception"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"d6b4331c0e31f7e3","tags":["feat-chain","force","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.psychometry"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.8ff0ec89e13b6d51"}}},{"_id":"7caa950385ef5e6e","name":"Weapon Specialization (Lightsabers)","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Duelist","tree":"Duelist","prerequisites":"","description":"Greater Weapon Focus (Lightsabers) You gain a +2 bonus on melee damage rolls with Lightsabers. This bonus stacks with the bonus granted by the Talent. Whenever you make multiple attacks with any type of Lightsaber as part of a Full Attack, you reduce the penalty on your attack rolls by 2. You can take this Talent multiple times; each time you take this Talent, you reduce the penalty on your attack rolls by an additional 2. See also: Maiming Foes When you deal damage with a Lightsaber that is equal to or greater than both the target's current Hit Points and the target's Damage Threshold (that is, when you would deal enough damage to kill your target), you may choose to use this Talent. Instead of dealing full damage, you instead deal half damage to your target and move it -1 step on the Condition Track. In addition, you sever one of your target's arms at the wrist or elbow joint, or one of the target's legs at the knee or ankle joint (your choice). Severing part of an arm prevents the target from wielding weapons or using tools in that hand, and imposes a -5 penalty on Skill Checks and Ability Checks keyed to Strength and Dexterity. Severing part of a leg knocks the target Prone, reduces the target's Speed by half, reduces its Carrying Capacity by half, and imposes a -5 penalty on Skill Checks and Ability Checks keyed to Strength and Dexterity. Because of the severity of such an injury, losing part of a limb causes a Persistent Condition that can only be removed by having Surgery successfully performed on you. A Cybernetic Prosthesis negates these reductions and penalties. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","benefit":"Greater Weapon Focus (Lightsabers) You gain a +2 bonus on melee damage rolls with Lightsabers. This bonus stacks with the bonus granted by the Talent. Whenever you make multiple attacks with any type of Lightsaber as part of a Full Attack, you reduce the penalty on your attack rolls by 2. You can take this Talent multiple times; each time you take this Talent, you reduce the penalty on your attack rolls by an additional 2. See also: Maiming Foes When you deal damage with a Lightsaber that is equal to or greater than both the target's current Hit Points and the target's Damage Threshold (that is, when you would deal enough damage to kill your target), you may choose to use this Talent. Instead of dealing full damage, you instead deal half damage to your target and move it -1 step on the Condition Track. In addition, you sever one of your target's arms at the wrist or elbow joint, or one of the target's legs at the knee or ankle joint (your choice). Severing part of an arm prevents the target from wielding weapons or using tools in that hand, and imposes a -5 penalty on Skill Checks and Ability Checks keyed to Strength and Dexterity. Severing part of a leg knocks the target Prone, reduces the target's Speed by half, reduces its Carrying Capacity by half, and imposes a -5 penalty on Skill Checks and Ability Checks keyed to Strength and Dexterity. Because of the severity of such an injury, losing part of a limb causes a Persistent Condition that can only be removed by having Surgery successfully performed on you. A Cybernetic Prosthesis negates these reductions and penalties. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"b3c5d90b5036f39b","tags":["burst-damage","condition-removal","controller","damage-reduction","defender","force","force-control","force-offense","leader","lightsaber","melee","mobility","scaling","striker","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.00a9210772a64a19"}}},{"_id":"dabe7e690aad3520","name":"Battle Strike","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"telekinetic","useTheForce":15,"time":"Swift Action","range":"Personal","target":"You","duration":"1 round","effect":"<p>You channel the Force to enhance your next melee attack. Your next melee attack this round gains a +1d6 bonus to damage.</p>","special":"<p>This bonus damage is Force damage and bypasses Damage Reduction.</p>","descriptor":["Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":94,"tags":["enhancement","damage","melee"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.f177dc6d65f76de9"}}},{"_id":"51db9a84b90e8d58","name":"Dark Rage","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/eye.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"Unknown","useTheForce":"","time":"standard","range":"","target":"","duration":"","effect":"","special":"","descriptor":"","dcChart":"","maintainable":false,"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1,"perDay":true}},"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"placeholder":true,"unresolved":"Dark Rage"}}},{"_id":"9f7a49b8cf5231a9","name":"Farseeing","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telepathic","useTheForce":20,"time":"1 minute","range":"Unlimited","target":"Special","duration":"Concentration","effect":"<p>You peer through the Force to see distant locations or events. You can observe a place you've been before or a person you know, regardless of distance.</p>","special":"<p>The GM may require additional checks for very distant or obscured visions.</p>","descriptor":["Mind-Affecting","Scrying"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":true,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":95,"tags":["utility","divination","scrying"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.0419ecb55f011f81"}}},{"_id":"d450145760f1e22e","name":"Force Lightning","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":4,"discipline":"dark-side","useTheForce":15,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One creature","duration":"Instantaneous","effect":"<p>You unleash devastating arcs of Force Lightning from your fingertips. The target takes lightning damage based on your Use the Force check result.</p>","special":"<p>This is a Dark Side power. Using it gains you a Dark Side Point.</p>","descriptor":["Dark Side","Force Lightning"],"dcChart":[{"dc":15,"effect":"2d6 lightning damage","description":"Target takes 2d6 lightning damage"},{"dc":20,"effect":"4d6 lightning damage","description":"Target takes 4d6 lightning damage"},{"dc":25,"effect":"6d6 lightning damage + stun","description":"Target takes 6d6 lightning damage and is stunned for 1 round"},{"dc":30,"effect":"8d6 lightning damage + stun 1d4","description":"Target takes 8d6 lightning damage and is stunned for 1d4 rounds"}],"maintainable":true,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":96,"tags":["attack","damage","dark-side","lightning"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.0a422b939edfad56"}}},{"_id":"af59e21b4f3135ed","name":"Force Slam","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telekinetic","useTheForce":20,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One creature or object","duration":"Instantaneous","effect":"<p>You use telekinetic force to violently slam your target against a surface. The target takes 4d6 damage and is knocked prone.</p>","special":"<p>The target must be within 6 squares of a solid surface (wall, floor, ceiling).</p>","descriptor":["Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":97,"tags":["attack","damage","telekinetic","prone"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.462a6c23e00c4dfc"}}},{"_id":"24459fca09fa1dcf","name":"Mind Trick","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"telepathic","useTheForce":15,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One creature","duration":"1 minute or until completed","effect":"<p>You influence a weak mind to believe what you tell them or follow a simple suggestion. The target must make a Will save (DC = your UTF check) or be affected.</p>","special":"<p>The suggestion must be reasonable and the target must be able to understand you.</p>","descriptor":["Mind-Affecting"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":98,"tags":["mind-control","suggestion","social"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.e6649f366d6c5737"}}},{"_id":"b9492c1bbe9bacdd","name":"Move Object","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telekinetic","useTheForce":15,"time":"Standard Action","range":"12 squares","target":"One object or creature","duration":"Concentration","effect":"<p>You move objects or creatures through the air using telekinesis. The maximum size/weight you can move depends on your Use the Force check result.</p>","special":"<p>Unwilling creatures can make a Will save (DC = your UTF check) to resist being moved.</p>","descriptor":["Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[{"dc":15,"effect":"Medium (50 kg)","description":"Move objects up to Medium size or 50 kg"},{"dc":20,"effect":"Large (250 kg)","description":"Move objects up to Large size or 250 kg"},{"dc":25,"effect":"Huge (1 ton)","description":"Move objects up to Huge size or 1 metric ton"},{"dc":30,"effect":"Gargantuan (5 tons)","description":"Move objects up to Gargantuan size or 5 metric tons"},{"dc":35,"effect":"Colossal (20 tons)","description":"Move objects up to Colossal size or 20 metric tons (starfighter-sized)"}],"maintainable":true,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":98,"tags":["telekinetic","movement","utility"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.289013a32bd179ad"}}},{"_id":"92ac9d68031ae2ae","name":"Rebuke","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telepathic","useTheForce":20,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One Force-sensitive creature","duration":"1 round","effect":"<p>You overwhelm a Force user with a powerful Force presence. If the target is Force-sensitive, they must make a Will save (DC = your UTF check) or be dazed for 1 round.</p>","special":"<p>This power only affects Force-sensitive creatures.</p>","descriptor":["Mind-Affecting"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":99,"tags":["debuff","force-user","daze"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.390074b44aedfa2a"}}},{"_id":"b64f8e1607ee99c4","name":"Unarmed","type":"weapon","img":"icons/svg/sword.svg","system":{"damage":"1d4+8","damageType":"kinetic","attackBonus":0,"attackAttribute":"str","range":"melee","weight":1,"cost":0,"equipped":true,"description":"","properties":[],"ammunition":{"type":"none","current":0,"max":0},"weaponCategory":"simple","proficiency":"simple","subcategory":""},"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"placeholder":true,"npc":{"flatAttackBonus":14,"flatDamageFormula":"1d4+8","useFlat":true}}}},{"_id":"50f3ef11539e3f01","name":"Lightsaber","type":"weapon","img":"icons/svg/sword.svg","system":{"damage":"2d8+10","damageType":"energy","attackBonus":0,"attackAttribute":"str","range":"melee","weight":1,"cost":12000,"equipped":true,"description":"<p>The elegant weapon of the Jedi and Sith. A blade of pure energy capable of cutting through nearly anything.</p>\n      <p><strong>Special:</strong> Ignores armor bonuses to Reflex Defense. Can deflect blaster bolts. Critical threat range 19-20. Requires exotic weapon proficiency.</p>","properties":["Lightsaber","Critical 19-20","Exotic","Armor-Piercing"],"ammunition":{"type":"none","current":0,"max":0},"weaponCategory":"melee","proficiency":"exotic","subcategory":"lightsaber","costNumeric":12000,"category":"lightsaber"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.weapons.weapon-lightsaber"},"swse":{"npc":{"flatAttackBonus":16,"flatDamageFormula":"2d8+10","useFlat":true}}}},{"_id":"bb562fc31d539599","name":"Lightsaber (with Rapid Strike)","type":"weapon","img":"icons/svg/sword.svg","system":{"damage":"3d8+10","damageType":"energy","attackBonus":0,"attackAttribute":"str","range":"melee","weight":1,"cost":12000,"equipped":true,"description":"<p>The elegant weapon of the Jedi and Sith. A blade of pure energy capable of cutting through nearly anything.</p>\n      <p><strong>Special:</strong> Ignores armor bonuses to Reflex Defense. Can deflect blaster bolts. Critical threat range 19-20. Requires exotic weapon proficiency.</p>","properties":["Lightsaber","Critical 19-20","Exotic","Armor-Piercing"],"ammunition":{"type":"none","current":0,"max":0},"weaponCategory":"melee","proficiency":"exotic","subcategory":"lightsaber","costNumeric":12000,"category":"lightsaber"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.weapons.weapon-lightsaber"},"swse":{"npc":{"flatAttackBonus":14,"flatDamageFormula":"3d8+10","useFlat":true}}}}],"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"import":{"source":"books","raw":{"Size":"Medium","Species":"Near-Human","Nonheroic Level":0,"Class Levels":{"Jedi":7,"Knight":5},"Destiny Points":2,"Force Points":6,"Dark Side Points":7,"Initiative":13,"Senses":"Improved Sense Force , Use the Force +18","Languages":["Basic","Ryl"],"Unassigned Languages":0,"Reflex Defense":25,"Flat-Footed Defense":24,"Fortitude Defense":26,"Will Defense":26,"Hit Points":114,"Damage Threshold":26,"Speed":"6 Squares; Running Attack","Melee Weapons":"Unarmed +14 (1d4+8), Lightsaber +16 (2d8+10), Lightsaber +14 (3d8+10) with Rapid Strike","Ranged Weapons":"By Weapon +13","Base Attack Bonus":12,"Grapple":14,"Attack Options":["Rapid Strike","Triple Crit (Lightsabers)"],"Special Actions":["Psychometry"],"Force Powers":["Battle Strike","Dark Rage","Farseeing","Force Lightning","Force Slam","Mind Trick","Move Object","Rebuke"],"Force Secrets":[],"Force Techniques":["Force Techniques : Force Point Recovery","Improved Sense Force"],"Strength":14,"Dexterity":13,"Constitution":14,"Intelligence":12,"Wisdom":15,"Charisma":14,"Talents":["Talents : Block","Dark Side Sense","Deflect","Force Perception","Lightsaber Defense","Psychometry","Weapon Specialization (Lightsabers)"],"Feats":["Feats : Combat Reflexes","Force Sensitivity","Force Training (3)","Rapid Strike","Running Attack","Skill Focus (Use the Force)","Triple Crit (Lightsabers)","Weapon Focus (Lightsabers)","Weapon Proficiency (Lightsabers)","Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)"],"Skills":["Skills : Acrobatics","Initiative","Knowledge (Galactic Lore)","Use the Force","may keep better result; may substitute for Perception checks)"],"Trained Skills":["Skills : Acrobatics","Initiative","Knowledge (Galactic Lore)","Use the Force","may keep better result; may substitute for Perception checks)"],"Species Traits":[],"Gear":"Lightsaber ( Self-Built ), Jedi Robes"},"mode":"play","sourcePack":"heroic","sourceAuthority":"statblock","playReady":true,"normalizedForPlay":true,"playNormalizationVersion":1}}}}
{"_id":"4c752b53f8849b80","name":"Haden Vazzar","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"isDroid":false,"droidDegree":"","attributes":{"str":{"base":13,"racial":0,"enhancement":0,"temp":0},"dex":{"base":14,"racial":0,"enhancement":0,"temp":0},"con":{"base":14,"racial":0,"enhancement":0,"temp":0},"int":{"base":10,"racial":0,"enhancement":0,"temp":0},"wis":{"base":16,"racial":0,"enhancement":0,"temp":0},"cha":{"base":10,"racial":0,"enhancement":0,"temp":0}},"skills":{"acrobatics":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"dex","favorite":false},"climb":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"str","favorite":false},"deception":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"cha","favorite":false},"endurance":{"trained":true,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"con","favorite":false},"gatherInformation":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"cha","favorite":false},"initiative":{"trained":true,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"dex","favorite":false},"jump":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"str","favorite":false},"knowledgeBureaucracy":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"int","favorite":false},"knowledgeGalacticLore":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"int","favorite":false},"knowledgeLifeSciences":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"int","favorite":false},"knowledgePhysicalSciences":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"int","favorite":false},"knowledgeSocialSciences":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"int","favorite":false},"knowledgeTactics":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"int","favorite":false},"knowledgeTechnology":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"int","favorite":false},"mechanics":{"trained":true,"focused":false,"m