:{"featType":"general","benefit":"You are proficient with pistols and do not take the -5 penalty when using them.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["non-force","ranged","scoundrel","scout","soldier"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier","Scout","Scoundrel"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{}},"effects":[{"_id":"04733e85-193e-4f4b-8792-c359083557d1","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Pistols)","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Weapon Proficiency (Pistols)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Pistols)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.e5d361d01d1b44e4"}}},{"_id":"40a175ed78f699c5","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"You are proficient with simple weapons and do not take the -5 penalty when using them.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["noble","non-force","scoundrel","scout","soldier"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier","Scout","Scoundrel","Noble"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{}},"effects":[{"_id":"220daaa7-e1b5-440d-98cd-10f5e586ef8b","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.2d680cc46a7972da"}}},{"_id":"6fdc34976d806c93","name":"Assault Tactics","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Military Tactics","prerequisites":"Trained in Initiative","benefit":"You can use the , Deployment Tactics, or Field Tactics Talent as a Swift Action, instead of a Move Action (provided you have the Talent in question). Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions During the first round of combat in an encounter (after the Surprise Round, if any), you can take your turn before any of your allies, but you must use either the Share Talent Prestige Class ability or a Talent from one of the following Talent Trees as part of your turn: Commando Talent Tree, Leadership Talent Tree, or Military Tactics Talent Tree. On the subsequent round, you return to your normal place in the Initiative Order. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide Prerequisite: When you use the Talent on an enemy, the target takes a cumulative -1 penalty to its Reflex Defense each time it is damaged by one of your allies (maximum -5 penalty). This penalty applies until the end of your next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide As a Swift Action, once per encounter, you can grant bonus Hit Points equal to 5 + one-half your Character Level to allies within 20 squares of you and in your line of sight. Damage is subtracted from the bonus Hit Points first, and any bonus Hit Points remaining at the end of the encounter go away. Bonus Hit Points from multiple sources do not stack. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions Your tactics confuse enemy commanders and tacticians that can see or otherwise observe your forces in action, such as when using sensors. After using the Share Talent special quality, make a Knowledge (Tactics) check as a Free Action. The result replaces the DC of any Talents that use Knowledge (Tactics) from the Military Tactics Talent Tree used against your or your allies. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions If you have already used a Talent in an encounter before granting the same Talent to an ally with your Share Talent special quality in the same encounter, any character who benefits from Share Talent gains one of the following bonuses when using that talent (if the Talent can be affected by more than one effect, the character using the Talent selects the desired effect): Reduce the Talent's DC by 5. Gain an additional +2 bonus to any bonus to attack, Defense, or damage used by the Talent. Reduce the amount of damage taken by the character through the use of the Talent by 10 points. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions","description":"You can use the , Deployment Tactics, or Field Tactics Talent as a Swift Action, instead of a Move Action (provided you have the Talent in question). Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions During the first round of combat in an encounter (after the Surprise Round, if any), you can take your turn before any of your allies, but you must use either the Share Talent Prestige Class ability or a Talent from one of the following Talent Trees as part of your turn: Commando Talent Tree, Leadership Talent Tree, or Military Tactics Talent Tree. On the subsequent round, you return to your normal place in the Initiative Order. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide Prerequisite: When you use the Talent on an enemy, the target takes a cumulative -1 penalty to its Reflex Defense each time it is damaged by one of your allies (maximum -5 penalty). This penalty applies until the end of your next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide As a Swift Action, once per encounter, you can grant bonus Hit Points equal to 5 + one-half your Character Level to allies within 20 squares of you and in your line of sight. Damage is subtracted from the bonus Hit Points first, and any bonus Hit Points remaining at the end of the encounter go away. Bonus Hit Points from multiple sources do not stack. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions Your tactics confuse enemy commanders and tacticians that can see or otherwise observe your forces in action, such as when using sensors. After using the Share Talent special quality, make a Knowledge (Tactics) check as a Free Action. The result replaces the DC of any Talents that use Knowledge (Tactics) from the Military Tactics Talent Tree used against your or your allies. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions If you have already used a Talent in an encounter before granting the same Talent to an ally with your Share Talent special quality in the same encounter, any character who benefits from Share Talent gains one of the following bonuses when using that talent (if the Talent can be affected by more than one effect, the character using the Talent selects the desired effect): Reduce the Talent's DC by 5. Gain an additional +2 bonus to any bonus to attack, Defense, or damage used by the Talent. Reduce the amount of damage taken by the character through the use of the Talent by 10 points. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions","class":"Officer","costNumeric":null,"category":"Officer","tree":"Military Tactics","treeId":"9253ace716c3e966","tags":["action-economy","ambush","controller","damage-reduction","defender","feat-chain","force","force-control","force-defense","force-offense","leader","leadership","mobility","positioning","scaling","scout","skills","striker","support","sustained-damage","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.assault_tactics"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.d9fe8a0c76d845d4"}}},{"_id":"9b765f065591c9b7","name":"Born Leader","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Naval Officer","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Prerequisites: Charisma 13, Intelligence 13, When you are the Commander of a Capital Ship, calculate its Reflex Defense using your Heroic Level plus one-half the ship's armor bonus (rounded down), the Pilot's Heroic Level, or the ship's Armor bonus, whichever is highest. In addition, all Gunners on your ship add one-half your Heroic Level, or one-half their Heroic Level, whichever is more, to damage rolls with Vehicle Weapons. Finally, you treat any generic crew as being one quality level higher (maximum of Ace, see Crew Quality).","description":"Prerequisites: Charisma 13, Intelligence 13, When you are the Commander of a Capital Ship, calculate its Reflex Defense using your Heroic Level plus one-half the ship's armor bonus (rounded down), the Pilot's Heroic Level, or the ship's Armor bonus, whichever is highest. In addition, all Gunners on your ship add one-half your Heroic Level, or one-half their Heroic Level, whichever is more, to damage rolls with Vehicle Weapons. Finally, you treat any generic crew as being one quality level higher (maximum of Ace, see Crew Quality).","class":"Noble","costNumeric":null,"category":"Noble","tree":"Naval Officer","treeId":"057a978a7dc1d5a7","tags":["armor","defender","noble","striker","support","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[{"_id":"f9275c38-3cb5-4ab3-aaa5-25e5722dcdd3","name":"Born Leader","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.defenses.will","mode":2,"value":"1"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Born Leader"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.born_leader"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.6a66ba6e0834dd6f"}}},{"_id":"44ea85b3d2875f4b","name":"Deployment Tactics","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Military Tactics","prerequisites":"","benefit":"You know how to use existing terrain to your best advantage. By using a Move Action, you can make a DC 15 Knowledge (Tactics) check. If the check succeeds, you and all allies within 10 squares of you can use whatever Cover is available to gain a +10 Cover bonus to Reflex Defense (instead of the normal +5 Cover bonus). Allies must be able to hear and understand you to gain this benefit, and the bonus lasts until the start of your next turn. This Talent provides no benefit to anyone who doesn't have Cover. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Prerequisite: As a Reaction, you can choose to take one-half or all of the damage dealt to an adjacent ally by a single attack. Similarly, as a Reaction, an adjacent ally can choose to take one-half or all of the damage dealt to you by a single attack (even if they don't have this Talent). Prerequisites: , Field Tactics An Officer learns to counter the tactics of their enemies. As a Standard Action, you can make a DC 15 Knowledge (Tactics) check. If the check succeeds, opponents in your line of sight lose all competence, insight, and morale bonuses on attack rolls, as well as any dodge bonuses to Reflex Defense, until the start of your next turn. If one or more enemy Officers are within your line of sight, the highest level Officer among them can attempt to Oppose your Knowledge (Tactics) check as a Reaction. If their Skill Check result is higher than yours, your attempt to Outmaneuver your opponents fails. As a Swift Action, you can take a -2 penalty to one Defense (Reflex, Fortitude, or Will) to gain a +1 competence bonus to another Defense until the start of your next turn.","description":"You know how to use existing terrain to your best advantage. By using a Move Action, you can make a DC 15 Knowledge (Tactics) check. If the check succeeds, you and all allies within 10 squares of you can use whatever Cover is available to gain a +10 Cover bonus to Reflex Defense (instead of the normal +5 Cover bonus). Allies must be able to hear and understand you to gain this benefit, and the bonus lasts until the start of your next turn. This Talent provides no benefit to anyone who doesn't have Cover. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Prerequisite: As a Reaction, you can choose to take one-half or all of the damage dealt to an adjacent ally by a single attack. Similarly, as a Reaction, an adjacent ally can choose to take one-half or all of the damage dealt to you by a single attack (even if they don't have this Talent). Prerequisites: , Field Tactics An Officer learns to counter the tactics of their enemies. As a Standard Action, you can make a DC 15 Knowledge (Tactics) check. If the check succeeds, opponents in your line of sight lose all competence, insight, and morale bonuses on attack rolls, as well as any dodge bonuses to Reflex Defense, until the start of your next turn. If one or more enemy Officers are within your line of sight, the highest level Officer among them can attempt to Oppose your Knowledge (Tactics) check as a Reaction. If their Skill Check result is higher than yours, your attempt to Outmaneuver your opponents fails. As a Swift Action, you can take a -2 penalty to one Defense (Reflex, Fortitude, or Will) to gain a +1 competence bonus to another Defense until the start of your next turn.","class":"Officer","costNumeric":null,"category":"Officer","tree":"Military Tactics","treeId":"9253ace716c3e966","tags":["action-economy","controller","defender","evasion","leader","mobility","positioning","scout","skills","striker","support"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.deployment_tactics"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.8a5f8b5c9b9fabaf"}}},{"_id":"1b12a6b9870ecee9","name":"Indomitable","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Commando","prerequisites":null,"benefit":"Once per day, move +5 steps up the condition track (not persistent conditions); may be taken multiple times.","description":"","class":"Soldier","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","treeId":"798ed0945cbdac1c","tree":"Commando","tags":["condition-removal","controller","mobility","scaling","soldier","striker","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.indomitable"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.b8aaf500d3069938"}}},{"_id":"c3e0850f56e43738","name":"Presence","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Influence","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Once per encounter, you can make a Persuasion check as a Standard Action to demand surrender from an opponent who has been reduced to one-half or less of its hit points. If your check result equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, it surrenders to you and your allies, drops any weapons it is holding, and takes no hostile actions. If the target is higher level than you, it gains a +5 bonus to its Will Defense. If you or any of your allies attack it, it no longer submits to your will and can act normally. You can only use this Talent against a particular target once per encounter. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Prerequisites: , Weaken Resolve Prerequisite: Once per round, when you deal damage equal to or greater than the target's Damage Threshold, you can make a Persuasion check as a Free Action; if the result equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, you fill the target with terror, causing it to flee from you at top speed for 1 minute. The target can't take Standard Actions, Swift Actions, or Full-Round Actions while fleeing, but the target stops fleeing and can act normally if it is wounded. As a Free Action or Reaction, the target can spend a Force Point (if it has not already spent one earlier in the round) to negate the effect. The effect is automatically negated if the target's level is equal to or higher than your Character Level. This is a Mind-Affecting fear effect. Unlike with other Mind-Affecting effects, you need only to hail a Vehicle to weaken the crew's resolve. When you deal damage that equals or exceeds a Vehicle's Damage Threshold, you may use this Talent; in addition, you may Ready an Action to use this Talent after any Gunner on your Vehicle deals damage that equals or exceeds a Vehicle's Damage Threshold. You make your check against the Vehicle's Commander; all Nonheroic crews are assumed to have a Will Defense of 10. The effect is automatically negated if the target Vehicle's Challenge Level is greater than your Heroic Level or your Vehicle's Challenge Level. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide Prerequisites: , Trained in Persuasion You get under an opponent's skin. Once per encounter, make a Persuasion check to Intimidate one creature within line of sight as a Standard Action. On a success, instead of the normal effect of an Intimidate application of the Persuasion skill, the affected creature can take only a single Swift Action on its next turn. If the target is a higher level than you, it gains a +5 bonus to its Will Defense against the Intimidate check. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide Prerequisites: , Trained in Persuasion Once per encounter, as a Reaction, you can make a Persuasion check to Intimidate one creature that is making a melee or ranged attack against you, and is within your line of sight. If you succeed, you impose a -5 penalty to that attack roll. If the target is a higher level than you, it gains a +5 bonus to its Will Defense against the Intimidate check. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook","description":"Once per encounter, you can make a Persuasion check as a Standard Action to demand surrender from an opponent who has been reduced to one-half or less of its hit points. If your check result equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, it surrenders to you and your allies, drops any weapons it is holding, and takes no hostile actions. If the target is higher level than you, it gains a +5 bonus to its Will Defense. If you or any of your allies attack it, it no longer submits to your will and can act normally. You can only use this Talent against a particular target once per encounter. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Prerequisites: , Weaken Resolve Prerequisite: Once per round, when you deal damage equal to or greater than the target's Damage Threshold, you can make a Persuasion check as a Free Action; if the result equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, you fill the target with terror, causing it to flee from you at top speed for 1 minute. The target can't take Standard Actions, Swift Actions, or Full-Round Actions while fleeing, but the target stops fleeing and can act normally if it is wounded. As a Free Action or Reaction, the target can spend a Force Point (if it has not already spent one earlier in the round) to negate the effect. The effect is automatically negated if the target's level is equal to or higher than your Character Level. This is a Mind-Affecting fear effect. Unlike with other Mind-Affecting effects, you need only to hail a Vehicle to weaken the crew's resolve. When you deal damage that equals or exceeds a Vehicle's Damage Threshold, you may use this Talent; in addition, you may Ready an Action to use this Talent after any Gunner on your Vehicle deals damage that equals or exceeds a Vehicle's Damage Threshold. You make your check against the Vehicle's Commander; all Nonheroic crews are assumed to have a Will Defense of 10. The effect is automatically negated if the target Vehicle's Challenge Level is greater than your Heroic Level or your Vehicle's Challenge Level. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide Prerequisites: , Trained in Persuasion You get under an opponent's skin. Once per encounter, make a Persuasion check to Intimidate one creature within line of sight as a Standard Action. On a success, instead of the normal effect of an Intimidate application of the Persuasion skill, the affected creature can take only a single Swift Action on its next turn. If the target is a higher level than you, it gains a +5 bonus to its Will Defense against the Intimidate check. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide Prerequisites: , Trained in Persuasion Once per encounter, as a Reaction, you can make a Persuasion check to Intimidate one creature that is making a melee or ranged attack against you, and is within your line of sight. If you succeed, you impose a -5 penalty to that attack roll. If the target is a higher level than you, it gains a +5 bonus to its Will Defense against the Intimidate check. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook","class":"Noble","costNumeric":null,"category":"Noble","tree":"Influence","treeId":"8375b9b26b679901","tags":["action-economy","damage-reduction","defender","force","force-defense","force-offense","melee","mobility","noble","positioning","ranged","skills","social","striker","support","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.presence"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.ec8f2ba706cc2c05"}}},{"_id":"824f16981ea11cab","name":"Weaken Resolve","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Influence","prerequisites":"","benefit":"As , except that the target doesn't stop fleeing from you if it is wounded.","description":"As , except that the target doesn't stop fleeing from you if it is wounded.","class":"Noble","costNumeric":null,"category":"Noble","tree":"Influence","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.presence"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"8375b9b26b679901","tags":["noble","striker"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.weaken_resolve"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.28c306c37ccb9fcf"}}},{"_id":"15a05515ef2ef28b","name":"Unarmed","type":"weapon","img":"icons/svg/sword.svg","system":{"damage":"1d6+7","damageType":"kinetic","attackBonus":0,"attackAttribute":"str","range":"melee","weight":1,"cost":0,"equipped":true,"description":"","properties":[],"ammunition":{"type":"none","current":0,"max":0},"weaponCategory":"simple","proficiency":"simple","subcategory":""},"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"placeholder":true,"npc":{"flatAttackBonus":10,"flatDamageFormula":"1d6+7","useFlat":true}}}},{"_id":"51a82864cf124050","name":"Shrapnel Pistol","type":"weapon","img":"icons/svg/sword.svg","system":{"damage":"2d6+5","damageType":"kinetic","attackBonus":0,"attackAttribute":"dex","range":"ranged","weight":1,"cost":0,"equipped":true,"description":"","properties":[],"ammunition":{"type":"none","current":0,"max":0},"weaponCategory":"simple","proficiency":"simple","subcategory":""},"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"placeholder":true,"unresolved":"Shrapnel Pistol","npc":{"flatAttackBonus":7,"flatDamageFormula":"2d6+5","useFlat":true}}}}],"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"import":{"source":"books","raw":{"Size":"Medium","Species":"Ebruchi","Nonheroic Level":0,"Class Levels":{"Noble":5,"Soldier":2,"Officer":3},"Destiny Points":1,"Force Points":5,"Dark Side Points":8,"Initiative":6,"Senses":"Perception +12","Languages":["Ebruchese","Sy Bisti"],"Unassigned Languages":0,"Reflex Defense":24,"Flat-Footed Defense":22,"Fortitude Defense":23,"Will Defense":28,"Hit Points":67,"Damage Threshold":28,"Speed":"6 Squares","Melee Weapons":"Unarmed +10 (1d6+7)","Ranged Weapons":"Shrapnel Pistol +7 (2d6+5)","Base Attack Bonus":8,"Grapple":10,"Attack Options":["Point-Blank Shot","Precise Shot"],"Special Actions":["Assault Tactics","Born Leader","Command Cover (+1)","Deployment Tactics","Indomitable","Presence","Quick Draw","Share Talent ( Indomitable )","Unsettling","Weaken Resolve"],"Force Powers":[],"Force Secrets":[],"Force Techniques":[],"Strength":14,"Dexterity":13,"Constitution":13,"Intelligence":12,"Wisdom":14,"Charisma":16,"Talents":["Talents : Assault Tactics","Born Leader","Deployment Tactics","Indomitable","Presence","Weaken Resolve"],"Feats":["Feats : Armor Proficiency (Light)","Armor Proficiency (Medium)","Improved Damage Threshold","Martial Arts I","Point-Blank Shot","Precise Shot","Quick Draw","Skill Focus (Persuasion)","Vehicular Combat","Weapon Proficiency (Pistols)","Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)"],"Skills":["Skills : Deception","Knowledge (Galactic Lore)","Knowledge (Tactics)","Perception","Persuasion","Pilot","Use Computer"],"Trained Skills":["Skills : Deception","Knowledge (Galactic Lore)","Knowledge (Tactics)","Perception","Persuasion","Pilot","Use Computer"],"Species Traits":[],"Gear":"Shrapnel Pistol (As Slugthrower Pistol ), Datapad , Expensive Garments"},"mode":"play","sourcePack":"heroic","sourceAuthority":"statblock","playReady":true,"normalizedForPlay":true,"playNormalizationVersion":1}}}}
{"_id":"5094633abd6da531","name":"Obi-Wan Kenobi","type":"npc","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"isDroid":false,"droidDegree":"","attributes":{"str":{"base":15,"racial":0,"enhancement":0,"temp":0},"dex":{"base":16,"racial":0,"enhancement":0,"temp":0},"con":{"base":14,"racial":0,"enhancement":0,"temp":0},"int":{"base":13,"racial":0,"enhancement":0,"temp":0},"wis":{"base":14,"racial":0,"enhancement":0,"temp":0},"cha":{"base":15,"racial":0,"enhancement":0,"temp":0}},"skills":{"acrobatics":{"trained":true,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"dex","favorite":false},"climb":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"str","favorite":false},"deception":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"cha","favorite":false},"endurance":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"con","favorite":false},"gatherInformation":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"cha","favorite":false},"initiative":{"trained":true,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"dex","favorite":false},"jump":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"str","favorite":false},"knowledgeBureaucracy":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"int","favorite":false},"knowledgeGalacticLore":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"int","favorite":false},"knowledgeLifeSciences":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"int","favorite":false},"knowledgePhysicalSciences":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"int","favorite":false},"knowledgeSocialSciences":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"int","favorite":false},"knowledgeTactics":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"int","favorite":false},"knowledgeTechnology":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"int","favorite":false},"mechanics":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"int","favorite":false},"perception":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"wis","favorite":false},"persuasion":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"cha","favorite":false},"pilot":{"trained":true,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"dex","favorite":false},"ride":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"dex","favorite":false},"stealth":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"dex","favorite":false},"survival":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"wis","favorite":false},"swim":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"str","favorite":false},"treatInjury":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"wis","favorite":false},"useComputer":{"trained":false,"focused":false,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"int","favorite":false},"useTheForce":{"trained":true,"focused":true,"miscMod":0,"selectedAbility":"cha","favorite":false}},"hp":{"value":129,"max":129,"temp":0,"bonus":0},"conditionTrack":{"current":0,"persistent":false,"penalty":0},"level":14,"size":"medium","speed":6,"defenses":{"reflex":{"total":30,"armor":0,"classBonus":0,"misc":{"auto":{},"user":{}},"ability":"dex","source":"level","level":0},"fort":{"total":31,"classBonus":0,"misc":{"auto":{},"user":{}},"ability":"con","level":0},"will":{"total":29,"classBonus":0,"misc":{"auto":{},"user":{}},"ability":"wis","level":0},"flatFooted":{"total":27}},"languages":["Basic","Shyriiwook (understand only)"],"destinyPoints":{"value":2,"max":2},"forcePoints":{"value":7,"max":7,"die":"1d6"},"darkSideScore":0,"damageThreshold":31,"bab":14,"race":"Human","class":"Jedi 7 / Knight 5 / Master 2","className":"Jedi 7 / Knight 5 / Master 2","biography":"<p><strong>Gear:</strong> Lightsaber ( Self-Built ), Comlink (Short-Range, Encrypted), Utility Belt with Medpac , Jedi Robes</p>\n<p><strong>Senses:</strong> Perception +9</p>\n<p><strong>Attack Options:</strong> Double Attack (Lightsabers), Severing Strike, Weapon Finesse</p>\n<p><strong>Special Actions:</strong> Equilibrium, Redirect Shot, Serenity</p>","derived":{},"npcProfile":{"kind":"heroic","mode":"play","sourceAuthority":"statblock","legalProfile":"heroic","legalState":"unchecked","importMode":"play","playReady":true,"statblockAuthority":true,"sourcePack":"heroic","normalizationVersion":1,"authority":{"hp":"statblock","defenses":"statblock","bab":"statblock","attacks":"statblock","skills":"statblock","damageThreshold":"statblock"}}},"items":[{"_id":"60cea31aabf3ed9d","name":"Human","type":"species","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"size":"Medium","speed":6,"abilities":"None","skillBonuses":[],"special":["Bonus Feat: Humans gain one bonus feat at 1st level","Bonus Trained Skill: Humans gain one additional trained skill at 1st level"],"languages":["Basic"],"source":"Core","description":"","tags":[],"visionTraits":[],"naturalWeapons":[],"movementTraits":[],"environmentalTraits":[],"combatTraits":{"naturalArmor":0,"weaponProficiencies":[],"otherTraits":[]},"techTraits":[],"forceTraits":[],"socialTraits":[],"bonusFeats":1,"bonusTrainedSkills":1,"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":700,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.species.species-human"}}},{"_id":"5111e2083a74eccc","name":"Armor Proficiency (light)","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"You are proficient with light armor and do not take armor check penalties on attack rolls.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":85,"tags":["armor","defender","non-force","scout","soldier"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier","Scout"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{"value":"No penalty on attacks and no <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Armor_Check_Penalty\" title=\"Armor Check Penalty\">Ar