,"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier","Scout"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{}},"effects":[{"_id":"3b695d0d-747b-4081-8b6c-8b5f8584ff43","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Rifles)","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Weapon Proficiency (Rifles)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Rifles)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.765ff8a34e58acac"}}},{"_id":"9c9052b2ab561b48","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"You are proficient with simple weapons and do not take the -5 penalty when using them.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["noble","non-force","scoundrel","scout","soldier"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier","Scout","Scoundrel","Noble"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{}},"effects":[{"_id":"220daaa7-e1b5-440d-98cd-10f5e586ef8b","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.2d680cc46a7972da"}}},{"_id":"9a1c3be1f5144234","name":"Blaster and Blade I","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Privateer","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Dual Weapon Mastery I, Weapon Proficiency (Advanced Melee Weapons), Weapon Proficiency (Pistols) When you are wielding both an Advanced Melee Weapon and a Pistol, you treat the Advanced Melee Weapon as though you were wielding it two-handed (including doubling your Strength bonus on damage rolls). Prerequisites: , I, Dual Weapon Mastery I, Weapon Proficiency (Advanced Melee Weapons), Weapon Proficiency (Pistols) When you are wielding both an Advanced Melee Weapon and a Pistol, you can make a Full Attack as a Standard Action instead of a Full-Round Action, provided you attack with both weapons. You are skilled at boarding hostile vessels. You ignore Cover (but not Improved Cover) with your Character Scale ranged attacks while aboard a Starship or Space Station. You know the typical weaknesses of Vehicles and Droids, and you know how to preserve such targets for capture rather than destroying them. When attacking with Ion weapons, you gain a +1 bonus on attack rolls and deal +1 die of Ion damage. Whenever you make multiple attacks with any type of Advanced Melee Weapon as a Full-Round Action (see Full Attack), you reduce the penalty on your attack rolls by 2. You can take this Talent multiple times; each time you take this Talent, you reduce the penalty on your attack rolls by an additional 2. When you deal damage with a Vehicle Weapon that is equal to or greater than both the target Vehicle's current Hit Points and the target Vehicle's Damage Threshold (that is, when you would deal enough damage to destroy the target Vehicle), you can choose to use this Talent. Instead of dealing full damage, you instead deal half damage to your target and move it -1 step along the Condition Track. In addition, you disable the ship's sublight engines and Hyperdrive. The ship cannot move or make a jump to lightspeed until it receives repairs.","description":"Dual Weapon Mastery I, Weapon Proficiency (Advanced Melee Weapons), Weapon Proficiency (Pistols) When you are wielding both an Advanced Melee Weapon and a Pistol, you treat the Advanced Melee Weapon as though you were wielding it two-handed (including doubling your Strength bonus on damage rolls). Prerequisites: , I, Dual Weapon Mastery I, Weapon Proficiency (Advanced Melee Weapons), Weapon Proficiency (Pistols) When you are wielding both an Advanced Melee Weapon and a Pistol, you can make a Full Attack as a Standard Action instead of a Full-Round Action, provided you attack with both weapons. You are skilled at boarding hostile vessels. You ignore Cover (but not Improved Cover) with your Character Scale ranged attacks while aboard a Starship or Space Station. You know the typical weaknesses of Vehicles and Droids, and you know how to preserve such targets for capture rather than destroying them. When attacking with Ion weapons, you gain a +1 bonus on attack rolls and deal +1 die of Ion damage. Whenever you make multiple attacks with any type of Advanced Melee Weapon as a Full-Round Action (see Full Attack), you reduce the penalty on your attack rolls by 2. You can take this Talent multiple times; each time you take this Talent, you reduce the penalty on your attack rolls by an additional 2. When you deal damage with a Vehicle Weapon that is equal to or greater than both the target Vehicle's current Hit Points and the target Vehicle's Damage Threshold (that is, when you would deal enough damage to destroy the target Vehicle), you can choose to use this Talent. Instead of dealing full damage, you instead deal half damage to your target and move it -1 step along the Condition Track. In addition, you disable the ship's sublight engines and Hyperdrive. The ship cannot move or make a jump to lightspeed until it receives repairs.","class":"Master Privateer","costNumeric":null,"category":"Master Privateer","tree":"Privateer","treeId":"df6678946610c554","tags":["action-economy","burst-damage","condition-removal","controller","damage-reduction","defender","dual-wield","mechanics","melee","mobility","positioning","ranged","scaling","scoundrel","skills","striker","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.blaster_and_blade_i"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.976c36831fecbd2b"}}},{"_id":"1fccc83b4e8ad109","name":"Born Leader","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Naval Officer","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Prerequisites: Charisma 13, Intelligence 13, When you are the Commander of a Capital Ship, calculate its Reflex Defense using your Heroic Level plus one-half the ship's armor bonus (rounded down), the Pilot's Heroic Level, or the ship's Armor bonus, whichever is highest. In addition, all Gunners on your ship add one-half your Heroic Level, or one-half their Heroic Level, whichever is more, to damage rolls with Vehicle Weapons. Finally, you treat any generic crew as being one quality level higher (maximum of Ace, see Crew Quality).","description":"Prerequisites: Charisma 13, Intelligence 13, When you are the Commander of a Capital Ship, calculate its Reflex Defense using your Heroic Level plus one-half the ship's armor bonus (rounded down), the Pilot's Heroic Level, or the ship's Armor bonus, whichever is highest. In addition, all Gunners on your ship add one-half your Heroic Level, or one-half their Heroic Level, whichever is more, to damage rolls with Vehicle Weapons. Finally, you treat any generic crew as being one quality level higher (maximum of Ace, see Crew Quality).","class":"Noble","costNumeric":null,"category":"Noble","tree":"Naval Officer","treeId":"057a978a7dc1d5a7","tags":["armor","defender","noble","striker","support","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[{"_id":"f9275c38-3cb5-4ab3-aaa5-25e5722dcdd3","name":"Born Leader","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.defenses.will","mode":2,"value":"1"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Born Leader"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.born_leader"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.6a66ba6e0834dd6f"}}},{"_id":"da5648c5981d2749","name":"Channel Energy","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Control","prerequisites":null,"benefit":"Convert energy from Negate Energy to activate any power in your suite.","description":"Convert energy damage you negate into the ability to activate a Force power.","costNumeric":null,"tree":"Control","treeId":"d3661aa9906bdc79","tags":["force"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.channel_energy"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.fb6b798fe0c6091f"}}},{"_id":"7c1f72b0ab755e96","name":"Drain Knowledge","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Dark Side","prerequisites":null,"benefit":"By touch, make a check vs target's Will Defense to drain knowledge; gain trained status in a skill or a Skill Focus if you already have the skill; target moves down the condition track; you gain a Dark Side Point.","description":"Drain knowledge by touch, gaining a trained skill or Skill Focus; target moves down the condition track.","costNumeric":null,"tree":"Dark Side","treeId":"de95d37c72b1c4cd","tags":["condition-removal","controller","defender","mobility","striker"]},"effects":[{"_id":"4e2c9d66-7b82-4596-b5c5-42b24e72de4d","name":"Drain Knowledge","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.skills.knowledge","mode":2,"value":"bonus"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Drain Knowledge"}}},{"_id":"a57d6a47-2cf4-4fcb-a558-8dae4e2bea79","name":"Drain Knowledge - DSP Increase","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.darkSideScore","mode":2,"value":"1"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Drain Knowledge"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.drain_knowledge"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.d46612d82307f0db"}}},{"_id":"3455459280415536","name":"Negate and Redirect","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/aura.svg","system":{"tree":"Unknown","prerequisite":"","benefit":"","special":"","uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perEncounter":false,"perDay":false}},"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"placeholder":true,"unresolved":"Negate and Redirect"}}},{"_id":"1ed480cc0c3b9218","name":"Rising Panic","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Blazing Chain","tree":"Blazing Chain","prerequisites":"","description":"You start a in an enemy who observes your attacks and actions, inhibiting the enemy's ability to respond. Once per round as a Reaction to an enemy damaging one of your allies or moving one of your allies down the Condition Track, you can make a Use the Force check against the target's Will Defense. If the check equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, you move the target -1 step on the Condition Track. An enemy moved to the bottom of the Condition Track by this Talent does not fall unconscious, but instead must spend its actions fleeing combat for one minute or until it moves up the Condition Track. This is a Mind-Affecting Fear effect.","benefit":"You start a in an enemy who observes your attacks and actions, inhibiting the enemy's ability to respond. Once per round as a Reaction to an enemy damaging one of your allies or moving one of your allies down the Condition Track, you can make a Use the Force check against the target's Will Defense. If the check equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, you move the target -1 step on the Condition Track. An enemy moved to the bottom of the Condition Track by this Talent does not fall unconscious, but instead must spend its actions fleeing combat for one minute or until it moves up the Condition Track. This is a Mind-Affecting Fear effect.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"427213bd55e04e27","tags":["action-economy","condition-removal","controller","defender","force","force-control","force-defense","force-offense","mobility","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.d091b5f6b34b4967"}}},{"_id":"5666185e28ddf0b4","name":"Spacehound","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Spacer","prerequisites":"","benefit":"You gain a +1 bonus on attack rolls made while aboard a Starship. This bonus applies to attacks made with Starship Weapons, as well as personal weapons used aboard a Starship. Prerequisite: Whenever you roll a Natural 20 on an attack roll made aboard a Starship, you gain one temporary Force Point. If the Force Point is not used before the end of the encounter, it is lost. This Talent works with both Weapon Systems and personal weapons used aboard a Starship. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Starship Raider When adjacent to an obstacle or barrier, you gain a +2 Cover bonus to your Reflex Defense. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions Prerequisites: , Starship Raider Whether you are taking on military targets on behalf of a resistance movement or you are out for personal gain, you are experienced at raiding Starships and similar targets. You can use each if the following Actions once per encounter: Clear a Path: Your attack forces an enemy to alter course or move out of your way. You must be fighting aboard a Starship to use this Action. As a Standard Action, make a ranged attack. If the attack hits, on its next turn your target must move its Speed to a square that is not adjacent to you. If the target is an enemy Starfighter engaged in a Dogfight, the target instead must attempt to disengage from the Dogfight. Covering Fire: You squeeze off several shots as you escape pursuing enemies. As a Full-Round Action, if you are the Pilot of a Vehicle, you may move the Vehicle up to twice its Speed and make a single ranged attack with one of the Pilot-controlled Vehicle Weapons at any point during that movement. If you hit and deal damage to a Vehicle with this attack, the target Vehicle takes a -2 penalty to attack rolls against your Vehicle until the end of your turn. Disabling Fire: Make a ranged attack with your Vehicle Weapon. If you make this attack against a Vehicle and hit and deal damage, you can choose one of the following to take effect until the end of your next turn: One of the target's Vehicle Weapons ceases to function. The target's Shield Rating is reduced to 0. The target's Hyperdrive is disabled. The target's Speed is reduced to 2 squares (Character Scale). Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Stellar Warrior Once per encounter, while on or in a Vehicle, you can move up to one-half your speed, or move the Vehicle up to one-half its speed if you are the Pilot, as a Swift Action. This movement does not provoke Attacks of Opportunity.","description":"You gain a +1 bonus on attack rolls made while aboard a Starship. This bonus applies to attacks made with Starship Weapons, as well as personal weapons used aboard a Starship. Prerequisite: Whenever you roll a Natural 20 on an attack roll made aboard a Starship, you gain one temporary Force Point. If the Force Point is not used before the end of the encounter, it is lost. This Talent works with both Weapon Systems and personal weapons used aboard a Starship. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Starship Raider When adjacent to an obstacle or barrier, you gain a +2 Cover bonus to your Reflex Defense. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions Prerequisites: , Starship Raider Whether you are taking on military targets on behalf of a resistance movement or you are out for personal gain, you are experienced at raiding Starships and similar targets. You can use each if the following Actions once per encounter: Clear a Path: Your attack forces an enemy to alter course or move out of your way. You must be fighting aboard a Starship to use this Action. As a Standard Action, make a ranged attack. If the attack hits, on its next turn your target must move its Speed to a square that is not adjacent to you. If the target is an enemy Starfighter engaged in a Dogfight, the target instead must attempt to disengage from the Dogfight. Covering Fire: You squeeze off several shots as you escape pursuing enemies. As a Full-Round Action, if you are the Pilot of a Vehicle, you may move the Vehicle up to twice its Speed and make a single ranged attack with one of the Pilot-controlled Vehicle Weapons at any point during that movement. If you hit and deal damage to a Vehicle with this attack, the target Vehicle takes a -2 penalty to attack rolls against your Vehicle until the end of your turn. Disabling Fire: Make a ranged attack with your Vehicle Weapon. If you make this attack against a Vehicle and hit and deal damage, you can choose one of the following to take effect until the end of your next turn: One of the target's Vehicle Weapons ceases to function. The target's Shield Rating is reduced to 0. The target's Hyperdrive is disabled. The target's Speed is reduced to 2 squares (Character Scale). Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Stellar Warrior Once per encounter, while on or in a Vehicle, you can move up to one-half your speed, or move the Vehicle up to one-half its speed if you are the Pilot, as a Swift Action. This movement does not provoke Attacks of Opportunity.","class":"Scoundrel","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scoundrel","tree":"Spacer","treeId":"5ea8c79492d40713","tags":["action-economy","controller","damage-reduction","defender","force","force-control","force-defense","force-offense","mobility","positioning","ranged","scaling","scoundrel","shields","striker","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.spacehound"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.fe0c3a64ca460542"}}},{"_id":"e4e1b885d8866bf4","name":"Starship Raider","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Spacer","prerequisites":"Spacehound","benefit":"+1 attack aboard starships, including with personal weapons.","description":"Gain +1 attack aboard starships with personal weapons.","class":"Scoundrel","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scoundrel","tree":"Spacer","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.spacehound"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"5ea8c79492d40713","tags":["feat-chain","scoundrel","striker","talent-chain"]},"effects":[{"_id":"e4be147d-37ec-4006-90a5-976c3d591ef7","name":"Starship Raider","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.attacks","mode":2,"value":"1"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Starship Raider"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.starship_raider"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.224906e573330bf2"}}},{"_id":"fa1caeb64f5755c1","name":"Tested in Battle","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Veteran","tree":"Veteran","prerequisites":"","description":"You know from first-hand experience that victory goes to those willing to take a chance. You can add your Wisdom bonus (minimum +1) to the damage roll when you make a successful Charge attack. Prerequisites: , Trained in Initiative You have seen more action in more places than most people know exist, and little in the galaxy gets you rattled. Any character using a Fear effect on you must roll twice, keeping the lower result on any Skill Checks and attack rolls. When you catch a Second Wind, you move +2 steps on the Condition Track in addition to regaining Hit Points.","benefit":"You know from first-hand experience that victory goes to those willing to take a chance. You can add your Wisdom bonus (minimum +1) to the damage roll when you make a successful Charge attack. Prerequisites: , Trained in Initiative You have seen more action in more places than most people know exist, and little in the galaxy gets you rattled. Any character using a Fear effect on you must roll twice, keeping the lower result on any Skill Checks and attack rolls. When you catch a Second Wind, you move +2 steps on the Condition Track in addition to regaining Hit Points.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"96c390430d7a4975","tags":["action-economy","condition-removal","controller","mobility","scout","skills","striker"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.cccea4e91352482a"}}},{"_id":"318f51a4f4db4cc5","name":"Battle Strike","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"telekinetic","useTheForce":15,"time":"Swift Action","range":"Personal","target":"You","duration":"1 round","effect":"<p>You channel the Force to enhance your next melee attack. Your next melee attack this round gains a +1d6 bonus to damage.</p>","special":"<p>This bonus damage is Force damage and bypasses Damage Reduction.</p>","descriptor":["Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":94,"tags":["enhancement","damage","melee"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.f177dc6d65f76de9"}}},{"_id":"2e29df47c78e2782","name":"Combustion","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/eye.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"Unknown","useTheForce":"","time":"standard","range":"","target":"","duration":"","effect":"","special":"","descriptor":"","dcChart":"","maintainable":false,"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1,"perDay":true}},"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"placeholder":true,"unresolved":"Combustion"}}},{"_id":"7bc573aa0733d9ba","name":"Force Slam","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telekinetic","useTheForce":20,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One creature or object","duration":"Instantaneous","effect":"<p>You use telekinetic force to violently slam your target against a surface. The target takes 4d6 damage and is knocked prone.</p>","special":"<p>The target must be within 6 squares of a solid surface (wall, floor, ceiling).</p>","descriptor":["Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":97,"tags":["attack","damage","telekinetic","prone"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.462a6c23e00c4dfc"}}},{"_id":"24431b14045e1a4f","name":"Force Stun","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telepathic","useTheForce":20,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One creature","duration":"1 round","effect":"<p>You use the Force to overwhelm your target's mind, stunning them. The target must make a Will save (DC = your UTF check) or be stunned for 1 round.</p>","special":"","descriptor":["Mind-Affecting"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":97,"tags":["attack","stun","mind-affecting"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.a214d4f56b4abe11"}}},{"_id":"063cd02db9d1fd3e","name":"Mind Trick","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"telepathic","useTheForce":15,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One creature","duration":"1 minute or until completed","effect":"<p>You influence a weak mind to believe what you tell them or follow a simple suggestion. The target must make a Will save (DC = your UTF check) or be affected.</p>","special":"<p>The suggestion must be reasonable and the target must be able to understand you.</p>","descriptor":["Mind-Affecting"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":98,"tags":["mind-control","suggestion","social"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.e6649f366d6c5737"}}},{"_id":"8d7de9c7a051ce41","name":"Move Object","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telekinetic","useTheForce":15,"time":"Standard Action","range":"12 squares","target":"One object or creature","duration":"Concentration","effect":"<p>You move objects or creatures through the air using telekinesis. The maximum size/weight you can move depends on your Use the Force check result.</p>","special":"<p>Unwilling creatures can make a Will save (DC = your UTF check) to resist being moved.</p>","descriptor":["Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[{"dc":15,"effect":"Medium (50 kg)","description":"Move objects up to Medium size or 50 kg"},{"dc":20,"effect":"Large (250 kg)","description":"Move objects up to Large size or 250 kg"},{"dc":25,"effect":"Huge (1 ton)","description":"Move objects up to Huge size or 1 metric ton"},{"dc":30,"effect":"Gargantuan (5 tons)","description":"Move objects up to Gargantuan size or 5 metric tons"},{"dc":35,"effect":"Colossal (20 tons)","description":"Move objects up to Colossal size or 20 metric tons (starfighter-sized)"}],"maintainable":true,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":98,"tags":["telekinetic","movement","utility"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.289013a32bd179ad"}}},{"_id":"627