ebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["non-force","ranged","scoundrel","scout","soldier"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier","Scout","Scoundrel"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{}},"effects":[{"_id":"04733e85-193e-4f4b-8792-c359083557d1","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Pistols)","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Weapon Proficiency (Pistols)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Pistols)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.e5d361d01d1b44e4"}}},{"_id":"363f8fc62f225acf","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"You are proficient with simple weapons and do not take the -5 penalty when using them.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["noble","non-force","scoundrel","scout","soldier"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier","Scout","Scoundrel","Noble"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{}},"effects":[{"_id":"220daaa7-e1b5-440d-98cd-10f5e586ef8b","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.2d680cc46a7972da"}}},{"_id":"8e107b44e5ff8651","name":"Assault Tactics","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Military Tactics","prerequisites":"Trained in Initiative","benefit":"You can use the , Deployment Tactics, or Field Tactics Talent as a Swift Action, instead of a Move Action (provided you have the Talent in question). Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions During the first round of combat in an encounter (after the Surprise Round, if any), you can take your turn before any of your allies, but you must use either the Share Talent Prestige Class ability or a Talent from one of the following Talent Trees as part of your turn: Commando Talent Tree, Leadership Talent Tree, or Military Tactics Talent Tree. On the subsequent round, you return to your normal place in the Initiative Order. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide Prerequisite: When you use the Talent on an enemy, the target takes a cumulative -1 penalty to its Reflex Defense each time it is damaged by one of your allies (maximum -5 penalty). This penalty applies until the end of your next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide As a Swift Action, once per encounter, you can grant bonus Hit Points equal to 5 + one-half your Character Level to allies within 20 squares of you and in your line of sight. Damage is subtracted from the bonus Hit Points first, and any bonus Hit Points remaining at the end of the encounter go away. Bonus Hit Points from multiple sources do not stack. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions Your tactics confuse enemy commanders and tacticians that can see or otherwise observe your forces in action, such as when using sensors. After using the Share Talent special quality, make a Knowledge (Tactics) check as a Free Action. The result replaces the DC of any Talents that use Knowledge (Tactics) from the Military Tactics Talent Tree used against your or your allies. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions If you have already used a Talent in an encounter before granting the same Talent to an ally with your Share Talent special quality in the same encounter, any character who benefits from Share Talent gains one of the following bonuses when using that talent (if the Talent can be affected by more than one effect, the character using the Talent selects the desired effect): Reduce the Talent's DC by 5. Gain an additional +2 bonus to any bonus to attack, Defense, or damage used by the Talent. Reduce the amount of damage taken by the character through the use of the Talent by 10 points. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions","description":"You can use the , Deployment Tactics, or Field Tactics Talent as a Swift Action, instead of a Move Action (provided you have the Talent in question). Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions During the first round of combat in an encounter (after the Surprise Round, if any), you can take your turn before any of your allies, but you must use either the Share Talent Prestige Class ability or a Talent from one of the following Talent Trees as part of your turn: Commando Talent Tree, Leadership Talent Tree, or Military Tactics Talent Tree. On the subsequent round, you return to your normal place in the Initiative Order. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide Prerequisite: When you use the Talent on an enemy, the target takes a cumulative -1 penalty to its Reflex Defense each time it is damaged by one of your allies (maximum -5 penalty). This penalty applies until the end of your next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide As a Swift Action, once per encounter, you can grant bonus Hit Points equal to 5 + one-half your Character Level to allies within 20 squares of you and in your line of sight. Damage is subtracted from the bonus Hit Points first, and any bonus Hit Points remaining at the end of the encounter go away. Bonus Hit Points from multiple sources do not stack. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions Your tactics confuse enemy commanders and tacticians that can see or otherwise observe your forces in action, such as when using sensors. After using the Share Talent special quality, make a Knowledge (Tactics) check as a Free Action. The result replaces the DC of any Talents that use Knowledge (Tactics) from the Military Tactics Talent Tree used against your or your allies. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions If you have already used a Talent in an encounter before granting the same Talent to an ally with your Share Talent special quality in the same encounter, any character who benefits from Share Talent gains one of the following bonuses when using that talent (if the Talent can be affected by more than one effect, the character using the Talent selects the desired effect): Reduce the Talent's DC by 5. Gain an additional +2 bonus to any bonus to attack, Defense, or damage used by the Talent. Reduce the amount of damage taken by the character through the use of the Talent by 10 points. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions","class":"Officer","costNumeric":null,"category":"Officer","tree":"Military Tactics","treeId":"9253ace716c3e966","tags":["action-economy","ambush","controller","damage-reduction","defender","feat-chain","force","force-control","force-defense","force-offense","leader","leadership","mobility","positioning","scaling","scout","skills","striker","support","sustained-damage","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.assault_tactics"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.d9fe8a0c76d845d4"}}},{"_id":"4ef18effe60a6cc1","name":"Bolster Ally","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Inspiration","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Inspire Confidence Whenever you hit an opponent with a melee or ranged attack, you can (as a Free Action) choose to give one ally within your line of sight a bonus to damage on their next attack equal to their Character Level. Once their fervor has been ignited, the affected ally doesn't need to remain within line of sight of you; if their next attack misses, they lose the bonus to damage granted by this Talent. Prerequisites: , Inspire Confidence, Ignite Fervor Whenever an ally within line of sight of you makes an attack that moves an opponent down the Condition Track (such as dealing damage that equals of exceeds the target's Damage Threshold), that ally moves the target an additional -1 step down the Condition Track. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Inspire Confidence Your allies hold you in such esteem that when you are threatened or injured, you can impel them to action. You can use each of the following actions once per encounter: Guardian: Choose one ally as a Swift Action. As long as you remain within 6 squares of the ally, you gain a +2 bonus to your Reflex Defense until the start of your next turn. Reprisal: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any target within your Range as a Standard Action. If your attack roll succeeds and if that target attacks you before the end of your next turn, one ally within 6 squares can make an attack against that target as a Reaction. To Me!: Spend a Swift Action. Whenever you take any damage before the beginning of your next turn, each ally within line of sight can move 2 squares as a Reaction. This movement does not provoke Attacks of Opportunity. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","description":"Inspire Confidence Whenever you hit an opponent with a melee or ranged attack, you can (as a Free Action) choose to give one ally within your line of sight a bonus to damage on their next attack equal to their Character Level. Once their fervor has been ignited, the affected ally doesn't need to remain within line of sight of you; if their next attack misses, they lose the bonus to damage granted by this Talent. Prerequisites: , Inspire Confidence, Ignite Fervor Whenever an ally within line of sight of you makes an attack that moves an opponent down the Condition Track (such as dealing damage that equals of exceeds the target's Damage Threshold), that ally moves the target an additional -1 step down the Condition Track. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Inspire Confidence Your allies hold you in such esteem that when you are threatened or injured, you can impel them to action. You can use each of the following actions once per encounter: Guardian: Choose one ally as a Swift Action. As long as you remain within 6 squares of the ally, you gain a +2 bonus to your Reflex Defense until the start of your next turn. Reprisal: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any target within your Range as a Standard Action. If your attack roll succeeds and if that target attacks you before the end of your next turn, one ally within 6 squares can make an attack against that target as a Reaction. To Me!: Spend a Swift Action. Whenever you take any damage before the beginning of your next turn, each ally within line of sight can move 2 squares as a Reaction. This movement does not provoke Attacks of Opportunity. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","class":"Noble","costNumeric":null,"category":"Noble","tree":"Inspiration","treeId":"72d32ebcbb607314","tags":["action-economy","condition-removal","controller","defender","force","force-control","force-defense","force-offense","leader","melee","mobility","noble","positioning","ranged","striker","support"]},"effects":[{"_id":"c5626626-5e0d-4051-b4c2-928434aef891","name":"Bolster Ally","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.hp.regen","mode":2,"value":"1"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Bolster Ally"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.bolster_ally"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.d6e7f7178e643717"}}},{"_id":"b4a13125a8a8db53","name":"Born Leader","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Naval Officer","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Prerequisites: Charisma 13, Intelligence 13, When you are the Commander of a Capital Ship, calculate its Reflex Defense using your Heroic Level plus one-half the ship's armor bonus (rounded down), the Pilot's Heroic Level, or the ship's Armor bonus, whichever is highest. In addition, all Gunners on your ship add one-half your Heroic Level, or one-half their Heroic Level, whichever is more, to damage rolls with Vehicle Weapons. Finally, you treat any generic crew as being one quality level higher (maximum of Ace, see Crew Quality).","description":"Prerequisites: Charisma 13, Intelligence 13, When you are the Commander of a Capital Ship, calculate its Reflex Defense using your Heroic Level plus one-half the ship's armor bonus (rounded down), the Pilot's Heroic Level, or the ship's Armor bonus, whichever is highest. In addition, all Gunners on your ship add one-half your Heroic Level, or one-half their Heroic Level, whichever is more, to damage rolls with Vehicle Weapons. Finally, you treat any generic crew as being one quality level higher (maximum of Ace, see Crew Quality).","class":"Noble","costNumeric":null,"category":"Noble","tree":"Naval Officer","treeId":"057a978a7dc1d5a7","tags":["armor","defender","noble","striker","support","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[{"_id":"f9275c38-3cb5-4ab3-aaa5-25e5722dcdd3","name":"Born Leader","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.defenses.will","mode":2,"value":"1"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Born Leader"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.born_leader"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.6a66ba6e0834dd6f"}}},{"_id":"eb4295c0971d5e71","name":"Inspire Haste","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Inspiration","prerequisites":null,"benefit":"An ally may make a skill check as a move action instead of a standard action.