,"scout","soldier"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier","Scout","Scoundrel","Noble"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{}},"effects":[{"_id":"220daaa7-e1b5-440d-98cd-10f5e586ef8b","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.2d680cc46a7972da"}}},{"_id":"7ec1946716ec7a61","name":"Improved Move Light Object","type":"feat","img":"systems/foundryvtt-swse/assets/icons/force-technique.png","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"You may make a Use the Force check to Move Light Object as a Swift Action instead of a Move Action. Using the light object as a projectile weapon requires a Move Action (instead of a Standard Action).","prerequisite":"Move Light Object","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Core","page":0,"tags":["force-technique"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"description":"<p>You may make a Use the Force check to Move Light Object as a Swift Action instead of a Move Action. Using the light object as a projectile weapon requires a Move Action (instead of a Standard Action).</p><p><strong>Related Power:</strong> Move Light Object</p><p><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Move Light Object</p>","relatedPower":"Move Light Object"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcetechniques.c406600924a7780e"}}},{"_id":"dc521755263652e0","name":"Battle Meditation","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Sense","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Link Using a meditative battle trance, Force-users are able to join their minds together, collectively becoming stronger. However, a masterful degree of will is required to prevent the participants from sharing their weaknesses as well as their strengths. As a Full-Round Action, you can designate a number of willing allies equal to your Charisma modifier within 12 squares of you. These allies must be Trained in the Use the Force skill. As long as you remain within 12 squares of each other, you can Aid Another on attack rolls and Skill Checks as a Reaction.","description":"Link Using a meditative battle trance, Force-users are able to join their minds together, collectively becoming stronger. However, a masterful degree of will is required to prevent the participants from sharing their weaknesses as well as their strengths. As a Full-Round Action, you can designate a number of willing allies equal to your Charisma modifier within 12 squares of you. These allies must be Trained in the Use the Force skill. As long as you remain within 12 squares of each other, you can Aid Another on attack rolls and Skill Checks as a Reaction.","class":"Jedi","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","tree":"Sense","treeId":"d6b4331c0e31f7e3","tags":["action-economy","force","force-offense","jedi","positioning","striker","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[{"_id":"0cdcb68b-7eeb-45d0-ae5c-575d13648a00","name":"Battle Meditation","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.attacks.allies","mode":2,"value":"1"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Battle Meditation"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.battle_meditation"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.9461c7aa79dd07c6"}}},{"_id":"c711ef9b8a735d6b","name":"Block","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Sith Alchemy","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Create Sith Amulet: You can create a Sith Amulet. The creation of a Sith Amulet requires 25,000 credits' worth of gems and other raw materials, and the creation process takes 1 week (this work can be spread out over several sessions and need not be consecutive). At the end of the process, you must spend a Force Point to complete the Sith Amulet, after which point it functions exactly as a Sith Amulet. Create Sith Armor: You can transform a suit of normal Battle Armor into the Dark Armor worn by Sith Lords. You must have a suit of Battle Armor to transform into the Dark Armor (Light Battle Armor becomes Light Dark Armor, Battle Armor becomes Dark Armor, and Heavy Battle Armor becomes Heavy Dark Armor). The transformation process takes 1 day for Light Dark Armor, 2 days for Dark Armor, and 3 days for Heavy Dark Armor. You must spend a Force Point at the end of the creation process to complete the Armor's transformation. Create Sith Talisman: You can spend a Force Point to imbue a portable object with the Dark Side, creating a Sith Talisman that provides offensive strength to a Force Power. Creating the Sith Talisman takes a Full-Round Action. While you wear or carry the Sith Talisman on your person, you add 1d6 to your damage with Force Powers. You increase your Dark Side Score by 1 when you first wear or carry a Sith Talisman. You can have only one Sith Talisman active at any given time, and if it is destroyed, you cannot create another one for 24 hours. Create Sith Weapon: You can alchemically treat a Simple Weapon (Melee) or an Advanced Melee Weapon, turning it into a Sith Weapon. You must spend a Force Point and spend 1 hour imbuing the Weapon with the properties of a Sith Alchemical Weapon (see also: Sith Alchemical Weapon Template). A Lightsaber does not ignore the Sith Weapon's DR, and characters who are proficient in the Weapon's use can treat it as a Lightsaber for the purposes of the , Deflect, and Redirect Shot Talents (and any Talents that have these Talents as a prerequisite). Additionally, as a Swift Action, the wielder of a Sith Weapon can spend a Force Point to gain a bonus equal to their Dark Side Score to the damage of their next attack made with the Weapon before the end of the encounter. This increases the wielder's Dark Side Score by 1.","description":"Create Sith Amulet: You can create a Sith Amulet. The creation of a Sith Amulet requires 25,000 credits' worth of gems and other raw materials, and the creation process takes 1 week (this work can be spread out over several sessions and need not be consecutive). At the end of the process, you must spend a Force Point to complete the Sith Amulet, after which point it functions exactly as a Sith Amulet. Create Sith Armor: You can transform a suit of normal Battle Armor into the Dark Armor worn by Sith Lords. You must have a suit of Battle Armor to transform into the Dark Armor (Light Battle Armor becomes Light Dark Armor, Battle Armor becomes Dark Armor, and Heavy Battle Armor becomes Heavy Dark Armor). The transformation process takes 1 day for Light Dark Armor, 2 days for Dark Armor, and 3 days for Heavy Dark Armor. You must spend a Force Point at the end of the creation process to complete the Armor's transformation. Create Sith Talisman: You can spend a Force Point to imbue a portable object with the Dark Side, creating a Sith Talisman that provides offensive strength to a Force Power. Creating the Sith Talisman takes a Full-Round Action. While you wear or carry the Sith Talisman on your person, you add 1d6 to your damage with Force Powers. You increase your Dark Side Score by 1 when you first wear or carry a Sith Talisman. You can have only one Sith Talisman active at any given time, and if it is destroyed, you cannot create another one for 24 hours. Create Sith Weapon: You can alchemically treat a Simple Weapon (Melee) or an Advanced Melee Weapon, turning it into a Sith Weapon. You must spend a Force Point and spend 1 hour imbuing the Weapon with the properties of a Sith Alchemical Weapon (see also: Sith Alchemical Weapon Template). A Lightsaber does not ignore the Sith Weapon's DR, and characters who are proficient in the Weapon's use can treat it as a Lightsaber for the purposes of the , Deflect, and Redirect Shot Talents (and any Talents that have these Talents as a prerequisite). Additionally, as a Swift Action, the wielder of a Sith Weapon can spend a Force Point to gain a bonus equal to their Dark Side Score to the damage of their next attack made with the Weapon before the end of the encounter. This increases the wielder's Dark Side Score by 1.","class":"Jedi","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","tree":"Sith Alchemy","treeId":"a67faf2ae089ab5d","tags":["action-economy","armor","dark-side","defender","force","force-offense","jedi","lightsaber","melee","mobility","ranged","striker","support","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.block"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.9379daa94a228c04"}}},{"_id":"e18333581abaa9d5","name":"Bolster Ally","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Inspiration","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Inspire Confidence Whenever you hit an opponent with a melee or ranged attack, you can (as a Free Action) choose to give one ally within your line of sight a bonus to damage on their next attack equal to their Character Level. Once their fervor has been ignited, the affected ally doesn't need to remain within line of sight of you; if their next attack misses, they lose the bonus to damage granted by this Talent. Prerequisites: , Inspire Confidence, Ignite Fervor Whenever an ally within line of sight of you makes an attack that moves an opponent down the Condition Track (such as dealing damage that equals of exceeds the target's Damage Threshold), that ally moves the target an additional -1 step down the Condition Track. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Inspire Confidence Your allies hold you in such esteem that when you are threatened or injured, you can impel them to action. You can use each of the following actions once per encounter: Guardian: Choose one ally as a Swift Action. As long as you remain within 6 squares of the ally, you gain a +2 bonus to your Reflex Defense until the start of your next turn. Reprisal: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any target within your Range as a Standard Action. If your attack roll succeeds and if that target attacks you before the end of your next turn, one ally within 6 squares can make an attack against that target as a Reaction. To Me!: Spend a Swift Action. Whenever you take any damage before the beginning of your next turn, each ally within line of sight can move 2 squares as a Reaction. This movement does not provoke Attacks of Opportunity. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","description":"Inspire Confidence Whenever you hit an opponent with a melee or ranged attack, you can (as a Free Action) choose to give one ally within your line of sight a bonus to damage on their next attack equal to their Character Level. Once their fervor has been ignited, the affected ally doesn't need to remain within line of sight of you; if their next attack misses, they lose the bonus to damage granted by this Talent. Prerequisites: , Inspire Confidence, Ignite Fervor Whenever an ally within line of sight of you makes an attack that moves an opponent down the Condition Track (such as dealing damage that equals of exceeds the target's Damage Threshold), that ally moves the target an additional -1 step down the Condition Track. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Inspire Confidence Your allies hold you in such esteem that when you are threatened or injured, you can impel them to action. You can use each of the following actions once per encounter: Guardian: Choose one ally as a Swift Action. As long as you remain within 6 squares of the ally, you gain a +2 bonus to your Reflex Defense until the start of your next turn. Reprisal: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any target within your Range as a Standard Action. If your attack roll succeeds and if that target attacks you before the end of your next turn, one ally within 6 squares can make an attack against that target as a Reaction. To Me!: Spend a Swift Action. Whenever you take any damage before the beginning of your next turn, each ally within line of sight can move 2 squares as a Reaction. This movement does not provoke Attacks of Opportunity. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","class":"Noble","costNumeric":null,"category":"Noble","tree":"Inspiration","treeId":"72d32ebcbb607314","tags":["action-economy","condition-removal","controller","defender","force","force-control","force-defense","force-offense","leader","melee","mobility","noble","positioning","ranged","striker","support"]},"effects":[{"_id":"c5626626-5e0d-4051-b4c2-928434aef891","name":"Bolster Ally","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.hp.regen","mode":2,"value":"1"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Bolster Ally"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.bolster_ally"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.d6e7f7178e643717"}}},{"_id":"51cf01afe1c76585","name":"Deflect","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Lightsaber Forms","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Redirect Shot","description":"Redirect Shot","class":"Jedi","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","tree":"Lightsaber Forms","treeId":"2bc2572e852832e4","tags":["jedi","lightsaber","melee","ranged"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.deflect"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.72c644f7a09b1186"}}},{"_id":"e096436455f272e0","name":"Lightsaber Defense","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Lightsaber Forms","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Niman When you use the Talent, you gain twice the normal deflection bonus to your Reflex Defense when you are wielding two Lightsabers. Prerequisite: When wielding a single Lightsaber in one hand, the deflection bonus you gain from the Talent increases by 2 (to a maximum of +5). When wielding a Lightsaber, you gain a +1 bonus to your Reflex Defense and Will Defense.","description":"Niman When you use the Talent, you gain twice the normal deflection bonus to your Reflex Defense when you are wielding two Lightsabers. Prerequisite: When wielding a single Lightsaber in one hand, the deflection bonus you gain from the Talent increases by 2 (to a maximum of +5). When wielding a Lightsaber, you gain a +1 bonus to your Reflex Defense and Will Defense.","class":"Jedi","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","tree":"Lightsaber Forms","treeId":"2bc2572e852832e4","tags":["defender","jedi","lightsaber","melee","striker"]},"effects":[{"_id":"fcdbf882-923a-4095-b0df-a1079c214099","name":"Lightsaber Defense","icon":"icons/svg/shield.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.defenses.reflex.misc","mode":2,"value":"1","priority":20}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Lightsaber Defense"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.lightsaber_defense"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.e8bf1222fd6289e4"}}},{"_id":"c499d7513896133d","name":"Force Thrust","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telekinetic","useTheForce":20,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One creature or object","duration":"Instantaneous","effect":"<p>You violently push your target away with telekinetic force. The target is pushed 6 squares away from you and knocked prone, taking 2d6 damage.</p>","special":"<p>If the target hits an obstacle during the push, they take an additional 1d6 damage per 2 squares not traveled.</p>","descriptor":["Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":97,"tags":["attack","movement","telekinetic","forced-movement"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.d51bf85903366b6b"}}},{"_id":"9b9473d649b4b11f","name":"Move Object","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telekinetic","useTheForce":15,"time":"Standard Action","range":"12 squares","target":"One object or creature","duration":"Concentration","effect":"<p>You move objects or creatures through the air using telekinesis. The maximum size/weight you can move depends on your Use the Force check result.</p>","special":"<p>Unwilling creatures can make a Will save (DC = your UTF check) to resist being moved.</p>","descriptor":["Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[{"dc":15,"effect":"Medium (50 kg)","description":"Move objects up to Medium size or 50 kg"},{"dc":20,"effect":"Large (250 kg)","description":"Move objects up to Large size or 250 kg"},{"dc":25,"effect":"Huge (1 ton)","description":"Move objects up to Huge size or 1 metric ton"},{"dc":30,"effect":"Gargantuan (5 tons)","description":"Move objects up to Gargantuan size or 5 metric tons"},{"dc":35,"effect":"Colossal (20 tons)","description":"Move objects up to Colossal size or 20 metric tons (starfighter-sized)"}],"maintainable":true,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":98,"tags":["telekinetic","movement","utility"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.289013a32bd179ad"}}},{"_id":"4f63a726de6a88fa","name":"Lightsaber","type":"weapon","img":"icons/svg/sword.svg","system":{"damage":"2d8+5","damageType":"energy","attackBonus":0,"attackAttribute":"str","range":"melee","weight":1,"cost":12000,"equipped":true,"description":"<p>The elegant weapon of the Jedi and Sith. A blade of pure energy capable of cutting through nearly anything.</p>\n      <p><strong>Special:</strong> Ignores armor bonuses to Reflex Defense. Can deflect blaster bolts. Critical threat range 19-20. Requires exotic weapon proficiency.</p>","properties":["Lightsaber","Critical 19-20","Exotic","Armor-Piercing"],"ammunition":{"type":"none","current":0,"max":0},"weaponCategory":"melee","proficiency":"exotic","subcategory":"lightsaber","costNumeric":12000,"category":"lightsaber"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.weapons.weapon-lightsaber"},"swse":{"npc":{"flatAttackBonus":9,"flatDamageFormula":"2d8+5","useFlat":true}}}}],"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"import":{"source":"books","raw":{"Size":"Medium","Species":"Vultan","Nonheroic Level":0,"Class Levels":{"Noble":1,"Jedi":7,"Knight":2},"Destiny Points":0,"Force Points":3,"Dark Side Points":0,"Initiative":11,"Senses":"Perception +9","Languages":["Basic","Bocce","Bothan","Dromnyr","Durese","Huttese","Tchuukthese"],"Unassigned Languages":0,"Reflex Defense":23,"Flat-Footed Defense":22,"Fortitude Defense":22,"Will Defense":21,"Hit Points":68,"Damage Threshold":22,"Speed":"6 Squares","Melee Weapons":"Lightsaber +9 (2d8+5)","Ranged Weapons":"By Weapon +9","Base Attack Bonus":8,"Grapple":9,"Attack Options":["Weapon Finesse"],"Special Actions":["Battle Meditation","Bolster Ally"],"Force Powers":["Force Thrust","Move Object"],"Force Secrets":[],"Force Techniques":["Force Techniques : Improved Move Light Object"],"Strength":10,"Dexterity":13,"Constitution":11,"Intelligence":15,"Wisdom":9,"Charisma":10,"Talents":["Talents : Battle Meditation","Block","Bolster Ally","Deflect","Lightsaber Defense"],"Feats":["Feats : Force Sensitivity","Force Training (2)","Linguist","Skill Focus (Knowledge (Galactic Lore))","Skill Focus (Pilot)","Skill Training (Mechanics)","Weapon Finesse","Weapon Proficiency (Lightsabers)","Weapon Proficiency (Pistols)","Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)"],"Skills":["Skills : Gather Information","Initiative","Knowledge (Galactic Lore)","Mechanics","Perception","Persuasion","Pilot","Use Computer","Use the Force"],"Trained Skills":["Skills : Gather Information","Initiative","Knowledge (Galactic Lore)","Mechanics","Perception","Persuasion","Pilot","Use Computer","Use the Force"],"Species Traits":[],"Gear":"Lightsaber ( Self-Built ), Utility Belt , Jedi Robes"},"mode":"play","sourcePack":"heroic","sourceAuthority":"statblock","playReady":true,"normalizedForPlay":true,"playNormalizationVersion":1}}}}
