quares, and it loses its Dexterity bonus to its Reflex Defense and is considered Flat-Footed. These effects occur in addition to the effect of . If you spend a Force Point, the target's Speed is reduced by 4 squares or half of its normal speed, whichever is the greater reduction. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions Once per encounter, you can make a single ranged attack with a handheld weapon as a Swift Action instead of a Standard Action. However, you cannot use your remaining Actions for an attack. Extended Critical Range (Pistols) Talent created by Wikia user LilLiteralist. When you are using a Pistol, you extend the weapon's critical range by 1 (for example, 19-20 instead of 20). However, anything other than a Natural 20 is not considered an automatic hit; if you roll anything other than a Natural 20 and still miss the target, you do not score a Critical Hit.","description":"Once per encounter, when you successfully use to move a target character -1 step on the Condition Track, the target suffers a Persistent Condition requiring 4 hours of rest or a DC 25 Treat Injury check to remove. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide Prerequisite: If you successfully use , until the target moves to the normal state on the Condition Track or until the end of the encounter, the target's Speed is reduced by 2 squares, and it loses its Dexterity bonus to its Reflex Defense and is considered Flat-Footed. These effects occur in addition to the effect of . If you spend a Force Point, the target's Speed is reduced by 4 squares or half of its normal speed, whichever is the greater reduction. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions Once per encounter, you can make a single ranged attack with a handheld weapon as a Swift Action instead of a Standard Action. However, you cannot use your remaining Actions for an attack. Extended Critical Range (Pistols) Talent created by Wikia user LilLiteralist. When you are using a Pistol, you extend the weapon's critical range by 1 (for example, 19-20 instead of 20). However, anything other than a Natural 20 is not considered an automatic hit; if you roll anything other than a Natural 20 and still miss the target, you do not score a Critical Hit.","class":"Gunslinger","costNumeric":null,"category":"Gunslinger","tree":"Gunslinger","treeId":"cb6f775cd227a3e3","tags":["action-economy","condition-removal","controller","damage-reduction","defender","feat-chain","force","force-control","force-defense","force-offense","mobility","positioning","precision","ranged","striker","sustained-damage","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.debilitating_shot"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.52f51a77fd60f56f"}}},{"_id":"0213ab958016dbeb","name":"Educated","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Lineage","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Sometimes you surprise others with your skill. Once per day, you may make an Untrained skill check as though you were Trained in the Skill. Exception: you cannot use this Talent to make an Untrained Use the Force check as though you were Trained in the skill, unless you have the Force Sensitivity feat. You can select this Talent multiple times; each time you do, you can use it one additional time per day. Each time you gain a level (including the level at which you select this Talent), you receive an amount of credits equal to 5,000 x your Class Level. You can spend these credits as you see fit. The credits appear in a civilized, accessible location of your choice or in your private bank account. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Starships of the Galaxy Prerequisites: , Trained in Knowledge (Technology) You are Trained in the Mechanics skill. Additionally, when installing new systems into a Vehicle, the efficiency of your designs reduces the time it takes to install the system by 25%. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide Prerequisites: , Intelligence 13 Select a number of Skills equal to your Intelligence modifier that you are not Trained in. You may now use Trained-only applications of those Skills, and they are considered Class Skills. You are not considered Trained in those Skills for any other purposes, and must still satisfy any other requirements in order to use the skill. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook Select one type of performance, such as acting, dancing, singing, or playing a musical instrument. You gain a +5 bonus on Persuasion checks to entertain for that type of performance. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook Prerequisites: , Intelligence 13 You have the ability to acquire aid and information from a long list of people. You may reroll any Gather Information check, but the result of the reroll must be accepted, even if it is worse. Additionally, the DC for any Persuasion checks made to reduce the cost of Bribery is reduced by 5.","description":"Sometimes you surprise others with your skill. Once per day, you may make an Untrained skill check as though you were Trained in the Skill. Exception: you cannot use this Talent to make an Untrained Use the Force check as though you were Trained in the skill, unless you have the Force Sensitivity feat. You can select this Talent multiple times; each time you do, you can use it one additional time per day. Each time you gain a level (including the level at which you select this Talent), you receive an amount of credits equal to 5,000 x your Class Level. You can spend these credits as you see fit. The credits appear in a civilized, accessible location of your choice or in your private bank account. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Starships of the Galaxy Prerequisites: , Trained in Knowledge (Technology) You are Trained in the Mechanics skill. Additionally, when installing new systems into a Vehicle, the efficiency of your designs reduces the time it takes to install the system by 25%. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide Prerequisites: , Intelligence 13 Select a number of Skills equal to your Intelligence modifier that you are not Trained in. You may now use Trained-only applications of those Skills, and they are considered Class Skills. You are not considered Trained in those Skills for any other purposes, and must still satisfy any other requirements in order to use the skill. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook Select one type of performance, such as acting, dancing, singing, or playing a musical instrument. You gain a +5 bonus on Persuasion checks to entertain for that type of performance. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook Prerequisites: , Intelligence 13 You have the ability to acquire aid and information from a long list of people. You may reroll any Gather Information check, but the result of the reroll must be accepted, even if it is worse. Additionally, the DC for any Persuasion checks made to reduce the cost of Bribery is reduced by 5.","class":"Noble","costNumeric":null,"category":"Noble","tree":"Lineage","treeId":"b5bb4154688c66ab","tags":["ambush","damage-reduction","force","mechanics","noble","scaling","skills","social","striker","support"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.educated"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.3e98c9f5a4f450ff"}}},{"_id":"a37f94cce0a735f9","name":"Evasion","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Survivor","prerequisites":null,"benefit":"If hit by an area attack, take half or no damage.","description":"Take half or no damage from area attacks.","class":"Scout","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scout","tree":"Survivor","treeId":"9b06340233eb3cdd","tags":["battlefield-control","evasion","scout","striker"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.evasion"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.5400bc8cb1200624"}}},{"_id":"c7318d299ed4677a","name":"Improved Stealth","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Camouflage","prerequisites":"","benefit":"You're very good at hiding when mobile. You take no penalty on your Stealth check when moving your normal Speed. This Talent applies to Stealth checks made while Piloting a Starship (see Starship Stealth). You may choose to reroll any Stealth check, but the result of the reroll must be accepted, even if it is worse. This Talent applies to Stealth checks made while Piloting a Starship (see Starship Stealth). Prerequisite: During a Surprise Round, if you make a ranged attack against a target that is Surprised, you can Aim at the target as a Free Action. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy at War If you start your turn with Total Concealment or Total Cover from a target, during that turn you can make a Stealth check as a Swift Action, opposed by the target's Perception check. If you succeed, the target is considered Flat-Footed against you until the end of your turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy","description":"You're very good at hiding when mobile. You take no penalty on your Stealth check when moving your normal Speed. This Talent applies to Stealth checks made while Piloting a Starship (see Starship Stealth). You may choose to reroll any Stealth check, but the result of the reroll must be accepted, even if it is worse. This Talent applies to Stealth checks made while Piloting a Starship (see Starship Stealth). Prerequisite: During a Surprise Round, if you make a ranged attack against a target that is Surprised, you can Aim at the target as a Free Action. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy at War If you start your turn with Total Concealment or Total Cover from a target, during that turn you can make a Stealth check as a Swift Action, opposed by the target's Perception check. If you succeed, the target is considered Flat-Footed against you until the end of your turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy","class":"Scout","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scout","tree":"Camouflage","treeId":"3926d582d2077489","tags":["action-economy","ambush","controller","mobility","perception","piloting","positioning","ranged","scout","skills","stealth","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.improved_stealth"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.073115894cad8cf9"}}},{"_id":"a1f68dfb08cd1277","name":"Presence","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Influence","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Once per encounter, you can make a Persuasion check as a Standard Action to demand surrender from an opponent who has been reduced to one-half or less of its hit points. If your check result equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, it surrenders to you and your allies, drops any weapons it is holding, and takes no hostile actions. If the target is higher level than you, it gains a +5 bonus to its Will Defense. If you or any of your allies attack it, it no longer submits to your will and can act normally. You can only use this Talent against a particular target once per encounter. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Prerequisites: , Weaken Resolve Prerequisite: Once per round, when you deal damage equal to or greater than the target's Damage Threshold, you can make a Persuasion check as a Free Action; if the result equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, you fill the target with terror, causing it to flee from you at top speed for 1 minute. The target can't take Standard Actions, Swift Actions, or Full-Round Actions while fleeing, but the target stops fleeing and can act normally if it is wounded. As a Free Action or Reaction, the target can spend a Force Point (if it has not already spent one earlier in the round) to negate the effect. The effect is automatically negated if the target's level is equal to or higher than your Character Level. This is a Mind-Affecting fear effect. Unlike with other Mind-Affecting effects, you need only to hail a Vehicle to weaken the crew's resolve. When you deal damage that equals or exceeds a Vehicle's Damage Threshold, you may use this Talent; in addition, you may Ready an Action to use this Talent after any Gunner on your Vehicle deals damage that equals or exceeds a Vehicle's Damage Threshold. You make your check against the Vehicle's Commander; all Nonheroic crews are assumed to have a Will Defense of 10. The effect is automatically negated if the target Vehicle's Challenge Level is greater than your Heroic Level or your Vehicle's Challenge Level. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide Prerequisites: , Trained in Persuasion You get under an opponent's skin. Once per encounter, make a Persuasion check to Intimidate one creature within line of sight as a Standard Action. On a success, instead of the normal effect of an Intimidate application of the Persuasion skill, the affected creature can take only a single Swift Action on its next turn. If the target is a higher level than you, it gains a +5 bonus to its Will Defense against the Intimidate check. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide Prerequisites: , Trained in Persuasion Once per encounter, as a Reaction, you can make a Persuasion check to Intimidate one creature that is making a melee or ranged attack against you, and is within your line of sight. If you succeed, you impose a -5 penalty to that attack roll. If the target is a higher level than you, it gains a +5 bonus to its Will Defense against the Intimidate check. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook","description":"Once per encounter, you can make a Persuasion check as a Standard Action to demand surrender from an opponent who has been reduced to one-half or less of its hit points. If your check result equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, it surrenders to you and your allies, drops any weapons it is holding, and takes no hostile actions. If the target is higher level than you, it gains a +5 bonus to its Will Defense. If you or any of your allies attack it, it no longer submits to your will and can act normally. You can only use this Talent against a particular target once per encounter. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Prerequisites: , Weaken Resolve Prerequisite: Once per round, when you deal damage equal to or greater than the target's Damage Threshold, you can make a Persuasion check as a Free Action; if the result equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, you fill the target with terror, causing it to flee from you at top speed for 1 minute. The target can't take Standard Actions, Swift Actions, or Full-Round Actions while fleeing, but the target stops fleeing and can act normally if it is wounded. As a Free Action or Reaction, the target can spend a Force Point (if it has not already spent one earlier in the round) to negate the effect. The effect is automatically negated if the target's level is equal to or higher than your Character Level. This is a Mind-Affecting fear effect. Unlike with other Mind-Affecting effects, you need only to hail a Vehicle to weaken the crew's resolve. When you deal damage that equals or exceeds a Vehicle's Damage Threshold, you may use this Talent; in addition, you may Ready an Action to use this Talent after any Gunner on your Vehicle deals damage that equals or exceeds a Vehicle's Damage Threshold. You make your check against the Vehicle's Commander; all Nonheroic crews are assumed to have a Will Defense of 10. The effect is automatically negated if the target Vehicle's Challenge Level is greater than your Heroic Level or your Vehicle's Challenge Level. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide Prerequisites: , Trained in Persuasion You get under an opponent's skin. Once per encounter, make a Persuasion check to Intimidate one creature within line of sight as a Standard Action. On a success, instead of the normal effect of an Intimidate application of the Persuasion skill, the affected creature can take only a single Swift Action on its next turn. If the target is a higher level than you, it gains a +5 bonus to its Will Defense against the Intimidate check. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide Prerequisites: , Trained in Persuasion Once per encounter, as a Reaction, you can make a Persuasion check to Intimidate one creature that is making a melee or ranged attack against you, and is within your line of sight. If you succeed, you impose a -5 penalty to that attack roll. If the target is a higher level than you, it gains a +5 bonus to its Will Defense against the Intimidate check. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook","class":"Noble","costNumeric":null,"category":"Noble","tree":"Influence","treeId":"8375b9b26b679901","tags":["action-economy","damage-reduction","defender","force","force-defense","force-offense","melee","mobility","noble","positioning","ranged","skills","social","striker","support","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.presence"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.ec8f2ba706cc2c05"}}},{"_id":"fb2d1cdc17bc4bf5","name":"Skirmisher","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Misfortune","prerequisites":"","benefit":"When you move at least 2 squares before your attack and end your move in a different square from where you started, you gain a +1 bonus to all your Defenses until the start of your next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy at War Prerequisites: , Sneak Attack Whenever you would gain the benefit of the Talent and you successfully hit your opponent, you deal Sneak Attack damage in addition to the normal damage dealt by the attack. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy","description":"When you move at least 2 squares before your attack and end your move in a different square from where you started, you gain a +1 bonus to all your Defenses until the start of your next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy at War Prerequisites: , Sneak Attack Whenever you would gain the benefit of the Talent and you successfully hit your opponent, you deal Sneak Attack damage in addition to the normal damage dealt by the attack. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy","class":"Scoundrel","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scoundrel","tree":"Misfortune","treeId":"67b59e020c1660eb","tags":["controller","defender","mobility","positioning","precision","scoundrel","striker"]},"effects":[{"_id":"b27e05f0-9859-46a5-92ab-7f844073dc03","name":"Skirmisher","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.attacks","mode":2,"value":"1"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Skirmisher"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.skirmisher"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.7b23e0812d6a8985"}}},{"_id":"2b0f866d77be278b","name":"Sneak Attack","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Misfortune","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Any time your opponent is Flat-Footed or otherwise denied its Dexterity bonus to Reflex Defense, you deal an additional 1d6 points of damage with a successful melee or ranged attack. You must be within 6 squares of the target to make a with a ranged weapon. You may select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select it, your damage increases by +1d6 (Maximum +10d6). Prerequisite: You can take advantage of your adversary's distractions, no matter how momentary or fleeting. Once per turn, when you Flank a target, you can treat that target as if they were Flat-Footed for one of your attacks. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy If you succeed on a Deception check against a target's Will Defense as a Swift Action, until the start of your next turn you can move though the Threatened Area of that target as part of your Move Action without provoking an Attack of Opportunity. Each Threatened square that you move through counts as 2 squares of movement. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Point-Blank Shot You can use the Talent against a target within 12 squares, instead of within 6 squares. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide You excel at seduction through deception. If you fail a Persuasion check to change a target's Attitude, you can immediately reroll the check using your Deception skill in lieu of your Persuasion skill. You must accept the result of the reroll, even if it is worse. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide Once per encounter as a Move Action, you can attempt to seize a held, carried, or worn object from an adjacent target by making a Disarm attack, with a +10 bonus on your attack roll. If the attack succeeds, you are now holding the object, and you cannot use this Talent in place of the Disarm Action. You cannot conceal the use of this Talent from the target. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy","description":"Any time your opponent is Flat-Footed or otherwise denied its Dexterity bonus to Reflex Defense, you deal an additional 1d6 points of damage with a successful melee or ranged attack. You must be within 6 squares of the target to make a with a ranged weapon. You may select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select it, your damage increases by +1d6 (Maximum +10d6). Prerequisite: You can take advantage of your adversary's distractions, no matter how momentary or fleeting. Once per turn, when you Flank a target, you can treat that target as if they were Flat-Footed for one of your attacks. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy If you succeed on a Deception check against a target's Will Defense as a Swift Action, until the start of your next turn you can move though the Threatened Area of that target as part of your Move Action without provoking an Attack of Opportunity. Each Threatened square that you move through counts as 2 squares of movement. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Point-Blank Shot You can use the Talent against a target within 12 squares, instead of within 6 squares. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide You excel at seduction through deception. If you fail a Persuasion check to change a target's Attitude, you can immediately reroll the check using your Deception skill in lieu of your Persuasion skill. You must accept the result of the reroll, even if it is worse. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide Once per encounter as a Move Action, you can attempt to seize a held, carried, or worn object from an adjacent target by making a Disarm attack, with a +10 bonus on your attack roll. If the attack succeeds, you are now holding the object, and you cannot use this Talent in place of the Disarm Action. You cannot conceal the use of this Talent from the target. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy","class":"Scoundrel","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scoundrel","tree":"Misfortune","treeId":"67b59e020c1660eb","tags":["action-economy","battlefield-control","controller","defender","melee","mobility","positioning","precision","ranged","scaling","scoundrel","skills","social","striker"]},"effects":[{"_id":"3195415b-2276-403c-9fb1-5d323d38d31a","name":"Sneak Attack","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.damage.flatfooted","mode":2,"value":"1d6"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Sneak Attack"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.sneak_attack"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.1505abc8babeeb84"}}},{"_id":"f0b2de23ee9a86f4","name":"Spontaneous Skill","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Lineage","prerequisites":"Educated","benefit":"Once per day, make a skill check as if trained; may be used multiple times per day with separate skills.","description":"Once per day, make a trained skill check even if untrained.","class":"Noble","costNumeric":null,"category":"Noble","tree":"Lineage","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.educated"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"b5bb4154688c66ab","tags":["feat-chain","noble","scaling","striker","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.spontaneous_skill"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.85fddc83428358ae"}}},{"_id":"164eee3a39bec92d","name":"Weaken Resolve","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Influence","prerequisites":"","benefit":"As , except that the target doesn't stop fleeing from you if it is wounded.","description":"As , except that the target doesn't stop fleeing from you if it is wounded.","class":"Noble","costNumeric":null,"category":"Noble","tree":"Influence","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.presence"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"8375b9b26b679901","tags":["noble","striker"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.weaken_resolve"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.28c306c37ccb9fcf"}}},{"_id":"f85b673d85ec6d