ined in one additional skill. You may take this feat multiple times.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":88,"tags":["noble","non-force","scaling","scoundrel","striker"],"bonus_feat_for":["Noble","Scoundrel"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{"value":"You become <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Trained\" title=\"Trained\">Trained</a> in one Class Skill."}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.a9f6de36f24ef202"}}},{"_id":"949ccdea2da57245","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Pistols)","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"You are proficient with pistols and do not take the -5 penalty when using them.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["non-force","ranged","scoundrel","scout","soldier"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier","Scout","Scoundrel"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{}},"effects":[{"_id":"04733e85-193e-4f4b-8792-c359083557d1","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Pistols)","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Weapon Proficiency (Pistols)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Pistols)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.e5d361d01d1b44e4"}}},{"_id":"a39b68ebcf36a321","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"You are proficient with simple weapons and do not take the -5 penalty when using them.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["noble","non-force","scoundrel","scout","soldier"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier","Scout","Scoundrel","Noble"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{}},"effects":[{"_id":"220daaa7-e1b5-440d-98cd-10f5e586ef8b","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.2d680cc46a7972da"}}},{"_id":"dfac946f699256ab","name":"Disruptive","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Misfortune","prerequisites":"","benefit":"As a Standard Action, you can do or say something that catches your enemies off guard. All opponents within 6 squares of you, and within your line of sight take a -2 penalty to their Defenses until the start of your next turn. The penalty is negated if line of sight is broken. This Talent has a range of 6 squares at Starship Scale. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy at War Prerequisites: , Walk the Line You can create opportunities to chip away at our opponents' defenses. You can use each of the following actions once per encounter as a Standard Action: Create Opening: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any target within your Range. If you damage the target, the target takes a -5 penalty to their Reflex Defense until the start of your next turn. Crippling Attack: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any target within your Range. Until the start of your next turn, the target takes a -2 penalty to their base speed. Vicious Attack: Make a melee or ranged attack within your Range against two opponents that are within 2 squares of each other. Make separate attack rolls at a -5 penalty against each target, but roll damage once only. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy You can fill your opponent with doubt by making a Persuasion check as a Standard Action against a single target that can hear and understand you within 12 squares of you. If your check result equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, the target takes a -2 penalty to its base speed, and if the target takes a Standard Action, it must also spend its Swift Action. This penalty lasts until the end of the target's next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy","description":"As a Standard Action, you can do or say something that catches your enemies off guard. All opponents within 6 squares of you, and within your line of sight take a -2 penalty to their Defenses until the start of your next turn. The penalty is negated if line of sight is broken. This Talent has a range of 6 squares at Starship Scale. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy at War Prerequisites: , Walk the Line You can create opportunities to chip away at our opponents' defenses. You can use each of the following actions once per encounter as a Standard Action: Create Opening: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any target within your Range. If you damage the target, the target takes a -5 penalty to their Reflex Defense until the start of your next turn. Crippling Attack: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any target within your Range. Until the start of your next turn, the target takes a -2 penalty to their base speed. Vicious Attack: Make a melee or ranged attack within your Range against two opponents that are within 2 squares of each other. Make separate attack rolls at a -5 penalty against each target, but roll damage once only. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy You can fill your opponent with doubt by making a Persuasion check as a Standard Action against a single target that can hear and understand you within 12 squares of you. If your check result equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, the target takes a -2 penalty to its base speed, and if the target takes a Standard Action, it must also spend its Swift Action. This penalty lasts until the end of the target's next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy","class":"Scoundrel","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scoundrel","tree":"Misfortune","treeId":"67b59e020c1660eb","tags":["action-economy","defender","melee","mobility","positioning","ranged","scaling","scoundrel","skills","social","striker"]},"effects":[{"_id":"4eefbe8a-47cc-4cee-a02a-7c11b76bd6b5","name":"Disruptive","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.morale.bonuses_suppressed","mode":5,"value":"true"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Disruptive"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.disruptive"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.91b335f8565b90ef"}}},{"_id":"68010801abf8d62c","name":"Knack","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Fortune","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Once per day, you can reroll an attack roll and take the better result. You can select this Talent multiple times; each time you select this Talent, you can use it one additional time per day. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Lucky Shot You are possessed of incredible luck and an uncanny ability to succeed where others would fail. You can use each of the following actions once per encounter as a Standard Action: Elude Enemy: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any target within your Range. If you damage the target, you gain a +2 bonus to your Reflex Defense against this target until the beginning of your next turn. Escape: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any target within your Range. If that target successfully damages you before the start of your next turn, you can immediately move 2 squares as a Reaction. This movement does not provoke Attacks of Opportunity. Make your Own Luck: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any target within your Range. If you miss this target, you gain a +2 bonus on your next attack roll. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Once per encounter, as a Reaction, you become immune to all Mind-Affecting effects until the end of your next turn (you can choose to ignore this for beneficial effects). Any Mind-Affecting effects currently afflicting you are also removed, though you can choose to retain any beneficial effects you currently have. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide Prerequisite: A successful hit against you is mitigated by an item you just happen to be wearing or carrying, or glances off your armor or clothing in just the right way. Once per encounter, as a Reaction, you can negate the damage from a single attack that would normally reduce you to 0 Hit Points. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Lucky Shot When making a ranged attack against a target with Cover, you can choose to reduce the benefit of that target's Cover by one step, from Improved Cover to Cover, or Cover to no Cover. You deal only half damage with this attack. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Lucky Shot Once per encounter, you can consider any single d20 roll of 16 or higher to be a Natural 20. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Lucky Shot Once per encounter, you can reroll the damage of one attack, keeping the better of the two results. Gambler's Fortune Talent data created by Sterling Hershey (source). Prerequisites: , Trained in Chosen Skill Select one of the following Skills: Knowledge (Any), Mechanics, Perception, or Use Computer. When making a reroll for that Skill, you may keep the better result.","description":"Once per day, you can reroll an attack roll and take the better result. You can select this Talent multiple times; each time you select this Talent, you can use it one additional time per day. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Lucky Shot You are possessed of incredible luck and an uncanny ability to succeed where others would fail. You can use each of the following actions once per encounter as a Standard Action: Elude Enemy: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any target within your Range. If you damage the target, you gain a +2 bonus to your Reflex Defense against this target until the beginning of your next turn. Escape: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any target within your Range. If that target successfully damages you before the start of your next turn, you can immediately move 2 squares as a Reaction. This movement does not provoke Attacks of Opportunity. Make your Own Luck: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any target within your Range. If you miss this target, you gain a +2 bonus on your next attack roll. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Once per encounter, as a Reaction, you become immune to all Mind-Affecting effects until the end of your next turn (you can choose to ignore this for beneficial effects). Any Mind-Affecting effects currently afflicting you are also removed, though you can choose to retain any beneficial effects you currently have. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide Prerequisite: A successful hit against you is mitigated by an item you just happen to be wearing or carrying, or glances off your armor or clothing in just the right way. Once per encounter, as a Reaction, you can negate the damage from a single attack that would normally reduce you to 0 Hit Points. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Lucky Shot When making a ranged attack against a target with Cover, you can choose to reduce the benefit of that target's Cover by one step, from Improved Cover to Cover, or Cover to no Cover. You deal only half damage with this attack. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Lucky Shot Once per encounter, you can consider any single d20 roll of 16 or higher to be a Natural 20. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Lucky Shot Once per encounter, you can reroll the damage of one attack, keeping the better of the two results. Gambler's Fortune Talent data created by Sterling Hershey (source). Prerequisites: , Trained in Chosen Skill Select one of the following Skills: Knowledge (Any), Mechanics, Perception, or Use Computer. When making a reroll for that Skill, you may keep the better result.","class":"Scoundrel","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scoundrel","tree":"Fortune","treeId":"cee9b9398682b7d0","tags":["action-economy","armor","controller","damage-reduction","defender","mechanics","melee","mobility","perception","positioning","ranged","scaling","scoundrel","skills","slicing","striker","support"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.knack"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.ac6baadb9d65ff7f"}}},{"_id":"f6650673b338d417","name":"Force Thrust","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telekinetic","useTheForce":20,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One creature or object","duration":"Instantaneous","effect":"<p>You violently push your target away with telekinetic force. The target is pushed 6 squares away from you and knocked prone, taking 2d6 damage.</p>","special":"<p>If the target hits an obstacle during the push, they take an additional 1d6 damage per 2 squares not traveled.</p>","descriptor":["Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":97,"tags":["attack","movement","telekinetic","forced-movement"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.d51bf85903366b6b"}}},{"_id":"7f64c0351fbcaf82","name":"Rebuke","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telepathic","useTheForce":20,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One Force-sensitive creature","duration":"1 round","effect":"<p>You overwhelm a Force user with a powerful Force presence. If the target is Force-sensitive, they must make a Will save (DC = your UTF check) or be dazed for 1 round.</p>","special":"<p>This power only affects Force-sensitive creatures.</p>","descriptor":["Mind-Affecting"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":99,"tags":["debuff","force-user","daze"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.390074b44aedfa2a"}}},{"_id":"efcfb1d0c6b00918","name":"Unarmed","type":"weapon","img":"icons/svg/sword.svg","system":{"damage":"1d4+1","damageType":"kinetic","attackBonus":0,"attackAttribute":"str","range":"melee","weight":1,"cost":0,"equipped":true,"description":"","properties":[],"ammunition":{"type":"none","current":0,"max":0},"weaponCategory":"simple","proficiency":"simple","subcategory":""},"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"placeholder":true,"npc":{"flatAttackBonus":4,"flatDamageFormula":"1d4+1","useFlat":true}}}},{"_id":"5ae3cdd6a052884a","name":"Lightsaber -1 (2d8 ())","type":"weapon","img":"icons/svg/sword.svg","system":{"damage":"1d4","damageType":"kinetic","attackBonus":0,"attackAttribute":"str","range":"melee","weight":1,"cost":0,"equipped":true,"description":"","properties":[],"ammunition":{"type":"none","current":0,"max":0},"weaponCategory":"simple","proficiency":"simple","subcategory":""},"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"placeholder":true,"unresolved":"Lightsaber -1","npc"