ight Melee Weapons and <a href=\"/wiki/Lightsabers\" title=\"Lightsabers\">Lightsabers</a>."},"prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"bab","min":1}],"_source":"canonical-csv"}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.252b67d6e31c377e"}}},{"_id":"b85ceb324eedcc98","name":"Weapon Focus","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"You gain a +1 bonus on attack rolls with the selected weapon group.","prerequisite":"Proficient with selected weapon group","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":88,"tags":["feat-chain","non-force","soldier","striker"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{"value":"+1 bonus on attack rolls with chosen weapon."}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.c41814601364b643"}}},{"_id":"3372d7572d9f81ea","name":"Weapon Proficiency","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"Ignore -5 penalty on attack rolls with weapons of a particular type.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["non-force"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{"value":"Ignore -5 penalty on attack rolls with weapons of a particular type."}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.ecc2471ac96ec2d4"}}},{"_id":"2e41c87c53257901","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"You are proficient with simple weapons and do not take the -5 penalty when using them.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["noble","non-force","scoundrel","scout","soldier"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier","Scout","Scoundrel","Noble"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{}},"effects":[{"_id":"220daaa7-e1b5-440d-98cd-10f5e586ef8b","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.2d680cc46a7972da"}}},{"_id":"790a83c6a74b3479","name":"Devastating Power","type":"feat","img":"systems/foundryvtt-swse/assets/icons/force-secret.png","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"When using a Force Power that deals damage, you can spend a Force Point to increase the Power's damage dice by 50%.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Core","page":0,"tags":["force-secret"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":"<p><strong>Cost:</strong> Force Point or Destiny Point</p><p>When using a Force Power that deals damage, you can spend a Force Point to increase the Power's damage dice by 50%.</p><p>Alternatively, you can spend a Destiny Point to double the amount of damage dice.</p>","cost":"Force Point or Destiny Point","alternativeCost":"Alternatively, you can spend a Destiny Point to double the amount of damage dice."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcesecrets.996848a2e0c0ac4f"}}},{"_id":"c18a2b66033014ae","name":"Distant Power","type":"feat","img":"systems/foundryvtt-swse/assets/icons/force-secret.png","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"When using a Force Power that has a range expressed numerically, you can spend a Force Point to multiply the range by 10.","prerequisite":"","special":"This Force Secret does not remove the line of sight requirements.","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Core","page":0,"tags":["force-secret"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":"<p><strong>Cost:</strong> Force Point or Destiny Point</p><p>When using a Force Power that has a range expressed numerically, you can spend a Force Point to multiply the range by 10.</p><p>Alternatively, you can spend a Destiny Point to increase the range to anywhere in the same Star System.</p><p><strong>Special:</strong> This Force Secret does not remove the line of sight requirements.</p>","cost":"Force Point or Destiny Point","alternativeCost":"Alternatively, you can spend a Destiny Point to increase the range to anywhere in the same Star System."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcesecrets.43f9645eabce838e"}}},{"_id":"7e26036a0245ccfc","name":"Multitarget Power","type":"feat","img":"systems/foundryvtt-swse/assets/icons/force-secret.png","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"When using a Force Power that affects a single target, you can spend a Force Point to affect one additional target.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Core","page":0,"tags":["force-secret"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":"<p><strong>Cost:</strong> Force Point or Destiny Point</p><p>When using a Force Power that affects a single target, you can spend a Force Point to affect one additional target.</p><p>Alternatively, you can spend a Destiny Point to affect one target per four Character Levels.</p>","cost":"Force Point or Destiny Point","alternativeCost":"Alternatively, you can spend a Destiny Point to affect one target per four Character Levels."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcesecrets.af908ace9a361603"}}},{"_id":"952fdea8ff211f63","name":"Quicken Power","type":"feat","img":"systems/foundryvtt-swse/assets/icons/force-secret.png","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"When using a Force Power that requires a Standard Action or Move Action to activate, you can spend a Force Point to activate the Force Power as a Swift Action instead.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Core","page":0,"tags":["force-secret"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":"<p><strong>Cost:</strong> Force Point or Destiny Point</p><p>When using a Force Power that requires a Standard Action or Move Action to activate, you can spend a Force Point to activate the Force Power as a Swift Action instead.</p><p>Alternatively, you can spend a Destiny Point to activate the Force Power as a Reaction instead.</p>","cost":"Force Point or Destiny Point","alternativeCost":"Alternatively, you can spend a Destiny Point to activate the Force Power as a Reaction instead."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcesecrets.52bf7b9a1a41de2b"}}},{"_id":"d205f074abc4b859","name":"Improved Sense Force","type":"feat","img":"systems/foundryvtt-swse/assets/icons/force-technique.png","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"You may use the Sense Force ability of the Use the Force Skill as a Move Action rather than a Full-Round Action.","prerequisite":"Sense Force","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Core","page":0,"tags":["force-technique"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"description":"<p>You may use the Sense Force ability of the Use the Force Skill as a Move Action rather than a Full-Round Action.</p><p><strong>Related Power:</strong> Sense Force</p><p><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Sense Force</p>","relatedPower":"Sense Force"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcetechniques.ad67b8f3959860f2"}}},{"_id":"19a9a17ab2c62d5b","name":"Force Point Recovery","type":"feat","img":"systems/foundryvtt-swse/assets/icons/force-technique.png","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"At the end of an encounter, you automatically recover 1 Force Point spent during the encounter.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Core","page":0,"tags":["force-technique"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"description":"<p>At the end of an encounter, you automatically recover 1 Force Point spent during the encounter.</p>","relatedPower":""},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcetechniques.056ab39b3ab9df10"}}},{"_id":"4970ab265fe27542","name":"Force Power Mastery","type":"feat","img":"systems/foundryvtt-swse/assets/icons/force-technique.png","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"Choose a single Force Power. You may Take 10 on Use the Force checks to activate this Force Power even when distracted or threatened.","prerequisite":"","special":"You may select this Force Technique multiple times; each time you select this Force Technique, it applies to a different Force Power.","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Core","page":0,"tags":["force-technique"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"description":"<p>Choose a single Force Power. You may Take 10 on Use the Force checks to activate this Force Power even when distracted or threatened.</p><p><strong>Special:</strong> You may select this Force Technique multiple times; each time you select this Force Technique, it applies to a different Force Power.</p>","relatedPower":""},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcetechniques.07cea7e3e8b21d69"}}},{"_id":"8fd4910f666583e1","name":"Ataru","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Lightsaber Forms","prerequisites":null,"benefit":"May apply Dexterity modifier to damage or double Dexterity bonus if two-handed instead of Strength.","description":"Add Dexterity modifier to damage, or double Dexterity bonus if two-handed, instead of Strength.","class":"Jedi Knight","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi Knight","tree":"Lightsaber Forms","treeId":"2bc2572e852832e4","tags":["jedi","lightsaber","melee","striker"]},"effects":[{"_id":"51d31037-d4be-4c4d-a5e5-b405e21aa08a","name":"Ataru - Apply DEX to Damage","icon":"icons/svg/wind.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.abilities.dex.applyToDamage","mode":5,"value":"true","priority":20}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Ataru"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.ataru"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.0b3f4075ed84aee0"}}},{"_id":"fc1e34996340979d","name":"Block","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Sith Alchemy","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Create Sith Amulet: You can create a Sith Amulet. The creation of a Sith Amulet requires 25,000 credits' worth of gems and other raw materials, and the creation process takes 1 week (this work can be spread out over several sessions and need not be consecutive). At the end of the process, you must spend a Force Point to complete the Sith Amulet, after which point it functions exactly as a Sith Amulet. Create Sith Armor: You can transform a suit of normal Battle Armor into the Dark Armor worn by Sith Lords. You must have a suit of Battle Armor to transform into the Dark Armor (Light Battle Armor becomes Light Dark Armor, Battle Armor becomes Dark Armor, and Heavy Battle Armor becomes Heavy Dark Armor). The transformation process takes 1 day for Light Dark Armor, 2 days for Dark Armor, and 3 days for Heavy Dark Armor. You must spend a Force Point at the end of the creation process to complete the Armor's transformation. Create Sith Talisman: You can spend a Force Point to imbue a portable object with the Dark Side, creating a Sith Talisman that provides offensive strength to a Force Power. Creating the Sith Talisman takes a Full-Round Action. While you wear or carry the Sith Talisman on your person, you add 1d6 to your damage with Force Powers. You increase your Dark Side Score by 1 when you first wear or carry a Sith Talisman. You can have only one Sith Talisman active at any given time, and if it is destroyed, you cannot create another one for 24 hours. Create Sith Weapon: You can alchemically treat a Simple Weapon (Melee) or an Advanced Melee Weapon, turning it into a Sith Weapon. You must spend a Force Point and spend 1 hour imbuing the Weapon with the properties of a Sith Alchemical Weapon (see also: Sith Alchemical Weapon Template). A Lightsaber does not ignore the Sith Weapon's DR, and characters who are proficient in the Weapon's use can treat it as a Lightsaber for the purposes of the , Deflect, and Redirect Shot Talents (and any Talents that have these Talents as a prerequisite). Additionally, as a Swift Action, the wielder of a Sith Weapon can spend a Force Point to gain a bonus equal to their Dark Side Score to the damage of their next attack made with the Weapon before the end of the encounter. This increases the wielder's Dark Side Score by 1.","description":"Create Sith Amulet: You can create a Sith Amulet. The creation of a Sith Amulet requires 25,000 credits' worth of gems and other raw materials, and the creation process takes 1 week (this work can be spread out over several sessions and need not be consecutive). At the end of the process, you must spend a Force Point to complete the Sith Amulet, after which point it functions exactly as a Sith Amulet. Create Sith Armor: You can transform a suit of normal Battle Armor into the Dark Armor worn by Sith Lords. You must have a suit of Battle Armor to transform into the Dark Armor (Light Battle Armor becomes Light Dark Armor, Battle Armor becomes Dark Armor, and Heavy Battle Armor becomes Heavy Dark Armor). The transformation process takes 1 day for Light Dark Armor, 2 days for Dark Armor, and 3 days for Heavy Dark Armor. You must spend a Force Point at the end of the creation process to complete the Armor's transformation. Create Sith Talisman: You can spend a Force Point to imbue a portable object with the Dark Side, creating a Sith Talisman that provides offensive strength to a Force Power. Creating the Sith Talisman takes a Full-Round Action. While you wear or carry the Sith Talisman on your person, you add 1d6 to your damage with Force Powers. You increase your Dark Side Score by 1 when you first wear or carry a Sith Talisman. You can have only one Sith Talisman active at any given time, and if it is destroyed, you cannot create another one for 24 hours. Create Sith Weapon: You can alchemically treat a Simple Weapon (Melee) or an Advanced Melee Weapon, turning it into a Sith Weapon. You must spend a Force Point and spend 1 hour imbuing the Weapon with the properties of a Sith Alchemical Weapon (see also: Sith Alchemical Weapon Template). A Lightsaber does not ignore the Sith Weapon's DR, and characters who are proficient in the Weapon's use can treat it as a Lightsaber for the purposes of the , Deflect, and Redirect Shot Talents (and any Talents that have these Talents as a prerequisite). Additionally, as a Swift Action, the wielder of a Sith Weapon can spend a Force Point to gain a bonus equal to their Dark Side Score to the damage of their next attack made with the Weapon before the end of the encounter. This increases the wielder's Dark Side Score by 1.","class":"Jedi","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","tree":"Sith Alchemy","treeId":"a67faf2ae089ab5d","tags":["action-economy","armor","dark-side","defender","force","force-offense","jedi","lightsaber","melee","mobility","ranged","striker","support","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.block"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.9379daa94a228c04"}}},{"_id":"a44add947d3a2839","name":"Deflect","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Lightsaber Forms","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Redirect Shot","description":"Redirect Shot","class":"Jedi","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","tree":"Lightsaber Forms","treeId":"2bc2572e852832e4","tags":["jedi","lightsaber","melee","ranged"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.deflect"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.72c644f7a09b1186"}}},{"_id":"c932ddd40121be3c","name":"Force Perception","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Sense","prerequisites":"","benefit":"You may spend a Force Point to reroll an Initiative check, keeping the better of the two rolls. Additionally, if you roll a natural 20 on the Initiative check reroll, you immediately regain the Force Point spent to activate this talent. Prerequisite: By focusing on a specific creature in your line of sight, you can gauge how strong in The Force they are. This takes a Standard Action and requires a Use the Force check. If your check result meets or beats the target's Will Defense, you know whether or not they have the Force Sensitivity feat, you know how many Force Powers they know (but not which ones specifically), and you know how many Force Points they currently have. Prerequisites: , Farseeing See also: On the Force, Visions, and Discretion Whenever you use the Farseeing Force Power, you can spend a Force Point as a Swift Action to see into the target's past or future instead of the present. You declare how far into the target's past or future you wish to look, up to a maximum of 1 year per your Character Level. Any information gained about a target's future is subject to change, depending on whether steps are taken to alter that future. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide As a Standard Action, you can spend a Force Point to ignore all Concealment for 1 minute. Prerequisites: , Farseeing As a Swift Action, you can peer into the future in search of signs of danger, removing one use of the Farseeing Force Power from your active Force Power Suite (as though you had just activated the Force Power). Any time before the end of your next turn when you are the target of an attack or Force Power, you can force your attacker to reroll the attack roll (or Use the Force check) against you, keeping the second result. This counts as using the Farseeing Force Power against the attacker, but this Talent replaces the normal rules and effect of that Force Power. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide Prerequisites: , Farseeing When you use the Farseeing Force Power, you can choose to target an object you hold instead of a character or creature. You can look into the targeted item's past, up to a maximum of 5 years per your Character Level. Any information gained about the object's past is based on the thoughts and emotions of the person holding or carrying the object at the time you perceive, which can skew the results of the vision. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide You can spend a Force Point to gain Low-Light Vision (see Visibility) for 1 minute or until the end of the encounter, whichever is longer. Homebrew Reference Book: Clone Wars Saga Edition Fan Sourcebook - Jedi Padawans Prerequisites: Once per encounter, you may spend a Force Point to gain a +1 insight bonus to your Reflex Defense and Will Defense for the remainder of the encounter, or until you are knocked unconscious.","description":"You may spend a Force Point to reroll an Initiative check, keeping the better of the two rolls. Additionally, if you roll a natural 20 on the Initiative check reroll, you immediately regain the Force Point spent to activate this talent. Prerequisite: By focusing on a specific creature in your line of sight, you can gauge how strong in The Force they are. This takes a Standard Action and requires a Use the Force check. If your check result meets or beats the target's Will Defense, you know whether or not they have the Force Sensitivity feat, you know how many Force Powers they know (but not which ones specifically), and you know how many Force Points they currently have. Prerequisites: , Farseeing See also: On the Force, Visions, and Discretion Whenever you use the Farseeing Force Power, you can spend a Force Point as a Swift Action to see into the target's past or future instead of the present. You declare how far into the target's past or future you wish to look, up to a maximum of 1 year per your Character Level. Any information gained about a target's future is subject to change, depending on whether steps are taken to alter that future. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide As a Standard Action, you can spend a Force Point to ignore all Concealment for 1 minute. Prerequisites: , Farseeing As a Swift Action, you can peer into the future in search of signs of danger, removing one use of the Farseeing Force Power from your active Force Power Suite (as though you had just activated the Force Power). Any time before the end of your next turn when you are the target of an attack or Force Power, you can force your attacker to reroll the attack roll (or Use the Force check) against you, keeping the second result. This counts as using the Farseeing Force Power against the attacker, but this Talent replaces the normal rules and effect of that Force Power. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide Prerequisites: , Farseeing When you use the Farseeing Force Power, you can choose to target an object you hold instead of a character or creature. You can look into the targeted item's past, up to a maximum of 5 years per your Character Level. Any information gained about the object's past is based on the thoughts and emotions of the person holding or carrying the object at the time you perceive, which can skew the results of the vision. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide You can spend a Force Point to gain Low-Light Vision (see Visibility) for 1 minute or until the end of the encounter, whichever is longer. Homebrew Reference Book: Clone Wars Saga Edition Fan Sourcebook - Jedi Padawans Prerequisites: Once per encounter, you may spend a Force Point to gain a +1 insight bonus to your Reflex Defense and Will Defense for the remainder of the encounter, or until you are knocked unconscious.","costNumeric":null,"tree":"Sense","treeId":"d6b4331c0e31f7e3","tags":["action-economy","defender","force","force-defense","force-offense","light-side","mobility","scout","skills","stealth","striker","support"]},"effects":[{"name":"Force Perception (Trained)","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.skills.perception.trained","mode":5,"value":"true"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Force Perception","effectType":"skill-trained"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.force_perception"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.a358402a9fc26c02"}}},{"_id":"341f7c44de3d9298","name":"Foresight","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Sense","prerequisites":"Force Perception","benefit":"Reroll Initiative; on a natural 20, regain a Force Point.","description":"You may reroll Initiative checks; on a natural 20, regain a Force Point.","costNumeric":null,"tree":"Sense","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.force_perception"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"d6b4331c0e31f7e3","tags":["feat-chain","force","scout","skills","talent-chain"]},"effects":[{"_id":"b419da31-d0ef-4d1d-8c11-7aaf9f1bab1c","name":"Foresight","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.initiative","mode":5,"value":"reroll"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Foresight"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.foresight"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.d10cdcba4faae7bb"}}},{"_id":"ac13de2461e050b9","name":"Multiattack Proficiency (Lightsabers) (2)","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/aura.svg","system":{"tree":"Unknown","prerequisite":"","benefit":"","special":"","uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perEncounter":false,"perDay":false}},"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"placeholder":true,"unresolved":"Multiattack Proficiency"}}},{"_id":"a388f3c8108d3225","name":"Redirect Shot","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Lightsaber Forms","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Whenever you redirect a deflected blaster bolt (see the Talent), you gain a +5 bonus on your ranged attack roll.","description":"Whenever you redirect a deflected blaster bolt (see the Talent), you gain a +5 bonus on your ranged attack roll.","class":"Jedi","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","tree":"Lightsaber Forms","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.deflect"},{"type":"bab","min":5}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"2bc2572e852832e4","tags":["jedi","lightsaber","melee","positioning","ranged","striker"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.redirect_shot"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.941c1dfd00e697da"}}},{"_id":"b82af4b231ed86a9","name":"Severing Strike","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Duelist","prerequisites":null,"benefit":"If you deal damage exceeding current HP and threshold, deal half damage and sever (special effect) while moving down the track.","description":"If damage exceeds the target's current hit points and damage threshold, deal half damage again, move the target down the condition track, and sever a limb.","class":"Jedi Knight","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi Knight","tree":"Duelist","treeId":"b3c5d90b5036f39b","tags":["jedi","striker"]},"effects":[{"_id":"8a7d9568-c68f-4b0e-a64a-0064e0dd2330","name":"Severing Strike","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.damage.limb_loss","mode":5,"value":"true"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Severing Strike"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.severing_strike"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.efd3308a8ccc22c6"}}},{"_id":"8985a64e08ad55ec","name":"Skilled Advisor","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Jedi Archivist","prerequisites":"","benefit":"You can Aid Another on the Knowledge checks of an ally within 6 squares of you as a Reaction for Knowledge skills you are Trained in. You can make a Use the Force check in place of a Knowledge check for any Knowledge skill you are not Trained in. You are considered Trained in that Knowledge skill for the purposes of using this Talent. If you are entitled to a Knowledge check reroll, you can reroll your Use the Force check instead (subject to the same circumstances and limitations). Prerequisite: When you use the Talent, the ally you aid gains one temporary Force Point at the end of their next turn. If the Force Point is not spent before the end of the encounter, it is lost. As a Swift Action, you can reroll a Knowledge check and keep the better of the two results. This can be used with any Knowledge skill you are Trained in.","description":"You can Aid Another on the Knowledge checks of an ally within 6 squares of you as a Reaction for Knowledge skills you are Trained in. You can make a Use the Force check in place of a Knowledge check for any Knowledge skill you are not Trained in. You are considered Trained in that Knowledge skill for the purposes of using this Talent. If you are entitled to a Knowledge check reroll, you can reroll your Use the Force check instead (subject to the same circumstances and limitations). Prerequisite: When you use the Talent, the ally you aid gains one temporary Force Point at the end of their next turn. If the Force Point is not spent before the end of the encounter, it is lost. As a Swift Action, you can reroll a Knowledge check and keep the better of the two results. This can be used with any Knowledge skill you are Trained in.","class":"Jedi","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","tree":"Jedi Archivist","treeId":"152047d6ab7896ad","tags":["action-economy","force","jedi","light-side","mobility","positioning","striker","support"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.skilled_advisor"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.35cbdbe9c91ba1d0"}}},{"_id":"3d94ba5147fd666d","name":"Visions","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Keetael","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Prerequisites: The long-lived Draethos are particularly adept at searching and understanding the past. When using Farseeing to look into the past, reduce your DC numbers by half. Also, you are able to see everything within 6 squares of your target clearly without spending a Force Point.","description":"Prerequisites: The long-lived Draethos are particularly adept at searching and understanding the past. When using Farseeing to look into the past, reduce your DC numbers by half. Also, you are able to see everything within 6 squares of your target clearly without spending a Force Point.","costNumeric":null,"tree":"Keetael","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.force_perception"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"dad3c0da191748c1","tags":["damage-reduction","force","positioning"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.visions"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.da12fc505efc5eea"}}},{"_id":"a6d9bffe203d1993","name":"Battle Strike","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"telekinetic","useTheForce":15,"time":"Swift Action","range":"Personal","target":"You","duration":"1 round","effect":"<p>You channel the Force to enhance your next melee attack. Your next melee attack this round gains a +1d6 bonus to damage.</p>","special":"<p>This bonus damage is Force damage and bypasses Damage Reduction.</p>","descriptor":["Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":94,"tags":["enhancement","damage","melee"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":2,"max":2},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.f177dc6d65f76de9"}}},{"_id":"2042fba905b223df","name":"Farseeing","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telepathic","useTheForce":20,"time":"1 minute","range":"Unlimited","target":"Special","duration":"Concentration","effect":"<p>You peer through the Force to see distant locations or events. You can observe a place you've been before or a person you know, regardless of distance.</p>","special":"<p>The GM may require additional checks for very distant or obscured visions.</p>","descriptor":["Mind-Affecting","Scrying"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":true,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":95,"tags":["utility","divination","scrying"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.0419ecb55f011f81"}}},{"_id":"07904d823085dfbe","name":"Force Disarm","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"telekinetic","useTheForce":15,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One creature","duration":"Instantaneous","effect":"<p>You use telekinetic force to wrench a weapon or object from your target's grasp. Make a Use the Force check opposed by the target's Strength check or Will Defense (whichever is higher).</p>","special":"<p>On success, the target drops one held object of your choice.</p>","descriptor":["Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":96,"tags":["combat","disarm","telekinetic"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.18f33f87a1ebee74"}}},{"_id":"93986f8318e689df","name":"Force Slam","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telekinetic","useTheForce":20,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One creature or object","duration":"Instantaneous","effect":"<p>You use telekinetic force to violently slam your target against a surface. The target takes 4d6 damage and is knocked prone.</p>","special":"<p>The target must be within 6 squares of a solid surface (wall, floor, ceiling).</p>","descriptor":["Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":97,"tags":["attack","damage","telekinetic","prone"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":2,"max":2},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.462a6c23e00c4dfc"}}},{"_id":"1aa372e19dc9bae5","name":"Force Thrust","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telekinetic","useTheForce":20,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One creature or object","duration":"Instantaneous","effect":"<p>You violently push your target away with telekinetic force. The target is pushed 6 squares away from you and knocked prone, taking 2d6 damage.</p>","special":"<p>If the target hits an obstacle during the push, they take an additional 1d6 damage per 2 squares not traveled.</p>","descriptor":["Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":97,"tags":["attack","movement","telekinetic","forced-movement"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.d51bf85903366b6b"}}},{"_id":"447c1f437f4813dd","name":"Mind Trick","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"telepathic","useTheForce":15,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One creature","duration":"1 minute or until completed","effect":"<p>You influence a weak mind to believe what you tell them or follow a simple suggestion. The target must make a Will save (DC = your UTF check) or be affected.</p>","special":"<p>The suggestion must be reasonable and the target must be able to understand you.</p>","descriptor":["Mind-Affecting"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":98,"tags":["mind-control","suggestion","social"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":2,"max":2},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.e6649f366d6c5737"}}},{"_id":"99f39e57decc06d9","name":"Move Object","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telekinetic","useTheForce":15,"time":"Standard Action","range":"12 squares","target":"One object or creature","duration":"Concentration","effect":"<p>You move objects or creatures through the air using telekinesis. The maximum size/weight you can move depends on your Use the Force check result.</p>","special":"<p>Unwilling creatures can make a Will save (DC = your UTF check) to resist being moved.</p>","descriptor":["Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[{"dc":15,"effect":"Medium (50 kg)","description":"Move objects up to Medium size or 50 kg"},{"dc":20,"effect":"Large (250 kg)","description":"Move objects up to Large size or 250 kg"},{"dc":25,"effect":"Huge (1 ton)","description":"Move objects up to Huge size or 1 metric ton"},{"dc":30,"effect":"Gargantuan (5 tons)","description":"Move objects up to Gargantuan size or 5 metric tons"},{"dc":35,"effect":"Colossal (20 tons)","description":"Move objects up to Colossal size or 20 metric tons (starfighter-sized)"}],"maintainable":true,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":98,"tags":["telekinetic","movement","utility"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":2,"max":2},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.289013a32bd179ad"}}},{"_id":"5fe358e4f20cdf1c","name":"Negate Energy","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telekinetic","useTheForce":20,"time":"Reaction","range":"Personal or touch","target":"You or one creature","duration":"Instantaneous","effect":"<p>You use the Force to absorb or deflect energy damage. The target gains energy resistance 20 against one energy attack.</p>","special":"<p>This power can be used as a Reaction when you or an ally is targeted by an energy attack.</p>","descriptor":["Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":99,"tags":["defense","energy-resistance","protection"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.be1ae263c498af3b"}}},{"_id":"79e9b97c4c15051b","name":"Rebuke","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telepathic","useTheForce":20,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One Force-sensitive creature","duration":"1 round","effect":"<p>You overwhelm a Force user with a powerful Force presence. If the target is Force-sensitive, they must make a Will save (DC = your UTF check) or be dazed for 1 round.</p>","special":"<p>This power only affects Force-sensitive creatures.</p>","descriptor":["Mind-Affecting"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":99,"tags":["debuff","force-user","daze"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":3,"max":3},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.390074b44aedfa2a"}}},{"_id":"19f168adee498ca1","name":"Surge","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"vital","useTheForce":15,"time":"Swift Action","range":"Personal","target":"You","duration":"1 round","effect":"<p>You use the Force to push your body beyond normal limits. You gain an additional move action this turn.</p>","special":"<p>This extra move action can be used to move or perform other move-action tasks.</p>","descriptor":["Vital"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":99,"tags":["enhancement","action-economy","movement"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":2,"max":2},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.1ac1084ca8f07114"}}},{"_id":"0ad823b5bcdf4b9c","name":"Vital Transfer","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":3,"discipline":"vital","useTheForce":15,"time":"Standard Action","range":"Touch","target":"One living creature","duration":"Instantaneous","effect":"<p>You channel the Force to heal injuries and restore vitality. The target recovers hit points based on your Use the Force check result.</p>","special":"<p>You cannot heal yourself with this power.</p>","descriptor":["Vital","Healing"],"dcChart":[{"dc":15,"effect":"2d6 healing","description":"Target heals 2d6 hit points"},{"dc":20,"effect":"4d6 healing","description":"Target heals 4d6 hit points"},{"dc":25,"effect":"6d6 healing + condition","description":"Target heals 6d6 hit points and removes one ongoing condition"},{"dc":30,"effect":"8d6 healing + all conditions","description":"Target heals 8d6 hit points and removes all ongoing conditions"}],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":99,"tags":["healing","vital","support"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.00b65e47a4dd7d76"}}},{"_id":"50099b10a6ec400d","name":"Unarmed","type":"weapon","img":"icons/svg/sword.svg","system":{"damage":"1d3+9","damageType":"kinetic","attackBonus":0,"attackAttribute":"str","range":"melee","weight":1,"cost":0,"equipped":true,"description":"","properties":[],"ammunition":{"type":"none","current":0,"max":0},"weaponCategory":"simple","proficiency":"simple","subcategory":""},"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"placeholder":true,"npc":{"flatAttackBonus":23,"flatDamageFormula":"1d3+9","useFlat":true}}}},{"_id":"47680f2fbef2f328","name":"Lightsaber","type":"weapon","img":"icons/svg/sword.svg","system":{"damage":"2d8+16","damageType":"energy","attackBonus":0,"attackAttribute":"str","range":"melee","weight":1,"cost":12000,"equipped":true,"description":"<p>The elegant weapon of the Jedi and Sith. A blade of pure energy capable of cutting through nearly anything.</p>\n      <p><strong>Special:</strong> Ignores armor bonuses to Reflex Defense. Can deflect blaster bolts. Critical threat range 19-20. Re