ype":"Weapon Proficiency (Rifles)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.765ff8a34e58acac"}}},{"_id":"b970c9e8c036dfd5","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"You are proficient with simple weapons and do not take the -5 penalty when using them.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["noble","non-force","scoundrel","scout","soldier"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier","Scout","Scoundrel","Noble"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{}},"effects":[{"_id":"220daaa7-e1b5-440d-98cd-10f5e586ef8b","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.2d680cc46a7972da"}}},{"_id":"afe7393515650ea1","name":"Assault Tactics","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Military Tactics","prerequisites":"Trained in Initiative","benefit":"You can use the , Deployment Tactics, or Field Tactics Talent as a Swift Action, instead of a Move Action (provided you have the Talent in question). Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions During the first round of combat in an encounter (after the Surprise Round, if any), you can take your turn before any of your allies, but you must use either the Share Talent Prestige Class ability or a Talent from one of the following Talent Trees as part of your turn: Commando Talent Tree, Leadership Talent Tree, or Military Tactics Talent Tree. On the subsequent round, you return to your normal place in the Initiative Order. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide Prerequisite: When you use the Talent on an enemy, the target takes a cumulative -1 penalty to its Reflex Defense each time it is damaged by one of your allies (maximum -5 penalty). This penalty applies until the end of your next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide As a Swift Action, once per encounter, you can grant bonus Hit Points equal to 5 + one-half your Character Level to allies within 20 squares of you and in your line of sight. Damage is subtracted from the bonus Hit Points first, and any bonus Hit Points remaining at the end of the encounter go away. Bonus Hit Points from multiple sources do not stack. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions Your tactics confuse enemy commanders and tacticians that can see or otherwise observe your forces in action, such as when using sensors. After using the Share Talent special quality, make a Knowledge (Tactics) check as a Free Action. The result replaces the DC of any Talents that use Knowledge (Tactics) from the Military Tactics Talent Tree used against your or your allies. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions If you have already used a Talent in an encounter before granting the same Talent to an ally with your Share Talent special quality in the same encounter, any character who benefits from Share Talent gains one of the following bonuses when using that talent (if the Talent can be affected by more than one effect, the character using the Talent selects the desired effect): Reduce the Talent's DC by 5. Gain an additional +2 bonus to any bonus to attack, Defense, or damage used by the Talent. Reduce the amount of damage taken by the character through the use of the Talent by 10 points. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions","description":"You can use the , Deployment Tactics, or Field Tactics Talent as a Swift Action, instead of a Move Action (provided you have the Talent in question). Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions During the first round of combat in an encounter (after the Surprise Round, if any), you can take your turn before any of your allies, but you must use either the Share Talent Prestige Class ability or a Talent from one of the following Talent Trees as part of your turn: Commando Talent Tree, Leadership Talent Tree, or Military Tactics Talent Tree. On the subsequent round, you return to your normal place in the Initiative Order. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide Prerequisite: When you use the Talent on an enemy, the target takes a cumulative -1 penalty to its Reflex Defense each time it is damaged by one of your allies (maximum -5 penalty). This penalty applies until the end of your next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide As a Swift Action, once per encounter, you can grant bonus Hit Points equal to 5 + one-half your Character Level to allies within 20 squares of you and in your line of sight. Damage is subtracted from the bonus Hit Points first, and any bonus Hit Points remaining at the end of the encounter go away. Bonus Hit Points from multiple sources do not stack. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions Your tactics confuse enemy commanders and tacticians that can see or otherwise observe your forces in action, such as when using sensors. After using the Share Talent special quality, make a Knowledge (Tactics) check as a Free Action. The result replaces the DC of any Talents that use Knowledge (Tactics) from the Military Tactics Talent Tree used against your or your allies. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions If you have already used a Talent in an encounter before granting the same Talent to an ally with your Share Talent special quality in the same encounter, any character who benefits from Share Talent gains one of the following bonuses when using that talent (if the Talent can be affected by more than one effect, the character using the Talent selects the desired effect): Reduce the Talent's DC by 5. Gain an additional +2 bonus to any bonus to attack, Defense, or damage used by the Talent. Reduce the amount of damage taken by the character through the use of the Talent by 10 points. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions","class":"Officer","costNumeric":null,"category":"Officer","tree":"Military Tactics","treeId":"9253ace716c3e966","tags":["action-economy","ambush","controller","damage-reduction","defender","feat-chain","force","force-control","force-defense","force-offense","leader","leadership","mobility","positioning","scaling","scout","skills","striker","support","sustained-damage","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.assault_tactics"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.d9fe8a0c76d845d4"}}},{"_id":"45d0ca11377fbc71","name":"Battle Analysis","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Commando","prerequisites":"Trained in Initiative","benefit":"When you make a ranged attack with a Pistol or Rifle, all allies within 6 squares of you when you made the attack gain a +1 bonus to Reflex Defense until the start of your next turn. Allies within range don't need to be within your line of sight to gain the bonus. When you use the Mechanics skill to Handle Explosives, the explosion deals +2 dice of damage. You may take this Talent multiple times; its effects stack. You can distract opponents and convince them that you are the most tempting (or most dangerous) target in the area. As a Swift Action, make a Persuasion check and compare the result to the Will Defense of all opponents within line of sight. If the check result exceeds an opponent's Will Defense, that opponent cannot attack any character within 6 squares of you until the start of your next turn as long as you do not have Cover against that opponent. (The affected opponent may still attack you, however.) If you are the Pilot of a Vehicle, you may use this Talent to protect allied Vehicles. You may use it to protect Vehicles no more than one size category larger than your own. Once per round, you may spend a Swift Action to shield a single adjacent ally from attacks, taking the damage and suffering the ill effects in your ally's stead. Until the start of your next turn, any attack made against the protected ally targets you instead. You may elect not to shield your protected ally against a given attack, provided the decision is made before the attack roll is made. If you are the Pilot of a Vehicle, you may use this Talent to protect allied Vehicles. You may use it to protect Vehicles no more than one size category larger than your own. Once per day as a Swift Action, you can move +5 steps on the Condition Track. This does not remove any Persistent Conditions that may be affecting you. This Talent does not affect the Condition Track of a Vehicle. You can select this talent multiple times. Each time you select this Talent, you can use it one additional time per day. You can catch a Second Wind one extra time per day. If you have this Talent and the Extra Second Wind feat, you can catch your Second Wind a total of three times per day. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy of Intrigue Prerequisite: Whenever you have the benefit of Cover, you can spend two Swift Actions to treat it as Improved Cover until the start of your next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Threats of the Galaxy Prerequisite: When one or more allies uses the Aid Another Action to give you a bonus to your attack roll, you gain a circumstance bonus equal to the total bonus provided to your damage roll. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook You add an additional die of damage when attacking with any weapon that has a Burst radius.","description":"When you make a ranged attack with a Pistol or Rifle, all allies within 6 squares of you when you made the attack gain a +1 bonus to Reflex Defense until the start of your next turn. Allies within range don't need to be within your line of sight to gain the bonus. When you use the Mechanics skill to Handle Explosives, the explosion deals +2 dice of damage. You may take this Talent multiple times; its effects stack. You can distract opponents and convince them that you are the most tempting (or most dangerous) target in the area. As a Swift Action, make a Persuasion check and compare the result to the Will Defense of all opponents within line of sight. If the check result exceeds an opponent's Will Defense, that opponent cannot attack any character within 6 squares of you until the start of your next turn as long as you do not have Cover against that opponent. (The affected opponent may still attack you, however.) If you are the Pilot of a Vehicle, you may use this Talent to protect allied Vehicles. You may use it to protect Vehicles no more than one size category larger than your own. Once per round, you may spend a Swift Action to shield a single adjacent ally from attacks, taking the damage and suffering the ill effects in your ally's stead. Until the start of your next turn, any attack made against the protected ally targets you instead. You may elect not to shield your protected ally against a given attack, provided the decision is made before the attack roll is made. If you are the Pilot of a Vehicle, you may use this Talent to protect allied Vehicles. You may use it to protect Vehicles no more than one size category larger than your own. Once per day as a Swift Action, you can move +5 steps on the Condition Track. This does not remove any Persistent Conditions that may be affecting you. This Talent does not affect the Condition Track of a Vehicle. You can select this talent multiple times. Each time you select this Talent, you can use it one additional time per day. You can catch a Second Wind one extra time per day. If you have this Talent and the Extra Second Wind feat, you can catch your Second Wind a total of three times per day. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy of Intrigue Prerequisite: Whenever you have the benefit of Cover, you can spend two Swift Actions to treat it as Improved Cover until the start of your next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Threats of the Galaxy Prerequisite: When one or more allies uses the Aid Another Action to give you a bonus to your attack roll, you gain a circumstance bonus equal to the total bonus provided to your damage roll. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook You add an additional die of damage when attacking with any weapon that has a Burst radius.","class":"Soldier","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","tree":"Commando","treeId":"798ed0945cbdac1c","tags":["action-economy","battlefield-control","burst-damage","condition-removal","controller","defender","feat-chain","force","force-control","force-defense","force-offense","mechanics","mobility","piloting","positioning","ranged","scaling","shields","skills","social","soldier","striker","support","sustained-damage","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.battle_analysis"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.7df2e8e4f18dc909"}}},{"_id":"eaf1ba1cd0bfeb46","name":"Commanding Presence","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Mercenary","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Your abilities on the battlefield are well known and feared. When you reduce an opponent to 0 Hit Points with an attack, you can make a Persuasion check as a Free Action against all targets within 6 squares. If your Persuasion check exceeds the target's Will Defense, that target takes a -2 penalty on attack rolls for the remainder of the encounter. This Talent affects any given target only once per encounter. This is a Mind-Affecting Fear effect. Your training makes you confident and disciplined in combat. When you successfully deal damage to an opponent in combat, you gain a +5 morale bonus to Will Defense until the start of your next turn. You lose this bonus to Will Defense if you are Surprised or Flat-Footed for any reason.","description":"Your abilities on the battlefield are well known and feared. When you reduce an opponent to 0 Hit Points with an attack, you can make a Persuasion check as a Free Action against all targets within 6 squares. If your Persuasion check exceeds the target's Will Defense, that target takes a -2 penalty on attack rolls for the remainder of the encounter. This Talent affects any given target only once per encounter. This is a Mind-Affecting Fear effect. Your training makes you confident and disciplined in combat. When you successfully deal damage to an opponent in combat, you gain a +5 morale bonus to Will Defense until the start of your next turn. You lose this bonus to Will Defense if you are Surprised or Flat-Footed for any reason.","class":"Soldier","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","tree":"Mercenary","treeId":"4007fa87192b5884","tags":["action-economy","ambush","battlefield-control","controller","damage-reduction","defender","leader","positioning","skills","social","soldier","striker"]},"effects":[{"_id":"ff1494c0-5d9c-4bd3-9b5c-bc93f28f4ea2","name":"Commanding Presence","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.leadership","mode":2,"value":"1"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Commanding Presence"}}},{"name":"Commanding Presence (Class Skill)","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.skills.persuasion.classSkill","mode":5,"value":"true"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Commanding Presence","effectType":"class-skill"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.commanding_presence"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.438e13c99c7b53a6"}}},{"_id":"c37e2a57708fc232","name":"Cover Fire","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Commando","prerequisites":"Battle Analysis","benefit":"When you make a ranged attack, allies within 6 squares gain +1 Defense until your next turn.","description":"","class":"Soldier","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.battle_analysis"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"798ed0945cbdac1c","tree":"Commando","tags":["defender","feat-chain","positioning","ranged","soldier","striker","talent-chain"]},"effects":[{"_id":"6a421fc4-15d4-4819-8d96-a2ffb7283d28","name":"Cover Fire","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.defenses.all","mode":2,"value":"1"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Cover Fire"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.cover_fire"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.049820827d7ef32b"}}},{"_id":"5d93ee8abbb98511","name":"Expert Gunner","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Gunner","prerequisites":"","benefit":"While your Vehicle is engaged in a Dogfight, you take no penalty on your attack rolls with Vehicle Weapons, even if you are not the Pilot. You gain a +1 bonus on attack rolls made using Vehicle Weapons. Prerequisite: Whenever an enemy Vehicle moves out of your square, or an adjacent square, you may make a single attack against that Vehicle as an Attack of Opportunity. Prerequisite: Whenever you deal damage to a Vehicle that equals or exceeds its Damage Threshold, you move that Vehicle an additional -1 step on the Condition Track. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Starships of the Galaxy Prerequisites: , System Hit Whenever you make an attack that causes a Vehicle to move -1 or more steps down the Condition Track, you may also cause it to lose one of the following systems: Hyperdrive, one Weapon System or Weapon Battery, or communications. The system remains inoperable until the target regains all steps on the Condition Track. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions Prerequisites: , Quick Trigger Once per encounter, when Piloting a Vehicle of Gargantuan size or smaller, you can make a Full Attack as a Standard Action. You can spend a Force Point to use this Talent one additional time in an encounter. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Starships of the Galaxy When firing a Vehicle Weapon, you treat the distance to the target as though it were one Range category less than it actually is. For example, when targeting an opponent at Short Range, you treat it as though it were at least Point-Blank Range for the purpose of determining bonuses or penalties. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions Prerequisite: You know how to overcharge your Vehicle's weapon to produce additional damage. As a Swift Action, you can overcharge your Vehicle's energy weapon and deal +1 die of damage on your next attack in the same turn. However, your weapon loses 1 die of damage on its subsequent attacks and cannot be overcharged again, until a full round passes without the weapon firing. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Starships of the Galaxy Prerequisite: Once per encounter, you may ready to fire a single weapon at the same target as an ally, and you coordinate with a single weapon of your ally. If both attacks hit, you add the damage of the two weapons together before applying the target's Shield Rating or Damage Reduction, and treat it as a single attack for purposes of exceeding the target's Damage Threshold.","description":"While your Vehicle is engaged in a Dogfight, you take no penalty on your attack rolls with Vehicle Weapons, even if you are not the Pilot. You gain a +1 bonus on attack rolls made using Vehicle Weapons. Prerequisite: Whenever an enemy Vehicle moves out of your square, or an adjacent square, you may make a single attack against that Vehicle as an Attack of Opportunity. Prerequisite: Whenever you deal damage to a Vehicle that equals or exceeds its Damage Threshold, you move that Vehicle an additional -1 step on the Condition Track. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Starships of the Galaxy Prerequisites: , System Hit Whenever you make an attack that causes a Vehicle to move -1 or more steps down the Condition Track, you may also cause it to lose one of the following systems: Hyperdrive, one Weapon System or Weapon Battery, or communications. The system remains inoperable until the target regains all steps on the Condition Track. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions Prerequisites: , Quick Trigger Once per encounter, when Piloting a Vehicle of Gargantuan size or smaller, you can make a Full Attack as a Standard Action. You can spend a Force Point to use this Talent one additional time in an encounter. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Starships of the Galaxy When firing a Vehicle Weapon, you treat the distance to the target as though it were one Range category less than it actually is. For example, when targeting an opponent at Short Range, you treat it as though it were at least Point-Blank Range for the purpose of determining bonuses or penalties. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions Prerequisite: You know how to overcharge your Vehicle's weapon to produce additional damage. As a Swift Action, you can overcharge your Vehicle's energy weapon and deal +1 die of damage on your next attack in the same turn. However, your weapon loses 1 die of damage on its subsequent attacks and cannot be overcharged again, until a full round passes without the weapon firing. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Starships of the Galaxy Prerequisite: Once per encounter, you may ready to fire a single weapon at the same target as an ally, and you coordinate with a single weapon of your ally. If both attacks hit, you add the damage of the two weapons together before applying the target's Shield Rating or Damage Reduction, and treat it as a single attack for purposes of exceeding the target's Damage Threshold.","class":"Ace Pilot","costNumeric":null,"category":"Ace Pilot","tree":"Gunner","treeId":"43ead399d82b8142","tags":["action-economy","condition-removal","controller","damage-reduction","defender","dual-wield","force","force-control","force-offense","mobility","piloting","positioning","scout","shields","skills","striker","support","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[{"_id":"19db7346-c8b7-44de-a92a-3a48795e7596","name":"Expert Gunner","icon":"icons/svg/gun.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.attacks.ranged","mode":2,"value":"1"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Expert Gunner"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.expert_gunner"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.befaa195df06b274"}}},{"_id":"192c3eba49682baa","name":"Inspire Confidence","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Inspiration","prerequisites":"","benefit":"You can't in yourself. As a Swift Action, you can encourage one of your allies within line of sight to make haste with a Skill Check. On that ally's next turn, that ally can make a Skill Check that normally requires a Standard Action, as a Move Action instead. Prerequisite: You can share your strength of will with your allies. Once per encounter as a Swift Action, you can grant all allies within line of sight a +2 morale bonus to their Will Defense. This bonus lasts for the remainder of the encounter, and once it is granted your allies need not remain within line of sight of you to retain this bonus.","description":"You can't in yourself. As a Swift Action, you can encourage one of your allies within line of sight to make haste with a Skill Check. On that ally's next turn, that ally can make a Skill Check that normally requires a Standard Action, as a Move Action instead. Prerequisite: You can share your strength of will with your allies. Once per encounter as a Swift Action, you can grant all allies within line of sight a +2 morale bonus to their Will Defense. This bonus lasts for the remainder of the encounter, and once it is granted your allies need not remain within line of sight of you to retain this bonus.","class":"Noble","costNumeric":null,"category":"Noble","tree":"Inspiration","treeId":"72d32ebcbb607314","tags":["action-economy","controller","defender","leader","mobility","noble","striker","support"]},"effects":[{"_id":"1faa089c-9609-46d8-8543-9a68ace3553b","name":"Inspire Confidence","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.attacks","mode":2,"value":"1"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Inspire Confidence"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.inspire_confidence"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.4d8882a28da30454"}}},{"_id":"73994ecdfa6b4153","name":"Quick Trigger","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Gunner","prerequisites":"Expert Gunner","benefit":"Can make attacks of opportunity with vehicle weapons.","description":"You may make attacks of opportunity with vehicle weapons.","class":"Ace Pilot","costNumeric":null,"category":"Ace Pilot","tree":"Gunner","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.expert_gunner"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"43ead399d82b8142","tags":["feat-chain","scout","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.quick_trigger"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.12ffb24378b60c13"}}},{"_id":"d7dc53790760aa9e","name":"Willpower","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Inspiration","prerequ