efit":"You are proficient with simple weapons and do not take the -5 penalty when using them.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["noble","non-force","scoundrel","scout","soldier"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier","Scout","Scoundrel","Noble"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{}},"effects":[{"_id":"220daaa7-e1b5-440d-98cd-10f5e586ef8b","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.2d680cc46a7972da"}}},{"_id":"e3aa57e8c28e836b","name":"Acute Senses","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Master Scout","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Keen Shot You are skilled at fighting armored characters, taking advantage of their weaknesses. You can use each of the following Actions once per encounter: Binding Hit: You dislodge an enemy's Armor, causing it to hinder the wearer's defenses. Make a melee or ranged attack as a Standard Action. If you hit and damage your target, the target loses its Armor bonus to its Reflex Defense and is Flat-Footed. This effect remains until the target spends a Standard Action to adjust its Armor. Blinding Fire: Make a melee or ranged attack as a Standard Action. If the attack hits and damages the target, the target takes a -2 penalty to all attacks until the end of your next turn. Additionally, all other creatures, Droids, and Vehicles have Concealment from the target until the end of your next turn. Slowing Shot: Your hit damages your target's Armor so that the target's movement is hindered. Make a melee or ranged attack as a Standard Action. If you hit and damage the target, the target's Speed is reduced by two squares until the end of your next turn.","description":"Keen Shot You are skilled at fighting armored characters, taking advantage of their weaknesses. You can use each of the following Actions once per encounter: Binding Hit: You dislodge an enemy's Armor, causing it to hinder the wearer's defenses. Make a melee or ranged attack as a Standard Action. If you hit and damage your target, the target loses its Armor bonus to its Reflex Defense and is Flat-Footed. This effect remains until the target spends a Standard Action to adjust its Armor. Blinding Fire: Make a melee or ranged attack as a Standard Action. If the attack hits and damages the target, the target takes a -2 penalty to all attacks until the end of your next turn. Additionally, all other creatures, Droids, and Vehicles have Concealment from the target until the end of your next turn. Slowing Shot: Your hit damages your target's Armor so that the target's movement is hindered. Make a melee or ranged attack as a Standard Action. If you hit and damage the target, the target's Speed is reduced by two squares until the end of your next turn.","class":"Scout","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scout","tree":"Master Scout","treeId":"dca33c0215264a02","tags":["action-economy","armor","controller","damage-reduction","defender","force","force-control","force-defense","force-offense","melee","mobility","positioning","ranged","scout","striker","support"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.acute_senses"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.f0166d26d9f6252a"}}},{"_id":"10844c6d830d75b8","name":"Armored Defense","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Knight's Armor","prerequisites":"","benefit":"When calculating your Reflex Defense, you may add your Heroic Level plus one-half your Armor bonus (rounded down), or your Armor bonus alone, whichever is higher. This Talent counts as both the Talent and the Improved Talent for the purposes of prerequisites. You are adept at using a Cortosis Gauntlet to parry Lightsaber attacks. You gain a +2 bonus when making an opposed Unarmed melee attack roll against a Lightsaber attack.","description":"When calculating your Reflex Defense, you may add your Heroic Level plus one-half your Armor bonus (rounded down), or your Armor bonus alone, whichever is higher. This Talent counts as both the Talent and the Improved Talent for the purposes of prerequisites. You are adept at using a Cortosis Gauntlet to parry Lightsaber attacks. You gain a +2 bonus when making an opposed Unarmed melee attack roll against a Lightsaber attack.","class":"Soldier","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","tree":"Knight's Armor","treeId":"ea01d740c91888b3","tags":["armor","defender","lightsaber","melee","scaling","soldier","striker","sustained-damage","unarmed"]},"effects":[{"_id":"28f1f3db-0c6f-4614-bdcf-000f1542a25b","name":"Armored Defense","icon":"icons/svg/shield.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.defenses.reflex.misc","mode":2,"value":"1","priority":20}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Armored Defense"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.armored_defense"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.4c236343b01ea763"}}},{"_id":"ff6fd00ba4e7af67","name":"Fool's Luck","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Fortune","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Once per encounter, you can turn a Critical Hit against you into a normal hit. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisite: Once per encounter, as a Reaction, you gain a +5 luck bonus to any one Defense until the start of your next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy","description":"Once per encounter, you can turn a Critical Hit against you into a normal hit. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisite: Once per encounter, as a Reaction, you gain a +5 luck bonus to any one Defense until the start of your next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy","class":"Scoundrel","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scoundrel","tree":"Fortune","treeId":"cee9b9398682b7d0","tags":["action-economy","defender","precision","scoundrel","striker"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.fools_luck"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.5319a796f2c4ff64"}}},{"_id":"02fbfb37e49e7d82","name":"Hunter's Mark","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Bounty Hunter","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Once per encounter as a Free Action, you may designate an opponent. For the rest of the encounter, when you succeed on a melee or ranged attack against that opponent, you gain a bonus on damage equal to your Class Level. Your skill as a Bounty Hunter is known throughout the galaxy, even on fringe worlds. When you are not Disguised, you may reroll any Persuasion checks made to Intimidate, keeping the better of the two results. You may choose to reroll any Gather Information checks made to Locate Individual, but you must accept the result of the reroll, even if it is worse. Prerequisites: , Hunter's Target This Talent applies only to an opponent you've designated as your Hunter's Target. Any attack or effect originating from the target that would normally move you along the Condition Track does not, in fact, move you along the Condition Track. Prerequisites: , Hunter's Target Prerequisites: , Hunter's Target, Nowhere to Hide Prerequisites: , Hunter's Target","description":"Once per encounter as a Free Action, you may designate an opponent. For the rest of the encounter, when you succeed on a melee or ranged attack against that opponent, you gain a bonus on damage equal to your Class Level. Your skill as a Bounty Hunter is known throughout the galaxy, even on fringe worlds. When you are not Disguised, you may reroll any Persuasion checks made to Intimidate, keeping the better of the two results. You may choose to reroll any Gather Information checks made to Locate Individual, but you must accept the result of the reroll, even if it is worse. Prerequisites: , Hunter's Target This Talent applies only to an opponent you've designated as your Hunter's Target. Any attack or effect originating from the target that would normally move you along the Condition Track does not, in fact, move you along the Condition Track. Prerequisites: , Hunter's Target Prerequisites: , Hunter's Target, Nowhere to Hide Prerequisites: , Hunter's Target","class":"Bounty Hunter","costNumeric":null,"category":"Bounty Hunter","tree":"Bounty Hunter","treeId":"a47ed82a822e3962","tags":["action-economy","condition-removal","controller","dual-wield","melee","mobility","positioning","ranged","scoundrel","skills","social","stealth","striker","support"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.hunters_mark"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.74fb6b37af983a4c"}}},{"_id":"4051e06c2f7a3899","name":"Hunter's Target","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Bounty Hunter","prerequisites":"Quick Draw","benefit":"As a Standard Action, you can instill bone-chilling fear in an opponent whom you selected for your . Make a Persuasion check against your target's Will Defense. If you equal or exceed your target's Will Defense, that target takes a -5 penalty to its Will Defense. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. The penalty remains as long as you have line of sight to your target and immediately ends if the line of sight is broken. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy of Intrigue Once per turn, whenever an opponent whom you selected for your attempts to Withdraw, you can make an Attack of Opportunity against that target. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions You are fast with the binders. As a Swift Action, when you successfully use the Grab Action against a target, you can use Binder Cuffs or similar restraints to bind one of the target's arms to one of your arms or to an adjacent object. You cannot use improvised materials, such as Mesh Tape, for this Talent, and the binders must be in your hands or readily available. You and the target both take a -2 penalty to attack rolls and Reflex Defense while bound together. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy of Intrigue Whenever you damage an opponent whom you selected for your , all allies gain a +2 bonus on their next attack roll against that opponent until the start of your next turn.","description":"As a Standard Action, you can instill bone-chilling fear in an opponent whom you selected for your . Make a Persuasion check against your target's Will Defense. If you equal or exceed your target's Will Defense, that target takes a -5 penalty to its Will Defense. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. The penalty remains as long as you have line of sight to your target and immediately ends if the line of sight is broken. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy of Intrigue Once per turn, whenever an opponent whom you selected for your attempts to Withdraw, you can make an Attack of Opportunity against that target. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions You are fast with the binders. As a Swift Action, when you successfully use the Grab Action against a target, you can use Binder Cuffs or similar restraints to bind one of the target's arms to one of your arms or to an adjacent object. You cannot use improvised materials, such as Mesh Tape, for this Talent, and the binders must be in your hands or readily available. You and the target both take a -2 penalty to attack rolls and Reflex Defense while bound together. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy of Intrigue Whenever you damage an opponent whom you selected for your , all allies gain a +2 bonus on their next attack roll against that opponent until the start of your next turn.","class":"Bounty Hunter","costNumeric":null,"category":"Bounty Hunter","tree":"Bounty Hunter","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.hunters_mark"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"a47ed82a822e3962","tags":["action-economy","defender","feat-chain","mobility","positioning","scoundrel","skills","social","striker","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.hunters_target"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.907906934ba3c563"}}},{"_id":"385eae467fe7495e","name":"Improved Armored Defense","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Armor Specialist","prerequisites":"Armored Defense","benefit":"Your Reflex Defense bonus equals either your heroic level + half your armor bonus, or your armor bonus.","description":"Your Reflex Defense bonus equals either your heroic level plus half your armor bonus or your armor bonus.","class":"Soldier","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","tree":"Armor Specialist","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.armored_defense"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"17cec542331cb4e4","tags":["armor","defender","feat-chain","soldier","striker","talent-chain"]},"effects":[{"_id":"842ee02b-8f7e-4a40-802a-c6fe553379a5","name":"Improved Armored Defense","icon":"icons/svg/shield.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.defenses.reflex","mode":2,"value":"2"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Improved Armored Defense"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.improved_armored_defense"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.394809ed8baff1b9"}}},{"_id":"5578e0a7ec82dea1","name":"Keen Shot","type":"talent","img