cient with pistols and do not take the -5 penalty when using them.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["non-force","ranged","scoundrel","scout","soldier"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier","Scout","Scoundrel"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{}},"effects":[{"_id":"04733e85-193e-4f4b-8792-c359083557d1","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Pistols)","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Weapon Proficiency (Pistols)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Pistols)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.e5d361d01d1b44e4"}}},{"_id":"4923078fd1babfed","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"You are proficient with simple weapons and do not take the -5 penalty when using them.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["noble","non-force","scoundrel","scout","soldier"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier","Scout","Scoundrel","Noble"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{}},"effects":[{"_id":"220daaa7-e1b5-440d-98cd-10f5e586ef8b","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.2d680cc46a7972da"}}},{"_id":"d675cd523d13ff7e","name":"Devastating Power","type":"feat","img":"systems/foundryvtt-swse/assets/icons/force-secret.png","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"When using a Force Power that deals damage, you can spend a Force Point to increase the Power's damage dice by 50%.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Core","page":0,"tags":["force-secret"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":"<p><strong>Cost:</strong> Force Point or Destiny Point</p><p>When using a Force Power that deals damage, you can spend a Force Point to increase the Power's damage dice by 50%.</p><p>Alternatively, you can spend a Destiny Point to double the amount of damage dice.</p>","cost":"Force Point or Destiny Point","alternativeCost":"Alternatively, you can spend a Destiny Point to double the amount of damage dice."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcesecrets.996848a2e0c0ac4f"}}},{"_id":"1900e8b2e0916bf7","name":"Distant Power","type":"feat","img":"systems/foundryvtt-swse/assets/icons/force-secret.png","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"When using a Force Power that has a range expressed numerically, you can spend a Force Point to multiply the range by 10.","prerequisite":"","special":"This Force Secret does not remove the line of sight requirements.","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Core","page":0,"tags":["force-secret"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":"<p><strong>Cost:</strong> Force Point or Destiny Point</p><p>When using a Force Power that has a range expressed numerically, you can spend a Force Point to multiply the range by 10.</p><p>Alternatively, you can spend a Destiny Point to increase the range to anywhere in the same Star System.</p><p><strong>Special:</strong> This Force Secret does not remove the line of sight requirements.</p>","cost":"Force Point or Destiny Point","alternativeCost":"Alternatively, you can spend a Destiny Point to increase the range to anywhere in the same Star System."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcesecrets.43f9645eabce838e"}}},{"_id":"e4b3212437387ca9","name":"Multitarget Power","type":"feat","img":"systems/foundryvtt-swse/assets/icons/force-secret.png","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"When using a Force Power that affects a single target, you can spend a Force Point to affect one additional target.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Core","page":0,"tags":["force-secret"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":"<p><strong>Cost:</strong> Force Point or Destiny Point</p><p>When using a Force Power that affects a single target, you can spend a Force Point to affect one additional target.</p><p>Alternatively, you can spend a Destiny Point to affect one target per four Character Levels.</p>","cost":"Force Point or Destiny Point","alternativeCost":"Alternatively, you can spend a Destiny Point to affect one target per four Character Levels."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcesecrets.af908ace9a361603"}}},{"_id":"c09cd352c8c5b049","name":"Quicken Power","type":"feat","img":"systems/foundryvtt-swse/assets/icons/force-secret.png","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"When using a Force Power that requires a Standard Action or Move Action to activate, you can spend a Force Point to activate the Force Power as a Swift Action instead.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Core","page":0,"tags":["force-secret"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":"<p><strong>Cost:</strong> Force Point or Destiny Point</p><p>When using a Force Power that requires a Standard Action or Move Action to activate, you can spend a Force Point to activate the Force Power as a Swift Action instead.</p><p>Alternatively, you can spend a Destiny Point to activate the Force Power as a Reaction instead.</p>","cost":"Force Point or Destiny Point","alternativeCost":"Alternatively, you can spend a Destiny Point to activate the Force Power as a Reaction instead."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcesecrets.52bf7b9a1a41de2b"}}},{"_id":"118eca4209f39519","name":"Force Point Recovery","type":"feat","img":"systems/foundryvtt-swse/assets/icons/force-technique.png","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"At the end of an encounter, you automatically recover 1 Force Point spent during the encounter.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Core","page":0,"tags":["force-technique"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"description":"<p>At the end of an encounter, you automatically recover 1 Force Point spent during the encounter.</p>","relatedPower":""},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcetechniques.056ab39b3ab9df10"}}},{"_id":"a86d42cf4ac67b02","name":"Improved Move Light Object","type":"feat","img":"systems/foundryvtt-swse/assets/icons/force-technique.png","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"You may make a Use the Force check to Move Light Object as a Swift Action instead of a Move Action. Using the light object as a projectile weapon requires a Move Action (instead of a Standard Action).","prerequisite":"Move Light Object","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Core","page":0,"tags":["force-technique"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"description":"<p>You may make a Use the Force check to Move Light Object as a Swift Action instead of a Move Action. Using the light object as a projectile weapon requires a Move Action (instead of a Standard Action).</p><p><strong>Related Power:</strong> Move Light Object</p><p><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Move Light Object</p>","relatedPower":"Move Light Object"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcetechniques.c406600924a7780e"}}},{"_id":"d661c7f17f780581","name":"Improved Sense Surroundings","type":"feat","img":"systems/foundryvtt-swse/assets/icons/force-technique.png","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"You may use the Sense Surroundings application of the Use the Force Skill as a Free Action rather than a Swift Action.","prerequisite":"Sense Surroundings","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Core","page":0,"tags":["force-technique"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"description":"<p>You may use the Sense Surroundings application of the Use the Force Skill as a Free Action rather than a Swift Action.</p><p><strong>Related Power:</strong> Sense Surroundings</p><p><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Sense Surroundings</p>","relatedPower":"Sense Surroundings"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcetechniques.4955b5076ca5da89"}}},{"_id":"6f5d173a111337c7","name":"Block","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Sith Alchemy","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Create Sith Amulet: You can create a Sith Amulet. The creation of a Sith Amulet requires 25,000 credits' worth of gems and other raw materials, and the creation process takes 1 week (this work can be spread out over several sessions and need not be consecutive). At the end of the process, you must spend a Force Point to complete the Sith Amulet, after which point it functions exactly as a Sith Amulet. Create Sith Armor: You can transform a suit of normal Battle Armor into the Dark Armor worn by Sith Lords. You must have a suit of Battle Armor to transform into the Dark Armor (Light Battle Armor becomes Light Dark Armor, Battle Armor becomes Dark Armor, and Heavy Battle Armor becomes Heavy Dark Armor). The transformation process takes 1 day for Light Dark Armor, 2 days for Dark Armor, and 3 days for Heavy Dark Armor. You must spend a Force Point at the end of the creation process to complete the Armor's transformation. Create Sith Talisman: You can spend a Force Point to imbue a portable object with the Dark Side, creating a Sith Talisman that provides offensive strength to a Force Power. Creating the Sith Talisman takes a Full-Round Action. While you wear or carry the Sith Talisman on your person, you add 1d6 to your damage with Force Powers. You increase your Dark Side Score by 1 when you first wear or carry a Sith Talisman. You can have only one Sith Talisman active at any given time, and if it is destroyed, you cannot create another one for 24 hours. Create Sith Weapon: You can alchemically treat a Simple Weapon (Melee) or an Advanced Melee Weapon, turning it into a Sith Weapon. You must spend a Force Point and spend 1 hour imbuing the Weapon with the properties of a Sith Alchemical Weapon (see also: Sith Alchemical Weapon Template). A Lightsaber does not ignore the Sith Weapon's DR, and characters who are proficient in the Weapon's use can treat it as a Lightsaber for the purposes of the , Deflect, and Redirect Shot Talents (and any Talents that have these Talents as a prerequisite). Additionally, as a Swift Action, the wielder of a Sith Weapon can spend a Force Point to gain a bonus equal to their Dark Side Score to the damage of their next attack made with the Weapon before the end of the encounter. This increases the wielder's Dark Side Score by 1.","description":"Create Sith Amulet: You can create a Sith Amulet. The creation of a Sith Amulet requires 25,000 credits' worth of gems and other raw materials, and the creation process takes 1 week (this work can be spread out over several sessions and need not be consecutive). At the end of the process, you must spend a Force Point to complete the Sith Amulet, after which point it functions exactly as a Sith Amulet. Create Sith Armor: You can transform a suit of normal Battle Armor into the Dark Armor worn by Sith Lords. You must have a suit of Battle Armor to transform into the Dark Armor (Light Battle Armor becomes Light Dark Armor, Battle Armor becomes Dark Armor, and Heavy Battle Armor becomes Heavy Dark Armor). The transformation process takes 1 day for Light Dark Armor, 2 days for Dark Armor, and 3 days for Heavy Dark Armor. You must spend a Force Point at the end of the creation process to complete the Armor's transformation. Create Sith Talisman: You can spend a Force Point to imbue a portable object with the Dark Side, creating a Sith Talisman that provides offensive strength to a Force Power. Creating the Sith Talisman takes a Full-Round Action. While you wear or carry the Sith Talisman on your person, you add 1d6 to your damage with Force Powers. You increase your Dark Side Score by 1 when you first wear or carry a Sith Talisman. You can have only one Sith Talisman active at any given time, and if it is destroyed, you cannot create another one for 24 hours. Create Sith Weapon: You can alchemically treat a Simple Weapon (Melee) or an Advanced Melee Weapon, turning it into a Sith Weapon. You must spend a Force Point and spend 1 hour imbuing the Weapon with the properties of a Sith Alchemical Weapon (see also: Sith Alchemical Weapon Template). A Lightsaber does not ignore the Sith Weapon's DR, and characters who are proficient in the Weapon's use can treat it as a Lightsaber for the purposes of the , Deflect, and Redirect Shot Talents (and any Talents that have these Talents as a prerequisite). Additionally, as a Swift Action, the wielder of a Sith Weapon can spend a Force Point to gain a bonus equal to their Dark Side Score to the damage of their next attack made with the Weapon before the end of the encounter. This increases the wielder's Dark Side Score by 1.","class":"Jedi","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","tree":"Sith Alchemy","treeId":"a67faf2ae089ab5d","tags":["action-economy","armor","dark-side","defender","force","force-offense","jedi","lightsaber","melee","mobility","ranged","striker","support","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.block"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.9379daa94a228c04"}}},{"_id":"05a9364b4607ce12","name":"Deflect","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Lightsaber Forms","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Redirect Shot","description":"Redirect Shot","class":"Jedi","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","tree":"Lightsaber Forms","treeId":"2bc2572e852832e4","tags":["jedi","lightsaber","melee","ranged"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.deflect"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.72c644f7a09b1186"}}},{"_id":"05f4a84e4784bc07","name":"Djem So","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Lightsaber Forms","prerequisites":null,"benefit":"Once per round, if hit in melee, make an immediate attack against that opponent.","description":"Once per round, when hit in melee, make an immediate attack against the attacker.","class":"Jedi Knight","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi Knight","tree":"Lightsaber Forms","treeId":"2bc2572e852832e4","tags":["jedi","lightsaber","melee","striker","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.djem_so"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.9dfce712a60a097f"}}},{"_id":"32e61ea424f9ee9d","name":"Equilibrium","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Force Adept","prerequisites":"","benefit":"The Force shields you against ailments, toxins, and radiation poisoning, making you immune to Disease, Poison, and Radiation. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions You are particularly in tune with The Living Force. When you successfully use Search Your Feelings, you gain a Force Point that must be used before the end of the encounter. If you use this Force Point in a manner that would end in unfavorable results (per Search Your Feelings), you raise your Dark Side Score by 1. lf you use the Force Point in an action that would normally raise your Dark Side Score, you raise your Dark Side Score by 2 instead. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions","description":"The Force shields you against ailments, toxins, and radiation poisoning, making you immune to Disease, Poison, and Radiation. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions You are particularly in tune with The Living Force. When you successfully use Search Your Feelings, you gain a Force Point that must be used before the end of the encounter. If you use this Force Point in a manner that would end in unfavorable results (per Search Your Feelings), you raise your Dark Side Score by 1. lf you use the Force Point in an action that would normally raise your Dark Side Score, you raise your Dark Side Score by 2 instead. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions","costNumeric":null,"tree":"Force Adept","treeId":"e35ee41362604227","tags":["action-economy","dark-side","defender","force","shields","support"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.equilibrium"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.328a880e60f2320f"}}},{"_id":"7d45200216f23e93","name":"Force Deception","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Sith","prerequisites":null,"benefit":"Use the Force replaces Deception checks and is treated as trained.","description":"Use the Force replaces Deception; you are considered trained.","class":"Sith Apprentice","costNumeric":null,"category":"Sith Apprentice","tree":"Sith","treeId":"d1037bc7a08ea80b","tags":["dark-side","force","jedi","skills","social"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.force_deception"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.a40e25585a6f8c2b"}}},{"_id":"bc1a7cacfc7d82c9","name":"Juyo","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Lightsaber Forms","prerequisites":"Prerequisites: Double Attack (Lightsabers), Skill Focus (Use the Force), Base Attack Bonus +12","benefit":"Weapon Focus (Lightsabers), Weapon Specialization (Lightsabers), Base Attack Bonus +12 When attacking with a Lightsaber, you score a critical hit on a natural roll of 19 or 20. However, a natural 19 is not considered an automatic hit; if you roll a natural 19 and still miss the target, you do not score a critical hit. Homebrew Reference Book: Clone Wars Saga Edition Fan Sourcebook - The Dark Side You may make a Deception check as a Swift Action (instead of a Standard Action) when attempting to Feint in combat. Maho-Kai Lightsaber Form Talent created by Wikia user SirenEyes. Whenever you make multiple attacks with any type of Lightsaber as part of a Full Attack, you may choose to forgo an attack and instead activate a Force Power that requires a Standard Action or Move Action to activate. When activating a Force Power in this manner, apply the attack roll penalty to the Use the Force check to activate the Force Power. You may only activate one Force Power in this manner each Round. Tripzest Lightsaber Form Talent created by Wikia user Droidscotty.","description":"Weapon Focus (Lightsabers), Weapon Specialization (Lightsabers), Base Attack Bonus +12 When attacking with a Lightsaber, you score a critical hit on a natural roll of 19 or 20. However, a natural 19 is not considered an automatic hit; if you roll a natural 19 and still miss the target, you do not score a critical hit. Homebrew Reference Book: Clone Wars Saga Edition Fan Sourcebook - The Dark Side You may make a Deception check as a Swift Action (instead of a Standard Action) when attempting to Feint in combat. Maho-Kai Lightsaber Form Talent created by Wikia user SirenEyes. Whenever you make multiple attacks with any type of Lightsaber as part of a Full Attack, you may choose to forgo an attack and instead activate a Force Power that requires a Standard Action or Move Action to activate. When activating a Force Power in this manner, apply the attack roll penalty to the Use the Force check to activate the Force Power. You may only activate one Force Power in this manner each Round. Tripzest Lightsaber Form Talent created by Wikia user Droidscotty.","class":"Jedi Knight","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi Knight","tree":"Lightsaber Forms","treeId":"2bc2572e852832e4","tags":["action-economy","burst-damage","controller","dark-side","feat-chain","force","force-control","force-offense","jedi","lightsaber","melee","mobility","precision","skills","social","striker","sustained-damage","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.juyo"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.5fd19be0deca1115"}}},{"_id":"ad82b59506eb8b26","name":"Lightsaber Throw","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Duelist","prerequisites":"","benefit":"You can spend a Force Point as a Standard Action to throw your Lightsaber at a group of opponents. You make a single ranged attack roll (treating the Lightsaber as a Thrown Weapon) and compare the result to the Reflex Defense of all targets in a 6-square line originating in your square. If your attack roll result exceeds a target's Reflex Defense, you deal normal Lightsaber damage to that target (dealing half damage if you fail to exceed the target's Reflex Defense). This attack is considered an Area Attack. You can pull your Lightsaber back to your hand as a Swift Action by making a DC 20 Use the Force check. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide","description":"You can spend a Force Point as a Standard Action to throw your Lightsaber at a group of opponents. You make a single ranged attack roll (treating the Lightsaber as a Thrown Weapon) and compare the result to the Reflex Defense of all targets in a 6-square line originating in your square. If your attack roll result exceeds a target's Reflex Defense, you deal normal Lightsaber damage to that target (dealing half damage if you fail to exceed the target's Reflex Defense). This attack is considered an Area Attack. You can pull your Lightsaber back to your hand as a Swift Action by making a DC 20 Use the Force check. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide","class":"Jedi","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","tree":"Duelist","treeId":"b3c5d90b5036f39b","tags":["action-economy","battlefield-control","controller","defender","force","force-control","force-defense","force-offense","jedi","lightsaber","melee","mobility","positioning","ranged","striker"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.lightsaber_throw"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.e54ecc0ff06e61f3"}}},{"_id":"7722fa0a0dbad658","name":"Power of the Dark Side","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Dark Side","prerequisites":"Dark Side Score equal to Wisdom Score","benefit":"Charisma 13 As a Standard Action, you grant yourself and all allies within 6 squares of you a +1 Force bonus to all Defenses until the end of the encounter. These bonuses are lost if you fall unconscious or die. Affected allies that move out of range lose the benefits for as long as they remain out of range. Prerequisite: Once per day, you can use a Force Power that normally takes a Standard Action or a Move Action as a Swift Action. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide Sometimes your anger consumes you. As a Swift Action, you can take a -5 penalty to your Will Defense to gain a +2 Force bonus on attack rolls. The penalty and bonus last until the beginning of your next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide Prerequisite: Whenever an effect would normally move you down the Condition Track, you may spend a Force Point and increase your Dark Side Score by 1 to negate that movement down the Condition Track. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual Once per encounter as a Swift Action, you can return one Force Power with the [Dark Side] descriptor to your Force Power Suite without spending a Force Point. You can select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select it, you can use it one additional time per encounter. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Threats of the Galaxy As a Standard Action, you can spend a Force Point to drain the knowledge of an opponent you touch; you must succeed on a Use the Force check (DC equal to the target's Will Defense) to activate this Talent, and if you fail to activate this Talent, you may not try again on the same target for one day. If successful, you immediately become Trained in one Skill that the target is Trained in; if you are already Trained in that Skill, you instead gain Skill Focus in that Skill. This effect lasts for one day. Additionally, your target moves -1 Persistent step along the Condition Track, and the Persistent Condition can be removed only by resting for 8 hours. Additionally, you can choose to instead sift through the mind of the target, looking for a specific piece of knowledge or information. Doing so requires you to make a Perception check against the target's Will Defense; success indicates that you pull the relevant information from the target's mind. When you do so, you do not gain the bonus Trained Skill or Skill Focus normally granted by this Talent, but otherwise the Talent functions as normal. Using this Talent increases your Dark Side Score by 1. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual When you die, you become a Dark Side Spirit until the end of the encounter. You continue to occupy a space in this form, but other creatures can occupy the same space or move through your space without impediment. As a Standard Action, you can attempt to possess an adjacent target. You must succeed on a Use the Force check against an adjacent target's Will Defense. If your check result equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, you deal 8d6 points of Stun damage to the target; if you reduce the target to 0 Hit Points or move it to the bottom of the Condition Track with this attack, you possess the target as though it were a willing host. Alternatively, as a Standard Action, you can transfer your essence into a single adjacent object, such as a Holocron or a Lightsaber. If you do so, you lie dormant within the object until another creature attempts to use that object, at which time you can emerge and attempt to possess the creature, as described above. If you do not possess a creature or object within 10 rounds of manifesting as a Dark Side Spirit, your spirit dissipates and ceases to exist. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide Prerequisite: When you roll a Natural 20 on a Use the Force check to activate a Force Power that directly deals damage to a target, you can choose not to regain all of your spent Force Powers as normal and instead the targets damaged by the Force Power take half that damage again at the start of their next turn. Only Force Powers that directly damage the target are subject to this Talent, including Corruption, Force Blast, Force Grip, Force Lightning, Force Slam, Force Thrust (only when spending a Force Point), and Repulse (only when spending a Force Point). Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook Prerequisite: You can create balls of unnatural energy, enabling you to make a ranged attack roll against the Reflex Defense of one target within 12 squares and line of sight, dealing 2d6 points of energy damage to the target on a successful attack. Using this Talent increases your Dark Side Score by 1. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook Prerequisites: , Swift Power When using a Force Power that directly inflicts damage, you treat the target's Damage Threshold as though it were 5 points lower when determining if the target moves along the Condition Track. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook Prerequisite: Whenever your character moves 3 or more squares in a round you gain Concealment; you may choose not to use this Talent when you move.","description":"Charisma 13 As a Standard Action, you grant yourself and all allies within 6 squares of you a +1 Force bonus to all Defenses until the end of the encounter. These bonuses are lost if you fall unconscious or die. Affected allies that move out of range lose the benefits for as long as they remain out of range. Prerequisite: Once per day, you can use a Force Power that normally takes a Standard Action or a Move Action as a Swift Action. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide Sometimes your anger consumes you. As a Swift Action, you can take a -5 penalty to your Will Defense to gain a +2 Force bonus on attack rolls. The penalty and bonus last until the beginning of your next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide Prerequisite: Whenever an effect would normally move you down the Condition Track, you may spend a Force Point and increase your Dark Side Score by 1 to negate that movement down the Condition Track. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual Once per encounter as a Swift Action, you can return one Force Power with the [Dark Side] descriptor to your Force Power Suite without spending a Force Point. You can select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select it, you can use it one additional time per encounter. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Threats of the Galaxy As a Standard Action, you can spend a Force Point to drain the knowledge of an opponent you touch; you must succeed on a Use the Force check (DC equal to the target's Will Defense) to activate this Talent, and if you fail to activate this Talent, you may not try again on the same target for one day. If successful, you immediately become Trained in one Skill that the target is Trained in; if you are already Trained in that Skill, you instead gain Skill Focus in that Skill. This effect lasts for one day. Additionally, your target moves -1 Persistent step along the Condition Track, and the Persistent Condition can be removed only by resting for 8 hours. Additionally, you can choose to instead sift through the mind of the target, looking for a specific piece of knowledge or information. Doing so requires you to make a Perception check against the target's Will Defense; success indicates that you pull the relevant information from the target's mind. When you do so, you do not gain the bonus Trained Skill or Skill Focus normally granted by this Talent, but otherwise the Talent functions as normal. Using this Talent increases your Dark Side Score by 1. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual When you die, you become a Dark Side Spirit until the end of the encounter. You continue to occupy a space in this form, but other creatures can occupy the same space or move through your space without impediment. As a Standard Action, you can attempt to possess an adjacent target. You must succeed on a Use the Force check against an adjacent target's Will Defense. If your check result equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, you deal 8d6 points of Stun damage to the target; if you reduce the target to 0 Hit Points or move it to the bottom of the Condition Track with this attack, you possess the target as though it were a willing host. Alternatively, as a Standard Action, you can transfer your essence into a single adjacent object, such as a Holocron or a Lightsaber. If you do so, you lie dormant within the object until another creature attempts to use that object, at which time you can emerge and attempt to possess the creature, as described above. If you do not possess a creature or object within 10 rounds of manifesting as a Dark Side Spirit, your spirit dissipates and ceases to exist. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide Prerequisite: When you roll a Natural 20 on a Use the Force check to activate a Force Power that directly deals damage to a target, you can choose not to regain all of your spent Force Powers as normal and instead the targets damaged by the Force Power take half that damage again at the start of their next turn. Only Force Powers that directly damage the target are subject to this Talent, including Corruption, Force Blast, Force Grip, Force Lightning, Force Slam, Force Thrust (only when spending a Force Point), and Repulse (only when spending a Force Point). Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook Prerequisite: You can create balls of unnatural energy, enabling you to make a ranged attack roll against the Reflex Defense of one target within 12 squares and line of sight, dealing 2d6 points of energy damage to the target on a successful attack. Using this Talent increases your Dark Side Score by 1. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook Prerequisites: , Swift Power When using a Force Power that directly inflicts damage, you treat the target's Damage Threshold as though it were 5 points lower when determining if the target moves along the Condition Track. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook Prerequisite: Whenever your character moves 3 or more squares in a round you gain Concealment; you may choose not to use this Talent when you move.","costNumeric":null,"tree":"Dark Side","treeId":"de95d37c72b1c4cd","tags":["action-economy","condition-removal","controller","damage-reduction","dark-side","defender","feat-chain","force","force-control","force-defense","force-offense","leader","light-side","lightsaber","melee","mobility","perception","positioning","ranged","scaling","skills","stealth","striker","support","sustained-damage","talent-chain"]},"effects":[{"_id":"b3ad7fe2-78a8-42b3-83dc-385122d061ed","name":"Power of the Dark Side","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.damage","mode":2,"value":"1"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Power of the Dark Side"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.power_of_the_dark_side"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.627bd3abd30b973f"}}},{"_id":"447802eb35d4f15e","name":"Severing Strike","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Duelist","prerequisites":null,"benefit":"If you deal damage exceeding current HP and threshold, deal half damage and sever (special effect) while moving down the track.","description":"If damage exceeds the target's current hit points and damage threshold, deal half damage again, move the target down the condition track, and sever a limb.","class":"Jedi Knight","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi Knight","tree":"Duelist","treeId":"b3c5d90b5036f39b","tags":["jedi","striker"]},"effects":[{"_id":"8a7d9568-c68f-4b0e-a64a-0064e0dd2330","name":"Severing Strike","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.damage.limb_loss","mode":5,"value":"true"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Severing Strike"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.severing_strike"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.efd3308a8ccc22c6"}}},{"_id":"c1b6dfb9ab1a7a0f","name":"Swift Power","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Dark Side","prerequisites":"Power of the Dark Side","benefit":"Once per day, use a swift action in place of a move or standard action to activate a Force power.","description":"Once per day, activate a Force power as a swift action.","costNumeric":null,"tree":"Dark Side","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.power_of_the_dark_side"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"de95d37c72b1c4cd","tags":["action-economy","controller","dark-side","feat-chain","force","force-control","mobility","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.swift_power"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.09609e71ba6cd4aa"}}},{"_id":"37e66756837f48da","name":"Weapon Specialization (Lightsabers)","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Duelist","tree":"Duelist","prerequisites":"","description":"Greater Weapon Focus (Lightsabers) You gain a +2 bonus on melee damage rolls with Lightsabers. This bonus stacks with the bonus granted by the Talent. Whenever you make multiple attacks with any type of Lightsaber as part of a Full Attack, you reduce the penalty on your attack rolls by 2. You can take this Talent multiple times; each time you take this Talent, you reduce the penalty on your attack rolls by an additional 2. See also: Maiming Foes When you deal damage with a Lightsaber that is equal to or greater than both the target's current Hit Points and the target's Damage Threshold (that is, when you would deal enough damage to kill your target), you may choose to use this Talent. Instead of dealing full damage, you instead deal half damage to your target and move it -1 step on the Condition Track. In addition, you sever one of your target's arms at the wrist or elbow joint, or one of the target's legs at the knee or ankle joint (your choice). Severing part of an arm prevents the target from wielding weapons or using tools in that hand, and imposes a -5 penalty on Skill Checks and Ability Checks keyed to Strength and Dexterity. Severing part of a leg knocks the target Prone, reduces the target's Speed by half, reduces its Carrying Capacity by half, and imposes a -5 penalty on Skill Checks and Ability Checks keyed to Strength and Dexterity. Because of the severity of such an injury, losing part of a limb causes a Persistent Condition that can only be removed by having Surgery successfully performed on you. A Cybernetic Prosthesis negates these reductions and penalties. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","benefit":"Greater Weapon Focus (Lightsabers) You gain a +2 bonus on melee damage rolls with Lightsabers. This bonus stacks with the bonus granted by the Talent. Whenever you make multiple attacks with any type of Lightsaber as part of a Full Attack, you reduce the penalty on your attack rolls by 2. You can take this Talent multiple times; each time you take this Talent, you reduce the penalty on your attack rolls by an additional 2. See also: Maiming Foes When you deal damage with a Lightsaber that is equal to or greater than both the target's current Hit Points and the target's Damage Threshold (that is, when you would deal enough damage to kill your target), you may choose to use this Talent. Instead of dealing full damage, you instead deal half damage to your target and move it -1 step on the Condition Track. In addition, you sever one of your target's arms at the wrist or elbow joint, or one of the target's legs at the knee or ankle joint (your choice). Severing part of an arm prevents the target from wielding weapons or using tools in that hand, and imposes a -5 penalty on Skill Checks and Ability Checks keyed to Strength and Dexterity. Severing part of a leg knocks the target Prone, reduces the target's Speed by half, reduces its Carrying Capacity by half, and imposes a -5 penalty on Skill Checks and Ability Checks keyed to Strength and Dexterity. Because of the severity of such an injury, losing part of a limb causes a Persistent Condition that can only be removed by having Surgery successfully performed on you. A Cybernetic Prosthesis negates these reductions and penalties. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"b3c5d90b5036f39b","tags":["burst-damage","condition-removal","controller","damage-reduction","defender","force","force-control","force-offense","leader","lightsaber","melee","mobility","scaling","striker","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.00a9210772a64a19"}}},{"_id":"deb9801786578302","name":"Wicked Strike","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Sith","prerequisites":"Weapon Focus (Lightsabers), Weapon Specialization (Lightsabers)","benefit":"On a lightsaber critical hit, move the target 2 steps down the condition track.","description":"On a lightsaber critical hit, move the target two steps down the condition track.","class":"Sith Apprentice","costNumeric":null,"category":"Sith Apprentice","tree":"Sith","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.weapon_specialization"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"d1037bc7a08ea80b","tags":["condition-removal","controller","dark-side","feat-chain","force","force-control","jedi","lightsaber","melee","mobility","precision","striker","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.wicked_strike"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.d350b28e72652d29"}}},{"_id":"560f8d2c5e473d79","name":"Battle Strike","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"telekinetic","useTheForce":15,"time":"Swift Action","range":"Personal","target":"You","duration":"1 round","effect":"<p>You channel the Force to enhance your next melee attack. Your next melee attack this round gains a +1d6 bonus to damage.</p>","special":"<p>This bonus damage is Force damage and bypasses Damage Reduction.</p>","descriptor":["Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":94,"tags":["enhancement","damage","melee"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":2,"max":2},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.f177dc6d65f76de9"}}},{"_id":"2882107a0ad6cf16","name":"Dark Rage","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/eye.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"Unknown","useTheForce":"","time":"standard","range":"","target":"","duration":"","effect":"","special":"","descriptor":"","dcChart":"","maintainable":false,"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1,"perDay":true}},"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"placeholder":true,"unresolved":"Dark Rage"}}},{"_id":"3fda5fcf83e0da3a","name":"Farseeing","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telepathic","useTheForce":20,"time":"1 minute","range":"Unlimited","target":"Special","duration":"Concentration","effect":"<p>You peer through the Force to see distant locations or events. You can observe a place you've been before or a person you know, regardless of distance.</p>","special":"<p>The GM may require additional checks for very distant or obscured visions.</p>","descriptor":["Mind-Affecting","Scrying"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":true,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":95,"tags":["utility","divination","scrying"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.0419ecb55f011f81"}}},{"_id":"cfde6d433bcded63","name":"Force Grip","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":3,"discipline":"dark-side","useTheForce":15,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One creature","duration":"Concentration","effect":"<p>You use the Force to telekinetically choke or crush your target. The target takes damage each round based on your Use the Force check result.</p>","special":"<p>This is a Dark Side power. The target is immobilized while gripped.</p>","descriptor":["Dark Side","Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[{"dc":15,"effect":"2d6 damage/round","description":"Target takes 2d6 damage per round and is immobilized"},{"dc":20,"effect":"4d6 damage/round","description":"Target takes 4d6 damage per round and is immobilized"},{"dc":25,"effect":"6d6 damage/round + lift","description":"Target takes 6d6 damage per round, is immobilized, and lifted off ground"},{"dc":30,"effect":"8d6 damage/round + crush","description":"Target takes 8d6 damage per round and is being crushed (fort save or die)"}],"maintainable":true,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":96,"tags":["attack","damage","dark-side","telekinetic","immobilize"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.f41a957f71e98a6a"}}},{"_id":"3c2fd9a3d209aa40","name":"Force Lightning","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":4,"discipline":"dark-side","useTheForce":15,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One creature","duration":"Instantaneous","effect":"<p>You unleash devastating arcs of Force Lightning from your fingertips. The target takes lightning damage based on your Use the Force check result.</p>","special":"<p>This is a Dark Side power. Using it gains you a Dark Side Point.</p>","descriptor":["Dark Side","Force Lightning"],"dcChart":[{"dc":15,"effect":"2d6 lightning damage","description":"Target takes 2d6 lightning damage"},{"dc":20,"effect":"4d6 lightning damage","description":"Target takes 4d6 lightning damage"},{"dc":25,"effect":"6d6 lightning damage + stun","description":"Target takes 6d6 lightning damage and is stunned for 1 round"},{"dc":30,"effect":"8d6 lightning damage + stun 1d4","description":"Target takes 8d6 lightning damage and is stunned for 1d4 rounds"}],"maintainable":true,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":96,"tags":["attack","damage","dark-side","lightning"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":3,"max":3},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.0a422b939edfad56"}}},{"_id":"1f766f0f1f1fb9ec","name":"Force Slam","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telekinetic","useTheForce":20,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One creature or object","duration":"Instantaneous","effect":"<p>You use telekinetic force to violently slam your target against a surface. The target takes 4d6 damage and is knocked prone.</p>","special":"<p>The target must be within 6 squares of a solid surface (wall, floor, ceiling).</p>","descriptor":["Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":97,"tags":["attack","damage","telekinetic","prone"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.462a6c23e00c4dfc"}}},{"_id":"b84adcb6cd027ce8","name":"Mind Trick","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"telepathic","useTheForce":15,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One creature","duration":"1 minute or until completed","effect":"<p>You influence a weak mind to believe what you tell them or follow a simple suggestion. The target must make a Will save (DC = your UTF check) or be affected.</p>","special":"<p>The suggestion must be reasonable and the target must be able to understand you.</p>","descriptor":["Mind-Affecting"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":98,"tags":["mind-control","suggestion","social"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.e6649f366d6c5737"}}},{"_id":"7e73f64f880548f3","name":"Move Object","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telekinetic","useTheForce":15,"time":"Standard Action","range":"12 squares","target":"One object or creature","duration":"Concentration","effect":"<p>You move objects or creatures through the air using telekinesis. The maximum size/weight you can move depends on your Use the Force check result.</p>","special":"<p>Unwilling creatures can make a Will save (DC = your UTF check) to resist being moved.</p>","descriptor":["Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[{"dc":15,"effect":"Medium (50 kg)","description":"Move objects up to Medium size or 50 kg"},{"dc":20,"effect":"Large (250 kg)","description":"Move objects up to Large size or 250 kg"},{"dc":25,"effect":"Huge (1 ton)","description":"Move objects up to Huge size or 1 metric ton"},{"dc":30,"effect":"Gargantuan (5 tons)","description":"Move objects up to Gargantuan size or 5 metric tons"},{"dc":35,"effect":"Colossal (20 tons)","description":"Move objects up to Colossal size or 20 metric tons (starfighter-sized)"}],"maintainable":true,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":98,"tags":["telekinetic","movement","utility"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.289013a32bd179ad"}}},{"_id":"5b258efb3e949ffc","name":"Rebuke","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telepathic","useTheForce":20,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One Force-sensitive creature","duration":"1 round","effect":"<p>You overwhelm a Force user with a powerful Force presence. If the target is Force-sensitive, they must make a Will save (DC = your UTF check) or be dazed for 1 round.</p>","special":"<p>This power only affects Force-sensitive creatures.</p>","descriptor":["Mind-Affecting"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":99,"tags":["debuff","force-user","daze"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":2,"max":2},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.390074b44aedfa2a"}}},{"_id":"f0166e7db496c747","name":"Surge","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"vital","useTheForce":15,"time":"Swift Action","range":"Personal","target":"You","duration":"1 round","effect":"<p>You use the Force to push your body beyond normal limits. You gain an additional move action this turn.</p>","special":"<p>This extra move action can be used to move or perform other move-action tasks.</p>","descriptor":["Vital"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":99,"tags":["enhancement","action-economy","movement"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.1ac1084ca8f07114"}}},{"_id":"f3b2e7f33a2baa6e","name":"Lightsaber","type":"weapon","img":"icons/svg/sword.svg","system":{"damage":"2d8+15","damageType":"energy","attackBonus":0,"attackAttribute":"str","range":"melee","weight":1,"cost":12000,"equipped":true,"description":"<p>The elegant weapon of the Jedi and Sith. A blade of pure energy capable of cutting through nearly anything.</p>\n      <p><strong>Special:</strong> Ignores armor bonuses to Reflex Defense. Can deflect blaster bolts. Critical threat range 19-20. Requires e