","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["non-force"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{"value":"Ignore -5 penalty on attack rolls with weapons of a particular type."}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.ecc2471ac96ec2d4"}}},{"_id":"ae817fdc432b2d0e","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Pistols)","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"You are proficient with pistols and do not take the -5 penalty when using them.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["non-force","ranged","scoundrel","scout","soldier"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier","Scout","Scoundrel"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{}},"effects":[{"_id":"04733e85-193e-4f4b-8792-c359083557d1","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Pistols)","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Weapon Proficiency (Pistols)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Pistols)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.e5d361d01d1b44e4"}}},{"_id":"5b01feefb5cec1a5","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"You are proficient with simple weapons and do not take the -5 penalty when using them.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["noble","non-force","scoundrel","scout","soldier"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier","Scout","Scoundrel","Noble"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{}},"effects":[{"_id":"220daaa7-e1b5-440d-98cd-10f5e586ef8b","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.2d680cc46a7972da"}}},{"_id":"5dabe05511e86a04","name":"Force Point Recovery","type":"feat","img":"systems/foundryvtt-swse/assets/icons/force-technique.png","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"At the end of an encounter, you automatically recover 1 Force Point spent during the encounter.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Core","page":0,"tags":["force-technique"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"description":"<p>At the end of an encounter, you automatically recover 1 Force Point spent during the encounter.</p>","relatedPower":""},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcetechniques.056ab39b3ab9df10"}}},{"_id":"90651ff852ad0e68","name":"Improved Lightning Burst","type":"feat","img":"systems/foundryvtt-swse/assets/icons/force-technique.png","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"When you use the Lightning Burst Force Power, also compare the result of your Use the Force check to each target's Fortitude Defense. If your check result equals or exceeds both a target's Reflex Defense and its Fortitude Defense, you push the target 1 square away from you and knock the target Prone. This movement does not provoke Attacks of Opportunity.","prerequisite":"Lightning Burst","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Legacy Era Campaign Guide","page":0,"tags":["force-technique"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"description":"<p>When you use the Lightning Burst Force Power, also compare the result of your Use the Force check to each target's Fortitude Defense. If your check result equals or exceeds both a target's Reflex Defense and its Fortitude Defense, you push the target 1 square away from you and knock the target Prone. This movement does not provoke Attacks of Opportunity.</p><p><strong>Related Power:</strong> Lightning Burst</p><p><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Lightning Burst</p>","relatedPower":"Lightning Burst"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcetechniques.2a15d6c28e351f14"}}},{"_id":"82e97761f2c54518","name":"Improved Sense Force","type":"feat","img":"systems/foundryvtt-swse/assets/icons/force-technique.png","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"You may use the Sense Force ability of the Use the Force Skill as a Move Action rather than a Full-Round Action.","prerequisite":"Sense Force","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Core","page":0,"tags":["force-technique"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"description":"<p>You may use the Sense Force ability of the Use the Force Skill as a Move Action rather than a Full-Round Action.</p><p><strong>Related Power:</strong> Sense Force</p><p><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Sense Force</p>","relatedPower":"Sense Force"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcetechniques.ad67b8f3959860f2"}}},{"_id":"5a8d4480b2e940bc","name":"Improved Telepathy","type":"feat","img":"systems/foundryvtt-swse/assets/icons/force-technique.png","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"Whenever you use the Telepathy ability of the Use the Force Skill, you can reroll your Use the Force check, keeping the better of the two results.","prerequisite":"Telepathy","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Core","page":0,"tags":["force-technique"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"description":"<p>Whenever you use the Telepathy ability of the Use the Force Skill, you can reroll your Use the Force check, keeping the better of the two results.</p><p><strong>Related Power:</strong> Telepathy</p><p><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Telepathy</p>","relatedPower":"Telepathy"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcetechniques.53cfa2d1e4fe25ba"}}},{"_id":"91f813d3aa768101","name":"Cause Mutation","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Sith Alchemy","prerequisites":null,"benefit":"Transform a creature into a Sith Abomination or Chrysalis Beast under your control; process takes days and yields creatures with new class level.","description":"Transform a creature into a Sith Abomination or Chrysalis Beast that serves you for a number of days equal to your class level.","class":"Sith Apprentice","costNumeric":null,"category":"Sith Apprentice","tree":"Sith Alchemy","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.sith_alchemy"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"a67faf2ae089ab5d","tags":["dark-side","force","force-control","jedi"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.cause_mutation"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.c59de6f440c92832"}}},{"_id":"9563ef0cfd061346","name":"Connections","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Lineage","prerequisites":"","benefit":"You have Influential Contacts within a certain organization, planet, or region who can provide concrete information to you on certain subjects. Once per day, you can have one of these contacts make a Skill Check on your behalf. The contact always Takes 20 on the Skill Check (even if the Skill would normally not allow Taking 20) and has a Skill modifier equal to 5 + one-half your Heroic Level. Contacting your Influential Contacts and receiving the benefit of the Skill Check takes a number of minutes equal to 10 x the Skill Check result. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide Prerequisite: , Influential Friends You have a powerful contact who has an extended sphere of influence. The contact could be an Imperial Senator, a high-level military officer, a regional governor, an infamous crime lord, or another person of similar significance. Once per encounter, you can invoke the name or office of your powerful contact and Take 20 on one Persuasion check, with no increase in the time needed to make the check. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook","description":"You have Influential Contacts within a certain organization, planet, or region who can provide concrete information to you on certain subjects. Once per day, you can have one of these contacts make a Skill Check on your behalf. The contact always Takes 20 on the Skill Check (even if the Skill would normally not allow Taking 20) and has a Skill modifier equal to 5 + one-half your Heroic Level. Contacting your Influential Contacts and receiving the benefit of the Skill Check takes a number of minutes equal to 10 x the Skill Check result. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide Prerequisite: , Influential Friends You have a powerful contact who has an extended sphere of influence. The contact could be an Imperial Senator, a high-level military officer, a regional governor, an infamous crime lord, or another person of similar significance. Once per encounter, you can invoke the name or office of your powerful contact and Take 20 on one Persuasion check, with no increase in the time needed to make the check. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook","class":"Noble","costNumeric":null,"category":"Noble","tree":"Lineage","treeId":"b5bb4154688c66ab","tags":["force","noble","skills","social","striker","support"]},"effects":[{"_id":"6708f25b-1035-4044-99fb-a15527d65e5c","name":"Connections","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.economy.blackMarketMultiplier","mode":2,"value":"-1"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Connections","effectType":"economy_bonus","economy":true}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.connections"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.e58a8ad63c1d8771"}}},{"_id":"f12929ae6861d850","name":"Dark Presence","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Dark Side","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Power of the Dark Side Whenever an ally of equal or higher level than you is killed or reduced to 0 hit points within your line of sight, you gain a +2 Force bonus on attack rolls and damage rolls until the end of the encounter. (Since Force bonuses do not stack, you don't get a higher bonus if more than one ally falls in the same encounter.)","description":"Power of the Dark Side Whenever an ally of equal or higher level than you is killed or reduced to 0 hit points within your line of sight, you gain a +2 Force bonus on attack rolls and damage rolls until the end of the encounter. (Since Force bonuses do not stack, you don't get a higher bonus if more than one ally falls in the same encounter.)","costNumeric":null,"tree":"Dark Side","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"attribute","ability":"cha","min":13},{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.power_of_the_dark_side"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"de95d37c72b1c4cd","tags":["damage-reduction","dark-side","force","force-offense","scaling","striker","support"]},"effects":[{"_id":"b278be01-b200-4515-abdb-7137e70ffebf","name":"Dark Presence","icon":"icons/svg/moon.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.defenses.all","mode":2,"value":"1"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Dark Presence"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.dark_presence"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.606e14c428f1d159"}}},{"_id":"a1d4bbb581b01afa","name":"Dark Scourge","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Sith","prerequisites":null,"benefit":"+1 attack vs Jedi.","description":"Gain +1 attack against Jedi.","class":"Sith Apprentice","costNumeric":null,"category":"Sith Apprentice","tree":"Sith","treeId":"d1037bc7a08ea80b","tags":["dark-side","force","force-offense","jedi","light-side","striker"]},"effects":[{"_id":"61d0eabf-a9cc-48bf-978a-ed42169959c6","name":"Dark Scourge","icon":"icons/svg/skull.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.attackBonus","mode":2,"value":"1"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Dark Scourge"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.dark_scourge"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.08fc3247755c5ebe"}}},{"_id":"798fce3996ef47f0","name":"Drain Knowledge","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Dark Side","prerequisites":null,"benefit":"By touch, make a check vs target's Will Defense to drain knowledge; gain trained status in a skill or a Skill Focus if you already have the skill; target moves down the condition track; you gain a Dark Side Point.","description":"Drain knowledge by touch, gaining a trained skill or Skill Focus; target moves down the condition track.","costNumeric":null,"tree":"Dark Side","treeId":"de95d37c72b1c4cd","tags":["condition-removal","controller","defender","mobility","striker"]},"effects":[{"_id":"4e2c9d66-7b82-4596-b5c5-42b24e72de4d","name":"Drain Knowledge","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.skills.knowledge","mode":2,"value":"bonus"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Drain Knowledge"}}},{"_id":"a57d6a47-2cf4-4fcb-a558-8dae4e2bea79","name":"Drain Knowledge - DSP Increase","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.darkSideScore","mode":2,"value":"1"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Drain Knowledge"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.drain_knowledge"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.d46612d82307f0db"}}},{"_id":"91789bfdcce950ae","name":"Power of the Dark Side","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Dark Side","prerequisites":"Dark Side Score equal to Wisdom Score","benefit":"Charisma 13 As a Standard Action, you grant yourself and all allies within 6 squares of you a +1 Force bonus to all Defenses until the end of the encounter. These bonuses are lost if you fall unconscious or die. Affected allies that move out of range lose the benefits for as long as they remain out of range. Prerequisite: Once per day, you can use a Force Power that normally takes a Standard Action or a Move Action as a Swift Action. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide Sometimes your anger consumes you. As a Swift Action, you can take a -5 penalty to your Will Defense to gain a +2 Force bonus on attack rolls. The penalty and bonus last until the beginning of your next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide Prerequisite: Whenever an effect would normally move you down the Condition Track, you may spend a Force Point and increase your Dark Side Score by 1 to negate that movement down the Condition Track. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual Once per encounter as a Swift Action, you can return one Force Power with the [Dark Side] descriptor to your Force Power Suite without spending a Force Point. You can select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select it, you can use it one additional time per encounter. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Threats of the Galaxy As a Standard Action, you can spend a Force Point to drain the knowledge of an opponent you touch; you must succeed on a Use the Force check (DC equal to the target's Will Defense) to activate this Talent, and if you fail to activate this Talent, you may not try again on the same target for one day. If successful, you immediately become Trained in one Skill that the target is Trained in; if you are already Trained in that Skill, you instead gain Skill Focus in that Skill. This effect lasts for one day. Additionally, your target moves -1 Persistent step along the Condition Track, and the Persistent Condition can be removed only by resting for 8 hours. Additionally, you can choose to instead sift through the mind of the target, looking for a specific piece of knowledge or information. Doing so requires you to make a Perception check against the target's Will Defense; success indicates that you pull the relevant information from the target's mind. When you do so, you do not gain the bonus Trained Skill or Skill Focus normally granted by this Talent, but otherwise the Talent functions as normal. Using this Talent increases your Dark Side Score by 1. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual When you die, you become a Dark Side Spirit until the end of the encounter. You continue to occupy a space in this form, but other creatures can occupy the same space or move through your space without impediment. As a Standard Action, you can attempt to possess an adjacent target. You must succeed on a Use the Force check against an adjacent target's Will Defense. If your check result equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, you deal 8d6 points of Stun damage to the target; if you reduce the target to 0 Hit Points or move it to the bottom of the Condition Track with this attack, you possess the target as though it were a willing host. Alternatively, as a Standard Action, you can transfer your essence into a single adjacent object, such as a Holocron or a Lightsaber. If you do so, you lie dormant within the object until another creature attempts to use that object, at which time you can emerge and attempt to possess the creature, as described above. If you do not possess a creature or object within 10 rounds of manifesting as a Dark Side Spirit, your spirit dissipates and ceases to exist. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide Prerequisite: When you roll a Natural 20 on a Use the Force check to activate a Force Power that directly deals damage to a target, you can choose not to regain all of your spent Force Powers as normal and instead the targets damaged by the Force Power take half that damage again at the start of their next turn. Only Force Powers that directly damage the target are subject to this Talent, including Corruption, Force Blast, Force Grip, Force Lightning, Force Slam, Force Thrust (only when spending a Force Point), and Repulse (only when spending a Force Point). Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook Prerequisite: You can create balls of unnatural energy, enabling you to make a ranged attack roll against the Reflex Defense of one target within 12 squares and line of sight, dealing 2d6 points of energy damage to the target on a successful attack. Using this Talent increases your Dark Side Score by 1. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook Prerequisites: , Swift Power When using a Force Power that directly inflicts damage, you treat the target's Damage Threshold as though it were 5 points lower when determining if the target moves along the Condition Track. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook Prerequisite: Whenever your character moves 3 or more squares in a round you gain Concealment; you may choose not to use this Talent when you move.","description":"Charisma 13 As a Standard Action, you grant yourself and all allies within 6 squares of you a +1 Force bonus to all Defenses until the end of the encounter. These bonuses are lost if you fall unconscious or die. Affected allies that move out of range lose the benefits for as long as they remain out of range. Prerequisite: Once per day, you can use a Force Power that normally takes a Standard Action or a Move Action as a Swift Action. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide Sometimes your anger consumes you. As a Swift Action, you can take a -5 penalty to your Will Defense to gain a +2 Force bonus on attack rolls. The penalty and bonus last until the beginning of your next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide Prerequisite: Whenever an effect would normally move you down the Condition Track, you may spend a Force Point and increase your Dark Side Score by 1 to negate that movement down the Condition Track. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual Once per encounter as a Swift Action, you can return one Force Power with the [Dark Side] descriptor to your Force Power Suite without spending a Force Point. You can select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select it, you can use it one additional time per encounter. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Threats of the Galaxy As a Standard Action, you can spend a Force Point to drain the knowledge of an opponent you touch; you must succeed on a Use the Force check (DC equal to the target's Will Defense) to activate this Talent, and if you fail to activate this Talent, you may not try again on the same target for one day. If successful, you immediately become Trained in one Skill that the target is Trained in; if you are already Trained in that Skill, you instead gain Skill Focus in that Skill. This effect lasts for one day. Additionally, your target moves -1 Persistent step along the Condition Track, and the Persistent Condition can be removed only by resting for 8 hours. Additionally, you can choose to instead sift through the mind of the target, looking for a specific piece of knowledge or information. Doing so requires you to make a Perception check against the target's Will Defense; success indicates that you pull the relevant information from the target's mind. When you do so, you do not gain the bonus Trained Skill or Skill Focus normally granted by this Talent, but otherwise the Talent functions as normal. Using this Talent increases your Dark Side Score by 1. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual When you die, you become a Dark Side Spirit until the end of the encounter. You continue to occupy a space in this form, but other creatures can occupy the same space or move through your space without impediment. As a Standard Action, you can attempt to possess an adjacent target. You must succeed on a Use the Force check against an adjacent target's Will Defense. If your check result equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, you deal 8d6 points of Stun damage to the target; if you reduce the target to 0 Hit Points or move it to the bottom of the Condition Track with this attack, you possess the target as though it were a willing host. Alternatively, as a Standard Action, you can transfer your essence into a single adjacent object, such as a Holocron or a Lightsaber. If you do so, you lie dormant within the object until another creature attempts to use that object, at which time you can emerge and attempt to possess the creature, as described above. If you do not possess a creature or object within 10 rounds of manifesting as a Dark Side Spirit, your spirit dissipates and ceases to exist. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide Prerequisite: When you roll a Natural 20 on a Use the Force check to activate a Force Power that directly deals damage to a target, you can choose not to regain all of your spent Force Powers as normal and instead the targets damaged by the Force Power take half that damage again at the start of their next turn. Only Force Powers that directly damage the target are subject to this Talent, including Corruption, Force Blast, Force Grip, Force Lightning, Force Slam, Force Thrust (only when spending a Force Point), and Repulse (only when spending a Force Point). Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook Prerequisite: You can create balls of unnatural energy, enabling you to make a ranged attack roll against the Reflex Defense of one target within 12 squares and line of sight, dealing 2d6 points of energy damage to the target on a successful attack. Using this Talent increases your Dark Side Score by 1. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook Prerequisites: , Swift Power When using a Force Power that directly inflicts damage, you treat the target's Damage Threshold as though it were 5 points lower when determining if the target moves along the Condition Track. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook Prerequisite: Whenever your character moves 3 or more squares in a round you gain Concealment; you may choose not to use this Talent when you move.","costNumeric":null,"tree":"Dark Side","treeId":"de95d37c72b1c4cd","tags":["action-economy","condition-removal","controller","damage-reduction","dark-side","defender","feat-chain","force","force-control","force-defense","force-offense","leader","light-side","lightsaber","melee","mobility","perception","positioning","ranged","scaling","skills","stealth","striker","support","sustained-damage","talent-chain"]},"effects":[{"_id":"b3ad7fe2-78a8-42b3-83dc-385122d061ed","name":"Power of the Dark Side","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.damage","mode":2,"value":"1"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Power of the Dark Side"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.power_of_the_dark_side"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.627bd3abd30b973f"}}},{"_id":"d5481a5d668265c7","name":"Sith Alchemy","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Sith Alchemy","prerequisites":"","benefit":"You can use your mastery of to create mutated abominations. You must have access to a willing (or unconscious) creature to which you will apply the Sith Abomination Template or the Chrysalis Beast Template. You also need a medical lab outfitted for the process, which requires a number of days equal to creature's modified CL. You must spend a Force Point at the completion of the process to complete the transformation. A creature you have mutated is considered to be a domesticated creature, but for you only (unless it was already a domesticated creature before its mutation). As a Standard Action, you can perform minor alchemical alterations to a Melee Weapon you wield. For the remainder of the encounter, you gain a +2 Equipment bonus on attack rolls with that Weapon. Additionally, once before the end of the encounter, you can sacrifice this bonus as a Free Action to gain a +5 Equipment bonus on a single damage roll you make with that Weapon. Your knowledge of allows you to imbue certain objects with the power of the Dark Side. You can perform any of the following Alchemical Transformations, though each time you do so, increase your Dark Side Score by 1. Prerequisite: You can modify an object with Sith Alchemy so that it gains a specific trait. Specific traits are listed in the Sith Alchemy Table, below. You can only perform one modification at a time. Unless otherwise noted, you cannot grant more than one benefit to a single object, and you cannot apply the same benefit more than once. You must spend a Force Point and devote 1 hour of uninterrupted work to apply a trait to the relevant object, and when you do so, you increase your Dark Side Score by 1.","description":"You can use your mastery of to create mutated abominations. You must have access to a willing (or unconscious) creature to which you will apply the Sith Abomination Template or the Chrysalis Beast Template. You also need a medical lab outfitted for the process, which requires a number of days equal to creature's modified CL. You must spend a Force Point at the completion of the process to complete the transformation. A creature you have mutated is considered to be a domesticated creature, but for you only (unless it was already a domesticated creature before its mutation). As a Standard Action, you can perform minor alchemical alterations to a Melee Weapon you wield. For the remainder of the encounter, you gain a +2 Equipment bonus on attack rolls with that Weapon. Additionally, once before the end of the encounter, you can sacrifice this bonus as a Free Action to gain a +5 Equipment bonus on a single damage roll you make with that Weapon. Your knowledge of allows you to imbue certain objects with the power of the Dark Side. You can perform any of the following Alchemical Transformations, though each time you do so, increase your Dark Side Score by 1. Prerequisite: You can modify an object with Sith Alchemy so that it gains a specific trait. Specific traits are listed in the Sith Alchemy Table, below. You can only perform one modification at a time. Unless otherwise noted, you cannot grant more than one benefit to a single object, and you cannot apply the same benefit more than once. You must spend a Force Point and devote 1 hour of uninterrupted work to apply a trait to the relevant object, and when you do so, you increase your Dark Side Score by 1.","costNumeric":null,"tree":"Sith Alchemy","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.dark_side_master"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"a67faf2ae089ab5d","tags":["action-economy","dark-side","force","force-offense","force-support","leader","melee","striker","support"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.sith_alchemy"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.eb4f3e8660bc476589d0323d4cc00845"}}},{"_id":"9cd45e43a90b6940","name":"Sith Alchemy Specialist","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Sith Alchemy","prerequisites":"Sith Alchemy","benefit":"Modify items to add Sith Alchemy traits.","description":"Modify items to gain Sith Alchemy traits.","class":"Sith Apprentice","costNumeric":null,"category":"Sith Apprentice","tree":"Sith Alchemy","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.sith_alchemy"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"a67faf2ae089ab5d","tags":["dark-side","feat-chain","force","jedi","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.sith_alchemy_specialist"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.9bee4563b328def7"}}},{"_id":"5af32ffc106c5bb5","name":"Visions","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Keetael","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Prerequisites: The long-lived Draethos are particularly adept at searching and understanding the past. When using Farseeing to look into the past, reduce your DC numbers by half. Also, you are able to see everything within 6 squares of your target clearly without spending a Force Point.","description":"Prerequisites: The long-lived Draethos are particularly adept at searching and understanding the past. When using Farseeing to look into the past, reduce your DC numbers by half. Also, you are able to see everything within 6 squares of your target clearly without spending a Force Point.","costNumeric":null,"tree":"Keetael","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.force_perception"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"dad3c0da191748c1","tags":["damage-reduction","force","positioning"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.visions"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.da12fc505efc5eea"}}},{"_id":"7d22970ad09f367c","name":"Farseeing","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telepathic","useTheForce":20,"time":"1 minute","range":"Unlimited","target":"Special","duration":"Concentration","effect":"<p>You peer through the Force to see distant locations or events. You can observe a place you've been before or a person you know, regardless of distance.</p>","special":"<p>The GM may require additional checks for very distant or obscured visions.</p>","descriptor":["Mind-Affecting","Scrying"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":true,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":95,"tags":["utility","divination","scrying"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":2,"max":2},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.0419ecb55f011f81"}}},{"_id":"02db7ae2ee1aaa98","name":"Fear","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/eye.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"Unknown","useTheForce":"","time":"standard","range":"","target":"","duration":"","effect":"","special":"","descriptor":"","dcChart":"","maintainable":false,"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":2,"max":2,"perDay":true}},"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"placeholder":true,"unresolved":"Fear"}}},{"_id":"24284d1ff6fc5f1f","name":"Force Grip","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":3,"discipline":"dark-side","useTheForce":15,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One creature","duration":"Concentration","effect":"<p>You use the Force to telekinetically choke or crush your target. The target takes damage each round based on your Use the Force check result.</p>","special":"<p>This is a Dark Side power. The target is immobilized while gripped.</p>","descriptor":["Dark Side","Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[{"dc":15,"effect":"2d6 damage/round","description":"Target takes 2d6 damage per round and is immobilized"},{"dc":20,"effect":"4d6 damage/round","description":"Target takes 4d6 damage per round and is immobilized"},{"dc":25,"effect":"6d6 damage/round + lift","description":"Target takes 6d6 damage per round, is immobilized, and lifted off ground"},{"dc":30,"effect":"8d6 damage/round + crush","description":"Target takes 8d6 damage per round and is being crushed (fort save or die)"}],"maintainable":true,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":96,"tags":["attack","damage","dark-side","telekinetic","immobilize"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.f41a957f71e98a6a"}}},{"_id":"d8bcedb76bd247bd","name":"Force Slam","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telekinetic","useTheForce":20,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One creature or object","duration":"Instantaneous","effect":"<p>You use telekinetic force to violently slam your target against a surface. The target takes 4d6 damage and is knocked prone.</p>","special":"<p>The target must be within 6 squares of a solid surface (wall, floor, ceiling).</p>","descriptor":["Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":97,"tags":["attack","damage","telekinetic","prone"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.462a6c23e00c4dfc"}}},{"_id":"9c64270d236bfe3c","name":"Mind Trick","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"telepathic","useTheForce":15,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One creature","duration":"1 minute or until completed","effect":"<p>You influence a weak mind to believe what you tell them or follow a simple suggestion. The target must make a Will save (DC = your UTF check) or be affected.</p>","special":"<p>The suggestion must be reasonable and the target must be able to understand you.</p>","descriptor":["Mind-Affecting"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":98,"tags":["mind-control","suggestion","social"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.e6649f366d6c5737"}}},{"_id":"58290bdcbfc7cdb4","name":"Move Object","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telekinetic","useTheForce":15,"time":"Standard Action","range":"12 squares","target":"One object or creature","duration":"Concentration","effect":"<p>You move objects or creatures through the air using telekinesis. The maximum size/weight you can move depends on your Use the Force check result.</p>","special":"<p>Unwilling creatures can make a Will save (DC = your UTF check) to resist being moved.</p>","descriptor":["Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[{"dc":15,"effect":"Medium (50 kg)","description":"Move objects up to Medium size or 50 kg"},{"dc":20,"effect":"Large (250 kg)","description":"Move objects up to Large size or 250 kg"},{"dc":25,"effect":"Huge (1 ton)","description":"Move objects up to Huge size or 1 metric ton"},{"dc":30,"effect":"Gargantuan (5 tons)","description":"Move objects up to Gargantuan size or 5 metric tons"},{"dc":35,"effect":"Colossal (20 tons)","description":"Move objects up to Colossal size or 20 metric tons (starfighter-sized)"}],"maintainable":true,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":98,"tags":["telekinetic","movement","utility"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.289013a32bd179ad"}}},{"_id":"48212f2a7814501f","name":"Rebuke","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telepathic","useTheForce":20,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One Force-sensitive creature","duration":"1 round","effect":"<p>You overwhelm a Force user with a powerful Force presence. If the target is Force-sensitive, they must make a Will save (DC = your UTF check) or be dazed for 1 round.</p>","special":"<p>This power only affects Force-sensitive creatures.</p>","descriptor":["Mind-Affecting"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":99,"tags":["debuff","force-user","daze"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":2,"max":2},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.390074b44aedfa2a"}}},{"_id":"a9db8b72af51a68b","name":"Unarmed","type":"weapon","img":"icons/svg/sword.svg","system":{"damage":"1d4+9","damageType":"kinetic","attackBonus":0,"attackAttribute":"str","range":"melee","weight":1,"cost":0,"equipped":true,"description":"","properties":[],"ammunition":{"type":"none","current":0,"max":0},"weaponCategory":"simple","proficiency":"simple","subcategory":""},"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"placeholder":true,"npc":{"flatAttackBonus":15,"flatDamageFormula":"1d4+9","useFlat":true}}}},{"_id":"38ccc5ea02aa1d7c","name":"Lightsaber","type":"weapon","img":"icons/svg/sword.svg","system":{"damage":"2d8+10","damageType":"energy","attackBonus":0,"attackAttribute":"str","range":"melee","weight":1,"cost":12000,"equipped":true,"description":"<p>The elegant weapon of the Jedi and Sith. A blade of pure energy capable of cutting through nearly anything.</p>\n      <p><strong>Special:</strong> Ignores armor bonuses to Reflex Defense. Can deflect blaster bolts. Critical threat range 19-20. Requires exotic weapon proficiency.</p>","properties":["Lightsaber","Critical 19-20","Exotic","Armor-Piercing"],"ammunition":{"type":"none","current":0,"max":0},"weaponCategory":"melee","proficiency":"exotic","subcategory":"lightsaber","costNumeric":12000,"category":"lightsaber"},"eff