"source":"feat","featName":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.2d680cc46a7972da"}}},{"_id":"8eb84b5874748bc6","name":"Art of Concealment","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Smuggling","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Smugglers must be quick to explain discrepancies in their cover stories. Once per day, you can Take 20 on a Deception check as a Standard Action when attempting to Deceive. Prerequisite: If you draw a concealed weapon and, before the end of the same round, make an attack against a target that failed to notice the item, the target is considered Flat-Footed against you. You can draw a concealed item or a stowed item as a Move Action. Additionally, if you have the Quick Draw feat, you can reduce this to a Swift Action. Smugglers have a knack for locating and negotiating illicit deals. When using Persuasion to Haggle for Restricted, Military, or Illegal goods you may roll twice, keeping the better of the two results. Sometimes a smuggler has to fight his way out of a bad situation. If you fail any Deception check to convey deceptive information, you can initiate combat and make a single Unarmed attack as a Free Action in the Surprise Round (or with a melee or ranged weapon, if you have the Quick Draw feat); all other combatants are considered Surprised even if they are aware of you.","description":"Smugglers must be quick to explain discrepancies in their cover stories. Once per day, you can Take 20 on a Deception check as a Standard Action when attempting to Deceive. Prerequisite: If you draw a concealed weapon and, before the end of the same round, make an attack against a target that failed to notice the item, the target is considered Flat-Footed against you. You can draw a concealed item or a stowed item as a Move Action. Additionally, if you have the Quick Draw feat, you can reduce this to a Swift Action. Smugglers have a knack for locating and negotiating illicit deals. When using Persuasion to Haggle for Restricted, Military, or Illegal goods you may roll twice, keeping the better of the two results. Sometimes a smuggler has to fight his way out of a bad situation. If you fail any Deception check to convey deceptive information, you can initiate combat and make a single Unarmed attack as a Free Action in the Surprise Round (or with a melee or ranged weapon, if you have the Quick Draw feat); all other combatants are considered Surprised even if they are aware of you.","class":"Scoundrel","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scoundrel","tree":"Smuggling","treeId":"9f7ca12cc084737a","tags":["action-economy","ambush","controller","damage-reduction","melee","mobility","positioning","ranged","scoundrel","skills","social","support","sustained-damage","unarmed"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.art_of_concealment"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.64cfde2d0cf6c523"}}},{"_id":"d2d879098c0f74db","name":"Fast Talker","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Smuggling","prerequisites":"Art of Concealment","benefit":"Once per day, take 20 on a Deception check as a standard action when attempting to deceive.","description":"Once per day, take 20 on a Deception check when deceiving.","class":"Scoundrel","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scoundrel","tree":"Smuggling","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.art_of_concealment"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"9f7ca12cc084737a","tags":["action-economy","feat-chain","scoundrel","skills","social","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.fast_talker"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.eeed98748becb161"}