ect\" href=\"/wiki/Trained_Skill\" title=\"Trained Skill\">Trained Skill</a>."}},"effects":[{"name":"Skill Focus","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.skills.perception.miscMod","mode":2,"value":"5","priority":20}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"transfer":true,"flags":{"swse":{"type":"skill-bonus","skill":"43c5941072ec78af","source":"Skill Focus"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.1592aaedf4b6e40a"}}},{"_id":"cf8af1ba5c93ada3","name":"Sniper","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"You may aim as a move action instead of a standard action when using a rifle or pistol.","prerequisite":"Point Blank Shot","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Galaxy at War","page":27,"tags":["action-economy","controller","feat-chain","mobility","non-force","ranged","soldier"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{"value":"You ignore <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Soft_Cover\" title=\"Soft Cover\">Soft Cover</a> when making a ranged attack."},"prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"bab","min":4}],"_source":"canonical-csv"}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.56367f3943ee8c17"}}},{"_id":"aeea100c0cb89b7e","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Pistols)","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"You are proficient with pistols and do not take the -5 penalty when using them.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["non-force","ranged","scoundrel","scout","soldier"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier","Scout","Scoundrel"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{}},"effects":[{"_id":"04733e85-193e-4f4b-8792-c359083557d1","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Pistols)","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Weapon Proficiency (Pistols)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Pistols)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.e5d361d01d1b44e4"}}},{"_id":"1e2bb8b1b4b75ea4","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"You are proficient with simple weapons and do not take the -5 penalty when using them.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["noble","non-force","scoundrel","scout","soldier"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier","Scout","Scoundrel","Noble"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{}},"effects":[{"_id":"220daaa7-e1b5-440d-98cd-10f5e586ef8b","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.2d680cc46a7972da"}}},{"_id":"b96a307cbaf82ff7","name":"Impel Ally I","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Mastermind","prerequisites":"","benefit":"You can spend two Swift Actions to grant one ally the ability to take a Standard Action or Move Action. The ally must move immediately on your turn, before you do anything else, or else the opportunity is wasted. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy of Intrigue Prerequisites: , I Once per encounter, you can spend three Swift Actions on consecutive turns to grant one ally the ability to take a Standard Action and a Move Action. The ally must act immediately on your turn when the final Swift Action is spent, before you do anything else, or the opportunity is wasted. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , I As a Standard Action, you can designate a target to be the object of your allies' wrath. While your allies have line of sight to you or until you are unconscious or dead, your allies gain a +2 morale bonus on attack rolls against the target and a +2 morale bonus on Skill Checks against that target. You can designate a new target on any round by using another Standard Action. You can only use this Talent against one opponent at a time. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions Prerequisites: , I When an ally uses an Action granted to him or her by you, the ally can reroll any attack or check made during that Action, taking the better result. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , I Once per encounter, you can spend three Swift Actions on consecutive turns to increase the speed of all allies within your line of sight of you by 2. The increased speed lasts until the start of your next turn after the third Swift Action is spent. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy","description":"You can spend two Swift Actions to grant one ally the ability to take a Standard Action or Move Action. The ally must move immediately on your turn, before you do anything else, or else the opportunity is wasted. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy of Intrigue Prerequisites: , I Once per encounter, you can spend three Swift Actions on consecutive turns to grant one ally the ability to take a Standard Action and a Move Action. The ally must act immediately on your turn when the final Swift Action is spent, before you do anything else, or the opportunity is wasted. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , I As a Standard Action, you can designate a target to be the object of your allies' wrath. While your allies have line of sight to you or until you are unconscious or dead, your allies gain a +2 morale bonus on attack rolls against the target and a +2 morale bonus on Skill Checks against that target. You can designate a new target on any round by using another Standard Action. You can only use this Talent against one opponent at a time. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions Prerequisites: , I When an ally uses an Action granted to him or her by you, the ally can reroll any attack or check made during that Action, taking the better result. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , I Once per encounter, you can spend three Swift Actions on consecutive turns to increase the speed of all allies within your line of sight of you by 2. The increased speed lasts until the start of your next turn after the third Swift Action is spent. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy","class":"Crime Lord","costNumeric":null,"category":"Crime Lord","tree":"Mastermind","treeId":"560cc7994b357a0d","tags":["action-economy","controller","leader","mobility","striker","support","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.impel_ally_i"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.aa32a31a179fe5c1"}}},{"_id":"0dd779a1d1f102a5","name":"Impel Ally II","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Mastermind","prerequisites":"Impel Ally I","benefit":"Designated ally can make a standard or move action immediately or the effect is wasted.","description":"An ally may immediately take a move or standard action or lose it.","class":"Crime Lord","costNumeric":null,"category":"Crime Lord","tree":"Mastermind","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.impel_ally_i"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"560cc7994b357a0d","tags":["action-economy","controller","feat-chain","mobility","support","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.impel_ally_ii"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.b11a87e70f957ed2"}}},{"_id":"f1285b5a8a0f44c9","name":"Impel Ally III","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Mastermind","prerequisites":"Impel Ally II","benefit":"Designated ally can take a standard and a move action immediately or the effect is wasted.","description":"An ally may immediately take both a move and standard action or lose them.","class":"Crime Lord","costNumeric":null,"category":"Crime Lord","tree":"Mastermind","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.impel_ally_ii"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"560cc7994b357a0d","tags":["action-economy","controller","feat-chain","mobility","support","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.impel_ally_iii"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.3f01107ed7779426"}}},{"_id":"4398c79d88e95d45","name":"Improved Weaken Resolve","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Influence","prerequisites":"Weaken Resolve","benefit":"As Weaken Resolve, but the target continues fleeing beyond the initial duration.","description":"Targets affected by Weaken Resolve continue fleeing.","class":"Noble","costNumeric":null,"category":"Noble","tree":"Influence","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.weaken_resolve"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"8375b9b26b679901","tags":["feat-chain","noble","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.improved_weaken_resolve"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.f3ac8054a0c60760"}}},{"_id":"5746c3e0e7d9635f","name":"Inspire Fear I","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Infamy","prerequisites":"","benefit":"As , except that the penalty increases to -2. Prerequisites: , I As , except that the penalty increases to -5. Your reputation as a Crime Lord is known throughout the galaxy, even on fringe worlds. When you are not Disguised, you may reroll any Persuasion checks made to Intimidate, keeping the better of the two results. Prerequisites: , I, II, Notorious Any opponent that is reduced to half Hit Points or fewer while within 6 squares of you takes a -2 penalty on all attack rolls and Skill Checks for the duration of the encounter. This is a Mind-Affecting Fear effect.","description":"As , except that the penalty increases to -2. Prerequisites: , I As , except that the penalty increases to -5. Your reputation as a Crime Lord is known throughout the galaxy, even on fringe worlds. When you are not Disguised, you may reroll any Persuasion checks made to Intimidate, keeping the better of the two results. Prerequisites: , I, II, Notorious Any opponent that is reduced to half Hit Points or fewer while within 6 squares of you takes a -2 penalty on all attack rolls and Skill Checks for the duration of the encounter. This is a Mind-Affecting Fear effect.","class":"Crime Lord","costNumeric":null,"category":"Crime Lord","tree":"Infamy","treeId":"c1be604242cb328f","tags":["damage-reduction","positioning","skills","social","striker"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.inspire_fear_i"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.cf4b1e5b126a2a7e"}}},{"_id":"51e07a017410e9ec","name":"Inspire Fear II","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Infamy","prerequisites":"Inspire Fear I","benefit":"Increase penalties to -2 on affected rolls.","description":"Increase Inspire Fear penalties to –2.","class":"Crime Lord","costNumeric":null,"category":"Crime Lord","tree":"Infamy","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.inspire_fear_i"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"c1be604242cb328f","tags":["feat-chain","talent-chain"]},"effects":[{"_id":"93101939-886b-4faf-a5cd-092f86e11d0f","name":"Inspire Fear II","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.morale.penalty","mode":2,"value":"2"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Inspire Fear II"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.inspire_fear_ii"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.71bc6b43ab504b90"}}},{"_id":"fdff786218d6fa36","name":"Inspire Fear III","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Infamy","prerequisites":"Inspire Fear II","benefit":"Increase penalties to -5 on affected rolls.","description":"Increase Inspire Fear penalties to –5.","class":"Crime Lord","costNumeric":null,"category":"Crime Lord","tree":"Infamy","treeId":"c1be604242cb328f","tags":["feat-chain","talent-chain"]},"effects":[{"_id":"6faffa94-f0e3-49f2-9f5d-28c547b44f0b","name":"Inspire Fear III","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.morale.penalty","mode":2,"value":"5"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Inspire Fear III"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.inspire_fear_iii"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.bd11bfb793096483"}}},{"_id":"ed0387fd868061ea","name":"Notorious","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Infamy","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Your reputation as a crime lord is known throughout the galaxy, even on fringe worlds. When you are not disguised, you may reroll any Persuasion checks made to intimidate others, keeping the better result.","description":"Your reputation as a crime lord is known throughout the galaxy, even on fringe worlds. When you are not disguised, you may reroll any Persuasion checks made to intimidate others, keeping the better result.","class":"Crime Lord","costNumeric":null,"category":"Crime Lord","tree":"Infamy","treeId":"c1be604242cb328f","tags":["leader","scoundrel","skills","social","striker","support"],"summary":"When not disguised, reroll Persuasion checks to intimidate and keep the better result.","source":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":210},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.notorious_infamy"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.09744041cdcc9e22"}}},{"_id":"adc94e51e1175b1a","name":"Presence","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Influence","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Once per encounter, you can make a Persuasion check as a Standard Action to demand surrender from an opponent who has been reduced to one-half or less of its hit points. If your check result equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, it surrenders to you and your allies, drops any weapons it is holding, and takes no hostile actions. If the target is higher level than you, it gains a +5 bonus to its Will Defense. If you or any of your allies attack it, it no longer submits to your will and can act normally. You can only use this Talent against a particular target once per encounter. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Prerequisites: , Weaken Resolve Prerequisite: Once per round, when you deal damage equal to or greater than the target's Damage Threshold, you can make a Persuasion check as a Free Action; if the result equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, you fill the target with terror, causing it to flee from you at top speed for 1 minute. The target can't take Standard Actions, Swift Actions, or Full-Round Actions while fleeing, but the target stops fleeing and can act normally if it is wounded. As a Free Action or Reaction, the target can spend a Force Point (if it has not already spent one earlier in the round) to negate the effect. The effect is automatically negated if the target's level is equal to or higher than your Character Level. This is a Mind-Affecting fear effect. Unlike with other Mind-Affecting effects, you need only to hail a Vehicle to weaken the crew's resolve. When you deal damage that equals or exceeds a Vehicle's Damage Threshold, you may use this Talent; in addition, you may Ready an Action to use this Talent after any Gunner on your Vehicle deals damage that equals or exceeds a Vehicle's Damage Threshold. You make your check against the Vehicle's Commander; all Nonheroic crews are assumed to have a Will Defense of 10. The effect is automatically negated if the target Vehicle's Challenge Level is greater than your Heroic Level or your Vehicle's Challenge Level. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide Prerequisites: , Trained in Persuasion You get under an opponent's skin. Once per encounter, make a Persuasion check to Intimidate one creature within line of sight as a Standard Action. On a success, instead of the normal effect of an Intimidate application of the Persuasion skill, the affected creature can take only a single Swift Action on its next turn. If the target is a higher level than you, it gains a +5 bonus to its Will Defense against the Intimidate check. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide Prerequisites: , Trained in Persuasion Once per encounter, as a Reaction, you can make a Persuasion check to Intimidate one creature that is making a melee or ranged attack against you, and is within your line of sight. If you succeed, you impose a -5 penalty to that attack roll. If the target is a higher level than you, it gains a +5 bonus to its Will Defense against the Intimidate check. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook","description":"Once per encounter, you can make a Persuasion check as a Standard Action to demand surrender from an opponent who has been reduced to one-half or less of its hit points. If your check result equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, it surrenders to you and your allies, drops any weapons it is holding, and takes no hostile actions. If the target is higher level than you, it gains a +5 bonus to its Will Defense. If you or any of your allies attack it, it no longer submits to your will and can act normally. You can only use this Talent against a particular target once per encounter. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Prerequisites: , Weaken Resolve Prerequisite: Once per round, when you deal damage equal to or greater than the target's Damage Threshold, you can make a Persuasion check as a Free Action; if the result equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, you fill the target with terror, causing it to flee from you at top speed for 1 minute. The target can't take Standard Actions, Swift Actions, or Full-Round Actions while fleeing, but the target stops fleeing and can act normally if it is wounded. As a Free Action or Reaction, the target can spend a Force Point (if it has not already spent one earlier in the round) to negate the effect. The effect is automatically negated if the target's level is equal to or higher than your Character Level. This is a Mind-Affecting fear effect. Unlike with other Mind-Affecting effects, you need only to hail a Vehicle to weaken the crew's resolve. When you deal damage that equals or exceeds a Vehicle's Damage Threshold, you may use this Talent; in addition, you may Ready an Action to use this Talent after any Gunner on your Vehicle deals damage that equals or exceeds a Vehicle's Damage Threshold. You make your check against the Vehicle's Commander; all Nonheroic crews are assumed to have a Will Defense of 10. The effect is automatically negated if the target Vehicle's Challenge Level is greater than your Heroic Level or your Vehicle's Challenge Level. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide Prerequisites: , Trained in Persuasion You get under an opponent's skin. Once per encounter, make a Persuasion check to Intimidate one creature within line of sight as a Standard Action. On a success, instead of the normal effect of an Intimidate application of the Persuasion skill, the affected creature can take only a single Swift Action on its next turn. If the target is a higher level than you, it gains a +5 bonus to its Will Defense against the Intimidate check. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide Prerequisites: , Trained in Persuasion Once per encounter, as a Reaction, you can make a Persuasion check to Intimidate one creature that is making a melee or ranged attack against you, and is within your line of sight. If you succeed, you impose a -5 penalty to that attack roll. If the target is a higher level than you, it gains a +5 bonus to its Will Defense against the Intimidate check. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook","class":"Noble","costNumeric":null,"category":"Noble","tree":"Influence","treeId":"8375b9b26b679901","tags":["action-economy","damage-reduction","defender","force","force-defense","force-offense","melee","mobility","noble","positioning","ranged","skills","social","striker","support","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.presence"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.ec8f2ba706cc2c05"}}},{"_id":"92c1142a7b7ff646","name":"Unsavory Reputation","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Infamy","prerequisites":"Inspire Fear III, Notorious","benefit":"When an opponent is reduced to half hit points within 6 squares of you, they take -2 to attack and skill checks for the rest of the encounter.","description":"When an opponent is reduced to half hit points within 6 squares, they take –2 attack and skill checks for the rest of the encounter.","class":"Crime Lord","costNumeric":null,"category":"Crime Lord","tree":"Infamy","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.inspire_fear_iii"},{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.notorious"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"c1be604242cb328f","tags":["damage-reduction","feat-chain","positioning","striker","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.unsavory_reputation"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.b0ecc747a76deb72"}}},{"_id":"3518b10a1fec254f","name":"Weaken Resolve","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Influence","prerequisites":"","benefit":"As , except that the target doesn't stop fleeing from you if it is wounded.","description":"As , except that the target doesn't stop fleeing from you if it is wounded.","class":"Noble","costNumeric":null,"category":"Noble","tree":"Influence","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.presence"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"8375b9b26b679901","tags":["noble","striker"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.weaken_resolve"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.28c306c37ccb9fcf"}}},{"_id":"100813f2e08e4158","name":"Wealth","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Lineage","prerequisites":null,"benefit":"At every level, gain credits equal to class level × 5000.","description":"Gain credits equal to character level × 5,000 each level.","class":"Noble","costNumeric":null,"category":"Noble","tree":"Lineage","treeId":"b5bb4154688c66ab","tags":["noble"]},"effects":[{"_id":"cd6b58ce-5144-4f39-a76a-720505ecdfc8","name":"Wealth","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","chan