4</p>\n<p><strong>Attack Options:</strong> Acrobatic Strike, Echani Training, Weapon Finesse</p>\n<p><strong>Special Actions:</strong> Adept Negotiator, Affliction, Equilibrium, Force Focus, Juyo, Power of the Dark Side, Serenity</p>","derived":{},"npcProfile":{"kind":"heroic","mode":"play","sourceAuthority":"statblock","legalProfile":"heroic","legalState":"unchecked","importMode":"play","playReady":true,"statblockAuthority":true,"sourcePack":"heroic","normalizationVersion":1,"authority":{"hp":"statblock","defenses":"statblock","bab":"statblock","attacks":"statblock","skills":"statblock","damageThreshold":"statblock"}}},"items":[{"_id":"1d0b00af70c34d59","name":"Human","type":"species","img":"icons/svg/mystery-man.svg","system":{"size":"Medium","speed":6,"abilities":"None","skillBonuses":[],"special":["Bonus Feat: Humans gain one bonus feat at 1st level","Bonus Trained Skill: Humans gain one additional trained skill at 1st level"],"languages":["Basic"],"source":"Core","description":"","tags":[],"visionTraits":[],"naturalWeapons":[],"movementTraits":[],"environmentalTraits":[],"combatTraits":{"naturalArmor":0,"weaponProficiencies":[],"otherTraits":[]},"techTraits":[],"forceTraits":[],"socialTraits":[],"bonusFeats":1,"bonusTrainedSkills":1,"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":700,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.species.species-human"}}},{"_id":"8fda20f4596d130e","name":"Acrobatic Strike","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"You can use Acrobatics to tumble through an enemy’s space and gain a +2 bonus on your next melee attack against that enemy.","prerequisite":"Acrobatics 15 ranks","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Galaxy at War","page":23,"tags":["feat-chain","melee","non-force","scout","striker"],"bonus_feat_for":["Scout"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{"value":"Gain +2 competence bonus on next attack against opponent you <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Tumble\" title=\"Tumble\">Tumble</a> past."},"prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"skillTrained","skill":"a6c5e98148aad9a9"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.419a502e59264382"}}},{"_id":"aecc73a82e2cd8b1","name":"Force Sensitivity","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"You can make Use the Force checks and gain access to Force Talents.","prerequisite":"Non-Droid","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":86,"tags":["feat-chain","force"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{"value":"You can make <a href=\"/wiki/Use_the_Force\" title=\"Use the Force\">Use the Force</a> checks and gain access to <a href=\"/wiki/Force_Talents\" title=\"Force Talents\">Force Talents</a>."}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.ddbeb23013d9e917"}}},{"_id":"3c650560ab45aeb2","name":"Force Training","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"You learn a number of Force powers equal to 1 + your Wisdom modifier.","prerequisite":"Force Sensitivity, Trained in Use the Force","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":94,"tags":["feat-chain","force","jedi","striker"],"bonus_feat_for":["Jedi"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"forcePowerGrants":1,"description":{"value":"Learn a number of <a href=\"/wiki/Force_Powers\" title=\"Force Powers\">Force Powers</a> equal to 1 + your <a href=\"/wiki/Wisdom\" title=\"Wisdom\">Wisdom</a> modifier (minimum 1)."},"prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"skillTrained","skill":"usetheforce"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"}},"effects":[{"_id":"d1c60a9b-78e6-4601-85a4-320794fa5a91","name":"Force Training","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Force Training","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Force Training"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.9b7b869a86f39190"}}},{"_id":"5ad561ea099ec4ea","name":"Martial Arts I","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"Increases damage from Unarmed attacks by one die step; gain +1 bonus to Reflex Defense.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":86,"tags":["defender","non-force","striker","unarmed"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{"value":"Increases damage from <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Unarmed\" title=\"Unarmed\">Unarmed</a> attacks by one die step; gain +1 bonus to <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Reflex_Defense\" title=\"Reflex Defense\">Reflex Defense</a>."}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.92f927c92ded9fcf"}}},{"_id":"d81d1124c08fe2d1","name":"Echani Training","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"martial_arts","benefit":"You can double the damage bonus provided by your Strength modifier to Unarmed Attacks (minimum +1) provided you make only one Unarmed attack this turn.\n\nOnce per encounter when you deal damage to a target with an Unarmed Attack you may make an immediate Unarmed Attack against the target's Fortitude Defense as a Free Action; if successful, you knock your opponent to the ground (Prone) in their current square, provided they are no more than one size larger than you.\n\nSpecial: Targets gain a bonus to their Fortitude Defense against being knocked Prone based on their size: Large +5, Huge +10, Gargantuan +20, Colossal +50. Unusually stable creatures (such as those with four legs) gain a +5 bonus to their Fortitude Defense against being knock Prone as well.","prerequisite":"Dexterity 13, Martial Arts I","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Star Wars Saga Edition","page":0,"tags":["action-economy","controller","defender","feat-chain","non-force","positioning","striker","support","sustained-damage","unarmed"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{"value":"In <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Unarmed\" title=\"Unarmed\">Unarmed</a> combat, increase damage, and knock opponent <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Prone\" title=\"Prone\">Prone</a> on Critical Hit."},"prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"attribute","ability":"dex","min":13}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"martialArtsFeat":true},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.f362e5a4ad0a98bd"}}},{"_id":"c331de51ba54c0b6","name":"Skill Focus","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"You gain a +5 bonus on all checks with the selected skill.","prerequisite":"Trained in the chosen skill","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":88,"tags":["feat-chain","noble","non-force","scoundrel","striker"],"bonus_feat_for":["Noble","Scoundrel"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{"value":"Gain +5 competence bonus on <a href=\"/wiki/Skill_Checks\" title=\"Skill Checks\">Skill Checks</a> with one <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Trained_Skill\" title=\"Trained Skill\">Trained Skill</a>."}},"effects":[{"name":"Skill Focus","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.skills.perception.miscMod","mode":2,"value":"5","priority":20}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"transfer":true,"flags":{"swse":{"type":"skill-bonus","skill":"43c5941072ec78af","source":"Skill Focus"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.1592aaedf4b6e40a"}}},{"_id":"07a929be93d22dfc","name":"Skill Focus","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"You gain a +5 bonus on all checks with the selected skill.","prerequisite":"Trained in the chosen skill","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":88,"tags":["feat-chain","noble","non-force","scoundrel","striker"],"bonus_feat_for":["Noble","Scoundrel"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{"value":"Gain +5 competence bonus on <a href=\"/wiki/Skill_Checks\" title=\"Skill Checks\">Skill Checks</a> with one <a class=\"mw-redirect\" href=\"/wiki/Trained_Skill\" title=\"Trained Skill\">Trained Skill</a>."}},"effects":[{"name":"Skill Focus","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.skills.perception.miscMod","mode":2,"value":"5","priority":20}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"transfer":true,"flags":{"swse":{"type":"skill-bonus","skill":"43c5941072ec78af","source":"Skill Focus"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.1592aaedf4b6e40a"}}},{"_id":"07584dfb5a902cef","name":"Weapon Finesse","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"You may use your Dexterity modifier instead of Strength for attack rolls with light melee weapons.","prerequisite":"Dex 13","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":88,"tags":["feat-chain","melee","non-force","scoundrel","scout"],"bonus_feat_for":["Scout","Scoundrel"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{"value":"Use <a href=\"/wiki/Dexterity\" title=\"Dexterity\">Dexterity</a> modifier instead of <a href=\"/wiki/Strength\" title=\"Strength\">Strength</a> modifier on attack rolls with Light Melee Weapons and <a href=\"/wiki/Lightsabers\" title=\"Lightsabers\">Lightsabers</a>."},"prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"bab","min":1}],"_source":"canonical-csv"}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.252b67d6e31c377e"}}},{"_id":"8c5f5b8f5807bbbf","name":"Weapon Focus","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"You gain a +1 bonus on attack rolls with the selected weapon group.","prerequisite":"Proficient with selected weapon group","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":88,"tags":["feat-chain","non-force","soldier","striker"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{"value":"+1 bonus on attack rolls with chosen weapon."}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.c41814601364b643"}}},{"_id":"d97666ccc9d1abfd","name":"Weapon Proficiency","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"Ignore -5 penalty on attack rolls with weapons of a particular type.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["non-force"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{"value":"Ignore -5 penalty on attack rolls with weapons of a particular type."}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.ecc2471ac96ec2d4"}}},{"_id":"83896d699f8557fa","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"You are proficient with simple weapons and do not take the -5 penalty when using them.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["noble","non-force","scoundrel","scout","soldier"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier","Scout","Scoundrel","Noble"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{}},"effects":[{"_id":"220daaa7-e1b5-440d-98cd-10f5e586ef8b","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.2d680cc46a7972da"}}},{"_id":"d5590fcb42674990","name":"Multitarget Power","type":"feat","img":"systems/foundryvtt-swse/assets/icons/force-secret.png","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"When using a Force Power that affects a single target, you can spend a Force Point to affect one additional target.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Core","page":0,"tags":["force-secret"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":"<p><strong>Cost:</strong> Force Point or Destiny Point</p><p>When using a Force Power that affects a single target, you can spend a Force Point to affect one additional target.</p><p>Alternatively, you can spend a Destiny Point to affect one target per four Character Levels.</p>","cost":"Force Point or Destiny Point","alternativeCost":"Alternatively, you can spend a Destiny Point to affect one target per four Character Levels."},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcesecrets.af908ace9a361603"}}},{"_id":"0d4c50422ec911f1","name":"Force Point Recovery","type":"feat","img":"systems/foundryvtt-swse/assets/icons/force-technique.png","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"At the end of an encounter, you automatically recover 1 Force Point spent during the encounter.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Core","page":0,"tags":["force-technique"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"description":"<p>At the end of an encounter, you automatically recover 1 Force Point spent during the encounter.</p>","relatedPower":""},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcetechniques.056ab39b3ab9df10"}}},{"_id":"0197dc4245719bda","name":"Improved Ionize","type":"feat","img":"systems/foundryvtt-swse/assets/icons/force-technique.png","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"When you use the Ionize Force Power, you can spend a Force Point to have the target take full Ion damage (instead of halving the Ion damage after comparing it to the target's Damage Threshold, as normal).","prerequisite":"Ionize","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide","page":0,"tags":["force-technique"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"description":"<p>When you use the Ionize Force Power, you can spend a Force Point to have the target take full Ion damage (instead of halving the Ion damage after comparing it to the target's Damage Threshold, as normal).</p><p><strong>Related Power:</strong> Ionize</p><p><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Ionize</p>","relatedPower":"Ionize"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcetechniques.c588db8cfb8b0ca3"}}},{"_id":"ff4524db8d06dff1","name":"Adept Negotiator","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Jedi Consular","prerequisites":"","benefit":"You can use your Use the Force modifier instead of your Persuasion check modifier when making a Persuasion check. You are considered Trained in the Persuasion skill. If you are entitled to a Persuasion check reroll, you may reroll your Use the Force check instead (subject to the same circumstances and limitations). Prerequisite: If you successfully use the Talent, your target moves an additional -1 step along the Condition Track. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. You affect the Condition Track of the specific character (usually the Vehicle's Commander), not a Starship. You can spend a Full-Round Action advising an ally, thereby granting them a +5 bonus on their next Skill Check. If you spend a Force Point, the bonus increases to +10. The target must be able to (and willing) to hear and understand your voice. You cannot advise yourself. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual As a Standard Action, you can peer into The Force and search for weaknesses in the defenses of your enemies. Make a Use the Force check against the Will Defense of a target creature within 12 squares of you and in your line of sight. If the Skill Check equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, that target takes a -2 penalty to their Reflex Defense against you and all allies who can hear and understand you until the end of your next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide Prerequisite: Whenever you damage an opponent with a Lightsaber attack, you can Take 10 on any Persuasion checks you make before the end of your next turn, even if you would not normally be able to. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide Prerequisite: Once per encounter as a Swift Action, you can choose one ally within your line of sight that can hear and understand you. Until the end of the encounter, that ally adds your Wisdom bonus to its Will Defense against Mind-Affecting effects. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide Once per turn as a Swift Action, you can spend a Force Point to let one adjacent ally use the Aid Another Action (as a Reaction) to assist you with a Skill Check. You must make the Skill Check before the end of your turn, or the benefit of the Aid Another Action is lost. An ally that has already used the Aid Another Action to assist you since the end of your last turn may not be targeted by this Talent. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide You gain a +2 insight bonus to your Will Defense. Also, as a Swift Action, you can spend a Force Point to give all allies within 6 squares of you a +2 insight bonus to their Will Defense that lasts for the remainder of the encounter. This bonus does not extend to allies outside the range of the effect, even if they move within 6 squares of you later on. Allies who benefit from this Talent must remain within 6 squares of you to retain the insight bonus, and they lose it if you are knocked unconscious or killed. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Rebellion Era Campaign Guide When you deal damage to a target by making a Lightsaber attack on your turn, you can use a Swift Action before the end of your turn to activate this Talent. If you do so, allies adjacent to the target at the time you make the attack gain a +2 circumstance bonus to melee attack rolls against the target until the start of your next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide","description":"You can use your Use the Force modifier instead of your Persuasion check modifier when making a Persuasion check. You are considered Trained in the Persuasion skill. If you are entitled to a Persuasion check reroll, you may reroll your Use the Force check instead (subject to the same circumstances and limitations). Prerequisite: If you successfully use the Talent, your target moves an additional -1 step along the Condition Track. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. You affect the Condition Track of the specific character (usually the Vehicle's Commander), not a Starship. You can spend a Full-Round Action advising an ally, thereby granting them a +5 bonus on their next Skill Check. If you spend a Force Point, the bonus increases to +10. The target must be able to (and willing) to hear and understand your voice. You cannot advise yourself. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual As a Standard Action, you can peer into The Force and search for weaknesses in the defenses of your enemies. Make a Use the Force check against the Will Defense of a target creature within 12 squares of you and in your line of sight. If the Skill Check equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, that target takes a -2 penalty to their Reflex Defense against you and all allies who can hear and understand you until the end of your next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide Prerequisite: Whenever you damage an opponent with a Lightsaber attack, you can Take 10 on any Persuasion checks you make before the end of your next turn, even if you would not normally be able to. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide Prerequisite: Once per encounter as a Swift Action, you can choose one ally within your line of sight that can hear and understand you. Until the end of the encounter, that ally adds your Wisdom bonus to its Will Defense against Mind-Affecting effects. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide Once per turn as a Swift Action, you can spend a Force Point to let one adjacent ally use the Aid Another Action (as a Reaction) to assist you with a Skill Check. You must make the Skill Check before the end of your turn, or the benefit of the Aid Another Action is lost. An ally that has already used the Aid Another Action to assist you since the end of your last turn may not be targeted by this Talent. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide You gain a +2 insight bonus to your Will Defense. Also, as a Swift Action, you can spend a Force Point to give all allies within 6 squares of you a +2 insight bonus to their Will Defense that lasts for the remainder of the encounter. This bonus does not extend to allies outside the range of the effect, even if they move within 6 squares of you later on. Allies who benefit from this Talent must remain within 6 squares of you to retain the insight bonus, and they lose it if you are knocked unconscious or killed. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Rebellion Era Campaign Guide When you deal damage to a target by making a Lightsaber attack on your turn, you can use a Swift Action before the end of your turn to activate this Talent. If you do so, allies adjacent to the target at the time you make the attack gain a +2 circumstance bonus to melee attack rolls against the target until the start of your next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide","class":"Jedi","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","tree":"Jedi Consular","treeId":"e99cfa9db8493573","tags":["action-economy","condition-removal","controller","defender","force","force-control","force-defense","force-offense","jedi","leader","light-side","lightsaber","melee","mobility","positioning","scout","skills","social","striker","support","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.adept_negotiator"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.7acc479dee2d3b10"}}},{"_id":"a242bd1840e8a384","name":"Affliction","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Sith","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Once per encounter, as a Reaction when you damage a Force-sensitive opponent, the dark taint of your power allows you to sap some of the opponent's strength, and convert it to personal power, regaining one spent Force Power. Additionally, the target loses one Force Point. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide See also: Sith Alchemy Talent Tree","description":"Once per encounter, as a Reaction when you damage a Force-sensitive opponent, the dark taint of your power allows you to sap some of the opponent's strength, and convert it to personal power, regaining one spent Force Power. Additionally, the target loses one Force Point. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide See also: Sith Alchemy Talent Tree","class":"Sith Apprentice","costNumeric":null,"category":"Sith Apprentice","tree":"Sith","treeId":"d1037bc7a08ea80b","tags":["action-economy","dark-side","force","force-offense","jedi","striker","support"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.affliction"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.776a0fa8ae532ccc"}}},{"_id":"18a30df1da9ddcf2","name":"Deflect","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Lightsaber Forms","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Redirect Shot","description":"Redirect Shot","class":"Jedi","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","tree":"Lightsaber Forms","treeId":"2bc2572e852832e4","tags":["jedi","lightsaber","melee","ranged"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.deflect"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.72c644f7a09b1186"}}},{"_id":"b99ba5208ab69045","name":"Equilibrium","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Force Adept","prerequisites":"","benefit":"The Force shields you against ailments, toxins, and radiation poisoning, making you immune to Disease, Poison, and Radiation. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions You are particularly in tune with The Living Force. When you successfully use Search Your Feelings, you gain a Force Point that must be used before the end of the encounter. If you use this Force Point in a manner that would end in unfavorable results (per Search Your Feelings), you raise your Dark Side Score by 1. lf you use the Force Point in an action that would normally raise your Dark Side Score, you raise your Dark Side Score by 2 instead. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions","description":"The Force shields you against ailments, toxins, and radiation poisoning, making you immune to Disease, Poison, and Radiation. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions You are particularly in tune with The Living Force. When you successfully use Search Your Feelings, you gain a Force Point that must be used before the end of the encounter. If you use this Force Point in a manner that would end in unfavorable results (per Search Your Feelings), you raise your Dark Side Score by 1. lf you use the Force Point in an action that would normally raise your Dark Side Score, you raise your Dark Side Score by 2 instead. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions","costNumeric":null,"tree":"Force Adept","treeId":"e35ee41362604227","tags":["action-economy","dark-side","defender","force","shields","support"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.equilibrium"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.328a880e60f2320f"}}},{"_id":"53a0593d8c0c1382","name":"Force Focus","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Control","prerequisites":null,"benefit":"DC 15 Use the Force check to regain one Force power.","description":"Make a Use the Force check to regain one expended Force power.","costNumeric":null,"tree":"Control","treeId":"d3661aa9906bdc79","tags":["force"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.force_focus"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.af51d4e76675b183"}}},{"_id":"0ab6b3f80d999d9e","name":"Force Suppression","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Control","prerequisites":null,"benefit":"Attempt to rebuke a Force power; if you fail, lessen its effect by one step; only works on powers with variable effects.","description":"Rebuke a Force power; on a failed rebuke, reduce its effect.","costNumeric":null,"tree":"Control","prerequisitesMeta":["Requires Force Power: rebuke Force power"],"treeId":"d3661aa9906bdc79","tags":["force"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.force_suppression"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.7fa47c5d2c33ed40"}}},{"_id":"50abf197735727b0","name":"Juyo","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Lightsaber Forms","prerequisites":"Prerequisites: Double Attack (Lightsabers), Skill Focus (Use the Force), Base Attack Bonus +12","benefit":"Weapon Focus (Lightsabers), Weapon Specialization (Lightsabers), Base Attack Bonus +12 When attacking with a Lightsaber, you score a critical hit on a natural roll of 19 or 20. However, a natural 19 is not considered an automatic hit; if you roll a natural 19 and still miss the target, you do not score a critical hit. Homebrew Reference Book: Clone Wars Saga Edition Fan Sourcebook - The Dark Side You may make a Deception check as a Swift Action (instead of a Standard Action) when attempting to Feint in combat. Maho-Kai Lightsaber Form Talent created by Wikia user SirenEyes. Whenever you make multiple attacks with any type of Lightsaber as part of a Full Attack, you may choose to forgo an attack and instead activate a Force Power that requires a Standard Action or Move Action to activate. When activating a Force Power in this manner, apply the attack roll penalty to the Use the Force check to activate the Force Power. You may only activate one Force Power in this manner each Round. Tripzest Lightsaber Form Talent created by Wikia user Droidscotty.","description":"Weapon Focus (Lightsabers), Weapon Specialization (Lightsabers), Base Attack Bonus +12 When attacking with a Lightsaber, you score a critical hit on a natural roll of 19 or 20. However, a natural 19 is not considered an automatic hit; if you roll a natural 19 and still miss the target, you do not score a critical hit. Homebrew Reference Book: Clone Wars Saga Edition Fan Sourcebook - The Dark Side You may make a Deception check as a Swift Action (instead of a Standard Action) when attempting to Feint in combat. Maho-Kai Lightsaber Form Talent created by Wikia user SirenEyes. Whenever you make multiple attacks with any type of Lightsaber as part of a Full Attack, you may choose to forgo an attack and instead activate a Force Power that requires a Standard Action or Move Action to activate. When activating a Force Power in this manner, apply the attack roll penalty to the Use the Force check to activate the Force Power. You may only activate one Force Power in this manner each Round. Tripzest Lightsaber Form Talent created by Wikia user Droidscotty.","class":"Jedi Knight","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi Knight","tree":"Lightsaber Forms","treeId":"2bc2572e852832e4","tags":["action-economy","burst-damage","controller","dark-side","feat-chain","force","force-control","force-offense","jedi","lightsaber","melee","mobility","precision","skills","social","striker","sustained-damage","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.juyo"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.5fd19be0deca1115"}}},{"_id":"a1051616ee5dee33","name":"Power of the Dark Side","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Dark Side","prerequisites":"Dark Side Score equal to Wisdom Score","benefit":"Charisma 13 As a Standard Action, you grant yourself and all allies within 6 squares of you a +1 Force bonus to all Defenses until the end of the encounter. These bonuses are lost if you fall unconscious or die. Affected allies that move out of range lose the benefits for as long as they remain out of range. Prerequisite: Once per day, you can use a Force Power that normally takes a Standard Action or a Move Action as a Swift Action. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide Sometimes your anger consumes you. As a Swift Action, you can take a -5 penalty to your Will Defense to gain a +2 Force bonus on attack rolls. The penalty and bonus last until the beginning of your next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide Prerequisite: Whenever an effect would normally move you down the Condition Track, you may spend a Force Point and increase your Dark Side Score by 1 to negate that movement down the Condition Track. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual Once per encounter as a Swift Action, you can return one Force Power with the [Dark Side] descriptor to your Force Power Suite without spending a Force Point. You can select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select it, you can use it one additional time per encounter. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Threats of the Galaxy As a Standard Action, you can spend a Force Point to drain the knowledge of an opponent you touch; you must succeed on a Use the Force check (DC equal to the target's Will Defense) to activate this Talent, and if you fail to activate this Talent, you may not try again on the same target for one day. If successful, you immediately become Trained in one Skill that the target is Trained in; if you are already Trained in that Skill, you instead gain Skill Focus in that Skill. This effect lasts for one day. Additionally, your target moves -1 Persistent step along the Condition Track, and the Persistent Condition can be removed only by resting for 8 hours. Additionally, you can choose to instead sift through the mind of the target, looking for a specific piece of knowledge or information. Doing so requires you to make a Perception check against the target's Will Defense; success indicates that you pull the relevant information from the target's mind. When you do so, you do not gain the bonus Trained Skill or Skill Focus normally granted by this Talent, but otherwise the Talent functions as normal. Using this Talent increases your Dark Side Score by 1. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual When you die, you become a Dark Side Spirit until the end of the encounter. You continue to occupy a space in this form, but other creatures can occupy the same space or move through your space without impediment. As a Standard Action, you can attempt to possess an adjacent target. You must succeed on a Use the Force check against an adjacent target's Will Defense. If your check result equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, you deal 8d6 points of Stun damage to the target; if you reduce the target to 0 Hit Points or move it to the bottom of the Condition Track with this attack, you possess the target as though it were a willing host. Alternatively, as a Standard Action, you can transfer your essence into a single adjacent object, such as a Holocron or a Lightsaber. If you do so, you lie dormant within the object until another creature attempts to use that object, at which time you can emerge and attempt to possess the creature, as described above. If you do not possess a creature or object within 10 rounds of manifesting as a Dark Side Spirit, your spirit dissipates and ceases to exist. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide Prerequisite: When you roll a Natural 20 on a Use the Force check to activate a Force Power that directly deals damage to a target, you can choose not to regain all of your spent Force Powers as normal and instead the targets damaged by the Force Power take half that damage again at the start of their next turn. Only Force Powers that directly damage the target are subject to this Talent, including Corruption, Force Blast, Force Grip, Force Lightning, Force Slam, Force Thrust (only when spending a Force Point), and Repulse (only when spending a Force Point). Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook Prerequisite: You can create balls of unnatural energy, enabling you to make a ranged attack roll against the Reflex Defense of one target within 12 squares and line of sight, dealing 2d6 points of energy damage to the target on a successful attack. Using this Talent increases your Dark Side Score by 1. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook Prerequisites: , Swift Power When using a Force Power that directly inflicts damage, you treat the target's Damage Threshold as though it were 5 points lower when determining if the target moves along the Condition Track. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook Prerequisite: Whenever your character moves 3 or more squares in a round you gain Concealment; you may choose not to use this Talent when you move.","description":"Charisma 13 As a Standard Action, you grant yourself and all allies within 6 squares of you a +1 Force bonus to all Defenses until the end of the encounter. These bonuses are lost if you fall unconscious or die. Affected allies that move out of range lose the benefits for as long as they remain out of range. Prerequisite: Once per day, you can use a Force Power that normally takes a Standard Action or a Move Action as a Swift Action. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide Sometimes your anger consumes you. As a Swift Action, you can take a -5 penalty to your Will Defense to gain a +2 Force bonus on attack rolls. The penalty and bonus last until the beginning of your next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide Prerequisite: Whenever an effect would normally move you down the Condition Track, you may spend a Force Point and increase your Dark Side Score by 1 to negate that movement down the Condition Track. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual Once per encounter as a Swift Action, you can return one Force Power with the [Dark Side] descriptor to your Force Power Suite without spending a Force Point. You can select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select it, you can use it one additional time per encounter. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Threats of the Galaxy As a Standard Action, you can spend a Force Point to drain the knowledge of an opponent you touch; you must succeed on a Use the Force check (DC equal to the target's Will Defense) to activate this Talent, and if you fail to activate this Talent, you may not try again on the same target for one day. If successful, you immediately become Trained in one Skill that the target is Trained in; if you are already Trained in that Skill, you instead gain Skill Focus in that Skill. This effect lasts for one day. Additionally, your target moves -1 Persistent step along the Condition Track, and the Persistent Condition can be removed only by resting for 8 hours. Additionally, you can choose to instead sift through the mind of the target, looking for a specific piece of knowledge or information. Doing so requires you to make a Perception check against the target's Will Defense; success indicates that you pull the relevant information from the target's mind. When you do so, you do not gain the bonus Trained Skill or Skill Focus normally granted by this Talent, but otherwise the Talent functions as normal. Using this Talent increases your Dark Side Score by 1. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual When you die, you become a Dark Side Spirit until the end of the encounter. You continue to occupy a space in this form, but other creatures can occupy the same space or move through your space without impediment. As a Standard Action, you can attempt to possess an adjacent target. You must succeed on a Use the Force check against an adjacent target's Will Defense. If your check result equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, you deal 8d6 points of Stun damage to the target; if you reduce the target to 0 Hit Points or move it to the bottom of the Condition Track with this attack, you possess the target as though it were a willing host. Alternatively, as a Standard Action, you can transfer your essence into a single adjacent object, such as a Holocron or a Lightsaber. If you do so, you lie dormant within the object until another creature attempts to use that object, at which time you can emerge and attempt to possess the creature, as described above. If you do not possess a creature or object within 10 rounds of manifesting as a Dark Side Spirit, your spirit dissipates and ceases to exist. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide Prerequisite: When you roll a Natural 20 on a Use the Force check to activate a Force Power that directly deals damage to a target, you can choose not to regain all of your spent Force Powers as normal and instead the targets damaged by the Force Power take half that damage again at the start of their next turn. Only Force Powers that directly damage the target are subject to this Talent, including Corruption, Force Blast, Force Grip, Force Lightning, Force Slam, Force Thrust (only when spending a Force Point), and Repulse (only when spending a Force Point). Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook Prerequisite: You can create balls of unnatural energy, enabling you to make a ranged attack roll against the Reflex Defense of one target within 12 squares and line of sight, dealing 2d6 points of energy damage to the target on a successful attack. Using this Talent increases your Dark Side Score by 1. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook Prerequisites: , Swift Power When using a Force Power that directly inflicts damage, you treat the target's Damage Threshold as though it were 5 points lower when determining if the target moves along the Condition Track. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook Prerequisite: Whenever your character moves 3 or more squares in a round you gain Concealment; you may choose not to use this Talent when you move.","costNumeric":null,"tree":"Dark Side","treeId":"de95d37c72b1c4cd","tags":["action-economy","condition-removal","controller","damage-reduction","dark-side","defender","feat-chain","force","force-control","force-defense","force-offense","leader","light-side","lightsaber","melee","mobility","perception","positioning","ranged","scaling","skills","stealth","striker","support","sustained-damage","talent-chain"]},"effects":[{"_id":"b3ad7fe2-78a8-42b3-83dc-385122d061ed","name":"Power of the Dark Side","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.damage","mode":2,"value":"1"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Power of the Dark Side"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.power_of_the_dark_side"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.627bd3abd30b973f"}}},{"_id":"305c533cdacf1f08","name":"Weapon Specialization (Lightsabers)","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Duelist","tree":"Duelist","prerequisites":"","description":"Greater Weapon Focus (Lightsabers) You gain a +2 bonus on melee damage rolls with Lightsabers. This bonus stacks with the bonus granted by the Talent. Whenever you make multiple attacks with any type of Lightsaber as part of a Full Attack, you reduce the penalty on your attack rolls by 2. You can take this Talent multiple times; each time you take this Talent, you reduce the penalty on your attack rolls by an additional 2. See also: Maiming Foes When you deal damage with a Lightsaber that is equal to or greater than both the target's current Hit Points and the target's Damage Threshold (that is, when you would deal enough damage to kill your target), you may choose to use this Talent. Instead of dealing full damage, you instead deal half damage to your target and move it -1 step on the Condition Track. In addition, you sever one of your target's arms at the wrist or elbow joint, or one of the target's legs at the knee or ankle joint (your choice). Severing part of an arm prevents the target from wielding weapons or using tools in that hand, and imposes a -5 penalty on Skill Checks and Ability Checks keyed to Strength and Dexterity. Severing part of a leg knocks the target Prone, reduces the target's Speed by half, reduces its Carrying Capacity by half, and imposes a -5 penalty on Skill Checks and Ability Checks keyed to Strength and Dexterity. Because of the severity of such an injury, losing part of a limb causes a Persistent Condition that can only be removed by having Surgery successfully performed on you. A Cybernetic Prosthesis negates these reductions and penalties. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","benefit":"Greater Weapon Focus (Lightsabers) You gain a +2 bonus on melee damage rolls with Lightsabers. This bonus stacks with the bonus granted by the Talent. Whenever you make multiple attacks with any type of Lightsaber as part of a Full Attack, you reduce the penalty on your attack rolls by 2. You can take this Talent multiple times; each time you take this Talent, you reduce the penalty on your attack rolls by an additional 2. See also: Maiming Foes When you deal damage with a Lightsaber that is equal to or greater than both the target's current Hit Points and the target's Damage Threshold (that is, when you would deal enough damage to kill your target), you may choose to use this Talent. Instead of dealing full damage, you instead deal half damage to your target and move it -1 step on the Condition Track. In addition, you sever one of your target's arms at the wrist or elbow joint, or one of the target's legs at the knee or ankle joint (your choice). Severing part of an arm prevents the target from wielding weapons or using tools in that hand, and imposes a -5 penalty on Skill Checks and Ability Checks keyed to Strength and Dexterity. Severing part of a leg knocks the target Prone, reduces the target's Speed by half, reduces its Carrying Capacity by half, and imposes a -5 penalty on Skill Checks and Ability Checks keyed to Strength and Dexterity. Because of the severity of such an injury, losing part of a limb causes a Persistent Condition that can only be removed by having Surgery successfully performed on you. A Cybernetic Prosthesis negates these reductions and penalties. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"b3c5d90b5036f39b","tags":["burst-damage","condition-removal","controller","damage-reduction","defender","force","force-control","force-offense","leader","lightsaber","melee","mobility","scaling","striker","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.00a9210772a64a19"}}},{"_id":"5cec44389bb1cc6e","name":"Dark Rage","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/eye.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"Unknown","useTheForce":"","time":"standard","range":"","target":"","duration":"","effect":"","special":"","descriptor":"","dcChart":"","maintainable":false,"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1,"perDay":true}},"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"placeholder":true,"unresolved":"Dark Rage"}}},{"_id":"a372c946698ce66f","name":"Ionize","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/eye.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"Unknown","useTheForce":"","time":"standard","range":"","target":"","duration":"","effect":"","special":"","descriptor":"","dcChart":"","maintainable":false,"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1,"perDay":true}},"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"placeholder":true,"unresolved":"Ionize"}}},{"_id":"4c91f47fa4187db1","name":"Force Grip","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":3,"discipline":"dark-side","useTheForce":15,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One creature","duration":"Concentration","effect":"<p>You use the Force to telekinetically choke or crush your target. The target takes damage each round based on your Use the Force check result.</p>","special":"<p>This is a Dark Side power. The target is immobilized while gripped.</p>","descriptor":["Dark Side","Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[{"dc":15,"effect":"2d6 damage/round","description":"Target takes 2d6 damage per round and is immobilized"},{"dc":20,"effect":"4d6 damage/round","description":"Target takes 4d6 damage per round and is immobilized"},{"dc":25,"effect":"6d6 damage/round + lift","description":"Target takes 6d6 damage per round, is immobilized, and lifted off ground"},{"dc":30,"effect":"8d6 damage/round + crush","description":"Target takes 8d6 damage per round and is being crushed (fort save or die)"}],"maintainable":true,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":96,"tags":["attack","damage","dark-side","telekinetic","immobilize"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.f41a957f71e98a6a"}}},{"_id":"7ed9da8eb55041e3","name":"Force Lightning","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":4,"discipline":"dark-side","useTheForce":15,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One creature","duration":"Instantaneous","effect":"<p>You unleash devastating arcs of Force Lightning from your fingertips. The target takes lightning damage based on your Use the Force check result.</p>","special":"<p>This is a Dark Side power. Using it gains you a Dark Side Point.</p>","descriptor":["Dark Side","Force Lightning"],"dcChart":[{"dc":15,"effect":"2d6 lightning damage","description":"Target takes 2d6 lightning damage"},{"dc":20,"effect":"4d6 lightning damage","description":"Target takes 4d6 lightning damage"},{"dc":25,"effect":"6d6 lightning damage + stun","description":"Target takes 6d6 lightning damage and is stunned for 1 round"},{"dc":30,"effect":"8d6 lightning damage + stun 1d4","description":"Target takes 8d6 lightning damage and is stunned for 1d4 rounds"}],"maintainable":true,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":96,"tags":["attack","damage","dark-side","lightning"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.0a422b939edfad56"}}},{"_id":"7e8db90daf8b808f","name":"Force Stun","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telepathic","useTheForce":20,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One creature","duration":"1 round","effect":"<p>You use the Force to overwhelm your target's mind, stunning them. The target must make a Will save (DC = your UTF check) or be stunned for 1 round.</p>","special":"","descriptor":["Mind-Affecting"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":97,"tags":["attack","stun","mind-affecting"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.a214d4f56b4abe11"}}},{"_id":"3b7d720c6b04e7c9","name":"Move Object","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telekinetic","useTheForce":15,"time":"Standard Action","range":"12 squares","target":"One object or creature","duration":"Concentration","effect":"<p>You move objects or creatures through the air using telekinesis. The maximum size/weight you can move depends on your Use the Force check result.</p>","special":"<p>Unwilling creatures can make a Will save (DC = your UTF check) to resist being moved.</p>","descriptor":["Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[{"dc":15,"effect":"Medium (50 kg)","description":"Move objects up to Medium size or 50 kg"},{"dc":20,"effect":"Large (250 kg)","description":"Move objects up to Large size or 250 kg"},{"dc":25,"effect":"Huge (1 ton)","description":"Move objects up to Huge size or 1 metric ton"},{"dc":30,"effect":"Gargantuan (5 tons)","description":"Move objects up to Gargantuan size or 5 metric tons"},{"dc":35,"effect":"Colossal (20 tons)","description":"Move objects up to Colossal size or 20 metric tons (starfighter-sized)"}],"maintainable":true,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":98,"tags":["telekinetic","movement","utility"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.289013a32bd179ad"}}},{"_id":"e7a4ef0c88f7e87b","name":"Rebuke","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telepathic","useTheForce":20,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One Force-sensitive creature","duration":"1 round","effect":"<p>You overwhelm a Force user with a powerful Force presence. If the target is Force-sensitive, they must make a Will save (DC = your UTF check) or be dazed for 1 round.</p>","special":"<p>This power only affects Force-sensitive creatures.</p>","descriptor":["Mind-Affecting"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":99,"tags":["debuff","force-user","daze"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.390074b44aedfa2a"}}},{"_id":"90f49c3772e8d9e7","name":"Wound","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/eye.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"Unknown","useTheForce":"","time":"standard","range":"","target":"","duration":"","effect":"","special":"","descriptor":"","dcChart":"","maintainable":false,"inSuite":true,"us