Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"You are proficient with simple weapons and do not take the -5 penalty when using them.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["noble","non-force","scoundrel","scout","soldier"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier","Scout","Scoundrel","Noble"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{}},"effects":[{"_id":"220daaa7-e1b5-440d-98cd-10f5e586ef8b","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.2d680cc46a7972da"}}},{"_id":"095d1a879e134e70","name":"Armored Defense","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Knight's Armor","prerequisites":"","benefit":"When calculating your Reflex Defense, you may add your Heroic Level plus one-half your Armor bonus (rounded down), or your Armor bonus alone, whichever is higher. This Talent counts as both the Talent and the Improved Talent for the purposes of prerequisites. You are adept at using a Cortosis Gauntlet to parry Lightsaber attacks. You gain a +2 bonus when making an opposed Unarmed melee attack roll against a Lightsaber attack.","description":"When calculating your Reflex Defense, you may add your Heroic Level plus one-half your Armor bonus (rounded down), or your Armor bonus alone, whichever is higher. This Talent counts as both the Talent and the Improved Talent for the purposes of prerequisites. You are adept at using a Cortosis Gauntlet to parry Lightsaber attacks. You gain a +2 bonus when making an opposed Unarmed melee attack roll against a Lightsaber attack.","class":"Soldier","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","tree":"Knight's Armor","treeId":"ea01d740c91888b3","tags":["armor","defender","lightsaber","melee","scaling","soldier","striker","sustained-damage","unarmed"]},"effects":[{"_id":"28f1f3db-0c6f-4614-bdcf-000f1542a25b","name":"Armored Defense","icon":"icons/svg/shield.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.defenses.reflex.misc","mode":2,"value":"1","priority":20}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Armored Defense"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.armored_defense"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.4c236343b01ea763"}}},{"_id":"17bc07d527f7a4ae","name":"Battle Analysis","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Commando","prerequisites":"Trained in Initiative","benefit":"When you make a ranged attack with a Pistol or Rifle, all allies within 6 squares of you when you made the attack gain a +1 bonus to Reflex Defense until the start of your next turn. Allies within range don't need to be within your line of sight to gain the bonus. When you use the Mechanics skill to Handle Explosives, the explosion deals +2 dice of damage. You may take this Talent multiple times; its effects stack. You can distract opponents and convince them that you are the most tempting (or most dangerous) target in the area. As a Swift Action, make a Persuasion check and compare the result to the Will Defense of all opponents within line of sight. If the check result exceeds an opponent's Will Defense, that opponent cannot attack any character within 6 squares of you until the start of your next turn as long as you do not have Cover against that opponent. (The affected opponent may still attack you, however.) If you are the Pilot of a Vehicle, you may use this Talent to protect allied Vehicles. You may use it to protect Vehicles no more than one size category larger than your own. Once per round, you may spend a Swift Action to shield a single adjacent ally from attacks, taking the damage and suffering the ill effects in your ally's stead. Until the start of your next turn, any attack made against the protected ally targets you instead. You may elect not to shield your protected ally against a given attack, provided the decision is made before the attack roll is made. If you are the Pilot of a Vehicle, you may use this Talent to protect allied Vehicles. You may use it to protect Vehicles no more than one size category larger than your own. Once per day as a Swift Action, you can move +5 steps on the Condition Track. This does not remove any Persistent Conditions that may be affecting you. This Talent does not affect the Condition Track of a Vehicle. You can select this talent multiple times. Each time you select this Talent, you can use it one additional time per day. You can catch a Second Wind one extra time per day. If you have this Talent and the Extra Second Wind feat, you can catch your Second Wind a total of three times per day. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy of Intrigue Prerequisite: Whenever you have the benefit of Cover, you can spend two Swift Actions to treat it as Improved Cover until the start of your next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Threats of the Galaxy Prerequisite: When one or more allies uses the Aid Another Action to give you a bonus to your attack roll, you gain a circumstance bonus equal to the total bonus provided to your damage roll. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook You add an additional die of damage when attacking with any weapon that has a Burst radius.","description":"When you make a ranged attack with a Pistol or Rifle, all allies within 6 squares of you when you made the attack gain a +1 bonus to Reflex Defense until the start of your next turn. Allies within range don't need to be within your line of sight to gain the bonus. When you use the Mechanics skill to Handle Explosives, the explosion deals +2 dice of damage. You may take this Talent multiple times; its effects stack. You can distract opponents and convince them that you are the most tempting (or most dangerous) target in the area. As a Swift Action, make a Persuasion check and compare the result to the Will Defense of all opponents within line of sight. If the check result exceeds an opponent's Will Defense, that opponent cannot attack any character within 6 squares of you until the start of your next turn as long as you do not have Cover against that opponent. (The affected opponent may still attack you, however.) If you are the Pilot of a Vehicle, you may use this Talent to protect allied Vehicles. You may use it to protect Vehicles no more than one size category larger than your own. Once per round, you may spend a Swift Action to shield a single adjacent ally from attacks, taking the damage and suffering the ill effects in your ally's stead. Until the start of your next turn, any attack made against the protected ally targets you instead. You may elect not to shield your protected ally against a given attack, provided the decision is made before the attack roll is made. If you are the Pilot of a Vehicle, you may use this Talent to protect allied Vehicles. You may use it to protect Vehicles no more than one size category larger than your own. Once per day as a Swift Action, you can move +5 steps on the Condition Track. This does not remove any Persistent Conditions that may be affecting you. This Talent does not affect the Condition Track of a Vehicle. You can select this talent multiple times. Each time you select this Talent, you can use it one additional time per day. You can catch a Second Wind one extra time per day. If you have this Talent and the Extra Second Wind feat, you can catch your Second Wind a total of three times per day. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy of Intrigue Prerequisite: Whenever you have the benefit of Cover, you can spend two Swift Actions to treat it as Improved Cover until the start of your next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Threats of the Galaxy Prerequisite: When one or more allies uses the Aid Another Action to give you a bonus to your attack roll, you gain a circumstance bonus equal to the total bonus provided to your damage roll. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook You add an additional die of damage when attacking with any weapon that has a Burst radius.","class":"Soldier","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","tree":"Commando","treeId":"798ed0945cbdac1c","tags":["action-economy","battlefield-control","burst-damage","condition-removal","controller","defender","feat-chain","force","force-control","force-defense","force-offense","mechanics","mobility","piloting","positioning","ranged","scaling","shields","skills","social","soldier","striker","support","sustained-damage","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.battle_analysis"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.7df2e8e4f18dc909"}}},{"_id":"a5e77ab6fb795300","name":"Elusive Dogfighter","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Expert Pilot","prerequisites":"Wisdom 13","benefit":"You are an expert at escaping Dogfights. When making an opposed check to Disengage from a Dogfight, you can reroll your Pilot check, taking the better result. If you fail, you remain in the Dogfight, but the Gunners on your Vehicle do not take penalties to their attack rolls. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy of Intrigue Once per encounter, if your Vehicle takes damage, make a Pilot check and compare the result to the Reflex Defense of one adjacent allied Vehicle. If your check result is higher, the allied Vehicle takes the damage instead. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Starships of the Galaxy Choose a single type of Vehicle from the following list: Airspeeder Capital Ship Space Transport Speeder Starfighter Walker When you are the Pilot or Gunner of that type of Vehicle, you gain a +2 bonus to all attack rolls with its Vehicle Weapons, and may Take 10 on any Pilot checks made while piloting that type of Vehicle, even when you are otherwise unable to. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Starships of the Galaxy As a Swift Action, you can make a DC 15 Pilot check to assist any allied Starfighter or Airspeeder within 2 squares at Starship Scale. If you succeed, the Pilot of that Vehicle gains a +5 bonus on all opposed Pilot checks relating to the Dogfight Action until the start of your next turn.","description":"You are an expert at escaping Dogfights. When making an opposed check to Disengage from a Dogfight, you can reroll your Pilot check, taking the better result. If you fail, you remain in the Dogfight, but the Gunners on your Vehicle do not take penalties to their attack rolls. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy of Intrigue Once per encounter, if your Vehicle takes damage, make a Pilot check and compare the result to the Reflex Defense of one adjacent allied Vehicle. If your check result is higher, the allied Vehicle takes the damage instead. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Starships of the Galaxy Choose a single type of Vehicle from the following list: Airspeeder Capital Ship Space Transport Speeder Starfighter Walker When you are the Pilot or Gunner of that type of Vehicle, you gain a +2 bonus to all attack rolls with its Vehicle Weapons, and may Take 10 on any Pilot checks made while piloting that type of Vehicle, even when you are otherwise unable to. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Starships of the Galaxy As a Swift Action, you can make a DC 15 Pilot check to assist any allied Starfighter or Airspeeder within 2 squares at Starship Scale. If you succeed, the Pilot of that Vehicle gains a +5 bonus on all opposed Pilot checks relating to the Dogfight Action until the start of your next turn.","class":"Ace Pilot","costNumeric":null,"category":"Ace Pilot","tree":"Expert Pilot","treeId":"b17c1515c06361d6","tags":["action-economy","defender","feat-chain","mobility","piloting","positioning","scaling","scout","skills","striker","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.elusive_dogfighter"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.fead6e3522fd458a"}}},{"_id":"7a45aaca302d8df0","name":"Penetrating Attack","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Weapon Master","prerequisites":"Weapon Focus (Chosen Weapon)","benefit":"This replaces the effects of the Talent. Choose one Exotic Weapon or weapon group with which you're proficient. You gain a +1 bonus on attack rolls with the chosen Exotic Weapon or weapon from the chosen group. This bonus stacks with the bonus granted by the Weapon Focus feat. You may select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select this Talent, it applies to a different Exotic Weapon or weapon group.","description":"This replaces the effects of the Talent. Choose one Exotic Weapon or weapon group with which you're proficient. You gain a +1 bonus on attack rolls with the chosen Exotic Weapon or weapon from the chosen group. This bonus stacks with the bonus granted by the Weapon Focus feat. You may select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select this Talent, it applies to a different Exotic Weapon or weapon group.","class":"Soldier","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","tree":"Weapon Master","treeId":"2f720d8b061f9bd0","tags":["feat-chain","leader","scaling","soldier","striker","talent-chain"]},"effects":[{"_id":"a0fba2f5-3da6-476e-9ac5-900be2d16e6b","name":"Penetrating Attack","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.combat.weaponGroupDRReduction","mode":2,"value":"5"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Penetrating Attack","effectType":"dr_reduction","weaponGroupSpecific":true,"notes":"Weapon group specific - applies when using designated weapon group"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.penetrating_attack"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.7d547902b8d9109e"}}},{"_id":"1240b63e30bd4b13","name":"Squadron Maneuvers","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Squadron Leader","prerequisites":"Prerequisites: Charisma 13, Force Sensitivity","benefit":"Prerequisites: Charisma 13, Wisdom 13, Starship Tactics, Once per encounter, when you use a non-attack pattern Starship Maneuver, you grant all ships in your squadron the ability to use the same Starship Maneuver once on their next turn. The Pilot of each ship that chooses to use the Starship Maneuver must make any Pilot checks or attack rolls the Starship Maneuver requires- your success or failure with the Starship Maneuver has no bearing on the success of other units in your squadron. Homebrew Reference Book: New Jedi Order Campaign Guide Prerequisites: Charisma 13, When you use the Talent, you may choose Talents that you possess from the Blockade Runner Talent Tree, and the Wingman Talent Tree as well as the Expert Pilot Talent Tree and Gunner Talent Tree. Homebrew Reference Book: New Jedi Order Campaign Guide Once per encounter, you may make a DC 20 Use the Force check as a Swift Action. Success indicates that as a Reaction, you may grant all members of your squadron a +2 Force bonus on attack rolls and a +2 Force bonus to their Reflex Defense for a number of rounds equal to 1 + your Charisma modifier (minimum 2 rounds).","description":"Prerequisites: Charisma 13, Wisdom 13, Starship Tactics, Once per encounter, when you use a non-attack pattern Starship Maneuver, you grant all ships in your squadron the ability to use the same Starship Maneuver once on their next turn. The Pilot of each ship that chooses to use the Starship Maneuver must make any Pilot checks or attack rolls the Starship Maneuver requires- your success or failure with the Starship Maneuver has no bearing on the success of other units in your squadron. Homebrew Reference Book: New Jedi Order Campaign Guide Prerequisites: Charisma 13, When you use the Talent, you may choose Talents that you possess from the Blockade Runner Talent Tree, and the Wingman Talent Tree as well as the Expert Pilot Talent Tree and Gunner Talent Tree. Homebrew Reference Book: New Jedi Order Campaign Guide Once per encounter, you may make a DC 20 Use the Force check as a Swift Action. Success indicates that as a Reaction, you may grant all members of your squadron a +2 Force bonus on attack rolls and a +2 Force bonus to their Reflex Defense for a number of rounds equal to 1 + your Charisma modifier (minimum 2 rounds).","class":"Ace Pilot","costNumeric":null,"category":"Ace Pilot","tree":"Squadron Leader","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"attribute","ability":"cha","min":13}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"dc1b8c5ce2a70394","tags":["action-economy","defender","feat-chain","force","force-defense","force-offense","leader","light-side","mobility","scout","striker","sustained-damage","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.squadron_maneuvers"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.991dbfc3a436b5a1"}}},{"_id":"3452c426f164a05e","name":"Squadron Tactics","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Squadron Leader","prerequisites":"Charisma 13, Starship Tactics, Squadron Maneuvers","benefit":"Once per encounter, grant a maneuver you use to every ship in your squadron next round.","description":"Once per encounter, grant a maneuver you use to every ship in your squadron next round.","class":"Ace Pilot","costNumeric":null,"category":"Ace Pilot","tree":"Squadron Leader","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"attribute","ability":"wis","min":13},{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.squadron_maneuvers"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"dc1b8c5ce2a70394","tags":["feat-chain","leader","scout","sustained-damage","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.squadron_tactics"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.ec12bc7f161a0893"}}},{"_id":"bc89f90aac5e0eed","name":"Unarmed","type":"weapon","img":"icons/svg/sword.svg","system":{"damage":"1d6+8","damageType":"kinetic","attackBonus":0,"attackAttribute":"str","range":"melee","weight":1,"cost":0,"equipped":true,"description":"","properties":[],"ammunition":{"type":"none","current":0,"max":0},"weaponCategory":"simple","proficiency":"simple","subcategory":""},"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"placeholder":true,"npc":{"flatAttackBonus":12,"flatDamageFormula":"1d6+8","useFlat":true}}}},{"_id":"039e28ffd0c04c95","name":"Blaster Pistol","type":"weapon","img":"icons/svg/sword.svg","system":{"damage":"3d6+6","damageType":"energy","attackBonus":0,"attackAttribute":"dex","range":"ranged","weight":1,"cost":500,"equipped":true,"description":"<p>The standard sidearm used throughout the galaxy. Reliable, common, and effective at close to medium range.</p>","properties":[],"ammunition":{"type":"none","current":0,"max":0},"weaponCategory":"ranged","proficiency":"pistols","subcategory":"pistol","costNumeric":500,"category":"pistol"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.weapons.weapon-blaster-pistol"},"swse":{"npc":{"flatAttackBonus":14,"flatDamageFormula":"3d6+6","useFlat":true}}}},{"_id":"db4dcf9898454194","name":"Weapon System","type":"weapon","img":"icons/svg/sword.svg","system":{"damage":"1d4","damageType":"kinetic","attackBonus":0,"attackAttribute":"dex","range":"ranged","weight":1,"cost":0,"equipped":true,"description":"","properties":[],"ammunition":{"type":"none","current":0,"max":0},"weaponCateg