iciency (Simple Weapons)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.2d680cc46a7972da"}}},{"_id":"c5951a12679f50d2","name":"Improved Stealth","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Camouflage","prerequisites":"","benefit":"You're very good at hiding when mobile. You take no penalty on your Stealth check when moving your normal Speed. This Talent applies to Stealth checks made while Piloting a Starship (see Starship Stealth). You may choose to reroll any Stealth check, but the result of the reroll must be accepted, even if it is worse. This Talent applies to Stealth checks made while Piloting a Starship (see Starship Stealth). Prerequisite: During a Surprise Round, if you make a ranged attack against a target that is Surprised, you can Aim at the target as a Free Action. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy at War If you start your turn with Total Concealment or Total Cover from a target, during that turn you can make a Stealth check as a Swift Action, opposed by the target's Perception check. If you succeed, the target is considered Flat-Footed against you until the end of your turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy","description":"You're very good at hiding when mobile. You take no penalty on your Stealth check when moving your normal Speed. This Talent applies to Stealth checks made while Piloting a Starship (see Starship Stealth). You may choose to reroll any Stealth check, but the result of the reroll must be accepted, even if it is worse. This Talent applies to Stealth checks made while Piloting a Starship (see Starship Stealth). Prerequisite: During a Surprise Round, if you make a ranged attack against a target that is Surprised, you can Aim at the target as a Free Action. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy at War If you start your turn with Total Concealment or Total Cover from a target, during that turn you can make a Stealth check as a Swift Action, opposed by the target's Perception check. If you succeed, the target is considered Flat-Footed against you until the end of your turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy","class":"Scout","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scout","tree":"Camouflage","treeId":"3926d582d2077489","tags":["action-economy","ambush","controller","mobility","perception","piloting","positioning","ranged","scout","skills","stealth","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.improved_stealth"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.073115894cad8cf9"}}},{"_id":"a87f27906a0546fb","name":"Sneak Attack","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Misfortune","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Any time your opponent is Flat-Footed or otherwise denied its Dexterity bonus to Reflex Defense, you deal an additional 1d6 points of damage with a successful melee or ranged attack. You must be within 6 squares of the target to make a with a ranged weapon. You may select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select it, your damage increases by +1d6 (Maximum +10d6). Prerequisite: You can take advantage of your adversary's distractions, no matter how momentary or fleeting. Once per turn, when you Flank a target, you can treat that target as if they were Flat-Footed for one of your attacks. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy If you succeed on a Deception check against a target's Will Defense as a Swift Action, until the start of your next turn you can move though the Threatened Area of that target as part of your Move Action without provoking an Attack of Opportunity. Each Threatened square that you move through counts as 2 squares of movement. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Point-Blank Shot You can use the Talent against a target within 12 squares, instead of within 6 squares. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide You excel at seduction through deception. If you fail a Persuasion check to change a target's Attitude, you can immediately reroll the check using your Deception skill in lieu of your Persuasion skill. You must accept the result of the reroll, even if it is worse. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide Once per encounter as a Move Action, you can attempt to seize a held, carried, or worn object from an adjacent target by making a Disarm attack, with a +10 bonus on your attack roll. If the attack succeeds, you are now holding the object, and you cannot use this Talent in place of the Disarm Action. You cannot conceal the use of this Talent from the target. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy","description":"Any time your opponent is Flat-Footed or otherwise denied its Dexterity bonus to Reflex Defense, you deal an additional 1d6 points of damage with a successful melee or ranged attack. You must be within 6 squares of the target to make a with a ranged weapon. You may select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select it, your damage increases by +1d6 (Maximum +10d6). Prerequisite: You can take advantage of your adversary's distractions, no matter how momentary or fleeting. Once per turn, when you Flank a target, you can treat that target as if they were Flat-Footed for one of your attacks. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy If you succeed on a Deception check against a target's Will Defense as a Swift Action, until the start of your next turn you can move though the Threatened Area of that target as part of your Move Action without provoking an Attack of Opportunity. Each Threatened square that you move through counts as 2 squares of movement. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Point-Blank Shot You can use the Talent against a target within 12 squares, instead of within 6 squares. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide You excel at seduction through deception. If you fail a Persuasion check to change a target's Attitude, you can immediately reroll the check using your Deception skill in lieu of your Persuasion skill. You must accept the result of the reroll, even if it is worse. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide Once per encounter as a Move Action, you can attempt to seize a held, carried, or worn object from an adjacent target by making a Disarm attack, with a +10 bonus on your attack roll. If the attack succeeds, you are now holding the object, and you cannot use this Talent in place of the Disarm Action. You cannot conceal the use of this Talent from the target. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy","class":"Scoundrel","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scoundrel","tree":"Misfortune","treeId":"67b59e020c1660eb","tags":["action-economy","battlefield-control","controller","defender","melee","mobility","positioning","precision","ranged","scaling","scoundrel","skills","social","striker"]},"effects":[{"_id":"3195415b-2276-403c-9fb1-5d323d38d31a","name":"Sneak Attack","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.damage.flatfooted","mode":2,"value":"1d6"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Sneak Attack"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.sneak_attack"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.1505abc8babeeb84"}}},{"_id":"fd83b8cb76690780","name":"Unarmed -1 (1d3)","type":"weapon","img":"icons/svg/sword.svg","system":{"damage":"1d4","damageType":"kinetic","attackBonus":0,"attackAttribute":"str","range":"melee","weight":1,"cost":0,"equipped":true,"description":"","properties":[],"ammunition":{"type":"none","current":0,"max":0},"weaponCategory":"simple","proficiency":"simple","subca