Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisite: Once per encounter, as a Reaction, you gain a +5 luck bonus to any one Defense until the start of your next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy","class":"Scoundrel","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scoundrel","tree":"Fortune","treeId":"cee9b9398682b7d0","tags":["action-economy","defender","precision","scoundrel","striker"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.fools_luck"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.5319a796f2c4ff64"}}},{"_id":"2faf77e5ac7b3ca0","name":"Knack","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Fortune","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Once per day, you can reroll an attack roll and take the better result. You can select this Talent multiple times; each time you select this Talent, you can use it one additional time per day. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Lucky Shot You are possessed of incredible luck and an uncanny ability to succeed where others would fail. You can use each of the following actions once per encounter as a Standard Action: Elude Enemy: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any target within your Range. If you damage the target, you gain a +2 bonus to your Reflex Defense against this target until the beginning of your next turn. Escape: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any target within your Range. If that target successfully damages you before the start of your next turn, you can immediately move 2 squares as a Reaction. This movement does not provoke Attacks of Opportunity. Make your Own Luck: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any target within your Range. If you miss this target, you gain a +2 bonus on your next attack roll. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Once per encounter, as a Reaction, you become immune to all Mind-Affecting effects until the end of your next turn (you can choose to ignore this for beneficial effects). Any Mind-Affecting effects currently afflicting you are also removed, though you can choose to retain any beneficial effects you currently have. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide Prerequisite: A successful hit against you is mitigated by an item you just happen to be wearing or carrying, or glances off your armor or clothing in just the right way. Once per encounter, as a Reaction, you can negate the damage from a single attack that would normally reduce you to 0 Hit Points. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Lucky Shot When making a ranged attack against a target with Cover, you can choose to reduce the benefit of that target's Cover by one step, from Improved Cover to Cover, or Cover to no Cover. You deal only half damage with this attack. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Lucky Shot Once per encounter, you can consider any single d20 roll of 16 or higher to be a Natural 20. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Lucky Shot Once per encounter, you can reroll the damage of one attack, keeping the better of the two results. Gambler's Fortune Talent data created by Sterling Hershey (source). Prerequisites: , Trained in Chosen Skill Select one of the following Skills: Knowledge (Any), Mechanics, Perception, or Use Computer. When making a reroll for that Skill, you may keep the better result.","description":"Once per day, you can reroll an attack roll and take the better result. You can select this Talent multiple times; each time you select this Talent, you can use it one additional time per day. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Lucky Shot You are possessed of incredible luck and an uncanny ability to succeed where others would fail. You can use each of the following actions once per encounter as a Standard Action: Elude Enemy: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any target within your Range. If you damage the target, you gain a +2 bonus to your Reflex Defense against this target until the beginning of your next turn. Escape: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any target within your Range. If that target successfully damages you before the start of your next turn, you can immediately move 2 squares as a Reaction. This movement does not provoke Attacks of Opportunity. Make your Own Luck: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any target within your Range. If you miss this target, you gain a +2 bonus on your next attack roll. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Once per encounter, as a Reaction, you become immune to all Mind-Affecting effects until the end of your next turn (you can choose to ignore this for beneficial effects). Any Mind-Affecting effects currently afflicting you are also removed, though you can choose to retain any beneficial effects you currently have. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide Prerequisite: A successful hit against you is mitigated by an item you just happen to be wearing or carrying, or glances off your armor or clothing in just the right way. Once per encounter, as a Reaction, you can negate the damage from a single attack that would normally reduce you to 0 Hit Points. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Lucky Shot When making a ranged attack against a target with Cover, you can choose to reduce the benefit of that target's Cover by one step, from Improved Cover to Cover, or Cover to no Cover. You deal only half damage with this attack. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Lucky Shot Once per encounter, you can consider any single d20 roll of 16 or higher to be a Natural 20. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Lucky Shot Once per encounter, you can reroll the damage of one attack, keeping the better of the two results. Gambler's Fortune Talent data created by Sterling Hershey (source). Prerequisites: , Trained in Chosen Skill Select one of the following Skills: Knowledge (Any), Mechanics, Perception, or Use Computer. When making a reroll for that Skill, you may keep the better result.","class":"Scoundrel","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scoundrel","tree":"Fortune","treeId":"cee9b9398682b7d0","tags":["action-economy","armor","controller","damage-reduction","defender","mechanics","melee","mobility","perception","positioning","ranged","scaling","scoundrel","skills","slicing","striker","support"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.knack"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.ac6baadb9d65ff7f"}}},{"_id":"4794f068b2454627","name":"Unarmed","type":"weapon","img":"icons/svg/sword.svg","system":{"damage":"1d4+1","damageType":"kinetic","attackBonus":0,"attackAttribute":"str","range":"melee","weight":1,"cost":0,"equipped":true,"description":"","properties":[],"ammunition":{"type":"none","current":0,"max":0},"weaponCategory":"simple","proficiency":"simple","subcategory":""},"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"placeholder":true,"npc":{"flatAttackBonus":2,"flatDamageFormula":"1d4+1","useFlat":true}}}},{"_id":"6dab49d490edd3ca","name":"Knife","type":"weapon","img":"icons/svg/sword.svg","system":{"damage":"1d4+1","damageType":"kinetic","attackBonus":0,"attackAttribute":"str","range":"melee","weight":1,"cost":0,"equipped":true,"description":"","properties":[],"ammunition":{"type":"none","current":0,"max":0},"weaponCategory":"simple","proficiency":"simple","subcategory":""},"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"placeholder":true,"unresolved":"Knife","npc":{"flatAttackBonus":2,"flatDamageFormula":"1d4+1","useFlat":true}}}},{"_id":"19001dbb4fc24d1a","name":"Blaster Pistol","type":"weapon","img":"icons/svg/sword.svg","system":{"damage":"3d6+2","damageTyp