ormalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":88,"tags":["feat-chain","non-force","soldier","striker"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{"value":"+1 bonus on attack rolls with chosen weapon."}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.c41814601364b643"}}},{"_id":"95bda71656e44869","name":"Weapon Proficiency","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"Ignore -5 penalty on attack rolls with weapons of a particular type.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["non-force"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{"value":"Ignore -5 penalty on attack rolls with weapons of a particular type."}},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.ecc2471ac96ec2d4"}}},{"_id":"5f34b61626876419","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","type":"feat","img":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","system":{"featType":"general","benefit":"You are proficient with simple weapons and do not take the -5 penalty when using them.","prerequisite":"","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":87,"tags":["noble","non-force","scoundrel","scout","soldier"],"bonus_feat_for":["Soldier","Scout","Scoundrel","Noble"],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"costNumeric":null,"description":{}},"effects":[{"_id":"220daaa7-e1b5-440d-98cd-10f5e586ef8b","name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.2d680cc46a7972da"}}},{"_id":"e64afb4f06971338","name":"Language Absorption","type":"feat","img":"systems/foundryvtt-swse/assets/icons/force-technique.png","system":{"featType":"force","benefit":"You can use telepathy to forcibly learn a language from another creature. If the target is unwilling, you must succeed a Use the Force check against the target's Will Defense, as with the Telepathy aspect of the Use the Force Skill. You retain the ability to speak and understand this language for 24 hours.","prerequisite":"Telepathy","special":"","normalText":"","sourcebook":"Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide","page":0,"tags":["force-technique"],"bonus_feat_for":[],"uses":{"current":0,"max":0,"perDay":false},"description":"<p>You can use telepathy to forcibly learn a language from another creature. If the target is unwilling, you must succeed a Use the Force check against the target's Will Defense, as with the Telepathy aspect of the Use the Force Skill. You retain the ability to speak and understand this language for 24 hours.</p><p><strong>Related Power:</strong> Telepathy</p><p><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Telepathy</p>","relatedPower":"Telepathy"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcetechniques.d36c0240ac48c171"}}},{"_id":"fb0d5365ba605c81","name":"Battle Meditation","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Sense","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Link Using a meditative battle trance, Force-users are able to join their minds together, collectively becoming stronger. However, a masterful degree of will is required to prevent the participants from sharing their weaknesses as well as their strengths. As a Full-Round Action, you can designate a number of willing allies equal to your Charisma modifier within 12 squares of you. These allies must be Trained in the Use the Force skill. As long as you remain within 12 squares of each other, you can Aid Another on attack rolls and Skill Checks as a Reaction.","description":"Link Using a meditative battle trance, Force-users are able to join their minds together, collectively becoming stronger. However, a masterful degree of will is required to prevent the participants from sharing their weaknesses as well as their strengths. As a Full-Round Action, you can designate a number of willing allies equal to your Charisma modifier within 12 squares of you. These allies must be Trained in the Use the Force skill. As long as you remain within 12 squares of each other, you can Aid Another on attack rolls and Skill Checks as a Reaction.","class":"Jedi","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","tree":"Sense","treeId":"d6b4331c0e31f7e3","tags":["action-economy","force","force-offense","jedi","positioning","striker","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[{"_id":"0cdcb68b-7eeb-45d0-ae5c-575d13648a00","name":"Battle Meditation","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.attacks.allies","mode":2,"value":"1"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Battle Meditation"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.battle_meditation"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.9461c7aa79dd07c6"}}},{"_id":"f6a09c75f9588783","name":"Buried Presence","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Agent Of Ossus","tree":"Agent Of Ossus","prerequisites":"Weapon Proficiency (Pistols) or Weapon Proficiency (Rifles)","description":"When you use either the Talent or the Vanish Talent, you affect one other willing adjacent target, granting it the effect of that Talent as well. You can select this Talent multiple times. Each time you do so, it increases the number of adjacent willing targets you affect by one. You can spend a Force Point as a Swift Action to substitute your Use the Force modifier for your ranged attack bonus when making attacks with a ranged weapon until the beginning of your next turn. You can make a Use the Force check as a Swift Action to vanish from the sight of a single target within line of sight. If the result of your Use the Force check exceeds the target's Will Defense, you gain Total Concealment from that target until the beginning of your next turn, or until you make an attack roll or Skill Check against the target.","benefit":"When you use either the Talent or the Vanish Talent, you affect one other willing adjacent target, granting it the effect of that Talent as well. You can select this Talent multiple times. Each time you do so, it increases the number of adjacent willing targets you affect by one. You can spend a Force Point as a Swift Action to substitute your Use the Force modifier for your ranged attack bonus when making attacks with a ranged weapon until the beginning of your next turn. You can make a Use the Force check as a Swift Action to vanish from the sight of a single target within line of sight. If the result of your Use the Force check exceeds the target's Will Defense, you gain Total Concealment from that target until the beginning of your next turn, or until you make an attack roll or Skill Check against the target.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"754907ded50d4f46","tags":["action-economy","defender","feat-chain","force","force-defense","force-offense","leader","mobility","positioning","ranged","scaling","striker","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.c913aa5322934cfd"}}},{"_id":"a9f77a6571bef8e7","name":"Charm Beast","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Felucian Shaman","prerequisites":"Force Blast","benefit":"Whenever you manage to shift the Attitude of a Beast to Indifferent or Friendly, you may treat that creature as a domesticated animal- but for you only (it remains undomesticated in its response to other creatures). Additionally, you may use this Beast as a Mount, as per the Ride skill, provided that it is at least one size category larger than you and has a comfortable place for you to sit. When you use the Force Blast Force Power, you can spend a Force Point to compare the result of your Use the Force check to the Reflex Defense of all other characters, creatures, and Droids within 2 squares of your target. If you exceed the Reflex Defense of those secondary targets, they also take damage from the Force Blast, and if you fail to exceed their Reflex Defense, they take half damage instead. This is considered to be an Area Attack against the secondary targets (but not against the original target). You can use the Telepathy application of the Use the Force skill as a Swift Action, and you automatically succeed (no roll required) if your target is a willing recipient on the same planet. You can spend a Force Point to infuse an unpowered melee weapon (one that does not require an Energy Cell) with the strength of The Force, making it resistant to the attacks of other Weapons. Infusing the weapon takes a Full-Round Action.","description":"Whenever you manage to shift the Attitude of a Beast to Indifferent or Friendly, you may treat that creature as a domesticated animal- but for you only (it remains undomesticated in its response to other creatures). Additionally, you may use this Beast as a Mount, as per the Ride skill, provided that it is at least one size category larger than you and has a comfortable place for you to sit. When you use the Force Blast Force Power, you can spend a Force Point to compare the result of your Use the Force check to the Reflex Defense of all other characters, creatures, and Droids within 2 squares of your target. If you exceed the Reflex Defense of those secondary targets, they also take damage from the Force Blast, and if you fail to exceed their Reflex Defense, they take half damage instead. This is considered to be an Area Attack against the secondary targets (but not against the original target). You can use the Telepathy application of the Use the Force skill as a Swift Action, and you automatically succeed (no roll required) if your target is a willing recipient on the same planet. You can spend a Force Point to infuse an unpowered melee weapon (one that does not require an Energy Cell) with the strength of The Force, making it resistant to the attacks of other Weapons. Infusing the weapon takes a Full-Round Action.","class":"Force Adept","costNumeric":null,"category":"Force Adept","tree":"Felucian Shaman","treeId":"8a61bf426391431b","tags":["action-economy","battlefield-control","defender","feat-chain","force","force-defense","force-offense","melee","mobility","positioning","striker","support","sustained-damage","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.charm_beast"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.bab9a1ce285f98b9"}}},{"_id":"e5029987cecc5ec8","name":"Deflect","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Lightsaber Forms","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Redirect Shot","description":"Redirect Shot","class":"Jedi","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","tree":"Lightsaber Forms","treeId":"2bc2572e852832e4","tags":["jedi","lightsaber","melee","ranged"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.deflect"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.72c644f7a09b1186"}}},{"_id":"65ba54bfa5294eab","name":"Force Perception","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Sense","prerequisites":"","benefit":"You may spend a Force Point to reroll an Initiative check, keeping the better of the two rolls. Additionally, if you roll a natural 20 on the Initiative check reroll, you immediately regain the Force Point spent to activate this talent. Prerequisite: By focusing on a specific creature in your line of sight, you can gauge how strong in The Force they are. This takes a Standard Action and requires a Use the Force check. If your check result meets or beats the target's Will Defense, you know whether or not they have the Force Sensitivity feat, you know how many Force Powers they know (but not which ones specifically), and you know how many Force Points they currently have. Prerequisites: , Farseeing See also: On the Force, Visions, and Discretion Whenever you use the Farseeing Force Power, you can spend a Force Point as a Swift Action to see into the target's past or future instead of the present. You declare how far into the target's past or future you wish to look, up to a maximum of 1 year per your Character Level. Any information gained about a target's future is subject to change, depending on whether steps are taken to alter that future. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide As a Standard Action, you can spend a Force Point to ignore all Concealment for 1 minute. Prerequisites: , Farseeing As a Swift Action, you can peer into the future in search of signs of danger, removing one use of the Farseeing Force Power from your active Force Power Suite (as though you had just activated the Force Power). Any time before the end of your next turn when you are the target of an attack or Force Power, you can force your attacker to reroll the attack roll (or Use the Force check) against you, keeping the second result. This counts as using the Farseeing Force Power against the attacker, but this Talent replaces the normal rules and effect of that Force Power. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide Prerequisites: , Farseeing When you use the Farseeing Force Power, you can choose to target an object you hold instead of a character or creature. You can look into the targeted item's past, up to a maximum of 5 years per your Character Level. Any information gained about the object's past is based on the thoughts and emotions of the person holding or carrying the object at the time you perceive, which can skew the results of the vision. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide You can spend a Force Point to gain Low-Light Vision (see Visibility) for 1 minute or until the end of the encounter, whichever is longer. Homebrew Reference Book: Clone Wars Saga Edition Fan Sourcebook - Jedi Padawans Prerequisites: Once per encounter, you may spend a Force Point to gain a +1 insight bonus to your Reflex Defense and Will Defense for the remainder of the encounter, or until you are knocked unconscious.","description":"You may spend a Force Point to reroll an Initiative check, keeping the better of the two rolls. Additionally, if you roll a natural 20 on the Initiative check reroll, you immediately regain the Force Point spent to activate this talent. Prerequisite: By focusing on a specific creature in your line of sight, you can gauge how strong in The Force they are. This takes a Standard Action and requires a Use the Force check. If your check result meets or beats the target's Will Defense, you know whether or not they have the Force Sensitivity feat, you know how many Force Powers they know (but not which ones specifically), and you know how many Force Points they currently have. Prerequisites: , Farseeing See also: On the Force, Visions, and Discretion Whenever you use the Farseeing Force Power, you can spend a Force Point as a Swift Action to see into the target's past or future instead of the present. You declare how far into the target's past or future you wish to look, up to a maximum of 1 year per your Character Level. Any information gained about a target's future is subject to change, depending on whether steps are taken to alter that future. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Force Unleashed Campaign Guide As a Standard Action, you can spend a Force Point to ignore all Concealment for 1 minute. Prerequisites: , Farseeing As a Swift Action, you can peer into the future in search of signs of danger, removing one use of the Farseeing Force Power from your active Force Power Suite (as though you had just activated the Force Power). Any time before the end of your next turn when you are the target of an attack or Force Power, you can force your attacker to reroll the attack roll (or Use the Force check) against you, keeping the second result. This counts as using the Farseeing Force Power against the attacker, but this Talent replaces the normal rules and effect of that Force Power. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide Prerequisites: , Farseeing When you use the Farseeing Force Power, you can choose to target an object you hold instead of a character or creature. You can look into the targeted item's past, up to a maximum of 5 years per your Character Level. Any information gained about the object's past is based on the thoughts and emotions of the person holding or carrying the object at the time you perceive, which can skew the results of the vision. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Clone Wars Campaign Guide You can spend a Force Point to gain Low-Light Vision (see Visibility) for 1 minute or until the end of the encounter, whichever is longer. Homebrew Reference Book: Clone Wars Saga Edition Fan Sourcebook - Jedi Padawans Prerequisites: Once per encounter, you may spend a Force Point to gain a +1 insight bonus to your Reflex Defense and Will Defense for the remainder of the encounter, or until you are knocked unconscious.","costNumeric":null,"tree":"Sense","treeId":"d6b4331c0e31f7e3","tags":["action-economy","defender","force","force-defense","force-offense","light-side","mobility","scout","skills","stealth","striker","support"]},"effects":[{"name":"Force Perception (Trained)","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.skills.perception.trained","mode":5,"value":"true"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Force Perception","effectType":"skill-trained"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.force_perception"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.a358402a9fc26c02"}}},{"_id":"7f954ccc7b4c83dc","name":"Illusion","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Krath","prerequisites":"","benefit":"As a Swift Action, you can reduce the penalty for large by one half (rounded down, minimum -1). You have a natural ability to use Dark Side artifacts, such as Sith Talismans and alchemical items. Once per encounter, you may spend a Force Point to treat the damage from a Sith Alchemical Weapon as though you had rolled the maximum damage on the dice. Once per encounter, using rudimentary Sith sorcery, you channel Dark Side energy in a manner that boosts one use of a Force Power. As a Swift Action, you can add 1 die of damage (if the Force Power deals damage) or extend the range of the Force Power by 6 squares (if it has a range beyond yourself or a single target). Using this Talent automatically adds the [Dark Side] descriptor to the Force Power used.","description":"As a Swift Action, you can reduce the penalty for large by one half (rounded down, minimum -1). You have a natural ability to use Dark Side artifacts, such as Sith Talismans and alchemical items. Once per encounter, you may spend a Force Point to treat the damage from a Sith Alchemical Weapon as though you had rolled the maximum damage on the dice. Once per encounter, using rudimentary Sith sorcery, you channel Dark Side energy in a manner that boosts one use of a Force Power. As a Swift Action, you can add 1 die of damage (if the Force Power deals damage) or extend the range of the Force Power by 6 squares (if it has a range beyond yourself or a single target). Using this Talent automatically adds the [Dark Side] descriptor to the Force Power used.","costNumeric":null,"tree":"Krath","treeId":"d29a7261c1be4b83","tags":["action-economy","damage-reduction","dark-side","force","force-offense","mobility","positioning","striker","support","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.illusion"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.8793a955bce166d2"}}},{"_id":"fc7db71a61f128c4","name":"Redirect Shot","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Lightsaber Forms","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Whenever you redirect a deflected blaster bolt (see the Talent), you gain a +5 bonus on your ranged attack roll.","description":"Whenever you redirect a deflected blaster bolt (see the Talent), you gain a +5 bonus on your ranged attack roll.","class":"Jedi","costNumeric":null,"category":"Jedi","tree":"Lightsaber Forms","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.deflect"},{"type":"bab","min":5}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"2bc2572e852832e4","tags":["jedi","lightsaber","melee","positioning","ranged","striker"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.redirect_shot"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.941c1dfd00e697da"}}},{"_id":"12db7218c7ee2844","name":"Telepathic Link","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Alter","prerequisites":"","benefit":"You naturally and unconsciously influence those who are regularly around you. Whenever you roll a natural 20 on an attack roll or Use the Force check, instead of regaining all your spent Force Powers, you may instead choose to grant one ally within 12 squares of you a temporary Force Point. If your ally does not use this temporary Force Point before the end of the encounter, it is lost. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide You form an enhanced with a willing ally, that possesses the Force Sensitivity feat, as a Swift Action. The is maintained until you choose to remove it (no Action required). As long as you remain within one kilometer of your target, you and the target can communicate telepathically as though you were speaking. Once per encounter, you may use a Force Power from your target's Force Power Suite (if the target consents), or you may allow the target to use one of your Force Powers. You may only have one active at a time. Force Bond Talent created by TheSagaContinues user fairytalejedi. Prerequisite: A becomes permanent between yourself and another possessing the Force Sensitivity Feat. While out of combat, you and the bonded individual can freely speak as if in the same location. By spending a Force Point to make a DC 25 Use the Force check, you may give or take a single item of Diminutive size or smaller.","description":"You naturally and unconsciously influence those who are regularly around you. Whenever you roll a natural 20 on an attack roll or Use the Force check, instead of regaining all your spent Force Powers, you may instead choose to grant one ally within 12 squares of you a temporary Force Point. If your ally does not use this temporary Force Point before the end of the encounter, it is lost. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide You form an enhanced with a willing ally, that possesses the Force Sensitivity feat, as a Swift Action. The is maintained until you choose to remove it (no Action required). As long as you remain within one kilometer of your target, you and the target can communicate telepathically as though you were speaking. Once per encounter, you may use a Force Power from your target's Force Power Suite (if the target consents), or you may allow the target to use one of your Force Powers. You may only have one active at a time. Force Bond Talent created by TheSagaContinues user fairytalejedi. Prerequisite: A becomes permanent between yourself and another possessing the Force Sensitivity Feat. While out of combat, you and the bonded individual can freely speak as if in the same location. By spending a Force Point to make a DC 25 Use the Force check, you may give or take a single item of Diminutive size or smaller.","costNumeric":null,"tree":"Alter","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"skillTrained","skill":"usetheforce"}],"_source":"fix5F-canonical"},"treeId":"6ac3416fb6aada56","tags":["action-economy","controller","dual-wield","force","force-control","force-offense","leader","light-side","mobility","positioning","support","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.telepathic_link"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.25dd9d9b3b66c048"}}},{"_id":"f7beec17bce10517","name":"Visions","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Keetael","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Prerequisites: The long-lived Draethos are particularly adept at searching and understanding the past. When using Farseeing to look into the past, reduce your DC numbers by half. Also, you are able to see everything within 6 squares of your target clearly without spending a Force Point.","description":"Prerequisites: The long-lived Draethos are particularly adept at searching and understanding the past. When using Farseeing to look into the past, reduce your DC numbers by half. Also, you are able to see everything within 6 squares of your target clearly without spending a Force Point.","costNumeric":null,"tree":"Keetael","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.force_perception"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"dad3c0da191748c1","tags":["damage-reduction","force","positioning"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.visions"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.da12fc505efc5eea"}}},{"_id":"40e4cf9ca9d66ecc","name":"Ballistakinesis","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/eye.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"Unknown","useTheForce":"","time":"standard","range":"","target":"","duration":"","effect":"","special":"","descriptor":"","dcChart":"","maintainable":false,"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1,"perDay":true}},"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"placeholder":true,"unresolved":"Ballistakinesis"}}},{"_id":"70088156379bf319","name":"Battle Strike","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"telekinetic","useTheForce":15,"time":"Swift Action","range":"Personal","target":"You","duration":"1 round","effect":"<p>You channel the Force to enhance your next melee attack. Your next melee attack this round gains a +1d6 bonus to damage.</p>","special":"<p>This bonus damage is Force damage and bypasses Damage Reduction.</p>","descriptor":["Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":94,"tags":["enhancement","damage","melee"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":2,"max":2},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.f177dc6d65f76de9"}}},{"_id":"f2e887e822dbc046","name":"Convection","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/eye.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"Unknown","useTheForce":"","time":"standard","range":"","target":"","duration":"","effect":"","special":"","descriptor":"","dcChart":"","maintainable":false,"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1,"perDay":true}},"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"placeholder":true,"unresolved":"Convection"}}},{"_id":"4e6a3e52ed48d570","name":"Crucitorn","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/eye.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"Unknown","useTheForce":"","time":"standard","range":"","target":"","duration":"","effect":"","special":"","descriptor":"","dcChart":"","maintainable":false,"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1,"perDay":true}},"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"placeholder":true,"unresolved":"Crucitorn"}}},{"_id":"46f4421170b608ac","name":"Farseeing","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telepathic","useTheForce":20,"time":"1 minute","range":"Unlimited","target":"Special","duration":"Concentration","effect":"<p>You peer through the Force to see distant locations or events. You can observe a place you've been before or a person you know, regardless of distance.</p>","special":"<p>The GM may require additional checks for very distant or obscured visions.</p>","descriptor":["Mind-Affecting","Scrying"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":true,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":95,"tags":["utility","divination","scrying"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.0419ecb55f011f81"}}},{"_id":"26d74e771487127d","name":"Fold Space","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/eye.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"Unknown","useTheForce":"","time":"standard","range":"","target":"","duration":"","effect":"","special":"","descriptor":"","dcChart":"","maintainable":false,"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1,"perDay":true}},"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"placeholder":true,"unresolved":"Fold Space"}}},{"_id":"4c0462f79e1cfa19","name":"Force Light","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/eye.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"Unknown","useTheForce":"","time":"standard","range":"","target":"","duration":"","effect":"","special":"","descriptor":"","dcChart":"","maintainable":false,"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1,"perDay":true}},"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"placeholder":true,"unresolved":"Force Light"}}},{"_id":"468e86fa3d51b579","name":"Force Shield","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/eye.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"Unknown","useTheForce":"","time":"standard","range":"","target":"","duration":"","effect":"","special":"","descriptor":"","dcChart":"","maintainable":false,"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1,"perDay":true}},"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"placeholder":true,"unresolved":"Force Shield"}}},{"_id":"df85ff3a7771ce1e","name":"Force Slam","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telekinetic","useTheForce":20,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One creature or object","duration":"Instantaneous","effect":"<p>You use telekinetic force to violently slam your target against a surface. The target takes 4d6 damage and is knocked prone.</p>","special":"<p>The target must be within 6 squares of a solid surface (wall, floor, ceiling).</p>","descriptor":["Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":97,"tags":["attack","damage","telekinetic","prone"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.462a6c23e00c4dfc"}}},{"_id":"3adc102dd8f90747","name":"Force Thrust","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telekinetic","useTheForce":20,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One creature or object","duration":"Instantaneous","effect":"<p>You violently push your target away with telekinetic force. The target is pushed 6 squares away from you and knocked prone, taking 2d6 damage.</p>","special":"<p>If the target hits an obstacle during the push, they take an additional 1d6 damage per 2 squares not traveled.</p>","descriptor":["Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":97,"tags":["attack","movement","telekinetic","forced-movement"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.d51bf85903366b6b"}}},{"_id":"ca6eb3793790610d","name":"Force Track","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"telepathic","useTheForce":15,"time":"1 minute","range":"Touch","target":"One creature","duration":"24 hours","effect":"<p>You place a Force 'mark' on your target, allowing you to track them through the Force. You always know the target's direction and approximate distance for the duration.</p>","special":"<p>The target can attempt a Will save (DC = your UTF check) to notice the mark.</p>","descriptor":["Mind-Affecting"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":97,"tags":["utility","tracking","detection"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.2466fc76adef817b"}}},{"_id":"48744bc3895fa3a3","name":"Mind Trick","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":1,"discipline":"telepathic","useTheForce":15,"time":"Standard Action","range":"6 squares","target":"One creature","duration":"1 minute or until completed","effect":"<p>You influence a weak mind to believe what you tell them or follow a simple suggestion. The target must make a Will save (DC = your UTF check) or be affected.</p>","special":"<p>The suggestion must be reasonable and the target must be able to understand you.</p>","descriptor":["Mind-Affecting"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":98,"tags":["mind-control","suggestion","social"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.e6649f366d6c5737"}}},{"_id":"a06d56a198c60c54","name":"Move Object","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telekinetic","useTheForce":15,"time":"Standard Action","range":"12 squares","target":"One object or creature","duration":"Concentration","effect":"<p>You move objects or creatures through the air using telekinesis. The maximum size/weight you can move depends on your Use the Force check result.</p>","special":"<p>Unwilling creatures can make a Will save (DC = your UTF check) to resist being moved.</p>","descriptor":["Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[{"dc":15,"effect":"Medium (50 kg)","description":"Move objects up to Medium size or 50 kg"},{"dc":20,"effect":"Large (250 kg)","description":"Move objects up to Large size or 250 kg"},{"dc":25,"effect":"Huge (1 ton)","description":"Move objects up to Huge size or 1 metric ton"},{"dc":30,"effect":"Gargantuan (5 tons)","description":"Move objects up to Gargantuan size or 5 metric tons"},{"dc":35,"effect":"Colossal (20 tons)","description":"Move objects up to Colossal size or 20 metric tons (starfighter-sized)"}],"maintainable":true,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition Core Rulebook","page":98,"tags":["telekinetic","movement","utility"],"inSuite":true,"uses":{"current":1,"max":1},"costNumeric":null},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.forcepowers.289013a32bd179ad"}}},{"_id":"051431327a3022e1","name":"Negate Energy","type":"force-power","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"powerLevel":2,"discipline":"telekinetic","useTheForce":20,"time":"Reaction","range":"Personal or touch","target":"You or one creature","duration":"Instantaneous","effect":"<p>You use the Force to absorb or deflect energy damage. The target gains energy resistance 20 against one energy attack.</p>","special":"<p>This power can be used as a Reaction when you or an ally is targeted by an energy attack.</p>","descriptor":["Telekinetic"],"dcChart":[],"maintainable":false,"sourcebook":"Saga Edition C