"name":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","icon":"icons/svg/upgrade.svg","changes":[],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"feat","featName":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)","effectType":"passive_effect","flagType":"Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.feats.2d680cc46a7972da"}}},{"_id":"a1d8c6f1082a5398","name":"Disruptive","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Misfortune","prerequisites":"","benefit":"As a Standard Action, you can do or say something that catches your enemies off guard. All opponents within 6 squares of you, and within your line of sight take a -2 penalty to their Defenses until the start of your next turn. The penalty is negated if line of sight is broken. This Talent has a range of 6 squares at Starship Scale. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy at War Prerequisites: , Walk the Line You can create opportunities to chip away at our opponents' defenses. You can use each of the following actions once per encounter as a Standard Action: Create Opening: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any target within your Range. If you damage the target, the target takes a -5 penalty to their Reflex Defense until the start of your next turn. Crippling Attack: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any target within your Range. Until the start of your next turn, the target takes a -2 penalty to their base speed. Vicious Attack: Make a melee or ranged attack within your Range against two opponents that are within 2 squares of each other. Make separate attack rolls at a -5 penalty against each target, but roll damage once only. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy You can fill your opponent with doubt by making a Persuasion check as a Standard Action against a single target that can hear and understand you within 12 squares of you. If your check result equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, the target takes a -2 penalty to its base speed, and if the target takes a Standard Action, it must also spend its Swift Action. This penalty lasts until the end of the target's next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy","description":"As a Standard Action, you can do or say something that catches your enemies off guard. All opponents within 6 squares of you, and within your line of sight take a -2 penalty to their Defenses until the start of your next turn. The penalty is negated if line of sight is broken. This Talent has a range of 6 squares at Starship Scale. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy at War Prerequisites: , Walk the Line You can create opportunities to chip away at our opponents' defenses. You can use each of the following actions once per encounter as a Standard Action: Create Opening: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any target within your Range. If you damage the target, the target takes a -5 penalty to their Reflex Defense until the start of your next turn. Crippling Attack: Make a single melee or ranged attack against any target within your Range. Until the start of your next turn, the target takes a -2 penalty to their base speed. Vicious Attack: Make a melee or ranged attack within your Range against two opponents that are within 2 squares of each other. Make separate attack rolls at a -5 penalty against each target, but roll damage once only. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy You can fill your opponent with doubt by making a Persuasion check as a Standard Action against a single target that can hear and understand you within 12 squares of you. If your check result equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, the target takes a -2 penalty to its base speed, and if the target takes a Standard Action, it must also spend its Swift Action. This penalty lasts until the end of the target's next turn. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy","class":"Scoundrel","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scoundrel","tree":"Misfortune","treeId":"67b59e020c1660eb","tags":["action-economy","defender","melee","mobility","positioning","ranged","scaling","scoundrel","skills","social","striker"]},"effects":[{"_id":"4eefbe8a-47cc-4cee-a02a-7c11b76bd6b5","name":"Disruptive","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.morale.bonuses_suppressed","mode":5,"value":"true"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Disruptive"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.disruptive"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.91b335f8565b90ef"}}},{"_id":"5a673a18f7e96764","name":"Impel Ally I","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Mastermind","prerequisites":"","benefit":"You can spend two Swift Actions to grant one ally the ability to take a Standard Action or Move Action. The ally must move immediately on your turn, before you do anything else, or else the opportunity is wasted. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy of Intrigue Prerequisites: , I Once per encounter, you can spend three Swift Actions on consecutive turns to grant one ally the ability to take a Standard Action and a Move Action. The ally must act immediately on your turn when the final Swift Action is spent, before you do anything else, or the opportunity is wasted. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , I As a Standard Action, you can designate a target to be the object of your allies' wrath. While your allies have line of sight to you or until you are unconscious or dead, your allies gain a +2 morale bonus on attack rolls against the target and a +2 morale bonus on Skill Checks against that target. You can designate a new target on any round by using another Standard Action. You can only use this Talent against one opponent at a time. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions Prerequisites: , I When an ally uses an Action granted to him or her by you, the ally can reroll any attack or check made during that Action, taking the better result. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , I Once per encounter, you can spend three Swift Actions on consecutive turns to increase the speed of all allies within your line of sight of you by 2. The increased speed lasts until the start of your next turn after the third Swift Action is spent. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy","description":"You can spend two Swift Actions to grant one ally the ability to take a Standard Action or Move Action. The ally must move immediately on your turn, before you do anything else, or else the opportunity is wasted. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Galaxy of Intrigue Prerequisites: , I Once per encounter, you can spend three Swift Actions on consecutive turns to grant one ally the ability to take a Standard Action and a Move Action. The ally must act immediately on your turn when the final Swift Action is spent, before you do anything else, or the opportunity is wasted. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , I As a Standard Action, you can designate a target to be the object of your allies' wrath. While your allies have line of sight to you or until you are unconscious or dead, your allies gain a +2 morale bonus on attack rolls against the target and a +2 morale bonus on Skill Checks against that target. You can designate a new target on any round by using another Standard Action. You can only use this Talent against one opponent at a time. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions Prerequisites: , I When an ally uses an Action granted to him or her by you, the ally can reroll any attack or check made during that Action, taking the better result. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , I Once per encounter, you can spend three Swift Actions on consecutive turns to increase the speed of all allies within your line of sight of you by 2. The increased speed lasts until the start of your next turn after the third Swift Action is spent. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy","class":"Crime Lord","costNumeric":null,"category":"Crime Lord","tree":"Mastermind","treeId":"560cc7994b357a0d","tags":["action-economy","controller","leader","mobility","striker","support","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.impel_ally_i"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.aa32a31a179fe5c1"}}},{"_id":"bfae08faf3930a0a","name":"Impel Ally II","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Mastermind","prerequisites":"Impel Ally I","benefit":"Designated ally can make a standard or move action immediately or the effect is wasted.","description":"An ally may immediately take a move or standard action or lose it.","class":"Crime Lord","costNumeric":null,"category":"Crime Lord","tree":"Mastermind","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.impel_ally_i"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"560cc7994b357a0d","tags":["action-economy","controller","feat-chain","mobility","support","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.impel_ally_ii"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.b11a87e70f957ed2"}}},{"_id":"b5243650859e56de","name":"Presence","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Influence","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Once per encounter, you can make a Persuasion check as a Standard Action to demand surrender from an opponent who has been reduced to one-half or less of its hit points. If your check result equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, it surrenders to you and your allies, drops any weapons it is holding, and takes no hostile actions. If the target is higher level than you, it gains a +5 bonus to its Will Defense. If you or any of your allies attack it, it no longer submits to your will and can act normally. You can only use this Talent against a particular target once per encounter. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Prerequisites: , Weaken Resolve Prerequisite: Once per round, when you deal damage equal to or greater than the target's Damage Threshold, you can make a Persuasion check as a Free Action; if the result equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, you fill the target with terror, causing it to flee from you at top speed for 1 minute. The target can't take Standard Actions, Swift Actions, or Full-Round Actions while fleeing, but the target stops fleeing and can act normally if it is wounded. As a Free Action or Reaction, the target can spend a Force Point (if it has not already spent one earlier in the round) to negate the effect. The effect is automatically negated if the target's level is equal to or higher than your Character Level. This is a Mind-Affecting fear effect. Unlike with other Mind-Affecting effects, you need only to hail a Vehicle to weaken the crew's resolve. When you deal damage that equals or exceeds a Vehicle's Damage Threshold, you may use this Talent; in addition, you may Ready an Action to use this Talent after any Gunner on your Vehicle deals damage that equals or exceeds a Vehicle's Damage Threshold. You make your check against the Vehicle's Commander; all Nonheroic crews are assumed to have a Will Defense of 10. The effect is automatically negated if the target Vehicle's Challenge Level is greater than your Heroic Level or your Vehicle's Challenge Level. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide Prerequisites: , Trained in Persuasion You get under an opponent's skin. Once per encounter, make a Persuasion check to Intimidate one creature within line of sight as a Standard Action. On a success, instead of the normal effect of an Intimidate application of the Persuasion skill, the affected creature can take only a single Swift Action on its next turn. If the target is a higher level than you, it gains a +5 bonus to its Will Defense against the Intimidate check. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide Prerequisites: , Trained in Persuasion Once per encounter, as a Reaction, you can make a Persuasion check to Intimidate one creature that is making a melee or ranged attack against you, and is within your line of sight. If you succeed, you impose a -5 penalty to that attack roll. If the target is a higher level than you, it gains a +5 bonus to its Will Defense against the Intimidate check. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook","description":"Once per encounter, you can make a Persuasion check as a Standard Action to demand surrender from an opponent who has been reduced to one-half or less of its hit points. If your check result equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, it surrenders to you and your allies, drops any weapons it is holding, and takes no hostile actions. If the target is higher level than you, it gains a +5 bonus to its Will Defense. If you or any of your allies attack it, it no longer submits to your will and can act normally. You can only use this Talent against a particular target once per encounter. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Prerequisites: , Weaken Resolve Prerequisite: Once per round, when you deal damage equal to or greater than the target's Damage Threshold, you can make a Persuasion check as a Free Action; if the result equals or exceeds the target's Will Defense, you fill the target with terror, causing it to flee from you at top speed for 1 minute. The target can't take Standard Actions, Swift Actions, or Full-Round Actions while fleeing, but the target stops fleeing and can act normally if it is wounded. As a Free Action or Reaction, the target can spend a Force Point (if it has not already spent one earlier in the round) to negate the effect. The effect is automatically negated if the target's level is equal to or higher than your Character Level. This is a Mind-Affecting fear effect. Unlike with other Mind-Affecting effects, you need only to hail a Vehicle to weaken the crew's resolve. When you deal damage that equals or exceeds a Vehicle's Damage Threshold, you may use this Talent; in addition, you may Ready an Action to use this Talent after any Gunner on your Vehicle deals damage that equals or exceeds a Vehicle's Damage Threshold. You make your check against the Vehicle's Commander; all Nonheroic crews are assumed to have a Will Defense of 10. The effect is automatically negated if the target Vehicle's Challenge Level is greater than your Heroic Level or your Vehicle's Challenge Level. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide Prerequisites: , Trained in Persuasion You get under an opponent's skin. Once per encounter, make a Persuasion check to Intimidate one creature within line of sight as a Standard Action. On a success, instead of the normal effect of an Intimidate application of the Persuasion skill, the affected creature can take only a single Swift Action on its next turn. If the target is a higher level than you, it gains a +5 bonus to its Will Defense against the Intimidate check. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide Prerequisites: , Trained in Persuasion Once per encounter, as a Reaction, you can make a Persuasion check to Intimidate one creature that is making a melee or ranged attack against you, and is within your line of sight. If you succeed, you impose a -5 penalty to that attack roll. If the target is a higher level than you, it gains a +5 bonus to its Will Defense against the Intimidate check. This is a Mind-Affecting effect. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook","class":"Noble","costNumeric":null,"category":"Noble","tree":"Influence","treeId":"8375b9b26b679901","tags":["action-economy","damage-reduction","defender","force","force-defense","force-offense","melee","mobility","noble","positioning","ranged","skills","social","striker","support","sustained-damage"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.presence"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.ec8f2ba706cc2c05"}}},{"_id":"4af0048a423f9905","name":"Walk the Line","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Misfortune","prerequisites":"Disruptive","benefit":"Enemies in line of sight take -2 to defenses until your next turn.","description":"Enemies in line of sight take -2 to all defenses until your next turn.","class":"Scoundrel","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scoundrel","tree":"Misfortune","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.disruptive"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"67b59e020c1660eb","tags":["defender","feat-chain","scoundrel","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.walk_the_line"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.3f8f5305eabc525e"}}},{"_id":"490682c1f7fea51a","name":"Weaken Resolve","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Influence","prerequisites":"","benefit":"As , except that the target doesn't stop fleeing from you if it is wounded.","description":"As , except that the target doesn't stop fleeing from you if it is wounded.","class":"Noble","costNumeric":null,"category":"Noble","tree":"Influence","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.presence"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"8375b9b26b679901","tags":["noble","striker"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.weaken_resolve"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.28c306c37ccb9fcf"}}},{"_id":"01099825c20d297f","name":"Unarmed","type":"weapon","img":"icons/svg/sword.svg","system":{"damage":"1d6+4","damageType":"kinetic","attackBonus":0,"attackAttribute":"str","range":"melee","weight":1,"cost":0,"equipped":true,"description":"","properties":[],"ammunition":{"type":"none","current":0,"max":0},"weaponCategory":"simple","proficiency":"simple","subcategory":""},"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"placeholder":true,"npc":{"flatAttackBonus":6,"flatDamageFormula":"1d6+4","useFlat":true}}}}],"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"import":{"source":"books","raw":{"Size":"Large","Species":"Hutt","Nonheroic Level":0,"Class Levels":{"Noble":4,"Scoundrel":3,"Lord":2},"Destiny Points":1,"Force Points":7,"Dark Side Points":6,"Initiative":10,"Senses":"Perception +17","Languages":["Basic","Bocce","Gamorrean","High Galactic","Huttese","Quarrenese","Rodese","Ryl","Shyriiwook (understand only)"],"Unassigned Languages":0,"Reflex Defense":22,"Flat-Footed Defense":21,"Fortitude Defense":21,"Will Defense":27,"Hit Points":57,"Damage Threshold":31,"Speed":"2 Squares","Melee Weapons":"Unarmed +6 (1d6+4)","Ranged Weapons":"By Weapon +7","Base Attack Bonus":6,"Grapple":12,"Attack Options":["Point-Blank Shot"],"Special Actions":["Command Cover (+1)","Disruptive","Impel Ally II","Presence","Walk the Line","Weaken Resolve"],"Force Powers":[],"Force Secrets":[],"Force Techniques":[],"Strength":10,"Dexterity":13,"Constitution":12,"Intelligence":16,"Wisdom":16,"Charisma":15,"Talents":["Talents : Disruptive","Impel Ally I","Impel Ally II","Presence","Walk the Line","Weaken Resolve"],"Feats":["Feats : Improved Damage Threshold","Improved Defenses","Linguist","Point-Blank Shot","Skill Focus (Deception)","Skill Focus (Perception)","Skill Focus (Persuasion)","Weapon Proficiency (Pistols)","Weapon Proficiency (Simple Weapons)"