ept at using a Cortosis Gauntlet to parry Lightsaber attacks. You gain a +2 bonus when making an opposed Unarmed melee attack roll against a Lightsaber attack.","description":"When calculating your Reflex Defense, you may add your Heroic Level plus one-half your Armor bonus (rounded down), or your Armor bonus alone, whichever is higher. This Talent counts as both the Talent and the Improved Talent for the purposes of prerequisites. You are adept at using a Cortosis Gauntlet to parry Lightsaber attacks. You gain a +2 bonus when making an opposed Unarmed melee attack roll against a Lightsaber attack.","class":"Soldier","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","tree":"Knight's Armor","treeId":"ea01d740c91888b3","tags":["armor","defender","lightsaber","melee","scaling","soldier","striker","sustained-damage","unarmed"]},"effects":[{"_id":"28f1f3db-0c6f-4614-bdcf-000f1542a25b","name":"Armored Defense","icon":"icons/svg/shield.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.defenses.reflex.misc","mode":2,"value":"1","priority":20}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Armored Defense"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.armored_defense"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.4c236343b01ea763"}}},{"_id":"ca34f8b73050c7ea","name":"Dastardly Strike","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Misfortune","tree":"Misfortune","prerequisites":"Combat Reflexes","description":"Whenever you deal damage to an opponent denied its Dexterity bonus to its Reflex Defense, you can choose not to move the target down the Condition Track and instead impose a -5 penalty on all your opponent's attack and melee damage rolls until the end of your next turn. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook At the start of your turn, you may spend a Force Point. Until the start of your next turn, you can make an Attack of Opportunity against a single opponent that has just taken damage from another character. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook When attacking with a Light Melee weapon, a Lightsaber, or any other weapon that benefits from the Weapon Finesse Feat, you may add an additional point of damage on a successful attack.","benefit":"Whenever you deal damage to an opponent denied its Dexterity bonus to its Reflex Defense, you can choose not to move the target down the Condition Track and instead impose a -5 penalty on all your opponent's attack and melee damage rolls until the end of your next turn. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook At the start of your turn, you may spend a Force Point. Until the start of your next turn, you can make an Attack of Opportunity against a single opponent that has just taken damage from another character. Homebrew Reference Book: Legacy of the Force Sourcebook When attacking with a Light Melee weapon, a Lightsaber, or any other weapon that benefits from the Weapon Finesse Feat, you may add an additional point of damage on a successful attack.","class":"","category":"","costNumeric":null,"treeId":"67b59e020c1660eb","tags":["condition-removal","controller","defender","feat-chain","force","force-control","force-defense","force-offense","lightsaber","melee","mobility","striker","talent-chain"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.9e4345faaaa94dd8"}}},{"_id":"406490709dc485e0","name":"Improved Armored Defense","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Armor Specialist","prerequisites":"Armored Defense","benefit":"Your Reflex Defense bonus equals either your heroic level + half your armor bonus, or your armor bonus.","description":"Your Reflex Defense bonus equals either your heroic level plus half your armor bonus or your armor bonus.","class":"Soldier","costNumeric":null,"category":"Soldier","tree":"Armor Specialist","prerequisitesStructured":{"type":"all","conditions":[{"type":"talent","id":"swse.talent.armored_defense"}],"_source":"canonical-csv"},"treeId":"17cec542331cb4e4","tags":["armor","defender","feat-chain","soldier","striker","talent-chain"]},"effects":[{"_id":"842ee02b-8f7e-4a40-802a-c6fe553379a5","name":"Improved Armored Defense","icon":"icons/svg/shield.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.defenses.reflex","mode":2,"value":"2"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Improved Armored Defense"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.improved_armored_defense"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.394809ed8baff1b9"}}},{"_id":"43f58d54bd037de7","name":"Murderous Arts I","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Assassin","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Whenever you successfully hit an opponent that you have Marked, your melee and ranged attack attacks deal an additional +1d6 damage. Once per encounter, when you drop a foe to 0 Hit Points or push an opponent to the bottom of the Condition Track, you can immediately take a bonus Standard Action. As a Move Action, you can move 1 square without provoking an Attack of Opportunity. When you make a ranged attack against a target that is not at Point-Blank Range, you add half your Class Level to your damage roll.","description":"Whenever you successfully hit an opponent that you have Marked, your melee and ranged attack attacks deal an additional +1d6 damage. Once per encounter, when you drop a foe to 0 Hit Points or push an opponent to the bottom of the Condition Track, you can immediately take a bonus Standard Action. As a Move Action, you can move 1 square without provoking an Attack of Opportunity. When you make a ranged attack against a target that is not at Point-Blank Range, you add half your Class Level to your damage roll.","class":"Assassin","costNumeric":null,"category":"Assassin","tree":"Assassin","treeId":"186daeee7bd65a69","tags":["action-economy","condition-removal","controller","melee","mobility","positioning","ranged","striker"]},"effects":[{"_id":"c7a47945-e3d7-4e53-a0eb-afa46e73b4bc","name":"Murderous Arts I","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.damage","mode":2,"value":"1d6"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Murderous Arts I"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.murderous_arts_i"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.0d58e041b9bf0be8"}}},{"_id":"15a24839011850c8","name":"Sneak Attack","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Misfortune","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Any time your opponent is Flat-Footed or otherwise denied its Dexterity bonus to Reflex Defense, you deal an additional 1d6 points of damage with a successful melee or ranged attack. You must be within 6 squares of the target to make a with a ranged weapon. You may select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select it, your damage increases by +1d6 (Maximum +10d6). Prerequisite: You can take advantage of your adversary's distractions, no matter how momentary or fleeting. Once per turn, when you Flank a target, you can treat that target as if they were Flat-Footed for one of your attacks. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy If you succeed on a Deception check against a target's Will Defense as a Swift Action, until the start of your next turn you can move though the Threatened Area of that target as part of your Move Action without provoking an Attack of Opportunity. Each Threatened square that you move through counts as 2 squares of movement. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Point-Blank Shot You can use the Talent against a target within 12 squares, instead of within 6 squares. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide You excel at seduction through deception. If you fail a Persuasion check to change a target's Attitude, you can immediately reroll the check using your Deception skill in lieu of your Persuasion skill. You must accept the result of the reroll, even if it is worse. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide Once per encounter as a Move Action, you can attempt to seize a held, carried, or worn object from an adjacent target by making a Disarm attack, with a +10 bonus on your attack roll. If the attack succeeds, you are now holding the object, and you cannot use this Talent in place of the Disarm Action. You cannot conceal the use of this Talent from the target. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy","description":"Any time your opponent is Flat-Footed or otherwise denied its Dexterity bonus to Reflex Defense, you deal an additional 1d6 points of damage with a successful melee or ranged attack. You must be within 6 squares of the target to make a with a ranged weapon. You may select this Talent multiple times. Each time you select it, your damage increases by +1d6 (Maximum +10d6). Prerequisite: You can take advantage of your adversary's distractions, no matter how momentary or fleeting. Once per turn, when you Flank a target, you can treat that target as if they were Flat-Footed for one of your attacks. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy If you succeed on a Deception check against a target's Will Defense as a Swift Action, until the start of your next turn you can move though the Threatened Area of that target as part of your Move Action without provoking an Attack of Opportunity. Each Threatened square that you move through counts as 2 squares of movement. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy Prerequisites: , Point-Blank Shot You can use the Talent against a target within 12 squares, instead of within 6 squares. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide You excel at seduction through deception. If you fail a Persuasion check to change a target's Attitude, you can immediately reroll the check using your Deception skill in lieu of your Persuasion skill. You must accept the result of the reroll, even if it is worse. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide Once per encounter as a Move Action, you can attempt to seize a held, carried, or worn object from an adjacent target by making a Disarm attack, with a +10 bonus on your attack roll. If the attack succeeds, you are now holding the object, and you cannot use this Talent in place of the Disarm Action. You cannot conceal the use of this Talent from the target. Reference Book: Star Wars Saga Edition Scum and Villainy","class":"Scoundrel","costNumeric":null,"category":"Scoundrel","tree":"Misfortune","treeId":"67b59e020c1660eb","tags":["action-economy","battlefield-control","controller","defender","melee","mobility","positioning","precision","ranged","scaling","scoundrel","skills","social","striker"]},"effects":[{"_id":"3195415b-2276-403c-9fb1-5d323d38d31a","name":"Sneak Attack","icon":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","changes":[{"key":"system.damage.flatfooted","mode":2,"value":"1d6"}],"disabled":false,"duration":{},"flags":{"swse":{"source":"talent","talentName":"Sneak Attack"}}}],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.sneak_attack"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.1505abc8babeeb84"}}},{"_id":"3bef3be41ef5cf3e","name":"Sniping Assassin","type":"talent","img":"icons/svg/item-bag.svg","system":{"talent_tree":"Assassin","prerequisites":"","benefit":"Once per encounter, when you make a ranged attack against a target that is not at Point-Blank Range, you can ignore your target's Armor bonus to their Reflex Defense. Prerequisites: , Sniping Marksman By taking only a single Swift Action, you can Aim at a target that is not within Point-Blank Range.","description":"Once per encounter, when you make a ranged attack against a target that is not at Point-Blank Range, you can ignore your target's Armor bonus to their Reflex Defense. Prerequisites: , Sniping Marksman By taking only a single Swift Action, you can Aim at a target that is not within Point-Blank Range.","class":"Assassin","costNumeric":null,"category":"Assassin","tree":"Assassin","treeId":"186daeee7bd65a69","tags":["action-economy","armor","defender","mobility","positioning","ranged"]},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"swse":{"id":"swse.talent.sniping_assassin"},"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.talents.6ea04b7286133846"}}},{"_id":"bf7acd7cb0efb157","name":"Unarmed","type":"weapon","img":"icons/svg/sword.svg","system":{"damage":"1d4+5","damageType":"kinetic","attackBonus":0,"attackAttribute":"str","range":"melee","weight":1,"cost":0,"equipped":true,"description":"","properties":[],"ammunition":{"type":"none","current":0,"max":0},"weaponCategory":"simple","proficiency":"simple","subcategory":""},"effects":[],"flags":{"swse":{"placeholder":true,"npc":{"flatAttackBonus":8,"flatDamageFormula":"1d4+5","useFlat":true}}}},{"_id":"81dbbb320fe68c28","name":"Sniper Blaster Rifle","type":"weapon","img":"icons/svg/sword.svg","system":{"damage":"3d10+5","damageType":"energy","attackBonus":0,"attackAttribute":"dex","range":"ranged","weight":8,"cost":2000,"equipped":true,"description":"<p>A precision long-range blaster rifle.</p>","properties":["Military","Accurate"],"ammunition":{"type":"none","current":0,"max":0},"weaponCategory":"ranged","proficiency":"rifles","subcategory":"rifle","costNumeric":2000,"category":"rifle"},"effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"core":{"sourceId":"Compendium.foundryvtt-swse.weapons.weapon-sniper-blaster-rifle"},"swse":{"npc":{"flatAttackBonus":11,"flatDamageFormula":"3d10+5","useFlat":true}}}},{"_id":"64920ffdb6a586a7","name":"Sniper Blaster Rifle (with Deadeye)","type":"weapon","img":"icons/svg/sword.svg","system":{"damage":"4d10+5","dama